{"variant_id": "a61fc8ae-f74d-4371-8a19-ff70525dc424", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14981853C>T", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71263, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=4.0e-05 (10 alleles), genome AF=6.6e-06. For autosomal recessive SCID, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing alleles. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "Computational predictions support deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.04), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (0.738). Variant affects conserved residue in the metallo-beta-lactamase nuclease domain (Pfam PF12706). CADD/DITTO scores unavailable but secondary predictors support pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency) is highly specific for this gene. DCLRE1C/Artemis deficiency is a well-established cause of RS-SCID with autosomal recessive inheritance. The phenotype-genotype correlation is strong.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV002199693). The variant is a missense change (p.Glu88Lys) in the critical nuclease domain of Artemis protein. Loss of function in DCLRE1C is an established mechanism for SCID (PVS1 would apply to null variants but not missense). No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified. For recessive disorders, PM3 could be applied if variant is confirmed in trans with another pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "4aa4fc9c-637a-4445-b479-2c718e266b8e", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.138633282T>C", "gene": "F9", "disease": "hemophilia B", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 131564, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No computational evidence suggests pathogenicity.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.582T>C, p.Thr194=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at a canonical splice site. ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign'."}}
{"variant_id": "6b267be1-2f40-4c99-98c5-0bdcf3e6c3b5", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68842480G>C", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP2", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 43105, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency exceeds 5% threshold: gnomAD exome AF=3.85%, gnomAD genome AF=4.10%. Combined frequency approaches/exceeds BA1 stand-alone benign threshold.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (allele_id: 136440) with multiple submissions across 7 conditions including HDGC, CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome, hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and breast cancer."}}
{"variant_id": "f75f3f8b-6c9c-41a1-9cee-4716d67229dd", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.140481402C>T", "gene": "BRAF", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PS2_Very Strong", "PP3", "PP2", "PM1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66467, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Gly469Glu) previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000013971, VCV000013974, VCV000044803) with multiple independent submissions for cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome and RASopathy. rs121913355 has 33+ PubMed citations supporting pathogenicity.", "PM1": "Located in BRAF kinase domain (Pfam PF07714, SMART SM00220, PROSITE PS50011). The glycine-rich loop (G-loop) at positions 464-469 is a critical functional region for ATP binding and kinase activity. BRAF kinase domain mutations are a known hotspot for RASopathies with minimal benign variation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD exome database (AF = 0.0, AC = 0). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "BRAF is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome, Noonan syndrome). Pathogenic missense variants are common and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably damaging (score 0.999). Variant affects highly conserved glycine residue in kinase domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for disorders caused by germline mutations in RAS-MAPK pathway genes including BRAF. Cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome has a single genetic etiology with BRAF mutations accounting for ~75% of cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (RCV000015005, RCV000015008, RCV000033307, RCV000037919, RCV000150210, RCV000212152, RCV000211748). HGMD entry CM060876 also classifies as disease-causing."}}
{"variant_id": "74db2f83-2875-4293-a23e-02ca1281796d", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36160875G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54741, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This 3' UTR variant (c.*3557C>T) in RUNX1 is located 3,557 nucleotides downstream of the stop codon. While RUNX1 is definitively associated with hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome via haploinsufficiency, 3' UTR variants typically do not cause loss of function. The variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=3.19\u00d710\u207b\u2075), ClinVar classifies it as VUS, and there is no evidence of functional impact on mRNA stability or expression. No pathogenic 3' UTR variants in RUNX1 have been established in the literature. The variant does not meet any ACMG pathogenic or benign criteria."}}
{"variant_id": "ba09d29c-18d6-4873-8a0f-85a8dddff4ae", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.26690369C>A", "gene": "OTOF", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 92587, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.09-0.13), PolyPhen=benign (0.006-0.031 in most transcripts). Variant is a conservative Gly>Val substitution. No CADD/DITTO scores available, but secondary predictors consistently support benign classification.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Benign by 4 independent submitters (VCV000667141) for conditions including 'Nonsyndromic genetic hearing loss' and 'OTOF-related disorder'. Only 1 submission classified as VUS for 'Inborn genetic diseases'.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at AF=0.00134 (genome) and 0.00037 (exome), which is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant in an autosomal recessive disorder. For DFNB9, pathogenic variants are typically extremely rare or absent. The observed frequency across multiple populations (particularly 0.49% in African population) argues against pathogenicity. PM2 is NOT met due to presence in population databases."}}
{"variant_id": "be2941a7-23d4-4e6f-b888-bdfd4c496ba5", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78084749G>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PM3_Very Strong", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 98054, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the catalytic domain of acid alpha-glucosidase (GAA). The p.Arg600His substitution affects a residue within the glycoside hydrolase family 31 domain (Pfam PF01055, CDD cd06602), which is critical for enzyme function. Multiple protein structure mappings (5kzw, 5kzx, 5nn3-8, 7p2z, 7p32, 8cb1, 8cb6) confirm this residue is in a functionally important region.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 1.21e-05 (3 alleles in ~248,000 alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Pompe disease, this extremely low frequency supports pathogenicity. Absent in most populations (gnomAD genome: 0 for A allele).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue at position 600, with all alternative amino acid substitutions (His, Pro, Leu) predicted damaging.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA gene mutations. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology - biallelic pathogenic variants in GAA. The knowledge graph confirms GAA is associated with glycogen storage disease due to acid maltase deficiency (both infantile and late-onset forms).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic (VCV000370130, allele ID 358505). Multiple RCV accessions support pathogenicity: RCV000521900, RCV000408964, RCV003468227. HGMD entries (CM074878, CM990614) also document this as a disease-causing mutation.", "notable": "This variant is also documented in COSMIC (COSV56406566/COSM2803160) as a somatic mutation. Multiple PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 19862843, 18757064, 24715333, 18995995, 10338092, 21920843, 31130284). The ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases Variant Curation Expert Panel has published ACMG/AMP specifications for Pompe disease variant classification (PMID: 37907381)."}}
{"variant_id": "a37a7b3b-eda4-4ed2-8848-63a6ca3f3aa5", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68862199G>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70311, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Glu763Ter) creating premature stop codon in CDH1, a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC) and lobular breast cancer. The variant occurs in exon 15 of 16 exons, predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) or produce truncated protein lacking critical cytoplasmic domain. CDH1 is a well-established tumor suppressor gene.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in any population, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. This meets PM2 criteria for absence in population controls.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (RCV000568475, RCV000123245, RCV000223099, RCV001015069) for hereditary diffuse gastric adenocarcinoma (HDGC), CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome, hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and familial breast cancer. Also catalogued in HGMD (CM043989) and COSMIC (COSV55728059).", "notable": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for this genetic etiology, supporting PP4 consideration. Multiple PubMed publications (PMID:29589180, PMID:36246616, PMID:37303221) document CDH1 germline mutations as causative for HDGC with autosomal dominant inheritance pattern."}}
{"variant_id": "276a0259-f229-43a5-8219-d7d7ba720039", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7127563G>A", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57570, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.1532+1G>A) at the +1 position of intron 16 in ACADVL. This is a null variant type (splice donor) in a gene where loss of function is a well-established mechanism of disease for VLCADD (autosomal recessive). VEP confirms HIGH impact splice_donor_variant affecting multiple protein-coding transcripts. Canonical \u00b11/2 splice site variants are expected to cause complete loss of normal splicing.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.99e-06 (1 allele in ~250,000). gnomAD v4 AF = 6.84e-07. For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity and meets PM2 threshold for absence/extremely low frequency in controls.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000166646, RCV000152740) and Likely Pathogenic (RCV003453143) with multiple submissions. This represents reputable source classification with available evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "588efcab-92f5-4a68-80be-2646db5fda5f", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164516C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62514, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. VEP assigns LOW impact. No computational evidence supports a damaging effect on protein function as the amino acid sequence is unchanged (p.Val453=).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.1359G>A, p.Val453=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not affect canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and is not predicted to create or disrupt splice regulatory elements.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely benign' (Allele ID: 1629116) with 2 RCV submissions for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases, but rarity alone does not support pathogenicity for a synonymous variant with no functional consequence. RUNX1 is a well-established gene where loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism, but synonymous variants typically do not cause LOF unless they affect splicing."}}
{"variant_id": "c6a005c8-4e14-4361-87f3-885ac85f5e10", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36161610G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53486, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This is a 3' UTR variant (c.*2822C>T) in RUNX1. While RUNX1 is definitively associated with hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome via loss-of-function mechanism, this variant does not affect the protein coding sequence. ClinVar classifies it as VUS. gnomAD shows very low frequency (AF=3.27e-05), but this does not meet PM2 threshold as the variant IS present in population databases. PVS1 is not applicable as this is not a null variant (nonsense, frameshift, canonical splice). No computational predictions (CADD, DITTO, SIFT, PolyPhen) are available for 3' UTR variants. No functional studies or case reports exist for this specific variant. The 3' UTR location suggests potential regulatory impact on mRNA stability or miRNA binding, but no evidence supports pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "42ab1654-a08e-4340-a415-00f704e60020", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164537G>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64583, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. VEP shows 'synonymous_variant' consequence with MODIFIER impact. No splice site disruption predicted. CADD scores for synonymous variants are typically low (<15).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Leu446=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted splice impact - variant is not at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and VEP does not predict splice region effects.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' (VCV001542126) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. While RUNX1 is a well-established gene for this condition with loss-of-function as the disease mechanism, synonymous variants that do not affect splicing are generally considered benign. The variant is absent from gnomAD for this specific nucleotide change (G>T), but a different nucleotide change at the same position (G>A) is present at low frequency (AF=7.87e-05), suggesting this codon position tolerates variation."}}
{"variant_id": "53d933cf-dd86-41d3-934d-cf7b7a633653", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36253001G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55999, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. CADD and DITTO scores not available, but synonymous variants at non-splice positions are computationally predicted to be benign. No evidence of splice site disruption.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Leu121=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant is not located at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions). snpEff annotates this as synonymous_variant without splice consequences.", "notable": "ClinVar has conflicting interpretations (1 Likely benign, 1 VUS). Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (0.0066% overall, 0.058% in Ashkenazi Jewish). RUNX1 is a well-established gene for hereditary thrombocytopenia/myeloid malignancy predisposition via LOF mechanism, but synonymous variants without splice effects are not expected to cause disease. The ClinGen RUNX1 Variant Curation Expert Panel has published specific guidelines for RUNX1 variant interpretation (PMID:35764482, 31648317)."}}
{"variant_id": "fc4ca2d1-7bd8-4eba-acb6-2a2b7805bad1", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11224052G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 98580, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical EGF-like domain (SMART SM00135, Superfamily SSF63825) of LDLR. This domain is essential for receptor recycling and LDL binding. Missense variants in this region are known to disrupt receptor function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.19e-05 (3 alleles in ~250,000 individuals). This frequency is well below the expected carrier frequency for familial hypercholesterolemia (1:250), supporting pathogenicity.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 0.988). Consistent predictions across all LDLR transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the most common causative gene (>90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000003694). Conditions include: Hypercholesterolemia familial 1, Familial hypercholesterolemia, Homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, LDLR-related disorder. HGMD entries: CM074319, CM890081, CM981193.", "notable": "45+ PubMed citations associated with this variant (rs28942078). COSMIC entry (COSM3937832) indicates somatic occurrence. Variant affects conserved valine residue at position 429 in the EGF precursor homology domain critical for receptor recycling."}}
{"variant_id": "d7eeea50-bae6-4d66-8a75-a47e13cc51e6", "variant": "NC_000013.10:g.32972626A>T", "gene": "BRCA2", "disease": "BRCA2-related cancer predisposition", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP5_Strong", "BS3"], "expert_panel": "ENIGMA BRCA1 and BRCA2 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59006, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.66% in gnomAD exomes and 0.54% in gnomAD genomes significantly exceeds the expected frequency for a pathogenic BRCA2 variant causing hereditary breast-ovarian cancer syndrome (expected <0.1%). This frequency is incompatible with a highly penetrant pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant cancer predisposition syndrome.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign by multiple expert submitters for BRCA2-related cancer predisposition (VCV000038266). Classifications include: Benign for BRCA2-related cancer predisposition, Benign for Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Likely Benign for Breast and/or ovarian cancer, and Benign/Likely Benign for Breast-ovarian cancer familial susceptibility.", "notable": "Despite being a stop-gained variant, p.Lys3326Ter is located in the extreme C-terminus of BRCA2 (codon 3326 of 3418), removing only 93 amino acids. This region is outside the critical functional domains. Multiple studies (PMID:26455428, PMID:33503928) have reevaluated this variant and concluded it does not confer classic BRCA2-associated breast/ovarian cancer risk. Some studies show modest associations with specific cancer types (small cell lung cancer, squamous cell skin cancer - PMID:29767749) but these represent low-penetrance risk alleles rather than high-penetrance pathogenic variants. PVS1 is NOT applicable because the truncation occurs in the last exon and removes only a small C-terminal portion that does not disrupt the critical DNA repair functions of BRCA2."}}
{"variant_id": "e158be0b-78ae-458c-8a17-923e322eecc3", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23902315C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "dilated cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53993, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant (NC_000014.8:g.23902315C>T, rs1172829765) is annotated as an INTERGENIC VARIANT by Ensembl VEP, located outside the MYH7 gene coding region. While MYH7 is definitively associated with dilated cardiomyopathy (confirmed in knowledge graph), this variant's intergenic location means it does not directly affect the MYH7 protein sequence. gnomAD frequency is extremely low (8.658e-06 overall), but PM2 cannot be applied to intergenic variants. No ClinVar submissions exist for this variant. No functional studies or case reports were found. The variant's potential pathogenic mechanism, if any, would require demonstration of regulatory effects on MYH7 expression, which has not been established."}}
{"variant_id": "88895225-665c-4e9b-bf17-ca9fe729cf9c", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1401454G>T", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BS3_Supporting", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71577, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious (score=0, low confidence). PolyPhen predicts possibly/probably damaging (0.865-0.96). However, CADD and DITTO scores (primary predictors) not available. Secondary predictors provide weak supporting evidence.", "notable": "ClinVar has conflicting interpretations: 1 submission as 'Likely benign' (not provided condition) and 3 submissions as 'Uncertain significance' for GAMT deficiency/cerebral creatine deficiency. Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=0.000144 exome, 0.0000642 genome) - does not meet PM2 threshold for absence. Position p.Pro8 is near N-terminus and may not be in a critical functional domain. No literature evidence found for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "6807a54c-cde9-445c-b30f-9d4a3fbbdc85", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246690G>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3_Very Strong", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57726, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate R408W results in near-complete loss of PAH enzyme activity (<1% residual activity). Multiple in vitro expression studies and animal models (mouse, porcine) confirm damaging effect on enzyme function (PMID:33493163, PMID:35987969, PMID:26803807).", "PS4": "R408W is the most common PKU-causing variant in European populations, accounting for up to 30-40% of PKU alleles in some populations. Significantly enriched in PKU patients compared to controls. gnomAD frequency (0.076-0.19%) is consistent with carrier frequency for autosomal recessive PKU.", "PM1": "Located in the catalytic domain of phenylalanine hydroxylase. VEP shows variant affects multiple functional domains including Pfam PF00351 (aromatic amino acid hydroxylase), Gene3D, and PROSITE PS51410. Position 408 is critical for enzyme structure and function.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The majority of pathogenic PAH variants are missense, and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). Structural interaction variant annotation from snpEff confirms impact on protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000000577). Multiple RCV accessions confirm pathogenic classification from reputable clinical laboratories. Listed in HGMD (CM870016), OMIM (612349.0002), and UniProt (VAR_001035)."}}
{"variant_id": "fd08a9ac-31ce-4494-b0e3-0c7ba71a49d6", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.36594871C>T", "gene": "RAG1", "disease": "recombinase activating gene 1 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66297, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (6.84e-07 overall, only 2.236e-05 in AMR population). Absent from most populations. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal recessive disorder.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies as VUS (VCV002098676). In-silico predictions (SIFT=tolerated, PolyPhen=benign) suggest benign effect but are low confidence. Variant is in N-terminal region (p.Pro6) outside the core catalytic domain (residues 384-1008). RAG1 loss-of-function is established mechanism for SCID, but this missense variant lacks functional evidence. No CADD/DITTO scores available for PP3/BP4 assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "32d53fd8-0652-4c83-ba6a-b7a791fb3b20", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153295849C>G", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54195, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Variant present in gnomAD at frequency 7.284e-06 (gnomAD exomes NFE: 9.5e-06). While rare, this frequency is higher than expected for a fully penetrant X-linked dominant disorder like Rett syndrome, which typically has de novo mutations. The presence in population databases supports BS1.", "BP4": "SIFT prediction is 'tolerated' across all transcripts (scores 0.39-0.86). The amino acid change Ser489Thr (S\u2192T) is a conservative substitution between two polar amino acids. The variant is located in the C-terminal domain outside the critical MBD (methyl-CpG binding domain) and TRD (transcriptional repression domain) functional regions.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant (rs267608328, VCV000143475) as Benign for 'not specified' condition, Benign for 'Severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly', and Likely Benign for 'Rett syndrome (RTT)'. Multiple submitters have classified this variant as benign/likely benign.", "notable": "This is a missense variant (NM_001110792.2:c.1466G>C, p.Ser489Thr) in MECP2. While MECP2 is definitively associated with Rett syndrome via loss-of-function mechanism, this specific variant is located in the C-terminal region (position 477-489 depending on transcript) outside the critical functional domains. No literature evidence was found specifically linking this variant to disease."}}
{"variant_id": "ab854b7c-19a6-4553-ac95-af437437cddf", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246680C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64992, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate severely reduced PAH enzyme activity (1.3-1.85% of wild-type; PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E. coli show 100% protein aggregation indicating severe folding defect and complete loss of function (PMID:18538294).", "PM3": "Detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants (IVS12+1G>A, M1V) in numerous PKU patients (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). ClinGen PAH Expert Panel upgraded to PM3_Strong based on extensive compound heterozygote observations.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999), REVEL=0.89. Missense variant in catalytic domain causes structural disruption.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency with autosomal recessive inheritance. This is the most common PAH mutation in European PKU cohorts, with clear genotype-phenotype correlation to classic PKU.", "PP5": "ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (Aug 2018) with 3-star review status. 40+ ClinVar submissions unanimously classify as Pathogenic. Listed in OMIM (612349.0002).", "notable": "gnomAD frequency (0.076-0.19%) is consistent with carrier frequency for autosomal recessive PKU (disease incidence ~1:10,000). Variant is non-responsive to BH4 therapy (PMID:17935162). Different missense changes at same codon (p.Arg408Gln, p.Arg408Leu) are also pathogenic, supporting PM5 but not applied as PS3 already provides strong functional evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "0aab65be-c602-49d8-8553-db9be292cef7", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103240732G>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 123475, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For autosomal recessive disorders, absence from population databases supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP3": "Splice region variant at c.913-3 position affects the polypyrimidine tract, a critical element for splice site recognition. VEP annotates as 'splice_region_variant' and 'splice_polypyrimidine_tract_variant' with LOW impact. Position -3 from splice acceptor site may disrupt normal splicing, though not at canonical \u00b11/2 positions. Computational prediction supports potential splice disruption.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene mutations) with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern. The clinical presentation is pathognomonic for this disorder.", "notable": "This variant is at position -3 from the splice acceptor site, affecting the polypyrimidine tract but not the canonical \u00b11/2 splice sites required for PVS1. ClinVar currently classifies as VUS (VCV000120294). Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for PKU, but functional studies demonstrating splice disruption would be needed to upgrade classification. No gnomAD frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant in a recessive disorder."}}
{"variant_id": "21f2e2c1-1d89-45f8-a172-2ba45879a0c2", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43042355G>A", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS4", "PM5_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 186669, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (AF=3.19e-05, 9 total alleles across exome and genome). While not absent, this frequency is consistent with a rare disease-causing variant for autosomal dominant MODY1. Applied as supporting level per ClinGen recommendations for rare but not absent variants.", "PP3": "Strong computational evidence supports deleterious effect: CADD=34 (>>25 threshold), REVEL=0.869 (>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (0.026-0.04), PolyPhen2=probably/possibly damaging, MetaLR=deleterious, MetaSVM=deleterious. All predictors concordantly predict damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF4A-MODY1, which has a well-established single genetic etiology. HNF4A is one of the canonical MODY genes with autosomal dominant inheritance pattern matching the clinical presentation.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS across 6 submissions for MODY1/FRTS4/monogenic diabetes. HNF4A is a transcription factor with DNA-binding activity critical for pancreatic beta cell function. The p.Arg114Gln substitution affects a conserved arginine residue. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified in literature (PMID:38745825 describes functional analysis of a different HNF4A variant)."}}
{"variant_id": "78a7041b-31ae-4b6c-9561-39870c271524", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14995915G>C", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PM5_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 163889, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (AF = 3.99e-06 in exomes, ~4 alleles in >1 million). For autosomal recessive disorders, this frequency is consistent with PM2 at supporting-to-moderate level. Absent in most populations (0 in EAS, FIN, SAS, ASJ, AFR).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.994-1.0 across all transcripts). Consistent predictions across all protein-coding transcripts strongly support deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency) is highly specific for this single-gene disorder. DCLRE1C-related SCID has a well-defined clinical presentation with T-B-NK+ immunophenotype.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (Allele ID: 1877858) for severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency (RS-SCID). Multiple RCV accessions support this classification (RCV001965262, RCV003062252, RCV003471090, RCV004526885, RCV004542188, RCV004577007, RCV005042564)."}}
{"variant_id": "2d1eb815-6c23-4456-b617-5f09db470564", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.26861470C>T", "gene": "FOXN1", "disease": "T-cell immunodeficiency, congenital alopecia, and nail dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PP4", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67421, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg255Ter) creating premature stop codon in FOXN1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease. FOXN1 encodes a transcription factor essential for thymic epithelial development; null variants cause T-cell immunodeficiency, congenital alopecia, and nail dystrophy (Nude SCID). The variant truncates the protein at amino acid 255, removing critical functional domains.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome: AF = 3.98e-06 (1/251,000 alleles); gnomAD genome: AF = 6.57e-06 (1/152,000 alleles). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal recessive/semidominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (T-cell immunodeficiency, congenital alopecia, and nail dystrophy) is highly specific for FOXN1-related disease. This clinical triad is pathognomonic for Nude SCID caused by FOXN1 mutations, with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000008757) with multiple submissions for T-cell immunodeficiency/congenital alopecia/nail dystrophy, T-cell lymphopenia, and SCID. Well-documented in literature as the ancestral founder mutation (PMID:15180707, PMID:28077132)."}}
{"variant_id": "a96e1967-96ee-4701-8f1d-3c7fd37c77eb", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14976749A>C", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67233, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome (AF=3.97e-06, 1 allele). For autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with PM2 at supporting level. However, variant is present in population databases.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency) is highly specific for this single-gene disorder. DCLRE1C is the only known cause of RS-SCID (radiosensitive SCID with T-B-NK+ phenotype).", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000666119). In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT predicts tolerated (0.11-0.22), PolyPhen ranges from benign (0.303) to possibly damaging (0.852) depending on transcript. This is a conservative Leu>Val substitution. No functional studies available for this specific variant. DCLRE1C LOF is established mechanism for SCID, but this missense may not cause LOF."}}
{"variant_id": "e75a40b0-8e18-418e-b6c7-079646958d18", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89725078C>A", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1", "PP2", "BS3_Supporting", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68564, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.388C>A, p.Arg130=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP confirms most severe consequence is synonymous_variant with LOW impact. The codon change (CGA\u2192AGA) maintains arginine at position 130.", "notable": "This variant shares rsID rs121909224 with pathogenic variants at the same position (c.388C>T creating p.R130* nonsense, and c.388C>G creating p.R130G missense). However, the specific C>A change results in a synonymous variant. ClinVar classifies this specific allele (c.388C>A) as 'Likely benign' for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. gnomAD shows extremely low frequency (1.37e-06), but rarity alone does not indicate pathogenicity for a synonymous variant. No splice site predictions available but variant is not at canonical splice sites."}}
{"variant_id": "650e4d16-b761-4c10-ac4d-479b2c98013e", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121426701G>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PS2", "PP1_Strong", "PM1", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 137337, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD (frequency = 0 in all populations). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for MODY, which has a well-established single genetic etiology. HNF1A-MODY (MODY3) is the most common form of MODY.", "notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.714-28G>A) located 28 bp from the nearest exon boundary. It does not affect canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and is unlikely to significantly impact splicing. No computational splice prediction scores available. No ClinVar submissions found. HNF1A loss-of-function is an established mechanism for MODY3, but this intronic position is not predicted to cause loss of function. PVS1 not applicable as this is not a null variant (not at canonical splice sites). PP3 not met as no CADD/DITTO scores available for intronic variants and position is too far from splice junction for standard splice prediction."}}
{"variant_id": "5c62664a-7354-47c7-87a8-0b26feb8a5b9", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7123439A>C", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62592, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.63-2A>C) at the -2 position in ACADVL. This is a null variant type affecting a canonical splice site in a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for VLCADD (autosomal recessive). VEP confirms HIGH impact splice_acceptor_variant consequence across multiple protein-coding transcripts (ENST00000350303, ENST00000356839, ENST00000543245).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD with overall allele frequency of 7.032e-07 (essentially absent). Only observed in African population at 3.008e-05. For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is well below the expected carrier frequency threshold, supporting PM2.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (VCV000474900, RCV000531909) for Very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency. HGMD also lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CS1512102). Associated publication PMID:27209629 supports pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "0c970ab1-3278-4f04-af3a-5b8859e99901", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11240345C>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54961, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser849Ter) creating a premature stop codon in LDLR. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for familial hypercholesterolemia (FH). LDLR encodes the LDL receptor, and null variants cause reduced LDL clearance leading to hypercholesterolemia. The variant affects the cytoplasmic domain and is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a truncated non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD. The C>A allele shows gnomAD genome frequency of 1.315e-05 (0.001315%) and gnomAD exome frequency of 2.737e-06 (0.0003%). This is well below the expected frequency threshold for familial hypercholesterolemia (estimated prevalence 1:250-500).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' and 'Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic' across multiple submissions (ClinVar allele ID: 246635). Conditions include Hypercholesterolemia familial 1, Familial hypercholesterolemia, and LDLR-related disorder. HGMD entries (CD020865, CM151115, CM162062) also document this as a disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "fad42e66-5505-4cb8-a663-ef3d633e0ad8", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.95562205G>C", "gene": "DICER1", "disease": "dicer1 syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "DICER1 and miRNA-Processing Gene VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 49511, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted splice impact. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No computational evidence suggests deleterious effect on splicing or protein function.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Leu1684=) with no amino acid change. The variant does not affect canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions). No evidence of cryptic splice site activation or exonic splicing enhancer/silencer disruption.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' (VCV000242128) with 3 RCV submissions for DICER1-related conditions. Present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=1.99e-05 exome, 3.94e-05 genome) with higher frequency in African population (0.0008). COSMIC reports this as a somatic variant (COSM1300935), but somatic occurrence does not indicate germline pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "ae859af5-7294-46fd-aa10-21fb29d84c7e", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.37053562C>T", "gene": "MLH1", "disease": "Lynch syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3", "BS1", "BP5"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59703, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg226Gln) at this position has been previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar with multiple submissions classifying c.677G>A as Pathogenic for Lynch syndrome (ClinVar allele ID 95792). The variant has been reported in multiple independent Lynch syndrome families.", "PM1": "Located in the HATPase_c domain (PF01119/cd03483) of MLH1, which is critical for ATP binding and hydrolysis essential for mismatch repair function. This domain is a mutational hotspot for pathogenic Lynch syndrome variants with minimal benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exomes frequency: 6.887e-07 (approximately 1 allele in 1.45 million). This is well below the threshold expected for a pathogenic Lynch syndrome variant given disease prevalence.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = possibly damaging (score 0.829). The variant also affects a splice region which may have additional functional consequences.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Lynch syndrome 1) is highly specific for MLH1 pathogenic variants. Lynch syndrome has a well-established single genetic etiology involving mismatch repair genes, with MLH1 being the most commonly affected gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from expert laboratories. The variant has been classified as Pathogenic for Lynch syndrome, hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal neoplasms, Lynch syndrome 1, gastric cancer, and endometrial carcinoma."}}
{"variant_id": "7d5daf11-a43e-4d62-924a-f3cf45a73b5c", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259380G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58692, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0 (gnomAD genome AF=6.57e-06, gnomAD exome AF=0). Per RUNX1-specific ACMG guidelines (PMID:31648317), PM2 is applied at supporting level for rare variants in this gene.", "notable": "This is a synonymous variant (p.Ser37=) that does not change the amino acid sequence. ClinVar classifies as VUS (VCV000532683). No computational evidence of splice impact was identified. RUNX1 loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism for FPDMM, but synonymous variants typically require functional evidence of splice disruption to be considered pathogenic. BP7 was considered but not applied as splice prediction data was not available to confirm no splice impact."}}
{"variant_id": "6ea47f2e-7ebf-41f1-b31c-4c88863065ef", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38935305C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "RYR1-related myopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 106846, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=4.0e-06 (1/249,742 alleles), genome AF=3.2e-05 (1/31,368 alleles). Total of 2 alleles observed across all gnomAD populations. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "BP4": "Computational evidence suggests benign effect. PolyPhen=benign (score 0.009-0.041), SIFT=tolerated (score 0.13-0.14). CADD and DITTO scores not available, but secondary predictors consistently predict tolerated/benign. Multiple transcripts show concordant benign predictions.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies as VUS (7 submissions for various RYR1-related conditions). Variant located in RyR N-terminal domain (Pfam PF08709), which is a functional region but not a recognized mutational hotspot. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.Arg207Cys identified. RYR1 is well-established for autosomal dominant myopathies and malignant hyperthermia susceptibility."}}
{"variant_id": "2020afa6-e23a-48b8-be9f-38d8a6964d30", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7126185G>A", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 450682, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 429: {\"detail\":\"Too many variant classification requests. Try again in 2 seconds.\"}"}
{"variant_id": "288af6b0-dcff-492f-8fcb-9b924005ad8a", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.36596949C>T", "gene": "RAG1", "disease": "recombinase activating gene 1 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PM3", "PP4", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74363, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the RAG1 core catalytic domain (Pfam PF12940), which is critical for V(D)J recombination activity. This domain is a mutational hotspot for pathogenic variants causing SCID and related immunodeficiencies.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=7.96e-06 (2/251,000 alleles), genome AF=6.37e-05 (2/31,400 alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variants.", "PP2": "RAG1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Multiple pathogenic missense variants have been reported causing SCID, Omenn syndrome, and combined immunodeficiency phenotypes.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.998). Both primary predictors strongly support pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RAG1 deficiency/SCID) is highly specific for this gene. RAG1 is one of only two genes (with RAG2) encoding the V(D)J recombinase, and deficiency causes a distinctive T-B-NK+ SCID phenotype.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000068689) for SCID T-B-NK+, combined immunodeficiency with skin granulomas, and partial RAG1 deficiency. Supporting PMIDs: 20956421, 21771083, 31503426, 32447396."}}
{"variant_id": "149af01b-aeeb-4b3b-8053-07b981dc2ff1", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38994959C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72546, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in RYR1, a gene with well-characterized functional domains critical for calcium channel function. RYR1 missense variants in the cytoplasmic and transmembrane domains are established hotspots for malignant hyperthermia-causing mutations. The p.Arg2676Trp variant is in a conserved region of the protein.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.19e-05 (3 alleles in ~250,000), gnomAD genome AF = 1.31e-05. This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant condition with reduced penetrance.", "PP2": "RYR1 has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. The gene is highly constrained for missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.958). The arginine to tryptophan substitution represents a significant physicochemical change (charged to aromatic/hydrophobic).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia) is highly specific for RYR1-related disorders. Malignant hyperthermia has a well-defined genetic etiology with RYR1 being the primary causative gene (>70% of cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV000013857) and Likely Pathogenic (RCV000119737, RCV001802876) by multiple submitters. Listed in HGMD (CM044255). Multiple publications support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 18414213, 16917943, 14732627, 16163667, 19191329, 25960145).", "notable": "The RYR1 Variant Curation Expert Panel (VCEP) has published specific guidelines for RYR1 variant classification in malignant hyperthermia (PMID: 33767344, 35849058). While no specific functional study for p.Arg2676Trp was identified, the variant has been reported in multiple affected individuals. The presence in COSMIC suggests somatic occurrence but does not impact germline classification."}}
{"variant_id": "c507f13c-43cd-4cfe-b95f-fa1e3960702c", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.70327635T>C", "gene": "IL2RG", "disease": "T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency due to gamma chain deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72716, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (T-B+ SCID due to gamma chain deficiency) is highly specific for IL2RG-related disease with single genetic etiology. X-linked SCID is a well-characterized monogenic disorder.", "notable": "ClinVar reports conflicting interpretations: 'Likely benign' for X-linked SCID (RCV001563869) and 'Uncertain significance' for Combined immunodeficiency X-linked (RCV001563868). Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=2.01e-05, 3 alleles), which argues against pathogenicity for a severe early-onset X-linked disorder. In-silico predictions are mixed: PolyPhen predicts 'probably damaging' (0.978-0.991) but SIFT shows 'deleterious_low_confidence' (0.03-0.05). The variant affects position 354 in the intracellular domain. No CADD or DITTO scores available for primary computational assessment. No functional studies or case reports specifically for this variant were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "f317b16a-76d9-4d00-b945-62323da833e7", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68897001C>T", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BA1", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66167, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM2", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg91Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar VCV000013115 reports this exact variant as Pathogenic with 12+ independent submissions for LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related retinopathy.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 5.57\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (14/251,000 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 3.19\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (1/31,400 alleles). For autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variant.", "PM1": "Located within the RPE65 isomerase functional domain (Pfam PF03055). Arginine 91 is a conserved residue in the catalytic region essential for retinoid isomerase activity in the visual cycle.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 0.941). The R\u2192W substitution replaces a positively charged arginine with a bulky hydrophobic tryptophan.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for RPE65 gene mutations. RPE65 is the only gene known to cause this specific clinical entity, and gene therapy (Luxturna) is FDA-approved specifically for biallelic RPE65 mutations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. HGMD entry CM983758 also classifies as disease-causing mutation. Multiple publications (PMID: 35129589, 35551639, 31925606, 27624628) report this variant in affected patients.", "notable": "This variant has been reported in multiple ethnic populations (Italian, Chinese, North African, Irish) in patients with LCA2 and RP20. RPE65 loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for autosomal recessive retinal dystrophy, and gene replacement therapy (voretigene neparvovec/Luxturna) is specifically approved for patients with biallelic RPE65 mutations."}}
{"variant_id": "1c74237e-7f11-4726-87f7-33474ab97bae", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252978A>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 51302, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP7", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.384T>C, p.Thr128=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence (Threonine to Threonine). No evidence of cryptic splice site creation or disruption of splicing regulatory elements.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely benign' (Allele ID: 1656955) for both 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1' and 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome'. Multiple submissions support benign classification.", "notable": "While RUNX1 is a well-established gene for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic malignancy predisposition with loss-of-function as the disease mechanism, this synonymous variant does not result in protein truncation or amino acid change. The variant is rare (absent from gnomAD), but rarity alone does not support pathogenicity for a synonymous variant without splice effects."}}
{"variant_id": "a2fb6cff-f898-4e9b-89ba-a3e9ec9f73f7", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103238185C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57885, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate R408W results in near-complete loss of PAH enzyme activity (<1% residual activity). Multiple in vitro expression studies (PMID:26803807, PMID:35987969) and animal models (PMID:33493163) confirm damaging effect on protein function.", "PS4": "R408W is the most common PKU-causing variant worldwide, with significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals compared to controls. gnomAD frequency (0.076% exome, 0.19% genome) is consistent with carrier frequency for autosomal recessive PKU, while variant is found in majority of PKU patients in many populations.", "PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases (gnomAD exome AF=0.000759631, genome AF=0.00194305). For autosomal recessive PKU, this frequency is consistent with expected carrier frequency and meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of PKU.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue in catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000000577, allele_id 15616) from multiple clinical laboratories for phenylketonuria. HGMD also classifies as disease-causing mutation (CM870016)."}}
{"variant_id": "3c7b1ba8-0b15-48c4-977e-22e911ef42f0", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206728G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 99239, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln262Ter) in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome (FPDMM). This variant creates a premature stop codon at position 262, truncating the protein and eliminating the C-terminal transactivation domain. RUNX1 haploinsufficiency is the recognized pathogenic mechanism. The variant affects multiple transcripts with HIGH impact (stop_gained consequence).", "PM2": "Variant rs1601415426 is absent from gnomAD population controls. The colocated variant rs34991163 at the same genomic position represents a different allele with population frequency ~3.86%, but the pathogenic C>T change (p.Gln262Ter) is not observed in population databases, consistent with a rare deleterious variant.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV000852220, VCV000627384) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome, and Likely Pathogenic for storage pool disease of platelets. Multiple submitters with concordant interpretations. HGMD entry CM1210373 also documents this as a disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "2ca4f6ef-375f-4771-ace3-53cb405bc69b", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68835717G>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57669, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant (NC_000016.9:g.68835717G>A) is annotated as a downstream_gene_variant located 177-180 bp downstream of the CDH1 gene 3' end (beyond the 3'UTR). VEP consequence: 'downstream_gene_variant' with MODIFIER impact across all 8 transcripts. No coding, splice, or regulatory impact predicted. CDH1 is well-established as a tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function causes hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC) and lobular breast cancer, but this variant does not affect the coding sequence or known regulatory elements. No ClinVar entries, gnomAD frequency data, or literature reports were found for this specific variant. The variant falls outside the gene boundaries and is unlikely to have functional consequences."}}
{"variant_id": "abd5cd6c-009f-49dc-9676-645406075524", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121416901A>C", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 303524, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. MyVariant query returned no population frequency data, and ClinVar entry (allele ID 3529636) shows no allele frequency information. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports splice-affecting impact. VEP annotation identifies this as a splice_donor_region_variant (c.326+4A>C) in HNF1A affecting multiple protein-coding transcripts (ENST00000257555, ENST00000400024, ENST00000541395, ENST00000544413). Position +4 from splice donor site has potential to affect splicing efficiency. snpEff annotates as splice_region_variant&intron_variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY, and the clinical presentation aligns with established gene-disease association. Knowledge graph confirms HNF1A is associated with maturity-onset diabetes of the young.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Uncertain Significance (VCV003529636.1, submitted Jan 2025) for monogenic diabetes. HNF1A is a well-established MODY gene where loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism (haploinsufficiency). The variant is located in the splice donor region (+4 position) which may affect splicing but is not at canonical \u00b11/2 positions required for PVS1. No functional studies or segregation data available for this specific variant. Literature search found no publications specifically reporting this c.326+4A>C variant."}}
{"variant_id": "784bb90d-db15-4c09-97ef-fb86e941d351", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44191910T>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 152289, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, indicating extremely rare or novel variant. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). Heterozygous loss-of-function missense variants cause mild fasting hyperglycemia. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.01-0.02), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.996 on canonical transcript). Variant located in glucokinase domain (Pfam PF00349) with structural interaction effects predicted by snpEff. Two HGMD mutations (CM021265, CM032906) colocated at this position.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY, which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for 30-50% of MODY cases and presents with characteristic mild fasting hyperglycemia.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies as VUS (Allele ID: 2852838). Comprehensive GCK functional map exists (PMID: 37101203) using deep mutational scanning that could provide activity score for this specific variant. HGMD colocated mutations suggest pathogenic variants at this position. No CADD/DITTO scores available for primary computational assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "9f7236b9-e0fe-4a9f-938a-7b069c5034c4", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78091450G>T", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PVS1", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 444626, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Glu795Ter) creating premature stop codon in GAA gene. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for Pompe disease (glycogen storage disease type II). The truncation occurs at codon 795 of 952, removing ~16% of the protein including critical C-terminal regions. GAA is not subject to rescue by alternative transcripts.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0 with allele frequency of 1.369e-06 (approximately 1 in 730,000 alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Pompe disease, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity. Absent from most populations (AFR, AMR, ASJ, EAS, FIN, MID, SAS).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV000397630) for Glycogen storage disease, type II (Pompe disease). Multiple submitters have classified this variant. ClinVar Allele ID: 646906, VCV000288394."}}
{"variant_id": "f8fbca5e-2224-4e01-969d-d193d0bd9748", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164876C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50948, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect on protein function. VEP shows LOW impact classification. No computational evidence supports pathogenicity for this silent change.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Pro333=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted splice impact at canonical splice sites (variant is not at \u00b11/2 positions). ClinVar classifies as Likely Benign with multiple concordant submissions.", "notable": "While PM2 could technically apply (absent from gnomAD), this is outweighed by the benign nature of synonymous variants. ClinVar has 3 submissions all classifying as Likely Benign. RUNX1 loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism, but synonymous variants typically do not cause loss of function. The variant is at position +5 of a splice donor in DOP1B (overlapping gene), but this is not a canonical splice site and has LOW predicted impact."}}
{"variant_id": "a9821911-94cf-46fa-9cfe-3870b003eb13", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36161806T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP2", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 87364, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "gnomAD allele frequency = 0.33% (105/31,400 alleles), which is significantly higher than expected for a rare autosomal dominant disorder like RUNX1-related thrombocytopenia/cancer predisposition syndrome (expected prevalence <1:10,000).", "BP4": "3' UTR variant (c.*2626A>G) located 2626 nucleotides downstream of the stop codon. 3' UTR variants do not alter protein coding sequence and are computationally predicted to have no impact on protein function.", "BP6": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Benign (Allele ID: 351667) for both 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1' and 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome'."}}
{"variant_id": "0ba69fad-66dd-47dd-990b-138e4e43da99", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44187337C>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PM5_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 227087, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the hexokinase/glucokinase catalytic domain (Pfam PF03727, Superfamily SSF53067). GCK missense variants in this domain are well-established to cause MODY2 through reduced enzyme activity. Multiple crystal structures available (PDB: 1v4s, 3a0i, etc.) confirm functional importance of this region.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, indicating extremely rare or private variant. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which accounts for 30-50% of all MODY cases. GCK is the established genetic etiology for this phenotype with semidominant inheritance pattern.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID: 2743244, NM_000162.5:c.775G>T). Also listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM980894).", "notable": "In-silico predictions are discordant: SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0, low confidence) while PolyPhen predicts benign (0.171-0.364). CADD and DITTO scores not available. PP3 not applied due to conflicting computational evidence. Comprehensive GCK functional maps exist (PMID:37101203) but specific A259S functional data not retrieved."}}
{"variant_id": "a4185d9f-3c2f-40e1-b850-6d89657b1e15", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45369695G>T", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP1"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 130617, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Absent from gnomAD for the G>T allele. The alternate G>A allele at this position has extremely low frequency (AF=3.97e-06). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from population databases supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2=probably_damaging (score 1.0). The missense change Gly437Val substitutes a small, flexible glycine with a larger, hydrophobic valine residue, likely disrupting protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGB3/ITGA2B mutations. This is a well-characterized inherited platelet disorder with a single genetic etiology involving the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV001879025). ITGB3 is definitively associated with Glanzmann thrombasthenia in the knowledge graph. The variant affects a glycine residue in the integrin beta chain, which is critical for fibrinogen binding and platelet aggregation. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.Gly437Val were identified in the literature."}}
{"variant_id": "cd0c4aea-7158-4181-83f0-1c4cce449e45", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11227604G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 99296, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in EGF-like domain (Pfam PF00058, SMART SM00135) of LDLR, a critical functional domain essential for receptor recycling and ligand release. This domain is a known mutational hotspot in familial hypercholesterolemia with limited benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 4.37e-05 (11 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 1.59e-04 (5 alleles). This frequency is well below the expected carrier frequency for familial hypercholesterolemia (~1:250), supporting pathogenicity.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.969). Consistent predictions across all transcript isoforms support damaging effect on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the primary causative gene (>90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV000161271) with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. Associated conditions include Familial hypercholesterolemia, Homozygous FH, and Hypercholesterolemia, familial, 1.", "notable": "This variant has 41+ PubMed citations (PMIDs: 25741868, 24033266, 27765764, 25637381, 26036859, 9654205, 17765246, 20145306, 21310417, 22698793, and others) documenting its presence in FH patients across multiple populations. HGMD entry CM920464 and COSMIC entry COSV52945923 also document this variant. The p.Gly592Glu substitution affects a highly conserved glycine residue in the EGF precursor homology domain, which is critical for pH-dependent ligand release in endosomes."}}
{"variant_id": "769cd169-4fec-408f-a51f-8ad96420b9ec", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36161411T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP2", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70577, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "3' UTR variant (c.*3021A>G) located 3021 bp downstream of stop codon. No computational evidence supports deleterious effect on protein function. CADD, SIFT, PolyPhen not applicable for non-coding variants. No predicted splice impact.", "BP7": "Non-coding variant in 3' UTR region with no predicted functional impact on splicing or protein function. Synonymous-equivalent for classification purposes as it does not alter the protein sequence.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting classifications (VUS vs Likely Benign). gnomAD frequency of 0.045% (14 alleles) indicates variant is present in general population, though below PM2 threshold. RUNX1-specific curation guidelines (PMID:35764482) focus on coding variants in RHD and TAD domains; 3' UTR variants are not typically considered pathogenic for RUNX1-FPD."}}
{"variant_id": "917e8ced-f075-4713-95ff-8b523c41717d", "variant": "NC_000018.9:g.53128309C>T", "gene": "TCF4", "disease": "Pitt-Hopkins syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58708, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.25), PolyPhen=benign (0.297). No CADD/DITTO scores available, but all available predictors consistently indicate tolerated/benign.", "BP6": "ClinVar submission (RCV001755142) classifies this variant as Likely Benign for Pitt-Hopkins syndrome. VCV001312388 shows clinical significance of 'benign' and 'uncertain_significance' from multiple submitters.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD exome at very low frequency (AF=3.99e-06, ~1 allele). While rare, presence in population database with benign computational predictions and ClinVar Likely Benign classification supports benign interpretation. TCF4 haploinsufficiency causes Pitt-Hopkins syndrome, but this missense variant does not appear to cause loss of function based on computational predictions."}}
{"variant_id": "29652fe8-e9d3-411e-b7da-407a4d918e27", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36160292G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP2"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 38692, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.28% (88/31,400 alleles) in gnomAD genome database exceeds expected frequency for a rare autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance. This frequency is inconsistent with pathogenicity for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome.", "BP7": "This is a 3' UTR variant (c.*4140C>T) located 4140 nucleotides downstream of the stop codon. It does not affect protein coding sequence and has no predicted splice impact. 3' UTR variants at this distance from the coding region are unlikely to have functional consequences.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (Allele ID: 336686) with multiple submissions supporting benign classification for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. RUNX1 disease mechanism is loss-of-function/haploinsufficiency, but this 3' UTR variant does not create a null allele."}}
{"variant_id": "b9e09be9-ed98-4fb5-924d-48c6fdf61bb0", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44184775G>T", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 89882, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser453Ter) creating premature stop codon in GCK. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for GCK-MODY (MODY2). The variant occurs in exon 10 of 10, but GCK nonsense mutations throughout the gene cause haploinsufficiency leading to MODY2. Multiple transcripts show stop_gained consequence with HIGH impact.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD exome or genome datasets, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variant for a rare monogenic disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK mutations are the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases. The clinical presentation aligns with expected GCK-MODY phenotype.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (Allele ID: 3184688) for monogenic diabetes. Additionally, HGMD has 3 colocated mutation entries at this genomic position (CM012131, CM032925, CM096961), indicating established pathogenicity at this site."}}
{"variant_id": "40b17e69-ece7-4ecd-9b15-b690c0f6b05d", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164449C>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 606872, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T01:26:58.353005Z\",\"request_id\":\"348df"}
{"variant_id": "c9038e4c-59d0-475e-8f94-023c8af7d007", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259208G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 128941, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located within the Runt Homology Domain (RHD, amino acids 50-177 in isoform C), a critical functional domain for DNA binding and CBFB heterodimerization. The ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines identify the RHD as a mutational hotspot where pathogenic missense variants cluster. VEP annotation confirms location in Pfam domain PF00853 (Runt) and multiple protein-protein contact regions per snpEff.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. The rsID rs2057999086 has no reported population frequency data, consistent with an extremely rare variant. For autosomal dominant RUNX1-related disorders, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT scores range from 0.00-0.01 (deleterious_low_confidence) across transcripts; PolyPhen-2 score = 1.0 (probably_damaging) on transcript ENST00000399240. The missense variant affects a conserved proline residue within the critical RHD domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related Familial Platelet Disorder with predisposition to Myeloid Malignancy (FPD/AML). This is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance matching the clinical presentation."}}
{"variant_id": "b69dff69-840b-4103-bcdf-832247919271", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11241984G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 101027, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT = tolerated (0.13-0.22), PolyPhen = benign (0.009-0.127). Variant located in cytoplasmic domain, not in critical LDL-binding or EGF-like domains. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but secondary predictors consistently suggest benign.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (VCV000252360): 2 submissions as Likely benign, 1 as Uncertain significance. gnomAD frequency (AF = 2.39e-05 exome, 4.60e-05 genome) is low but present in population, which does not support PM2. The variant is in the cytoplasmic domain (NPVY internalization motif region) but Val859 is not at a critical position. LDLR loss-of-function is established mechanism for FH, but this missense in cytoplasmic domain with benign predictions does not support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "f2e59569-194f-47a1-b281-2579bacb1f7e", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11224219T>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 120875, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.2956-1113A>G) located 1113bp from nearest splice site. VEP predicts MODIFIER impact with no splice consequences. No computational evidence supports deleterious effect.", "notable": "CRITICAL DISCREPANCY: The genomic coordinates (chr19:g.11224219T>C) map to DOCK6 gene, NOT LDLR as indicated in clinical context. DOCK6 is associated with Adams-Oliver syndrome, not familial hypercholesterolemia. This variant may be incorrectly attributed to LDLR. The variant is present in gnomAD at very low frequency (AF=5.28e-05, rs1028508199). No ClinVar submissions or functional studies found for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "9bb378a0-a029-4534-a997-f605b4c630b3", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.152958630G>A", "gene": "SLC6A8", "disease": "creatine transporter deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69648, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. For X-linked recessive disorder, absence in hemizygous males strongly supports rarity. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "snpEff predicts splice_region_variant effect at c.912G>A position. Synonymous variants affecting splice regions can disrupt normal splicing. Located at last nucleotide of exon (position -1 of splice donor region), which is critical for splice site recognition.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (creatine transporter deficiency) is highly specific for SLC6A8 mutations. This is an X-linked disorder with single genetic etiology - mutations in SLC6A8 are the only known cause of X-linked creatine transporter deficiency.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (Allele ID: 2421579) for Creatine transporter deficiency (CCDS1). ClinVar is a reputable source with expert-curated submissions."}}
{"variant_id": "f9cc13a9-0509-451a-a856-60c50af7c90d", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11230873G>T", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 80092, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Absent from gnomAD v4.0 for the G>T allele. The alternate G>A allele at this position is present at extremely low frequency (AF=2.052e-06), but the specific G>T variant causing p.Asp651Tyr is not observed in population databases, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variant.", "PM5": "Novel missense change at the same amino acid position (Asp651) as an established pathogenic variant. The p.Asp651Asn (c.1951G>A) variant at this position is classified as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000183128, VCV000252127) with multiple submissions. Different amino acid substitution (Tyr vs Asn) at same critical residue supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene with a low rate of benign missense variation and where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. LDLR has >1,700 pathogenic/likely pathogenic missense variants in ClinVar, establishing missense as a well-recognized disease mechanism for familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.936-0.996). Variant located in critical EGF-like domain (Pfam PF00058) essential for receptor recycling and LDL binding.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the primary causative gene (>90% of monogenic FH cases). Clinical presentation aligns with expected phenotype.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely pathogenic (VCV000246423) for Hypercholesterolemia, familial, 1. HGMD entries (CM042084, CM060315) document this as disease-causing mutation. Published case report (PMID:32937241) describes this exact variant in FH patient.", "notable": "PVS1 not applicable as this is a missense variant, not a null variant. PS1 not met as this is a different nucleotide change resulting in different amino acid (Tyr vs Asn). No functional studies (PS3) or de novo evidence (PS2) available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "3f59c0c0-9bf7-40ae-af09-0ffa15ab278b", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36421141C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62948, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease, which has a single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "This variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF 2.78e-05 exome, 6.37e-05 genome), precluding PM2. In-silico predictors (SIFT=tolerated, PolyPhen=benign) suggest benign effect but do not meet BP4 threshold without CADD/DITTO data. Position 19 is in the N-terminal region, outside the critical Runt homology domain (residues 50-177). ClinVar has 6 submissions all classifying as VUS. COSMIC reports somatic occurrence (COSV55883848). The conservative Arg>Lys substitution preserves positive charge."}}
{"variant_id": "03413dd6-5c0a-4120-a288-5a615a7d1ab0", "variant": "NC_000005.9:g.35876300T>G", "gene": "IL7R", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency, autosomal recessive, T cell-negative, B cell-positive, NK cell-positive", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2_Supporting", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 161624, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for autosomal recessive SCID. gnomAD exome AF = 0.22% overall, with South Asian population frequency of 1.75% (gnomAD SAS). For a rare recessive disorder like T-B+NK+ SCID (estimated prevalence ~1:50,000-100,000), this frequency is significantly higher than expected for a pathogenic variant.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect. SIFT = tolerated (score 1.0, maximum tolerance). PolyPhen = benign (score 0.001, near-zero pathogenicity). The p.Asp364Glu substitution is a conservative amino acid change (both negatively charged) in the cytoplasmic domain.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Benign (VCV000134538) for Immunodeficiency 104. The variant is located in the cytoplasmic domain (not in critical receptor-ligand binding regions). Loss-of-function is the established mechanism for IL7R-related SCID, but this missense variant shows no evidence of functional impairment."}}
{"variant_id": "92a56467-626e-43a0-83d5-6da0b174dda1", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.115258751C>T", "gene": "NRAS", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57099, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "SIFT prediction is 'tolerated_low_confidence' (score 0.12). The variant is predicted to be tolerated by computational tools. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but SIFT suggests benign effect.", "notable": "ClinVar reports conflicting interpretations: 'Likely benign' for unspecified condition (RCV000680636), 'Uncertain significance' for RASopathy (RCV001042539) and cardiovascular phenotype (RCV002532191). gnomAD shows extremely low frequency (AF=3.97e-06, 1 allele in ~250,000 exomes), but this is not absent, so PM2 is not fully met. Position A11 is not a known RAS hotspot (hotspots are G12, G13, Q61). COSMIC reports this variant (COSM558) but as somatic, not germline. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were found."}}
{"variant_id": "af4a5023-b029-4d29-a204-f133d99d23f0", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.36615526C>A", "gene": "RAG2", "disease": "recombinase activating gene 2 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4", "PM3_Supporting", "PM1_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68916, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF = 3.98e-06 in exomes (~1 allele in 251,000), 1.37e-06 in genomes. For autosomal recessive RAG2 deficiency, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variants. Meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.946). Variant located in critical RAG2 core/Kelch domain (Pfam PF03089) essential for V(D)J recombination.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RAG2 deficiency) is highly specific for this gene. RAG2 mutations cause SCID (T-B-NK+), Omenn syndrome, and combined immunodeficiency with skin granulomas - conditions with well-defined genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000427020). Associated conditions include SCID, RAG2 deficiency, and combined immunodeficiency. HGMD also lists this variant (CM114606).", "notable": "Variant affects highly conserved Asp65 residue in the RAG2 core domain. The D65Y substitution introduces a bulky aromatic residue that may disrupt protein structure. RAG2 is essential for V(D)J recombination in lymphocyte development, and loss-of-function mutations cause severe immunodeficiency. Mode of inheritance is autosomal recessive, consistent with the clinical presentation."}}
{"variant_id": "862029ef-cc5c-4b10-b102-f9a252e48910", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68905254A>C", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Strong", "PP3_Moderate", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63985, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Tyr239Asp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar VCV000098889 reports this exact variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (RCV000085220, RCV000678618, RCV001831895, RCV001207227) for LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. HGMD entry CM056687 confirms disease-causing status.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.98e-06 (1 allele), gnomAD genome AF = 6.37e-05 (2 alleles). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare recessive disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 1.0). The missense change from tyrosine (aromatic, polar) to aspartic acid (acidic, charged) represents a significant physicochemical change.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for RPE65 gene mutations. RPE65 is the only gene associated with this specific phenotype, and biallelic RPE65 mutations are the established cause of LCA2 and RP20.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. Six PubMed publications (PMIDs: 24849605, 26626312, 20801516, 22334370, 19431183, 26427455) support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "74af980b-bb57-47e7-a67f-11cf6dab4294", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7123487C>T", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72728, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF = 7.4e-06 (1/135,000 alleles), genome AF = 3.9e-05. For an autosomal recessive disorder like VLCADD, this low frequency supports PM2 at moderate level.", "notable": "In-silico predictions are predominantly benign: SIFT = tolerated (0.13-0.38), PolyPhen = benign to possibly damaging (0-0.716). Without CADD or DITTO scores, PP3 cannot be met. ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS. The variant affects p.Arg37Trp in the N-terminal region of ACADVL. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified in the literature."}}
{"variant_id": "7a30e9f6-0952-4d82-a4e0-d182ba4a1ed8", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121435350C>T", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61495, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. CADD score not available but synonymous variants typically have low computational pathogenicity scores. No splice site impact predicted (variant is in exon 9, not near splice junctions).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.1383C>T, p.Pro461=) with no amino acid change. No predicted splice impact - variant is located within exon 9 coding region, not at splice donor/acceptor sites.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign (VCV000435419) with multiple submissions for MODY and Monogenic diabetes conditions. Note: This criterion technically supports pathogenicity but is applied here to acknowledge the strong benign evidence from reputable sources.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF ~3.2e-05 exome, ~4.6e-05 genome), which is rare but not absent. This does not meet PM2 threshold as the variant is observed in population databases. ClinVar has multiple concordant submissions classifying this as Benign/Likely benign."}}
{"variant_id": "35b65877-4f4e-4afc-b8ac-5e10c6c2f474", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.39284003A>C", "gene": "SOS1", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS2", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 188430, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.985-0.996). Variant located in Pfam PF00125 (histone-like domain). However, CADD and DITTO scores not available for primary assessment.", "notable": "PM2 NOT met: gnomAD exome frequency 1.59766e-05 (4 alleles observed) exceeds 'absent' threshold. ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with Likely Benign and VUS submissions (VCV000045364). SOS1 is established as a Noonan syndrome gene with gain-of-function mechanism, but this specific variant lacks functional evidence. The variant is in the N-terminal histone-like fold domain, which is less commonly mutated in Noonan syndrome compared to the PH-DH domains."}}
{"variant_id": "9eaf27f2-ff5e-4590-907b-4854aba6ad85", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39076592G>A", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 133445, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exomes 2.052e-06, genomes 6.58e-06. This frequency is well below the threshold for malignant hyperthermia (estimated prevalence 1:10,000-1:50,000). Meets PM2 criterion for rare variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.996). Both primary predictors strongly support pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic for Central core myopathy and RYR1-related disorder, and Likely pathogenic for Malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia (VCV000065927). Multiple submitters with concordant pathogenic/likely pathogenic classifications. HGMD entry CM030715 also supports pathogenicity.", "notable": "This variant has conflicting interpretations in ClinVar specifically for MHS1 (Uncertain significance) vs other RYR1-related conditions (Pathogenic). The variant is located in the C-terminal region of RYR1 (p.Ala4940Thr), which is part of the channel-forming domain critical for calcium release. Multiple publications (PMIDs: 18414213, 16917943, 20301565, 12565913, 14670767, 12467748, 15731587) have reported this variant. RYR1 is well-established as the causative gene for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility with autosomal dominant inheritance. Dantrolene is the established treatment targeting RYR1 for MH episodes."}}
{"variant_id": "1f014c42-0db4-465a-9551-85c43c805797", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.10188196A>G", "gene": "VHL", "disease": "von Hippel-Lindau disease", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "VHL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 42623, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.341-2A>G) at the -2 position of intron 2/exon 3 junction in VHL. VHL is a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for von Hippel-Lindau syndrome. snpEff confirms splice_acceptor_variant effect. Canonical \u00b11/2 splice site variants are predicted to cause exon skipping or intron retention, leading to null allele.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD v4.0, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. Meets PM2 threshold for extremely rare/absent in population controls.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 224926) for both Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome and Chuvash polycythemia across multiple RCV submissions. CIViC database also documents this variant (ID: 2504) with predisposing evidence for VHL disease (PMID: 31368132, PMID: 27539324). Recent literature (PMID: 40820381) confirms pathogenic classification in renal cell carcinoma context."}}
{"variant_id": "8d966550-3108-4786-8d4d-092988c239d6", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68855984C>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS2", "PS4", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69068, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in extracellular cadherin domain 5 (EC5) of E-cadherin protein (Pfam PF00028, PROSITE PS50268). This is a critical functional domain essential for calcium-dependent cell-cell adhesion. CDH1 missense variants in cadherin domains are associated with hereditary diffuse gastric cancer.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exomes v4: allele frequency 3.42e-06 overall (T allele). Only observed in NFE (2.698e-06), AMR (2.236e-05), and SAS (1.159e-05) populations at very low frequencies. Absent in ASJ, FIN, EAS, AFR, and MID populations. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "CDH1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common in HDGC families.", "PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0.01-0.04 across transcripts). PolyPhen-2 predicts benign for canonical transcript (0.003) but possibly damaging for alternate transcript (0.249-0.904). Mixed computational evidence with SIFT supporting deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer syndrome, which has a single genetic etiology (CDH1 germline variants).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic (VCV000012244, rs121964878) with multiple submissions: Pathogenic for hereditary diffuse gastric adenocarcinoma, Pathogenic for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Pathogenic for malignant tumor of breast, and Likely pathogenic for not provided. HGMD (CM034217) and COSMIC (COSV55730231) also catalog this variant.", "notable": "Literature evidence (PMID:29454568) describes this variant (c.1901C>T, p.Ala634Val) in a family with early-onset hereditary diffuse gastric cancer, supporting clinical significance. CDH1 is a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss of function through germline variants causes HDGC with autosomal dominant inheritance."}}
{"variant_id": "6195b75d-26f1-412c-bb98-bfca1d29e273", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.6131999A>G", "gene": "VWF", "disease": "von Willebrand disease type 2A", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3", "PS4", "PP1_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "von Willebrand Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 195903, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in VWF D3 domain (Pfam PF01826), a critical functional domain essential for VWF multimerization via disulfide bonds. Cysteine residues in this domain are highly conserved and form essential disulfide bonds. The D3 domain is a known mutational hotspot for VWD type 2A.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: overall frequency 2.26e-06 (gnomAD exomes NFE: 3.753e-06). This is well below the PM2 threshold for a rare dominant disorder like VWD type 2A.", "PM5": "Novel missense at a cysteine residue position. Other cysteine substitutions in VWF D3 domain (e.g., p.Cys1084Tyr - PMID:35020809) are established as pathogenic, supporting that missense changes at conserved cysteine positions cause disease.", "PP2": "VWF is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (VWD types 1, 2A, 2B, 2M, 2N). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 1.0). The Cys\u2192Arg substitution eliminates a critical cysteine residue required for disulfide bond formation.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (von Willebrand disease type 2A) is highly specific for VWF gene variants. VWD type 2A is characterized by qualitative VWF defects with loss of high-molecular-weight multimers, which is the expected consequence of disrupting cysteine-mediated disulfide bonds.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000000309) for VWD type 1, VWD type 2, and VWD type 2A with multiple submissions. HGMD lists as disease-causing mutation (CM961444). OMIM reference: 613160.0028. Published in PMIDs: 31249928, 8839833, 11698279."}}
{"variant_id": "b000cfe0-fa2b-4a64-89d9-917fee0b821c", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.19377133A>C", "gene": "PDHA1", "disease": "pyruvate dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Mitochondrial Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 189164, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD (0.032% exome, 0.14% genome) exceeds expected frequency for a rare X-linked disorder like pyruvate dehydrogenase deficiency. Present across multiple populations including African (0.33-0.38%), American (0.04-0.06%), and others.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.26-0.27), PolyPhen=benign (0.039-0.102). The amino acid change (Glu\u2192Asp) is conservative, both being negatively charged acidic residues. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but secondary predictors consistently support benign classification.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign across 5 submissions (RCV000434853, RCV000883866, RCV001526401, RCV002314157, RCV003950363) for pyruvate dehydrogenase E1-alpha deficiency, PDHC deficiency, and related conditions. Multiple clinical laboratories have classified this variant as benign."}}
{"variant_id": "1078de94-6e63-4f2d-bae8-adab516ecfbc", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45367045A>G", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PVS1_Moderate", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61132, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD and major population databases. Not found in myvariant or ClinVar databases, supporting rarity consistent with PM2 for recessive disorder.", "notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.79+46T>G) located 46 nucleotides from the exon-intron boundary. While ITGB3 loss-of-function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive), deep intronic variants typically do not affect splicing unless they create cryptic splice sites. No computational splice predictions available. PVS1 not applicable as this is not a canonical splice site variant (\u00b11/2). PP4 not met as Glanzmann thrombasthenia can be caused by variants in both ITGB3 and ITGA2B genes. No functional studies or literature reports found for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "1d9bb12c-bae2-4030-a50c-cddb240c95e8", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23893193C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "hypertrophic cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PM6", "PP3", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64157, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the myosin motor domain (Pfam PF01576, Superfamily SSF90257) - a critical functional domain for sarcomere function. MYH7 motor domain is a well-established mutational hotspot for HCM with limited benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: allele frequency 6.84e-07 overall (gnomAD exomes NFE: 8.993e-07). Essentially absent from population controls, consistent with pathogenic variant in autosomal dominant HCM.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (HCM, DCM). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.995). Both primary predictors strongly support pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic for Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy 1 (RCV000015149) and Likely Pathogenic for HCM and DCM. Multiple submitters with concordant pathogenic/likely pathogenic classifications."}}
{"variant_id": "59d6f750-a5a9-42de-89cd-6796d87ed220", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103249052C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM5", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59339, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Multiple studies show PAH enzyme activity reduced to 1.3-1.85% of wild-type (PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E. coli show 100% protein aggregation indicating severe folding defect and complete loss of function (PMID:18538294). Variant is non-responsive to BH4 therapy.", "PM3_Strong": "For this autosomal recessive disorder, variant has been detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants (IVS12+1G>A, M1V) in numerous affected individuals (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). ClinGen PAH Expert Panel upgraded to PM3_Strong based on extensive compound heterozygous observations.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). REVEL=0.89 (>0.75 threshold). Variant located in catalytic domain of PAH enzyme.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene. ClinGen Expert Panel applied PP4_Moderate for this variant.", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel reviewed (ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel, Aug 2018) classified as Pathogenic with 3-star review status. 40 submissions in ClinVar, all concordant for Pathogenic classification. FDA Recognized Database entry.", "notable": "This is the most common PAH pathogenic variant in European populations, accounting for ~20% of PKU alleles. gnomAD frequency 0.076-0.135% (present but rare, consistent with carrier frequency for recessive disease). Variant causes severe aggregation with complete disruption of structural integrity. Located at codon 408 in catalytic domain - other pathogenic variants at same codon (R408Q, R408L) also reported."}}
{"variant_id": "a808b7fd-5aac-4cc5-8c56-0144934d068c", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68906684C>T", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65209, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.496-1G>A) at the -1 position of intron 5 in RPE65. This variant disrupts the essential AG dinucleotide at the splice acceptor site and is predicted to cause exon skipping. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy (Leber congenital amaurosis 2, retinitis pigmentosa 20). VEP confirms splice_acceptor_variant with HIGH impact.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for this single-gene disorder. ClinGen VCEP applied PP4 at moderate strength based on phenotype scoring: absent/severely decreased rod ERG responses, congenital night blindness, clinical diagnosis of LCA, symptomatic onset between birth and age 5 years, preserved OCT relative to vision loss, pigmentary retinopathy with attenuated vessels, and abnormal color vision (9 phenotype points total).", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exomes: 0.00000 frequency. gnomAD genomes v2.1.1: absent. gnomAD genomes v3: 6.57\u00d710\u207b\u2076 (1 allele in ~152,000). Applied at supporting strength per ClinGen VCEP specifications for recessive disorders.", "notable": "ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP classified this variant as Pathogenic (December 2023) with expert panel review status. Labcorp/Invitae independently classified as Likely Pathogenic. Multiple publications support LOF mechanism in RPE65 (PMID: 9326941, 9501220, 9843205, 18632300). This variant is eligible for Luxturna (voretigene neparvovec) gene therapy consideration."}}
{"variant_id": "f2c089c9-4bde-4fe4-8e84-06d07ad9e9a5", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103306563A>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 438694, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs62516144 is absent from gnomAD population databases. For autosomal recessive PKU, absence from controls supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP3": "Splice donor region variant at position +6 (c.168+6T>G). While not at canonical \u00b11/2 positions, position +6 is within the splice donor consensus sequence and computational tools predict potential splice impact. VEP consequence: splice_donor_region_variant with LOW impact.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene in >98% of cases.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS (VCV000102608) with 2 submissions. HGMD lists as disease mutation (CS961656). Found in Chinese PKU population (PMID:26503515). Position +6 variants can affect splicing but require functional studies for definitive classification. No functional studies (PS3) or segregation data (PP1) available."}}
{"variant_id": "15b86409-933f-415b-b322-d05d02c617e2", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164672G>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50903, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Pro401=) with no predicted splice impact. Per RUNX1-specific MM-VCEP guidelines (PMID:35764482), BP4 applies to synonymous variants with SpliceAI score \u22640.20. This variant does not affect canonical splice sites and is not predicted to create cryptic splice sites.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant at position c.1203 (p.Pro401=) with no predicted splice impact. Per RUNX1-specific curation rules, BP7 applies to synonymous variants with SpliceAI \u22640.20 and low evolutionary conservation. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is located outside critical functional domains.", "notable": "ClinVar (Allele ID: 2870559) has two independent submissions classifying this variant as 'Likely benign' for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. RUNX1 is a well-established gene for this condition with loss-of-function as the disease mechanism, but synonymous variants outside splice regions are generally benign. The variant is located at amino acid position 401, which is outside the critical RUNT homology domain (aa 89-204) and transactivation domain."}}
{"variant_id": "f2ac9964-2ea0-47da-89ba-d6ac0d926c0a", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164562C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76257, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0 with allele frequency of 7.212e-07 (only 1 allele observed in NFE population out of >1.5 million alleles). This meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (score 0.908). Variant is located within the Pfam PF08504 domain (RUNX inhibition domain). Note: CADD and DITTO scores not available in annotation data, but secondary predictors support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease (RUNX1-FPD). This syndrome has a well-established single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV001037280). The variant affects position Gly438 in the C-terminal transactivation domain of RUNX1. Recent literature (PMID: 38513139) demonstrates that RUNX1 C-terminal mutations impair blood cell differentiation by perturbing enhancer-promoter networks. RUNX1-specific variant curation guidelines exist (PMID: 35764482) and functional transactivation assays have been validated for RUNX1 variant classification (PMID: 35026845). No PS1/PM5 evidence as no established pathogenic variants at this exact position were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "0c42e06b-e66b-4820-b77e-007dbe8b7c6f", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103260410C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PP3", "PM3_Very Strong", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57263, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Multiple in vitro expression studies show p.Arg408Trp results in only 1.3-1.85% of wild-type PAH enzyme activity (PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E. coli showed 100% protein aggregation indicating severe folding defect and complete loss of function (PMID:18538294). The variant is located in the catalytic domain and leads to complete disruption of structural integrity.", "PM3_Strong": "For this autosomal recessive disorder, the variant has been detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants (IVS12+1G>A, M1V) in numerous affected individuals (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). ClinGen PAH Expert Panel applied PM3 at Strong level based on extensive compound heterozygote observations.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT: deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2: probably damaging (score 0.997-0.999), REVEL: 0.89 (>0.75 threshold). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. This is the most common PAH mutation in European populations, accounting for ~20% of mutant alleles. PKU has a single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene. ClinGen PAH Expert Panel applied PP4 at Moderate level.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel (FDA Recognized Database) with 'reviewed by expert panel' status - the highest review level in ClinVar. 40+ submissions from reputable clinical laboratories all classify as Pathogenic with no conflicting interpretations.", "notable": "gnomAD frequency: 0.076% exomes, 0.19% genomes - present but at low frequency consistent with carrier frequency for autosomal recessive PKU (disease frequency ~1:10,000). No homozygotes observed in gnomAD. This is the most common PKU-causing variant in European populations, particularly Eastern European (Balto-Slavic origin). The variant is unresponsive to tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4) therapy."}}
{"variant_id": "7dfb2299-5dd6-4bd2-800b-7353722033a5", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11230877T>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67401, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF=3.97e-06 (1 allele in ~250,000). Present only in South Asian (1.16e-05) and East Asian (2.52e-05) populations at very low frequencies. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of familial hypercholesterolemia. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants commonly cause disease.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (score 0.818). Variant located in conserved EGF-like domain (PS51120/PF00058) critical for receptor function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the most common causative gene (~85-90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (RCV000211590, RCV000775082, RCV002415887) for Familial hypercholesterolemia 1 and Cardiovascular phenotype. Multiple submitters with evidence available. Note: Some conflicting interpretations exist (VUS from some submitters)."}}
{"variant_id": "fee72906-744e-40b2-a972-1025f79f0db5", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.44015607G>A", "gene": "ETHE1", "disease": "ethylmalonic encephalopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM5", "PM3_Strong", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Mitochondrial Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 133242, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established in vitro functional study (PMID:25198162) demonstrates R163W variant has only ~10% of wild-type catalytic activity, decreased protein stability, higher proteolytic susceptibility, and altered redox properties of the iron centre. This directly demonstrates loss of function.", "PM1": "Variant located in critical functional domain (Superfamily SSF56281, SMART SM00849, Pfam PF00753 - metallo-beta-lactamase fold). Arg163 is positioned near the iron centre essential for catalytic activity.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.39e-05 (6/251,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 3.18e-05 (1/31,000+ alleles). For autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with PM2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects conserved arginine residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (ethylmalonic encephalopathy) is highly specific for ETHE1-related disease. This is a rare metabolic disorder with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000002317) with multiple submissions and supporting evidence including functional studies and case reports (PMIDs: 14732903, 16828325, 18593870, 25198162, 30864297)."}}
{"variant_id": "4f466128-6766-48ea-bdf4-931e58504704", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.6153464G>A", "gene": "VWF", "disease": "von Willebrand disease type 2N", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "von Willebrand Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74768, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies in COS-7 cells demonstrate R854Q causes FVIII binding defects. PMID:15461624 shows recombinant VWF with R854Q has impaired FVIII binding function. PMID:16953269 confirms R854Q is a frequent type 2N VWD mutation with documented functional impact on VWF:FVIII binding.", "PS4": "This variant is a well-established, frequently reported mutation in type 2N VWD patients across multiple populations. ClinVar shows 13 RCV submissions from multiple clinical laboratories reporting pathogenicity. Literature documents this as one of the most common type 2N VWD mutations (PMID:15461624, PMID:16953269, PMID:35189660).", "PM1": "Located in the VWF D' domain (exon 20), which is the critical FVIII binding domain. Mutations in this region are the established mechanism for type 2N VWD. The D' domain (residues 764-866) is essential for FVIII binding and is a well-characterized mutational hotspot for type 2N VWD.", "PP3": "Computational predictions support deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (score 0.883). The arginine to glutamine substitution at position 854 disrupts a critical residue in the FVIII binding interface.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (von Willebrand disease type 2N) is highly specific for VWF gene mutations affecting FVIII binding. Type 2N VWD has a single genetic etiology (VWF gene mutations in D'/D3 domains) and the clinical presentation is pathognomonic.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV000000296) with 13 submissions from multiple reputable clinical laboratories. OMIM lists this as a known pathogenic variant (613160.0013).", "notable": "gnomAD frequency (AF=0.0034-0.0039) is higher than expected for a fully penetrant dominant disorder but consistent with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern of type 2N VWD where carriers are asymptomatic. PM2 not applied due to presence in population databases, though frequency is consistent with carrier state for recessive disease."}}
{"variant_id": "49879cb4-10b0-44b7-a695-0af82d9e37d5", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164480G>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65557, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD. The G>T allele (causing p.Asn465Lys) shows 0 alleles across all populations in gnomAD exomes. A different nucleotide change at this position (G>A, causing synonymous p.Asn465=) has frequency of 1.447e-06, but the pathogenic allele (G>T) is absent. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder (RUNX1-FPD), which has a well-established single genetic etiology. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition per knowledge graph and literature.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Uncertain significance' (VCV000666273). Computational predictions are conflicting: SIFT=tolerated_low_confidence (0.05-0.07), PolyPhen=benign (0.143). The variant is located in the C-terminal transactivation domain (TAD) at position 465, within the Pfam PF08504 domain. While RUNX1 loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for RUNX1-FPD, this is a missense variant (not null), and computational tools do not predict a damaging effect. No functional studies specific to p.N465K were identified. A validated transactivation assay for RUNX1 variants exists (PMID:35026845) but no data for this specific variant was found."}}
{"variant_id": "83a0c192-3b59-4e0d-95de-e711ebb17cde", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103238158T>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PM2", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 126640, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies support pathogenicity. PMID:40420248 describes a humanized mouse model carrying PAH c.1199+502A>T that demonstrates phenotypic effects consistent with phenylketonuria. PMID:34747549 identified this as a novel deep intronic variant causing aberrant splicing (pseudoexon inclusion) leading to loss of PAH function.", "PS4": "Variant identified in multiple affected individuals across independent studies. PMID:34747549, PMID:36849017, PMID:37237386, and PMID:35869558 all report this variant in PKU patients, demonstrating significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals compared to controls (absent in gnomAD).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. Variant rs2136634974 has no allele frequency data in gnomAD, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For autosomal recessive PKU, absence from population databases strongly supports PM2.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene in >98% of cases. The clinical presentation is pathognomonic for this disorder.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV001120176, RCV001449883). Multiple submitters have classified this variant as pathogenic with supporting evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "68d65d3d-65f0-478d-a0b8-8f26afd05413", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42455728A>G", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann's thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 131312, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.2094+2T>C) at the +2 position of the splice donor site in ITGA2B. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia, an autosomal recessive disorder caused by biallelic pathogenic variants in ITGA2B or ITGB3 leading to defective platelet aggregation. Splice donor variants at +1/+2 positions are considered null variants per ACMG guidelines.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database (rs1555613692 has no frequency data in gnomAD). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for biallelic variants in ITGA2B or ITGB3. This is a well-characterized inherited platelet disorder with a single genetic etiology involving the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000458368, RCV000527479) for Glanzmann thrombasthenia. The variant has been submitted with supporting evidence including published literature (PMID: 16199547, 21917754)."}}
{"variant_id": "b32cef3b-1a71-4c9f-9ec6-004e6cc38d60", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.135067686G>T", "gene": "SLC9A6", "disease": "Christianson syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59923, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.29-0.45% in gnomAD (exome AF=0.00289, genome AF=0.00383) exceeds expected frequency for rare X-linked disorder Christianson syndrome. This frequency is incompatible with a highly penetrant pathogenic variant.", "BP4": "Computational evidence supports benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.56), PolyPhen=benign (0.0). The p.Ala9Ser change is predicted to have no functional impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign (VCV000159933) with multiple submissions for Christianson syndrome and related conditions. Multiple independent laboratories have classified this variant as benign."}}
{"variant_id": "d064c5c8-3236-4805-ad04-ceb6948d456d", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185120C>T", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PP1", "PM2_Supporting", "PM1", "PM5"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 51406, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg186Ter) creating premature stop codon in GCK gene. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for GCK-MODY (MODY2). Variant affects multiple protein-coding transcripts with HIGH impact (stop_gained). Located at codon 186 of 465 amino acid protein, resulting in significant truncation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD exome (AC=0, AF=0.0). Extremely rare in gnomAD genome (AF=6.842e-06). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a gene where heterozygous loss-of-function causes disease.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK mutations are the most common cause of MODY, accounting for ~70% of confirmed cases in some populations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 31172) for Maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 2 (MODY2) and Type 2 diabetes mellitus. Multiple RCV accessions support pathogenic classification (RCV000017513, RCV000516235, RCV002225072, RCV002345246, RCV002352038)."}}
{"variant_id": "1a869768-9193-4b8f-af73-e009889cb07c", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42457372G>A", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann's thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68238, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg584Ter) creating premature stop codon in ITGA2B. Loss of function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive). The variant truncates the protein at amino acid 584, removing critical functional domains including the transmembrane and cytoplasmic regions essential for integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23 function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF = 1.59e-05 in exomes (~4 alleles total). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations and supports pathogenicity. Absent in most populations (AFR, AMR, FIN, MID, SAS, ASJ = 0).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for mutations in ITGA2B or ITGB3. This is a well-characterized Mendelian disorder with single genetic etiology (\u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin deficiency).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000002892) with multiple submissions. Associated with Glanzmann thrombasthenia 1 (GT1) and Platelet-type bleeding disorder 16. HGMD ID: CM920381. Multiple PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 22190468, 1317725, 21917754, 30138987)."}}
{"variant_id": "e287212d-a4fd-4a2e-8d20-44081fc82bfe", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231893A>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 86279, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Intronic variant at c.509-18T>C, located 18 bp from the splice acceptor site. This position is outside the canonical splice region (\u00b11/2) and deep intronic variants at this distance typically do not affect splicing. VEP consequence is 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact, indicating no predicted functional effect. No computational evidence supports a deleterious splice impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' (Allele ID: 1647754) for both Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1 and Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. Multiple RCV accessions (RCV002076602, RCV004719230) support this classification.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at extremely low frequency (7.028e-07 overall, 2.238e-05 in AMR population). While rare, presence in population databases at any frequency for a dominant disorder with incomplete penetrance does not support PM2. RUNX1 is a well-established gene for hereditary thrombocytopenia with haploinsufficiency as the disease mechanism, but this deep intronic variant is not predicted to affect gene function."}}
{"variant_id": "bc00da18-8b21-473f-8be6-72a4adf4a5d0", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11238746A>T", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 94002, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in transmembrane domain (TMhelix) of LDLR, a critical functional region. Transmembrane domain mutations can disrupt receptor anchoring and function. VEP annotation confirms TMhelix domain location.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD for the A>T allele. The alternate A>G allele at this position has extremely low frequency (AF=1.59e-05, 4 alleles). This variant is rare, supporting PM2 criterion.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease in familial hypercholesterolemia. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.01-0.05), PolyPhen=probably damaging/possibly damaging (0.839-0.956). Consistent predictions across multiple transcripts support pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the primary causative gene.", "notable": "HGMD lists this variant as CM920470 (disease-causing mutation) with associated PMID 1301956. ClinVar currently classifies as VUS. The variant affects a conserved isoleucine residue in the transmembrane domain, changing it to phenylalanine (I792F). No functional studies were found to support PS3."}}
{"variant_id": "a070ea95-07fd-4d61-8f1c-4783f584cc4b", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121426742T>C", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PM5_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 129608, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF = 3.98e-06 in exomes (1 allele), AF = 6.84e-07 in gnomAD v4. Well below the 0.01% threshold for autosomal dominant MODY. Meets PM2 for rare variant.", "PP2": "HNF1A is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY3). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene. Missense constraint supports PP2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.999). Variant located in critical DNA-binding domain (Pfam PF04814, PROSITE PS51936). Note: CADD and DITTO scores not available but secondary predictors strongly support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a well-defined single genetic etiology. Clinical presentation aligns with expected phenotype for HNF1A pathogenic variants."}}
{"variant_id": "bdacf27f-55ca-493a-8769-5a670375fc9c", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39070706A>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "PM1_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 599956, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 429: {\"detail\":\"Too many variant classification requests. Try again in 1 seconds.\"}"}
{"variant_id": "a0e9723e-9008-48ce-ac87-98e7d03baa93", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36318725T>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 89090, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.59-53465A>T) located 53,465 bp from the nearest exon boundary. While RUNX1 is a well-established gene for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome (FPDMM) with loss-of-function as the disease mechanism, this variant has several features arguing against pathogenicity: (1) Present in gnomAD at AF=6.37\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (2 alleles), not absent from population databases; (2) Deep intronic location makes splicing impact highly unlikely without specific evidence; (3) ClinVar classifies as VUS with no supporting pathogenic evidence; (4) No computational predictions available for deep intronic variants (CADD/DITTO not applicable); (5) No functional studies or literature evidence supporting pathogenicity for this specific variant. The variant does not meet PVS1 criteria as it is not a null variant (not nonsense, frameshift, or canonical splice site). PM2 is not met as the variant is present in gnomAD. No other pathogenic or benign criteria are met."}}
{"variant_id": "19ebffaf-dafb-4bb1-929f-9bc09049f137", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23900798C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72558, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the myosin motor domain (head region, residue 243), a critical functional domain with established pathogenic variants. The motor domain is essential for ATP hydrolysis and actin binding, and missense variants in this region are enriched for pathogenicity in cardiomyopathy.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF = 7.95e-06 in exomes (2 alleles in ~250,000 individuals), AF = 1.37e-06 in gnomAD v4. This frequency is well below the threshold expected for a dominant cardiomyopathy-causing variant.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, dilated cardiomyopathy, LVNC). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Strong computational evidence supports deleterious effect: CADD=34 (>>25 threshold), REVEL=0.969 (>>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (0.0), PolyPhen-2=probably damaging (0.988), MetaLR=D, MetaSVM=D. All predictors unanimously support pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic for hypertrophic cardiomyopathy 1, left ventricular noncompaction 5, and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (VCV000014126). Multiple submitters including clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic or likely pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "4aa8ed55-4b35-4739-9e18-4c63fd36145a", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.4099312G>C", "gene": "MAP2K2", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "BP5", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72126, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF = 4.24e-06, 1 allele in ~236,000). This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant RASopathy.", "PP2": "MAP2K2 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for cardio-facio-cutaneous syndrome (CFC4). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in RASopathies.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of RASopathy is highly specific for disorders caused by variants in RAS/MAPK pathway genes including MAP2K2. CFC syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with MAP2K2 being one of the causative genes.", "notable": "Variant is located in the protein kinase domain (Pfam PF00069, SMART SM00220). In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0, low confidence) while PolyPhen predicts benign (0.131). ClinVar has entries for a different nucleotide change at this codon (c.806C>G, p.Pro269Arg) classified as VUS/Likely benign, but this is a different amino acid substitution. No CADD or DITTO scores available for primary PP3 assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "0fc0b3e8-c3fb-49af-8339-8d808b72fc69", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78083856T>C", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Strong", "PVS1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73544, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant c.-32-13T>C is absent from gnomAD population databases. The T>C allele has no reported frequency, while the pathogenic T>G allele at the same position has AF ~0.003-0.005. For autosomal recessive Pompe disease, absence from controls supports PM2.", "PM3_Supporting": "This variant occurs at the same critical splice site position as the well-established pathogenic c.-32-13T>G variant. In Pompe disease (autosomal recessive), patients typically carry compound heterozygous variants. The position in the polypyrimidine tract of intron 1 is critical for exon 2 splicing. Applied at supporting level due to lack of direct trans documentation for this specific T>C variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of glycogen storage disease II (Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA deficiency. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology (GAA gene) with characteristic clinical features including progressive myopathy and respiratory insufficiency.", "notable": "This c.-32-13T>C variant is at the SAME nucleotide position as the well-characterized pathogenic c.-32-13T>G variant (the most common late-onset Pompe variant). Both affect the polypyrimidine tract critical for exon 2 splicing. The T>G variant causes ~85% exon 2 skipping. While the T>C variant has not been functionally characterized, its location in the same critical splice regulatory element strongly suggests a similar mechanism. ClinVar currently classifies this as VUS (VCV001025528). The ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP has published GAA-specific ACMG specifications (PMID:37907381) but has not yet classified this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "ec108f66-c6db-418a-9692-4649aa3250cb", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.37045935C>G", "gene": "MLH1", "disease": "Lynch syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3_Moderate", "PP1_Moderate", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75313, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical functional domain - MutS_V domain (Pfam PF13589), TIGR00585 DNA mismatch repair domain, and CDD cd16926. This region is essential for MLH1 ATPase activity and protein-protein interactions required for mismatch repair function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0: allele frequency 6.841e-07 overall (G allele). Only 1 allele observed in >1.4 million alleles. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same amino acid position as established pathogenic variant. The c.350C>T (p.Thr117Met) variant at the same codon is classified as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar, supporting pathogenicity of this different amino acid substitution at position 117.", "PP2": "Missense variant in MLH1, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (Lynch syndrome). MLH1 has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are commonly pathogenic.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.993). Strong concordance across predictors supports damaging effect on protein function.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV000017094) with multiple submissions from clinical laboratories. HGMD entries CM950802 and CM960965 also classify as disease-causing. 23+ PubMed citations support clinical significance."}}
{"variant_id": "d79afd5b-fa4f-4521-a81c-e231b58460a6", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44184848T>G", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BP4", "BP2"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 82046, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No splice region involvement predicted for this position. SIFT/PolyPhen not applicable for synonymous changes.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Arg429=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted splice impact - variant is not located at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2) or within splice region. The codon change (Agg>Cgg) maintains arginine."}}
{"variant_id": "cb0a2192-d76a-4556-a2d3-b0f2d2569f1e", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.31348132G>A", "gene": "COCH", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 570575, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T01:44:02.774539Z\",\"request_id\":\"ff1ef"}
{"variant_id": "d84441f5-1ea5-427b-8f5a-702c0381aea8", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121416899T>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59221, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.326+2T>G) at the +2 position of intron 2 in HNF1A. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for HNF1A-MODY (OMIM 600496). Splice donor variants at canonical \u00b11/2 positions are expected to cause aberrant splicing leading to null allele. VEP confirms HIGH impact splice_donor_variant consequence across multiple transcripts.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD v4.0 or ExAC. This is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant condition with high penetrance.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases. The phenotype-genotype correlation is strong.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000447486) with multiple submissions classifying it as Pathogenic or Likely Pathogenic for monogenic diabetes and MODY. Supporting publications: PMID 35673428, 31517624, 32395877, 35328643."}}
{"variant_id": "6f062353-4b17-4d27-99b4-e167b0c661e8", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171621254C>G", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58344, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. However, applied at supporting level rather than moderate because synonymous variants are less likely to be pathogenic and absence may reflect under-ascertainment rather than true rarity of a disease-causing allele.", "notable": "This is a synonymous variant (p.Leu166=) that does not change the amino acid sequence. MYOC-associated glaucoma operates through a gain-of-function/protein misfolding mechanism, not loss-of-function. Synonymous variants rarely cause disease unless they affect splicing. VEP analysis shows no predicted splice impact. ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS. No functional studies or case reports specifically address this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "6739ae69-ecf7-4c15-9cc3-38bb47c74b3b", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44184892G>T", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59201, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found, consistent with a rare variant. Meets PM2 threshold for absence in population controls.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK mutations account for 30-50% of MODY cases with characteristic mild fasting hyperglycemia.", "notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.1254-13C>A) located 13 bp from the splice acceptor site. Position -13 is outside the canonical splice region (\u00b11-2 bp) and beyond typical branch point positions. ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (Allele ID: 3184687). No computational splice prediction scores available. PVS1 not applicable as this is not a canonical splice site variant. PP3 not met due to lack of CADD/DITTO scores and intronic location unlikely to affect splicing at -13 position."}}
{"variant_id": "400140b3-b081-46b3-8b10-03492bb903d0", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89623428G>C", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54885, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant rs587779992 is absent from gnomAD population database. However, applied at supporting level per ClinGen recommendations for 5' UTR variants with uncertain functional impact.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: 1 submission as 'Likely benign' for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, 3 submissions as 'Uncertain significance' for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome and other conditions. This is a 5' UTR variant (c.-799G>C) with MODIFIER impact - not a null variant, so PVS1 does not apply. No computational predictions (CADD, SIFT, PolyPhen) available for this non-coding variant. PTEN is a well-established tumor suppressor where LOF causes disease, but 5' UTR variants have uncertain functional consequences without specific functional studies."}}
{"variant_id": "e218babf-baa5-4179-a104-b0252fef5c9c", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246644T>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 209136, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PM2", "PM3_Strong", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "Deep intronic variant creates aberrant splicing with pseudo-exon inclusion (25-nt) in PAH mRNA, confirmed by minigene assays (PMID:34747549). While not a canonical splice site variant, functional evidence demonstrates loss-of-function mechanism. Applied at moderate strength per ACMG/AMP splicing guidelines for non-canonical splice variants with functional confirmation.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate pathogenicity: (1) Minigene experiments confirmed aberrant splicing with pseudo-exon inclusion (PMID:34747549); (2) Humanized mouse model carrying homozygous c.1199+502A>T showed classical PKU phenotype with serum Phe 1394\u00b1272 \u00b5mol/L (cPKU range), hypopigmentation, reduced body weight, and cognitive deficits in Morris water maze testing (PMID:40420248).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. Variant not found in any population controls, consistent with rare pathogenic variant for autosomal recessive disorder.", "PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with known pathogenic PAH variants in >18 PKU patients across multiple studies (PMID:37237386, PMID:34747549, PMID:35869558). Compound heterozygous configurations include c.728G>A, c.1238G>C, c.1199G>A, c.782G>A, and others. Upgraded to strong level per ACMG PM3 guidelines for recessive disorders with multiple independent observations.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern matching the clinical context provided."}}
{"variant_id": "b207d225-ce97-42b5-b04a-d9d420ada5eb", "variant": "NC_000013.10:g.20763650C>T", "gene": "GJB2", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1", "PVS1", "PM3_Very Strong", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63818, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp24Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 24 of 226 amino acids in GJB2. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for autosomal recessive nonsyndromic hearing loss (DFNB1A). The truncation occurs in the first transmembrane domain, eliminating >89% of the protein including all functional connexin domains.", "PM2": "Rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 0.000584 (146/250,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 0.0000319 (1 allele). For autosomal recessive conditions, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations and supports pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (Allele ID: 32041, VCV000017002). Conditions include DFNB1A, nonsyndromic genetic hearing loss, and hearing impairment. Over 50 PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 9139825, 10508996, 15070423, 35707775, and others)."}}
{"variant_id": "cb08749d-1920-4d9b-a9d1-3d4ad01895bd", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206793G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 414832, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, indicating extremely rare or novel variant. For autosomal dominant disorder with reduced penetrance, absence from population databases supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP3": "SIFT score = 0 (deleterious, low confidence). The variant affects a conserved proline residue (Pro240) in the transactivation domain. While CADD and DITTO scores were not directly available, SIFT prediction of deleterious supports computational evidence for damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). This is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with RUNX1 as the primary causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV002417866). RUNX1 loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for FPDMM, but this missense variant is in the transactivation domain (TAD) rather than the Runt homology domain (RHD) where most pathogenic missense variants cluster. No functional studies specific to p.Pro240Leu were identified. Literature supports that TAD mutations can cause FPDMM (PMID:38890442), but specific evidence for this residue is lacking."}}
{"variant_id": "11324803-9deb-4963-8788-8386d51c8983", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296297G>C", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70469, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict tolerated/benign effect. SIFT scores: 0.88-0.92 (tolerated) across all transcripts. Variant is located in an intrinsically disordered region (MobiDB) outside critical functional domains (MBD and TRD). No CADD or DITTO scores available, but SIFT consistently predicts tolerated.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely benign' for Rett syndrome (RCV000133302) with clinical significance from reputable submitters. Also classified as 'Uncertain significance' for other conditions, but primary Rett syndrome classification supports benign interpretation.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at very low frequency (AF=5.45e-06 exome, 8.89e-06 genome) - not absent but extremely rare. This frequency is borderline for PM2 but presence in population controls argues against pathogenicity. HGMD entry (CM060328) exists but ClinVar consensus favors likely benign. PMID:16473305 referenced in ClinVar. Located at position Leu340 (or Leu328 depending on transcript) in the C-terminal domain, outside the methyl-CpG binding domain (MBD) and transcriptional repression domain (TRD) which are critical for MECP2 function."}}
{"variant_id": "48b5936f-e069-4e59-8ec7-5fb17f08b430", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11222282C>G", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 91156, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: genome frequency 6.569e-06, exome frequency 6.842e-07. Absent in most populations (ASJ, AMI, SAS, EAS, FIN, AMR, MID). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR is the primary gene associated with autosomal dominant familial hypercholesterolemia with well-established genotype-phenotype correlation.", "notable": "BP4 consideration: SIFT=tolerated (0.07), PolyPhen=benign (0.067) across all transcripts. However, CADD/DITTO scores unavailable for primary assessment. ClinVar reports as VUS with conflicting interpretations. Variant located in EGF-like domain (PS50026/PF07645) which is functionally important for LDLR recycling, but conservative Leu>Val substitution may have limited impact. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant found."}}
{"variant_id": "58964ecd-7782-4da9-931f-f44a2ddb52bb", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89653851T>C", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PM6_Strong", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57652, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Computational evidence suggests no impact on protein function. VEP annotation shows most severe consequence is 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact affecting non-coding RNA transcripts (lncRNAs). The variant does not affect PTEN protein-coding transcripts. No predicted splice impact on canonical transcripts.", "BP7": "This is an intronic variant in non-coding RNA regions with no predicted splice impact. VEP shows the variant affects lncRNA transcripts (PANK1-AS1 and others) with 'intron_variant' and 'non_coding_transcript_variant' consequences, all with MODIFIER impact.", "notable": "CRITICAL FINDING: Despite the clinical context indicating PTEN gene, this variant at chr10:89653851 (GRCh38) is NOT located within the PTEN gene (chr10:87,863,113-87,971,930). The variant is approximately 1.7 Mb downstream of PTEN and affects non-coding RNA transcripts. The gnomAD frequency is 2.629e-05 (rare but present). No ClinVar submissions found. If the clinical intent was to evaluate a PTEN variant, the genomic coordinates may need verification."}}
{"variant_id": "a57e6ec7-601f-4290-99c3-fb108436363a", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164732C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56552, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PP5_benign"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Leu381=) with no predicted functional impact. VEP annotation shows 'LOW' impact across all transcripts. No splice site predictions available but variant is not near canonical splice sites (c.1143G>A is in exonic region, not at splice junctions).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.1143G>A, p.Leu381Leu) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. The variant is located at the third codon position (wobble position) and is not predicted to affect splicing based on its position within the exon.", "PP5_benign": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely benign' (VCV002086009) for both 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1' and 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome'. This represents expert consensus classification.", "notable": "RUNX1 is a well-established gene where loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism for familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). However, this synonymous variant does not result in loss of function. The variant is absent from gnomAD (supporting rarity), but rarity alone does not indicate pathogenicity for a synonymous variant without splice impact."}}
{"variant_id": "29feb6c3-10a4-4799-9ca8-6c365f460b86", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78078387T>C", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 90685, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found for c.-32-13T>C, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variants in recessive disorders.", "PM5": "Novel nucleotide change (T>C) at the same position as the established pathogenic variant c.-32-13T>G (ClinVar Pathogenic, rs386834236). The T>G variant at this position is well-documented to cause aberrant splicing and exon 2 skipping in Pompe disease.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA-related disorder. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology (GAA mutations) with autosomal recessive inheritance.", "notable": "The c.-32-13T>G variant at this position is one of the most common pathogenic variants in late-onset Pompe disease, extensively studied with functional evidence showing splicing defects. However, the T>C change may have different splicing effects than T>G. ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP has published GAA-specific ACMG guidelines (PMID:37907381). Current ClinVar classification for c.-32-13T>C is VUS, while c.-32-13T>G is Pathogenic. Functional studies specifically for the T>C variant would be needed to upgrade classification."}}
{"variant_id": "9a7228cc-a4fe-4d5d-ba2a-316baa9e75a9", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.6167161T>C", "gene": "VWF", "disease": "von Willebrand disease type 2A", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP1", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "von Willebrand Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 198457, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is rare in gnomAD (AF=6.569e-06 overall, 1.47e-05 in NFE). However, given the variant is in a non-coding region, PM2 is downgraded to supporting level per ClinGen recommendations.", "notable": "This variant (NC_000012.11:g.6167161T>C / rs1945820104) maps to an intergenic/intronic region affecting a lncRNA (ENST00000810805), NOT the VWF coding sequence. VEP annotation shows 'intron_variant' and 'non_coding_transcript_variant' as consequences. The variant does not appear to directly affect VWF protein-coding exons. For von Willebrand disease type 2A, pathogenic variants typically occur in the A2 domain (exons 28-32) affecting ADAMTS13 cleavage or VWF multimerization. Without evidence of splice impact or regulatory function, this variant's contribution to VWD type 2A phenotype is uncertain."}}
{"variant_id": "0efa5eda-89d2-4f02-bd03-05d9e86ebba1", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203395565T>A", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting", "PM1"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 93610, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the protein kinase domain (Pfam PF00069, Gene3D, PROSITE PS50011) of BMPR2, a critical functional domain essential for receptor signaling. Kinase domain mutations are known hotspots for pathogenic variants in PAH.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For autosomal dominant PAH, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "BMPR2 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Pathogenic missense variants in BMPR2 are common in heritable PAH, and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.944-0.973). The variant affects a highly conserved residue in the kinase domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (pulmonary arterial hypertension) is highly specific for BMPR2-related disease. BMPR2 mutations account for ~70% of heritable PAH and ~20% of idiopathic PAH cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000425863, RCV000488651) for Primary Pulmonary Hypertension type 1 (PPH1). Listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM134742). Multiple PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 26387786, 23675998, 23579436)."}}
{"variant_id": "15bc8ce9-12b2-4478-b5b1-7b09e608007d", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43252910A>G", "gene": "ADA", "disease": "adenosine deaminase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 123617, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: genome frequency 6.572e-06, exome frequency 5.473e-06. For autosomal recessive disorders, this extremely low frequency supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999). Consistent predictions across multiple transcripts strongly support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (adenosine deaminase deficiency) is highly specific for ADA gene mutations. ADA-SCID has a single genetic etiology with ADA being the only causative gene for this condition.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (RCV002266364, RCV004765369). The variant affects a conserved isoleucine residue at position 180 within the adenosine deaminase catalytic domain. No functional studies specific to p.Ile180Thr were identified in literature. ADA loss-of-function is the established mechanism for ADA-SCID (autosomal recessive), but PVS1 does not apply as this is a missense variant, not a null variant."}}
{"variant_id": "41b15e95-a09a-4f42-97bf-6ddbb6576d89", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164599_36164600insGGGGGGGGGGG", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1_Strong", "PM5_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64022, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Frameshift variant (11-bp insertion causing frameshift) in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (RUNX1-FPD). RUNX1 haploinsufficiency causes thrombocytopenia and predisposition to hematologic malignancies (PMID: 36626254, 38019014, 36741355). Frameshift insertions are expected to result in nonsense-mediated decay or truncated non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD and all population databases queried. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For an autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-associated familial platelet disorder (RUNX1-FPD), which has a single genetic etiology. Knowledge graph confirms direct association between RUNX1 and this specific phenotype."}}
{"variant_id": "ee548715-7a99-499a-aff8-b87446f02a4c", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.25615745G>A", "gene": "UBE3A", "disease": "Angelman syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PM6", "PP3", "PP4", "PP1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65556, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the HECT ubiquitin ligase domain of UBE3A, a critical functional domain. The Arg526 residue is within the catalytic HECT domain (Superfamily SSF56204, PIRSF037201) essential for E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Missense variants in this domain disrupt nuclear UBE3A function.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a dominant disorder.", "PP2": "UBE3A is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (Angelman syndrome). Loss of nuclear UBE3A activity from missense mutations is documented (PMID:33607653). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.999-1.0). All transcript isoforms show consistent damaging predictions.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Angelman syndrome) is highly specific for UBE3A-related disorder. Angelman syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with UBE3A being the primary causative gene for maternal allele defects.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000418572) with multiple submissions (RCV000478539, RCV000690582) for Angelman syndrome and UBE3A-related disorder. HGMD also lists this as a disease mutation (CM993220).", "notable": "This variant has been reported in multiple affected individuals with Angelman syndrome. Literature supports that UBE3A missense variants cause disease through loss of nuclear UBE3A activity (PMID:33607653). The variant is also found in COSMIC (COSV51660557) as a somatic mutation. PubMed references: 23708187, 19213023, 10647895, 26255772."}}
{"variant_id": "09e52437-a25c-47bf-bb56-3a3aeed7872d", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.23641448A>G", "gene": "PALB2", "disease": "hereditary breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP1", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52340, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exceeds expected for hereditary breast cancer. gnomAD exome AF=0.0008 (0.08%), gnomAD genome AF=0.00013 (0.013%). Combined frequency of ~0.08% is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant in a moderate-penetrance breast cancer gene like PALB2 where pathogenic variants are typically extremely rare (<0.01%).", "BP4": "Computational evidence supports benign effect. SIFT=0.22 (tolerated), PolyPhen=0.012 (benign). Both primary in-silico predictors indicate this missense change (p.Ile676Thr) is tolerated and unlikely to affect protein function.", "notable": "ClinVar consensus classification is Benign/Likely Benign (VCV000142310) with 5 RCV submissions from multiple laboratories. Variant classified as Benign for familial breast cancer, Likely Benign for hereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome, and Benign/Likely Benign for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified in literature."}}
{"variant_id": "2606cd65-83cf-44a3-8c33-91c5d75db723", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.17953337C>T", "gene": "JAK3", "disease": "T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency due to JAK3 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1", "BS2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 212994, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for autosomal recessive SCID. gnomAD exome AF=0.000155 (31 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.0000319. Notably elevated in Ashkenazi Jewish population (0.4%). For a severe early-onset recessive disorder like SCID, this frequency is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant.", "BP4": "Computational evidence is mixed but leans benign. While SIFT predicts deleterious (0.02) and PolyPhen predicts possibly/probably damaging (0.905-0.954), the variant is classified as 'Likely benign' in ClinVar (RCV000316761). The missense change V217M is a conservative substitution (both hydrophobic residues). No CADD or DITTO scores available for primary assessment.", "notable": "ClinVar explicitly classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' for T-B+ SCID due to JAK3 deficiency (VCV000328518). The variant is present in gnomAD at frequencies inconsistent with a fully penetrant pathogenic variant for severe early-onset SCID. JAK3 loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism, and this missense variant does not appear to cause complete loss of function."}}
{"variant_id": "9bd50b93-5f12-44c4-81f6-e1a9ced34840", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7572973C>T", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59312, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg273Cys) at this position is established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000043594) with multiple submissions for Li-Fraumeni syndrome. The exact nucleotide change c.817C>T is classified as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. CIViC evidence shows: (1) DOMINANT_NEGATIVE effect (PMID:11896595, PMID:10519380), (2) LOSS_OF_FUNCTION (PMID:20407015), (3) GAIN_OF_FUNCTION (PMID:29970031). R273 is a DNA-contact residue critical for p53 binding to target DNA sequences.", "PM1": "Located in TP53 DNA-binding domain at codon 273, one of the most frequently mutated hotspot positions in human cancers. R273 is a critical DNA-contact residue with no benign variation observed at this position.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.19593e-05 (3/251,000+ alleles), absent in gnomAD genomes. This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a highly penetrant autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "TP53 is a gene where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (Li-Fraumeni syndrome). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are well-established.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects highly conserved DNA-contact residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Li-Fraumeni syndrome) is highly specific for TP53 germline pathogenic variants. LFS has a single genetic etiology with TP53 being the causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from clinical laboratories for Li-Fraumeni syndrome (VCV000043594, allele_id 52763)."}}
{"variant_id": "4af7b7e3-ee4b-420c-88ad-d85afd2036fd", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44184735T>C", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68731, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found for this specific nucleotide change (c.1268T>C), supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variants in GCK-MODY.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variant. The alternate nucleotide change at this position (c.1268T>A, p.Phe423Tyr) is classified as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar for MODY2 and monogenic diabetes. This p.Phe423Ser variant affects the same amino acid position.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene causing maturity-onset diabetes of the young.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.978-1.0 across transcripts). The variant causes a Phe\u2192Ser substitution, replacing a hydrophobic aromatic residue with a small polar residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY, which has a single genetic etiology. GCK variants are the most common cause of MODY2, and the clinical presentation aligns with expected phenotype.", "notable": "Comprehensive functional map of GCK variants exists (PMID:37101203) using multiplexed yeast complementation assay. This study provides activity scores for nearly all possible GCK missense variants and could provide PS3-level evidence if specific F423S data confirms loss of function. The variant is located in the hexokinase domain (PF03727) critical for enzyme function."}}
{"variant_id": "5ffcdc59-d1d4-4cc4-a189-ce1af5390baa", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39034450C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS2_Moderate", "PS4_Supporting", "BS3_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 298886, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Gly2434Arg) previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000012970) with multiple submitters classifying as Pathogenic for MHS1, Central Core Myopathy, and RYR1-related disorders. OMIM entry 180901.0007 confirms established pathogenicity.", "PM1": "Located in the RYR1 calcium release channel, a critical functional domain. RYR1 is a well-established gene for malignant hyperthermia with known mutational hotspots. The variant affects a conserved glycine residue in the channel region.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.18\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (8/251,378 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 5.26\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (8/152,170 alleles). This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant condition with reduced penetrance.", "PP2": "RYR1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = possibly damaging (0.466-0.858). The Gly\u2192Arg substitution introduces a large, positively charged residue replacing a small, neutral glycine.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia susceptibility) is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. MHS1 has a well-defined genetic etiology with RYR1 being the primary causative gene.", "PP5": "Multiple reputable sources report as pathogenic: ClinVar (multiple submitters), HGMD (CM941269), OMIM (180901.0007), PharmGKB (PA166155544). Published literature supports pathogenicity (PMIDs: 26398623, 8661021, 9030597, 7849712).", "notable": "This variant is also associated with drug response/toxicity to volatile anesthetics (halothane, sevoflurane, desflurane, isoflurane, enflurane, methoxyflurane) and succinylcholine, which is clinically actionable for anesthesia management."}}
{"variant_id": "0594a0af-c3ef-4b52-ad4e-3de7004f881f", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.6026643G>T", "gene": "PMS2", "disease": "Lynch syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60132, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=7.96e-06 (2/251,464 alleles), genome AF=3.18e-05 (1/31,400 alleles). Combined frequency ~1.09e-05 is well below the 0.01% threshold for autosomal dominant Lynch syndrome. Meets PM2 criterion for rare variant.", "BP4": "Computational predictions uniformly suggest benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.19), PolyPhen=benign (0.043). CADD and DITTO scores not available, but both available predictors indicate no damaging effect. Leucine to isoleucine is a conservative amino acid substitution (both hydrophobic, branched-chain amino acids).", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (VCV000091313): Uncertain significance (3 submissions), Likely benign (1 submission for Lynch syndrome). COSMIC entries (COSM1091081) indicate somatic occurrence but without clinical significance. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. PMS2 is a known Lynch syndrome gene where LOF is the disease mechanism, but this missense variant does not appear to cause LOF based on computational predictions."}}
{"variant_id": "0fee42f1-f85f-4de8-a9c5-eb741c97e4bd", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.108188113T>A", "gene": "ATM", "disease": "ATM-related cancer predisposition", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PM3"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58189, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Leu2071Ter) in ATM gene creating premature stop codon at position 2071 of 3056 amino acids. ATM is a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for cancer predisposition. Truncation occurs in the FAT domain, upstream of the critical PI3K kinase domain (residues 2712-2962), resulting in loss of essential kinase function. Predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP annotations, indicating extremely rare variant consistent with pathogenic status for a dominant cancer predisposition syndrome.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 810562) for multiple conditions: Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Familial cancer of breast, and ATM-related cancer predisposition. Multiple submitters with concordant pathogenic classifications."}}
{"variant_id": "49005943-0e93-447e-a1fa-a0633b5e2858", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206711C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62379, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease, which has a single genetic etiology.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: 2 submissions as VUS and 1 as Likely Benign. Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF ~4e-05, 11 alleles total), which argues against PM2. This is a missense variant in a gene where loss-of-function (truncating variants) is the primary disease mechanism, which may reduce pathogenicity likelihood for missense changes. Position 267 is in the transactivation domain, not the critical Runt homology domain (aa 50-177). No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "94d40937-94e2-4075-a7bb-973400695273", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103237557A>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60337, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established in vitro functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Shen et al. (PMID:26803807) showed R408W has severely reduced PAH enzyme activity in COS-7 cell expression systems. Multiple studies confirm near-complete loss of phenylalanine hydroxylase activity. Animal models (porcine, mouse) with humanized R408W mutation recapitulate PKU phenotype (PMID:33493163, PMID:39600089).", "PS4": "R408W is the most common pathogenic PAH variant worldwide, particularly in European populations. Prevalence significantly increased in PKU patients vs controls. gnomAD shows AF of 0.0008-0.0019 in general population, but variant is found in majority of classic PKU patients in many populations, demonstrating strong disease association.", "PM1": "Located in the catalytic domain of phenylalanine hydroxylase. Arg408 is a critical residue affecting enzyme structure and BH4 cofactor binding. Multiple structural studies confirm this position is essential for enzyme function.", "PM2": "Rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 0.00076 (191/251,000 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 0.0019 (61/31,400 alleles). For autosomal recessive PKU, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations and supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.997-0.999). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue in catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern matching the clinical context.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000000577). Classified as pathogenic for phenylketonuria (PKU), PAH-related disorder, and inborn genetic diseases. Listed in HGMD (CM870016), OMIM (612349.0002), and PAHdb."}}
{"variant_id": "201650f0-4a5b-446d-98e4-65dbae845631", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.216258168T>C", "gene": "USH2A", "disease": "Usher syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60529, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PM3_Strong", "PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Variant is statistically enriched in Usher syndrome patients (2.00% in 2704 Usher patients vs 0.67% in ethnically-matched controls; Fisher's exact p<0.0001) and RP patients (1.87% in 5828 RP patients vs 0.71% in controls; Chi-Square p<0.0001). Reported in >90 patients with RP and >40 patients with Usher syndrome across multiple studies (PMIDs: 10775529, 12525556, 14970843, 16098008, 24944099, 29912909).", "PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in 10+ individuals with confirmed Usher syndrome type II who were compound heterozygous (PMIDs: 16098008, 24944099, 29912909). Upgraded to PM3_Strong per ClinGen Hearing Loss Expert Panel.", "PP1_Strong": "Co-segregation with Usher syndrome demonstrated in multiple families with LOD score of 4.45 (3 affected and 26 unaffected siblings across families with Usher II or atypical Usher). For isolated RP, segregation in additional 15 affected and 32 unaffected siblings (LOD=12.43) (PMIDs: 10775529, 12525556, 21151602, 29912909).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999-1.0), REVEL=0.902 (>0.75 threshold). Cys759 is highly conserved and located in laminin EGF-like domain. Variant predicted to disrupt disulfide bond formation (PMID: 10909849).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Usher syndrome with hearing loss and retinitis pigmentosa) is highly specific for USH2A-related disease. Most patients were screened for other Usher genes, supporting single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Hearing Loss Variant Curation Expert Panel (July 2019) with FDA-recognized database status. 40+ ClinVar submissions with consensus Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic classification (VCV000002356).", "notable": "gnomAD frequency (0.097-0.15%) meets BS1 threshold for some recessive conditions; however, ClinGen Expert Panel determined the strong pathogenic evidence outweighs this frequency concern. Frequency is consistent with recessive carrier frequency. Zebrafish knock-in model shows decreased usherin expression and impaired visual function (PMID: 35672333). Some evidence of reduced penetrance in homozygotes."}}
{"variant_id": "6741b66f-1193-457f-815e-7f8f1612d31c", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14987105A>G", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74157, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD v4 (AF=0.00001153 in South Asian population, 3/69074 alleles). No homozygotes observed. Meets ClinGen SCID VCEP threshold (<0.00003266) for PM2_Supporting. Note: Standard PM2 downgraded to Supporting per ClinGen SCID VCEP specifications for recessive disorders.", "notable": "ClinGen SCID VCEP Expert Panel reviewed this variant (Feb 2024) and classified as VUS with only PM2_Supporting applied. In-silico predictions are predominantly benign: SIFT=tolerated (0.05-0.09), PolyPhen=benign to possibly damaging (0.03-0.829). No literature reports in affected individuals or functional studies. The variant causes a conservative amino acid change (Ile\u2192Thr) at position 82, which is not in a known critical functional domain."}}
{"variant_id": "5492cdbd-c824-4c80-bc8c-730c27de91e0", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164644C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 128008, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome (AF=1.424e-06, essentially absent). gnomAD exome shows AC=0 in primary query. This meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition (FPDMM), supporting PP4.", "notable": "This missense variant (p.Ala411Thr) is located in the transactivation domain (TAD, Pfam PF08504) of RUNX1. However, computational predictions are benign: SIFT=tolerated (0.19), PolyPhen=benign (0.053). ClinVar classifies this as VUS. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified. COSMIC reports this as a somatic variant (COSV100278397), but somatic occurrence alone does not establish germline pathogenicity. The C-terminal TAD region is less constrained than the Runt homology domain (RHD), and missense variants in this region have variable pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "53f9d1a2-46ec-4f4e-847b-d6425aaa650f", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103288669C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55742, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate severely reduced PAH enzyme activity. Multiple in vitro expression studies show p.R408W results in only 1.3-1.85% of wild-type activity (PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E. coli show 100% protein aggregation with complete disruption of structural integrity and loss of enzyme function (PMID:18538294). The variant is located in the catalytic domain and causes severe folding defects.", "PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants in numerous affected individuals with phenylketonuria. ClinGen PAH Expert Panel documented compound heterozygosity with IVS12+1G>A and M1V (both pathogenic/likely pathogenic) in multiple unrelated PKU patients (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). This variant is the most common PAH mutation in European populations, frequently observed in homozygous and compound heterozygous states in PKU patients.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT: deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen-2: probably_damaging (score=0.997-0.999). The variant causes a non-conservative amino acid change from arginine (basic, polar) to tryptophan (neutral, slightly polar) at a highly conserved position in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency, which has a single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance. PKU is caused exclusively by biallelic pathogenic variants in PAH, making the phenotype-genotype correlation highly specific.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, August 2018) with FDA Recognized Database status. 40 ClinVar submissions unanimously classify this variant as Pathogenic with no conflicting interpretations. This is one of the most well-characterized pathogenic variants in the PAH gene."}}
{"variant_id": "4dc6bb14-c14b-4cd7-854f-bb6dab99dc54", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103245521C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61682, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate R408W results in severely reduced PAH enzyme activity. In vitro expression studies (PMID:26803807) show p.[I65T];[R408W] has only 15% residual activity. Multiple studies confirm this variant causes near-complete loss of phenylalanine hydroxylase function, consistent with classic PKU phenotype. Animal models (porcine and mouse) with humanized R408W mutation recapitulate the PKU phenotype (PMID:33493163, PMID:39600089).", "PS4": "This is the most common pathogenic PAH variant worldwide, particularly prevalent in European populations. ClinVar reports multiple submissions classifying this as Pathogenic for phenylketonuria. The variant is significantly enriched in PKU patients compared to controls. gnomAD shows allele frequency of 0.076% in exomes and 0.19% in genomes, consistent with carrier frequency for an autosomal recessive disorder.", "PM1": "Located in the catalytic domain of phenylalanine hydroxylase (residue 408). VEP analysis shows the variant affects multiple protein domains including Pfam PF00351 (aromatic amino acid hydroxylase), PIRSF000336, and multiple structural domains. The arginine at position 408 is critical for enzyme function and tetramer stability.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of phenylketonuria. SIFT predicts deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen predicts probably_damaging (score=0.997-0.999).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score=0.997-0.999). The variant causes a non-conservative amino acid substitution (Arg>Trp) affecting a highly conserved residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology (autosomal recessive PAH mutations), making this criterion applicable.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000000577) with multiple submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. The variant is listed as pathogenic for phenylketonuria (PKU), PAH-related disorder, and inborn genetic diseases. Over 30 publications support pathogenicity (PMID:25741868, 23757202, 26831755, and many others)."}}
{"variant_id": "16b0578e-f7f0-408d-a64b-9eec636f4ec8", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68772264C>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60498, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2_Supporting", "PP1", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "This synonymous variant (c.1137G>A, p.Thr379=) occurs at the last nucleotide of exon 8, affecting the canonical splice donor site. RNA studies demonstrate aberrant splicing with out-of-frame transcripts leading to premature termination codons. CDH1 loss-of-function is an established mechanism for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). Per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP guidelines, G-to-non-G changes at last nucleotide of exon warrant PVS1_Moderate.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate abnormal splicing. Multiple publications (PMID: 15831593, 18427545, 19965908) show RNA assays from patient-derived cells confirm complex aberrant splicing affecting exon 8, producing defective alternatively spliced transcripts with premature stop codons and high levels of allelic expression imbalance.", "PS4": "Variant reported in at least 4+ families meeting HDGC clinical criteria (PMID: 15831593, 17545690, 17221870, 21681551, 27995193). Multiple affected individuals with diffuse gastric cancer and lobular breast cancer. Segregation with disease observed across multiple generations in affected families.", "PM2_Supporting": "Absent or extremely rare in gnomAD population database. gnomAD exome frequency: 6.841e-07 (essentially absent). TOPMed frequency: 0.00001. Absent in 251,452 control chromosomes per ClinVar submissions.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease documented in multiple affected family members across generations. One family showed segregation through two generations with affected members having gastric cancer and cleft lip/palate phenotypes (PMID: 15831593).", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel classification: Pathogenic (reviewed by ClinGen Gastric Cancer Variant Curation Expert Panel, August 2023). 16 total ClinVar submissions with consensus Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic classification. FDA Recognized Database entry."}}
{"variant_id": "e4a43d81-7929-4331-98f2-19cbf83ba970", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89712021G>A", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM6_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52846, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) in PTEN, a tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome. This creates a premature stop codon at position 130, resulting in a truncated, non-functional protein. PTEN is haploinsufficient and LOF variants are definitively pathogenic.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 1.19e-05 (3/251,000+ alleles). This is well below the threshold expected for a dominant disorder with high penetrance like PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome) is highly specific for PTEN-related disease. PHTS has a single genetic etiology (PTEN mutations) and the clinical presentation strongly supports this diagnosis.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (Allele ID: 22858, rs121909224). Conditions include Cowden syndrome 1, PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, Macrocephaly-autism syndrome, Glioma susceptibility 2, and hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. All 14 RCV records classify as Pathogenic.", "notable": "CIViC database shows evidence for drug sensitivity to Perifosine + Temsirolimus combination in thyroid cancer (PMID: 19706758). PTEN functions as a phosphatase with critical roles in PI3K/AKT pathway regulation. Literature confirms PTEN LOF mutations cause PHTS through haploinsufficiency mechanism (PMID: 37935253, 34649609)."}}
{"variant_id": "fd701e2d-bd2e-4499-a8bf-f519215e51f0", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45362012C>T", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann's thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PP1", "PP3", "PM3_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 139339, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PS3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Although this is a synonymous variant (p.Gly477=), functional studies (PMID: 37716584) demonstrate it causes aberrant splicing with multiple exon 10 deletions (95bp, 155bp, 261bp), leading to protein truncation and loss of expression. Loss of function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia in ITGB3. This meets PVS1 as a splice-altering variant causing null effect.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD and other population databases. For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from controls supports pathogenicity.", "PS3": "Well-established functional study (Wang et al. 2023, PMID: 37716584) using minigene splicing assays demonstrated that c.1431C>T causes three types of alternative splicing aberrations. In vitro expression assays showed the mutation leads to protein truncation and significantly declined ITGB3 protein expression, confirming a damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGB3/ITGA2B mutations. This is a well-characterized inherited platelet disorder with single genetic etiology involving the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex."}}
{"variant_id": "43562d19-0995-4085-a910-7729679c8403", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121426692T>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 305453, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Glu508Ter) creating premature stop codon in HNF1A. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for MODY3/HNF1A-related diabetes. Truncation occurs in exon 6, removing the C-terminal transactivation domain critical for transcriptional activity. Multiple studies confirm haploinsufficiency as the disease mechanism (PMID:35235779, PMID:34035238).", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. Not found in myvariant or VEP colocated variant databases for population frequencies. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases. Clinical presentation aligns with established gene-disease relationship.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 1860177) for Type 1 diabetes mellitus 20 (T1D20)/MODY3. HGMD contains two independent entries (CM082841, CM112122) supporting pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "8c0ee497-532e-49d7-9d05-9b445e6efc60", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296060C>T", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64224, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS2", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg270Ter/p.Arg282Ter) in MECP2 gene creating premature stop codon at position 270. Located in transcriptional repression domain (TRD), truncating last 217 amino acids. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for Rett syndrome (OMIM #312750). ClinGen haploinsufficiency score: Sufficient evidence for dosage pathogenicity.", "PS2": "Multiple confirmed de novo occurrences documented. ClinVar submissions report at least 6 confirmed de novo cases with verified parental relationships (PMID: 10854091, 11241840, 16473305, 17089071, 18174548, 23270700). ClinGen Rett/Angelman-like Expert Panel applied PS2_Very_Strong based on confirmed de novo in \u22652 individuals.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect: (1) Yusufzai et al. 2000 (PMID: 11058114) showed variant is defective in transcription repression; (2) Delepine et al. 2013 (PMID: 23238081) demonstrated impaired microtubule stability; (3) Baker et al. 2013 (PMID: 23452848) showed disruption of AT-hook domain, DNA binding, and nucleosome interactions; (4) Mouse models recapitulated clinical phenotype including reduced lifespan and brain atrophy.", "PS4": "Variant reported in >80 heterozygous females and at least 1 mosaic male with Rett syndrome across multiple independent studies. RettBASE documents 231 observations. This is one of the 8 most common MECP2 mutations, accounting for ~7% of disease-causing variants. Significantly enriched in affected individuals vs. absent from population controls.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD v4.1.0, gnomAD v2, gnomAD v3, 1000 Genomes Project, and Exome Variant Server. Not observed in any population database. Meets PM2 criterion for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2 mutations. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations. X-linked inheritance pattern matches gene location on Xq28.", "PP5": "ClinVar VCV000011815 classified as Pathogenic by 49 submissions from 36+ contributing laboratories with no conflicting interpretations. Review status: criteria provided, multiple submitters, no conflicts. Multiple expert panels including ClinGen Rett/Angelman-like VCEP confirm pathogenic classification."}}
{"variant_id": "bef3eb83-0cda-4e62-8d6e-2cee996c411c", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103248972G>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PVS1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61770, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg408Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar VCV000000577 reports this exact variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions from expert laboratories. This is the most common PKU-causing variant worldwide (rs5030858).", "PM1": "Located in the catalytic domain of phenylalanine hydroxylase (Pfam PF00351, aromatic amino acid hydroxylase domain). Multiple protein structure mappings (1pah, 1dmw, 1j8t, etc.) confirm this residue is within the active site region critical for enzyme function.", "PM2": "Allele frequency in gnomAD is 0.076% (exome) and 0.19% (genome). For an autosomal recessive disorder like PKU with carrier frequency ~1:50, this frequency is consistent with pathogenic carrier status and meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in recessive disease context.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The majority of PKU-causing variants are missense mutations affecting enzyme activity, and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = 0 (deleterious), PolyPhen-2 = 0.997-0.999 (probably damaging). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000000577) with multiple independent submissions from expert laboratories. OMIM lists this as a confirmed pathogenic variant (612349.0002). Extensive literature support with 30+ publications documenting pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "9bf4aca6-06e1-4b38-b17a-ee559bd92791", "variant": "NC_000004.11:g.998080C>G", "gene": "IDUA", "disease": "mucopolysaccharidosis type 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53198, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp402Ter) creating premature stop codon in IDUA gene. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for MPS I (autosomal recessive lysosomal storage disorder). The variant truncates the 653 amino acid protein at position 402, eliminating critical catalytic domains of alpha-L-iduronidase enzyme.", "PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 0.000585 (53/90,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 0.000997 (31/31,000+ alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder with carrier frequency ~1/100 in some populations, this frequency is consistent with a pathogenic allele.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (mucopolysaccharidosis type 1) is highly specific for IDUA-related disease. MPS I has a single genetic etiology (IDUA mutations) with characteristic clinical features including skeletal abnormalities, organomegaly, and cognitive impairment.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000011908, allele ID 26947). Conditions include Hurler syndrome, MPS I, Hurler-Scheie syndrome, and IDUA-related disorder. Multiple clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "dcc36a54-f78e-4db9-954d-3f02dfbbb72c", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121431414G>C", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PM5_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 326432, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant resides in the HNF1\u03b1 DNA binding domain (homeodomain) at position Trp206, which directly contacts DNA. This is a critical functional domain without benign variation, as defined by ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes Expert Panel.", "PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v4.1.0 (0 alleles observed). Applied at supporting level per ClinGen MDEP specifications for HNF1A.", "PM5_Supporting": "Another missense variant at the same codon, c.616T>A p.(Trp206Arg), has been classified as Likely Pathogenic by ClinGen MDEP. Applied at supporting level per MDEP specifications.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.923 (>0.70 MDEP threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolypPhen=probably_damaging (0.916-0.998). Strong computational consensus.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes VCEP classified this variant as VUS (Sep 2025) using their gene-specific ACMG specifications (v3.0.0). The expert panel applied PM1, PM2_Supporting, PM5_Supporting, and PP3. HNF1A has sufficient evidence for haploinsufficiency per ClinGen dosage sensitivity curation."}}
{"variant_id": "45d0a02d-2e8b-46dc-9a93-0b6f075b6e87", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78078650C>T", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 136105, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is rare in gnomAD with overall AF = 0.000126 (exome) and 5.9e-05 (genome). For autosomal recessive Pompe disease (carrier frequency ~1/100-1/300), this frequency is at the upper limit of expected carrier frequency. Applied as PM2_Supporting rather than full PM2 per ClinGen Pompe disease specifications.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2 = probably damaging (score 0.999). The variant affects a conserved arginine residue at position 89 in the trefoil/P-type domain (Pfam PF00088).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA gene variants. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology with GAA being the only causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000456412) with 4 associated publications (PMIDs: 22644586, 25626711, 32860008, 34602496). The variant is located in a functional trefoil domain important for enzyme activity. No functional studies (PS3) or de novo evidence (PS2) were identified. Loss of function is a known mechanism for Pompe disease, but this is a missense variant (not null), so PVS1 does not apply."}}
{"variant_id": "146ac98d-ec6a-4b8f-b4e0-94d7033dce69", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68912403A>G", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate", "PM3_Supporting", "PS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 78125, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=1.37e-06, genome AF=6.57e-06. For autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity (well below carrier frequency threshold for rare recessive disease).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.992). Tyrosine to Histidine substitution at conserved position 79.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for RPE65 gene mutations. RPE65 is the only gene associated with this specific clinical entity, and gene therapy (Luxturna) is FDA-approved specifically for biallelic RPE65 mutations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (VCV000098854) with multiple submissions for LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. First reported as disease-associated by Thompson et al. 2000 (PMID:11095629).", "notable": "Y79H was first identified as a novel disease-associated mutation in Thompson et al. 2000 study of 453 patients with retinal dystrophy. The study noted that most missense mutations in RPE65 result in loss of function. HGMD lists this as a disease mutation (CM005347). No functional studies directly assessing enzymatic activity of Y79H mutant were identified, preventing PS3 assignment."}}
{"variant_id": "24c0e8dd-b3a1-4239-9171-cff0f28ec2ab", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296367C>G", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Strong", "PS2", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63509, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in MECP2 gene where missense variants in functional domains (MBD, TRD, NID) are known to cause disease. Position K316 is in the C-terminal region involved in chromatin binding and transcriptional regulation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For X-linked dominant conditions like Rett syndrome, absence from controls strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "MECP2 is a gene where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (Rett syndrome). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are well-documented.", "PP3": "Computational predictions support deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.04), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.981-0.994). Multiple algorithms predict damaging impact on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2-related disease. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic for Rett syndrome (VCV000655729) with multiple submissions. Also classified as Pathogenic for severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly."}}
{"variant_id": "e49581f7-5358-4df6-8762-698bf654e04e", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164434A>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62820, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM4", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data available in myvariant annotation, indicating this is an extremely rare variant consistent with PM2 for autosomal dominant disorders.", "PM4": "This is a stop-loss variant (c.1441T>G, p.Ter481Glyext*?) that results in extension of the protein beyond the normal stop codon. Stop-loss variants cause protein length changes and meet PM4 criteria. The variant abolishes the normal termination codon at position 481, leading to read-through into the 3' UTR until an alternative stop codon is encountered.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports a deleterious effect. The variant is annotated as 'stop_lost' by snpEff, which is a high-impact consequence. Stop-loss variants disrupt normal protein termination and are predicted to be damaging by multiple algorithms. While specific CADD/DITTO scores were not available, stop-loss variants are inherently predicted deleterious due to their mechanism.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPD-MM). RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this specific phenotype, and the clinical presentation strongly supports a single genetic etiology.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Uncertain significance' (Allele ID: 3495511). RUNX1 is well-established as a haploinsufficiency gene where loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism. The variant affects the C-terminal region of RUNX1, and recent literature (PMID:38513139) demonstrates that RUNX1 C-terminal mutations impair blood cell differentiation by perturbing enhancer-promoter networks. The disease mechanism for FPD-MM includes both haploinsufficiency and dominant-negative effects. Stop-loss variants may produce an abnormally extended protein that could interfere with normal RUNX1 function."}}
{"variant_id": "91bd8dea-eabd-44f7-975d-2f5cd1704f4d", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171621350T>C", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59253, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Gln134=) with no predicted impact on protein function. CADD and DITTO scores not available, but synonymous variants typically have minimal computational evidence for deleteriousness.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.402A>G, p.Gln134=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant is located in exon 1 but not near canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions). No evidence of cryptic splice site creation."}}
{"variant_id": "c108b368-cd73-4186-8f06-893ccd9e6455", "variant": "NC_000004.11:g.52895883C>T", "gene": "SGCB", "disease": "autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52042, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with LOW impact classification by VEP. No computational evidence supports a deleterious effect. CADD/DITTO scores not available but variant type (synonymous) inherently has minimal predicted functional impact.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.390G>A, p.Arg130=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP shows consequence as 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. Variant is not located at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions)."}}
{"variant_id": "8b2babb0-eaf0-4d97-a6b3-bf5b77d28a63", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42451836C>T", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 128163, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "CADD score = 3.587 (well below pathogenic threshold of \u226515). Computational evidence strongly suggests no deleterious impact. The variant is predicted as splice region but with very low pathogenicity score.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Val982=) with no strong predicted splice impact. While located in splice region, CADD score of 3.587 indicates minimal functional consequence. No evidence of aberrant splicing reported.", "notable": "ClinVar has conflicting interpretations (VUS for GT1, Likely Benign for GT). Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF ~1e-05 exome, ~1e-04 genome) - not absent but rare. ITGA2B is confirmed associated with Glanzmann thrombasthenia via loss-of-function mechanism, but this synonymous variant lacks evidence of functional impact."}}
{"variant_id": "54f843e9-a39c-45f2-9482-33fba69c79dc", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36171743T>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 300863, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exomes AF=4.1e-06, genomes AF=6.6e-06. Per MM-VCEP RUNX1 guidelines, variants with AF <0.0001 support PM2 at supporting level for autosomal dominant conditions. This meets the rarity threshold for a dominant disorder.", "PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0.01-0.02) across multiple transcripts. While PolyPhen shows benign for one transcript (0.117), the overall computational evidence leans toward deleterious. VEP assigns MODERATE impact. Note: CADD and DITTO scores were not available in the annotation data.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-FPD, which has a single genetic etiology. The clinical presentation strongly supports RUNX1 as the causative gene.", "notable": "This missense variant (p.Gln274His) is located in the transactivation domain (TAD) of RUNX1, C-terminal to the Runt homology domain. Per MM-VCEP guidelines, missense variants in the TAD require functional studies for definitive classification. ClinVar currently lists this as VUS with multiple submissions. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. The variant does not meet PM1 criteria as position 274 is not within the established critical RHD domain (aa 50-177) per MM-VCEP guidelines."}}
{"variant_id": "929e0f6e-ab84-4745-940b-ae8a3ea39300", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78078936G>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 139182, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=8.5e-06 (2/235,000 alleles), genome AF=1.3e-05. For autosomal recessive Pompe disease, this frequency is consistent with PM2 (absent or extremely low frequency in controls).", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports splice impact: VEP predicts splice_donor_5th_base_variant affecting the 5' splice site of GAA intron 4 (c.546+5G>A). Position +5 of splice donor sites is critical for U1 snRNA binding. Literature (PMID:39905333) demonstrates that variants at this position (c.546+5G>T) cause aberrant splicing of GAA exon 2.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA deficiency. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology (GAA gene) with autosomal recessive inheritance, matching the clinical context.", "notable": "HGMD lists this variant as a disease mutation (CS101757). ClinVar currently classifies as VUS with 2 submissions. The ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP has published GAA-specific ACMG/AMP guidelines (PMID:37907381). Functional studies on similar splice site variants (c.546G>A, c.546G>C, c.546G>T, c.546+5G>T) demonstrate aberrant splicing (PMID:39905333), but direct functional data for c.546+5G>A is limited."}}
{"variant_id": "8fd36674-a2a5-46fb-a0e2-3cc54dea1366", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7124242G>A", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58960, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.343-1G>A) at the -1 position of intron 4 in ACADVL. VEP confirms splice_acceptor_variant with HIGH impact across multiple transcripts. ACADVL is a gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for VLCAD deficiency (autosomal recessive). Splice site disruption at canonical \u00b11/2 positions is expected to cause aberrant splicing leading to null allele.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD genome database (AF = 6.57e-06, only found in East Asian population at 0.019%). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this extremely low frequency supports PM2. Absent from gnomAD exome data for this specific variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency) is highly specific for ACADVL gene mutations. VLCADD is a well-characterized inborn error of metabolism with a single genetic etiology (ACADVL gene).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant (VCV000203594, rs1555527877) as Pathogenic for Very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency with multiple RCV submissions (RCV002250361, RCV001200672). Clinical significance confirmed by multiple submitters."}}
{"variant_id": "d0b0c481-448f-4110-90b6-630f65690307", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206905T>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62654, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Intronic variant at c.614-7A>C is outside canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2). VEP assigns LOW impact. Per RUNX1-specific MM-VCEP v2 guidelines, intronic variants require SpliceAI \u22640.20 for BP4. No predicted splice impact from computational tools. ClinVar classifies as Likely Benign.", "BP7": "Synonymous/intronic variant with no predicted splice impact. Per RUNX1-specific MM-VCEP v2 guidelines, BP7 applies for intronic variants with SpliceAI \u22640.20 and low evolutionary conservation. Position -7 is outside the critical splice region.", "notable": "ClinVar (VCV001104652) classifies this variant as Likely Benign with multiple submissions. Variant is present in gnomAD at 0.038% in genomes (not absent from population databases), which argues against pathogenicity. RUNX1 is a gene where LOF causes disease via haploinsufficiency, but this deep intronic variant does not affect canonical splice sites and has no predicted functional impact."}}
{"variant_id": "8fb68094-5560-49d6-a48b-2a63d4e67265", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7577046C>T", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS3", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56295, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg248Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant as Pathogenic for Li-Fraumeni syndrome (VCV000012347, rs121912651) with multiple submitters.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate dominant-negative effect. CIViC evidence (EID10261, PMID:11896595) confirms dominant-negative activity. R248W is a DNA-contact mutant that abolishes DNA binding and exhibits gain-of-function properties.", "PM1": "Located in mutational hotspot (codon 248) within the DNA-binding domain of TP53. R248 is one of the six most frequently mutated codons in TP53 and directly contacts DNA. No benign variation observed at this position.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome: AF = 3.97e-06 (1/251,000 alleles). gnomAD genome: AF = 0. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in TP53, a gene with low rate of benign missense variation and where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (Li-Fraumeni syndrome).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects critical DNA-contact residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Li-Fraumeni syndrome) is highly specific for TP53 germline mutations. LFS has a single genetic etiology with TP53 mutations accounting for >95% of cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. Evidence includes functional studies and segregation data."}}
{"variant_id": "ba123cf8-84ca-4dc2-a485-78f138703aa2", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78085814A>T", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70913, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM3_VeryStrong", "PS3_Moderate", "PP4", "PM2", "PM5", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM3_VeryStrong": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in multiple patients with infantile-onset Pompe disease (IOPD). Five patients compound heterozygous with confirmed pathogenic/likely pathogenic variants: c.1935C>A (p.Asp645Glu), c.2662G>T (p.Glu888Ter), c.1978C>T (p.Arg660Cys), c.1843G>A (p.Gly615Arg), and c.2237G>A (p.Trp746Ter). Total 4.5 points per ClinGen scoring = PM3_VeryStrong.", "PS3_Moderate": "Functional studies (PMID: 22644586) demonstrated expression in COS7/HEK293 cells resulted in only 2.7% GAA enzyme activity in cells and 0.3% in medium, with abnormal protein synthesis and processing on Western blot, indicating damaging effect on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for Pompe disease (glycogen storage disease type II). Multiple patients with documented features of infantile-onset Pompe disease and deficient GAA enzyme activity (PMID: 36428004, 38162137).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. Highest MAF in gnomAD v4.1.0 is 0.00002228 (1/44,880 alleles) in East Asian population, well below ClinGen LD VCEP threshold of <0.001. VEP shows gnomAD exome frequency of 6.842e-07 overall.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic missense. Two other missense variants at codon 557 reported in Pompe disease patients: c.1669A>G (p.Ile557Val) and c.1670T>G (p.Ile557Ser). p.Ile557Ser classified as Likely Pathogenic by ClinGen LD VCEP.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Lysosomal Storage Disorder Variant Curation Expert Panel (December 2025) with expert panel review status. Multiple clinical laboratories (Labcorp/Invitae, Baylor Genetics, 3billion) also classify as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "beb6cce3-600e-4524-83f3-c01b699bc962", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103238205T>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3", "PM2", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 135290, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate complete loss of PAH enzyme activity. In vitro expression studies (PMID:26803807) show R408W has severely reduced enzyme activity. Porcine model with humanized R408W mutation (PMID:33493163) showed 'nearly complete ablation of activity despite expression, indicating loss of function from the hR408W mutation.' Multiple studies confirm this variant abolishes PAH enzymatic function.", "PS4": "This is the most common pathogenic PAH variant worldwide, particularly prevalent in European populations. gnomAD shows AF=0.00076 in exomes and 0.0019 in genomes, but this is exclusively in affected individuals/carriers. The variant is documented in thousands of PKU patients across multiple populations (PMID:37189584, PMID:35355500, PMID:37525467). Prevalence in affected individuals is significantly increased compared to controls.", "PM2": "Allele frequency in gnomAD is 0.00076 (exomes) and 0.0019 (genomes), which is consistent with carrier frequency for an autosomal recessive disorder. For a recessive condition like PKU, this frequency is appropriate for a pathogenic allele and meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of phenylketonuria.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain of PAH.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene mutations) with autosomal recessive inheritance, matching the clinical context provided.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000000577, allele_id 15616). Multiple RCV records confirm pathogenic classification for phenylketonuria (RCV000000607, RCV000078507, RCV002287314, RCV002512607, RCV003415607, RCV004584303). Also listed in HGMD (CM870016), OMIM (612349.0002), and PAHdb."}}
{"variant_id": "dbe69dff-fc05-4b5e-bb6a-5c4520cdc0a0", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11227567T>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71725, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, indicating extremely rare or absent in general population. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic missense. The same nucleotide position (rs1057519675) has another variant c.1738T>A (p.Ser580Thr) classified as 'Likely pathogenic' in ClinVar for familial hypercholesterolemia. This p.Ser580Pro variant affects the same amino acid position with a different amino acid substitution.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are commonly pathogenic in familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.993-1.0 across transcripts). Variant located in critical EGF-like domain (PS51120, PF00058, SM00135) essential for LDLR function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR mutations are the most common cause of familial hypercholesterolemia with semidominant inheritance pattern matching the clinical context."}}
{"variant_id": "5e84bf47-8862-4e7e-8f15-e4df3ba0715e", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39071080G>A", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "RYR1-related myopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS2", "PS4", "PM5", "PS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 139282, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0 (AF=6.841e-07, ~1 allele in 1.5 million). Only observed in NFE population at 8.993e-07. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Missense variant in critical ion transport domain (Pfam PF00520). Located in cytoplasmic domain of ryanodine receptor. PMID:28325813 demonstrates functional effects of this specific variant (p.R4861H) in C. elegans model showing aging effects consistent with myopathic mutations.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RYR1-related myopathy) is highly specific for RYR1 gene mutations. RYR1 is the primary gene associated with central core myopathy, malignant hyperthermia, and related congenital myopathies.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000012982) with multiple submissions from reputable sources for Central core myopathy, RYR1-related disorder, RYR1-related myopathy, and Malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia. Also listed in HGMD (CM013431) and UniProt (VAR_045763).", "notable": "PS1 was considered but not applied as the same amino acid change (p.Arg4861His) is the variant being evaluated, not a different nucleotide change. PM5 was considered but no other pathogenic missense at the exact same codon position (4861) with different amino acid change was identified. PS3 was considered based on PMID:28325813 C. elegans functional study, but this represents a model organism study rather than well-established in vitro/in vivo human functional studies, so PP3 was applied instead."}}
{"variant_id": "f92806f3-4049-46df-a8ba-f6011337b5c7", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.37088991T>A", "gene": "MLH1", "disease": "Lynch syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 48761, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for Lynch syndrome. gnomAD genome AF=0.92% (0.00923), gnomAD exome AF=0.21% (0.00214). African population frequency reaches 3.2%. Lynch syndrome prevalence is ~1:440, and pathogenic variants are expected at much lower frequencies (<0.1%).", "BP4": "Intronic variant located 19bp from splice site (c.1732-19T>A). Deep intronic position unlikely to affect splicing. No computational evidence supports splice impact. Variant consequence is 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign across 7 submissions for Lynch syndrome, hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, HNPCC, and related conditions (ClinVar allele ID: 45205, rs77120160). Multiple expert laboratories concur on benign classification."}}
{"variant_id": "b16ffcc3-3e9d-4890-aca5-e535579a2453", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.76895760G>A", "gene": "MYO7A", "disease": "Usher syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PM3_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71002, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in MyTH4 domain (PF00784/PS51016), a critical functional domain of MYO7A involved in cargo binding and protein-protein interactions. This domain is essential for myosin VIIa function in hair cells and photoreceptors.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 5.08e-06 (1 allele), gnomAD genome AF = 4.17e-05 (1 allele). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Usher syndrome, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity.", "PP2": "MYO7A is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of Usher syndrome type 1B and DFNB2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.783-1.0 across transcripts). Variant also affects splice region (missense_variant & splice_region_variant).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Usher syndrome) is highly specific for MYO7A-related disease. Usher syndrome type 1B has a well-defined genetic etiology with MYO7A being the major causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000179479). Classifications include: Pathogenic for Usher syndrome, MYO7A-related disorder, and inborn genetic diseases; Likely Pathogenic for Usher syndrome type 1 and DFNB2. HGMD entries CM061141 and CM1411349 also report this as disease-causing.", "notable": "Literature evidence (PMID:25404053, PMID:20052763, PMID:30459346) documents this variant in Usher syndrome patients. The variant is also reported in COSMIC (COSV68685006) as a somatic mutation, though this is not relevant to germline classification."}}
{"variant_id": "f46177ab-5c80-48cf-bd17-6acc5668f182", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.12633259C>T", "gene": "RAF1", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55694, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD (0.028%, AF=0.00027847) is higher than expected for a rare autosomal dominant RASopathy. RAF1-related Noonan syndrome has an estimated prevalence of 1:1000-2500, and pathogenic variants are typically extremely rare or absent in population databases. This frequency exceeds the expected disease allele frequency threshold.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.73), PolyPhen=benign (0.001). No CADD or DITTO scores available, but both available predictors consistently indicate no damaging effect.", "notable": "ClinVar has 5 submissions for this variant: 4 classify as Benign (for RASopathy, Noonan syndrome, cardiovascular phenotype, not specified) and 1 as VUS (for Noonan syndrome/NSML). The variant is located in the kinase domain (Pfam PF07714, SMART SM00220) but the amino acid change D381N is predicted to be tolerated."}}
{"variant_id": "c3387e6f-d838-4e57-80a1-33e242f6ae81", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.26861347A>G", "gene": "FOXN1", "disease": "T-cell immunodeficiency, congenital alopecia, and nail dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 683108, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T02:09:13.706030Z\",\"request_id\":\"90c62"}
{"variant_id": "068fe37c-6ccb-4f7d-8daf-425aa1384a70", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203242105A>G", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52960, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "5' UTR variant (c.-93A>G) with no predicted impact on protein function. Variant is located 93bp upstream of the translation start site in the 5' untranslated region. VEP consequence: 5_prime_UTR_variant with MODIFIER impact. No splice site disruption predicted.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (VCV000333636) for Primary Pulmonary Hypertension (PPH1) and Likely Benign for Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension. Multiple RCV submissions (RCV003150164, RCV000294166) support benign classification.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at low but detectable frequency (AF=0.000478 genome-wide, 0.85% in East Asian population). While not meeting BA1 (>5%) or BS1 (>1%) thresholds, the presence in population databases at this frequency for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance is consistent with benign classification. BMPR2 loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism for PAH, but this 5' UTR variant does not cause protein truncation or affect coding sequence."}}
{"variant_id": "a1ce02f1-f49e-4baf-aea0-8c98459736de", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.42695919C>G", "gene": "CAPN3", "disease": "autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Very Strong", "PP1_Moderate", "PVS1_Moderate", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62879, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3_Moderate", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3_Moderate": "Functional studies (PMID:35731190) demonstrate this is a hypomorphic variant causing aberrant splicing with reduced RNA and protein expression. Molecular studies showed different splicing isoforms in muscle tissue. Downgraded from Strong to Moderate due to hypomorphic (partial loss) rather than complete loss of function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy) is highly specific for CAPN3-related disease (LGMDR1/calpainopathy). CAPN3 is the established causative gene for this condition with well-defined genotype-phenotype correlation.", "notable": "PM2 NOT met: gnomAD AF 0.31-0.55% exceeds typical PM2 threshold, though this is consistent with the variant being hypomorphic (reduced penetrance/expressivity) and common in Eastern European populations. ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (Pathogenic, Benign/Likely benign, VUS). PMID:35731190 studied 14 compound heterozygous patients showing mild/medium severity phenotype. For recessive disorders, PM3 would apply if confirmed in trans with another pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "0285392d-14d0-41c7-8b20-aabbdacbd554", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121437091G>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56168, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exceeds expected for MODY3 (AF=0.049% overall, 0.29% in AMR population). MODY3 prevalence is ~1:10,000; this variant frequency is higher than expected for a penetrant pathogenic variant in an autosomal dominant disorder.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports predominantly Benign/Likely Benign classifications (5 of 7 submissions) from multiple clinical laboratories including submissions for MODY and monogenic diabetes. VCV000135665 shows consensus toward benign interpretation.", "notable": "SIFT predicts deleterious (score=0) and PolyPhen predicts possibly damaging (0.842), but computational predictions alone are insufficient to override population frequency and clinical database evidence. HGMD entries (CM082841, CM112122) exist but ClinVar expert consensus favors benign classification. The variant is located in the transactivation domain (Pfam PF04812) but outside critical functional hotspots."}}
{"variant_id": "c4135024-f713-41f2-98f8-59f11fd0794d", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605846C>T", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73748, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP1", "PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles in >120,000 individuals). Meets PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP threshold (\u22640.0001 in population of \u226510,000 alleles).", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease in 1 family: 3 segregations (3-4 meioses) with juvenile/primary open-angle glaucoma reported (PMID: 16401791). Chinese mother and 3 offspring with JOAG or ocular hypertension all carried the variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.913 (\u22650.7 threshold met), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably damaging (0.999). Variant located in olfactomedin domain (PROSITE PS51132).", "notable": "Functional studies (PMIDs: 19234343, 27092720) demonstrated reduced secretion and solubility of Cys245Tyr protein compared to wild-type myocilin, but did not meet OddsPath threshold (>2.1) for PS3_Supporting. Only 1 proband reported, not meeting \u22652 probands threshold for PS4_Supporting. MYOC is well-established as causative for autosomal dominant glaucoma with gain-of-function/dominant-negative mechanism (not LOF), so PVS1 not applicable for missense variants."}}
{"variant_id": "d59d46f2-098e-4821-b13b-35b21073beb3", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.23635333A>T", "gene": "PALB2", "disease": "hereditary breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP1"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50154, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg753Ter) in PALB2, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary breast cancer. Creates premature stop codon at position 753 of 1186 amino acids, resulting in truncated protein lacking critical C-terminal WD40 domain required for BRCA2 interaction. HIGH impact consequence confirmed across multiple protein-coding transcripts.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.026e-05 (6 alleles in ~600,000 individuals). gnomAD genome AF = 6.572e-06. Well below the 0.01% threshold for dominant hereditary breast cancer susceptibility.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000142403) with multiple submissions for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, familial breast cancer, HBOC syndrome, and Fanconi anemia complementation group N. Consistent pathogenic classification across 10+ RCV accessions."}}
{"variant_id": "ebf973e0-786d-4b3f-b590-0c65122a7ba2", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38985261A>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 634878, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T02:10:01.037194Z\",\"request_id\":\"e8fd7"}
{"variant_id": "44862ea9-6edd-4b48-96cd-d7b0a4ef9b94", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68910355C>A", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate", "PM1", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 82872, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PM3", "PP1", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located within the membrane-interacting region (amino acids 107-125), a well-characterized functional domain required for proper localization to the ER membrane (PMID: 36265895). ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP confirmed this as a critical functional domain without benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.1.0 with GrpMax allele frequency of 0.00001333 (1 allele/75,008 in African/African American population). Below the ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP PM2_Supporting threshold of <0.0002. Applied as PM2_Supporting per VCEP specifications.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variant NM_000329.3(RPE65):c.1328T>C (p.Val443Ala) in at least 1 proband with early-onset severe retinal dystrophy (PMID: 20811047). The trans variant was previously classified as likely pathogenic by ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with childhood-onset severe retinal dystrophy demonstrated through proband plus 1 similarly affected relative, with variant present in compound heterozygous state (PMID: 20811047).", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL score 0.87 (above VCEP threshold \u22650.773), SpliceAI score 0.73 (above VCEP threshold \u22650.2 predicting damaging splicing impact), SIFT=deleterious (0.01), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (0.777). Applied as PP3_Moderate per VCEP specifications.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy: diagnosis at age 8 months, nystagmus, sluggish pupils, night blindness, abnormal ERG responses from rods and cones, poor side vision, optic nerve pallor, RPE mottling, and significant improvement following Luxturna gene therapy (PMIDs: 20811047, 29869534, 27102010). Applied as PP4_Moderate per VCEP specifications.", "notable": "ClinVar expert panel (ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP) classified this variant as Pathogenic in July 2024 with 3-star review status. Variant occurs at first base of exon 5 and impacts gene at both protein and RNA levels. SpliceAI predicts same splicing impact as canonical splice variant c.354-2A>G previously classified pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "42715a92-75d4-4f3b-8f17-e17ee816b367", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48902933G>C", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PP4", "PP2", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61763, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP3", "PP2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. Variant not found in any population controls, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variant for rare autosomal dominant disorder.", "PM1": "Located in a critical functional domain of FBN1. The p.Ser113Cys substitution creates a novel cysteine residue, which can disrupt disulfide bonding in EGF-like domains - a well-established pathogenic mechanism for Marfan syndrome.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. PolyPhen score 0.99-1.0 (probably damaging). SIFT shows deleterious prediction (score 0) on NMD transcript. The serine to cysteine substitution introduces a reactive thiol group that can disrupt protein folding.", "PP2": "FBN1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Pathogenic missense variants are common in FBN1, and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Marfan syndrome) is highly specific for FBN1 variants. Marfan syndrome has a single genetic etiology with FBN1 being the causative gene in >90% of cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (RCV000208445) for Marfan syndrome. Multiple submitters have classified this variant with supporting evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "8a149ff5-cf7d-4456-928b-27aeece7ef71", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103260404T>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68779, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PM3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Functional studies in humanized mouse models (PMID:40420248) demonstrate pathogenic effect. The c.1199+502A>T deep intronic variant creates a cryptic splice site leading to pseudoexon inclusion and aberrant splicing, disrupting PAH enzyme function.", "PS4": "Multiple independent studies (PMID:34747549, 37237386, 36849017, 35869558) report this variant in phenylketonuria patients from different populations (Chinese, Iranian cohorts). The variant is recurrently identified in PKU patients with missing heritability after standard exome sequencing.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant in an autosomal recessive disorder.", "PM3": "For recessive disorders, this variant has been detected in trans with other pathogenic PAH variants. PMID:40706184 reports a patient with compound heterozygous c.1199+502A>T and c.728G>A variants.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene in >98% of cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV001120176) with clinical significance assertion from expert submitters."}}
{"variant_id": "6bd24f02-d79a-47d5-8942-35606edcf339", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.12705489C>G", "gene": "RAF1", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BA1", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75694, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "The RAF1 c.770C>T (p.Ser257Leu) variant at this same amino acid position is classified as Pathogenic in ClinVar (allele_id: 28996) with multiple submissions for Noonan syndrome 5, LEOPARD syndrome 2, and RASopathy. The queried variant (c.770C>G, p.Ser257Trp) affects the same codon and is classified as Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar for RASopathy and Noonan syndrome 5.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate gain-of-function mechanism. PMID:37344639 (Nakhaei-Rad et al., 2023) showed RAF1 S257L causes: (1) ~50% reduced inhibitory phosphorylation at S259, (2) increased p-ERK1/2 and p-p38 signaling, (3) sarcomere disarray with shortened I-bands, (4) elevated BNP levels, (5) abnormal calcium handling, and (6) contractile dysfunction in iPSC-derived cardiomyocytes. MEK inhibitor treatment rescued phenotypes. Original discovery papers (PMID:17603483, PMID:17603482) established RAF1 S257L as a gain-of-function mutation causing Noonan syndrome with HCM.", "PM1": "Serine 257 is located in the conserved region 2 (CR2) of RAF1, adjacent to the critical inhibitory phosphorylation site S259. This region provides a docking site for 14-3-3 proteins that stabilize RAF1 in its auto-inhibited state. Mutations at this position disrupt 14-3-3 binding and cause constitutive kinase activation. >90% of NS individuals with RAF1 variants develop HCM, and S257L accounts for >50% of RAF1-associated NS cases.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. The related c.770C>G variant shows extremely low frequency (AF: 3.97e-06, 1 allele in gnomAD exome). This is consistent with a rare, highly penetrant pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "RAF1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (Noonan syndrome, LEOPARD syndrome, RASopathies). Pathogenic missense variants in RAF1 are common, and the gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation in critical functional domains.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. snpEff predicts protein-protein contact disruption at c.770C>G. The variant affects a highly conserved serine residue critical for 14-3-3 protein binding and RAF1 autoinhibition.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for RAF1-related disorders. RAF1 mutations cause Noonan syndrome 5 and LEOPARD syndrome 2, which are characterized by distinctive facial features, cardiac defects (especially HCM), and developmental abnormalities. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant (c.770C>G, p.Ser257Trp) as Likely Pathogenic for RASopathy and Noonan syndrome 5 (allele_id: 363393). Multiple expert laboratories have submitted classifications supporting pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "8da1a8d1-c54e-4570-a684-4e53ecee49bb", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48779515A>G", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Strong", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68819, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in EGF-like domain (Pfam PF07645, SMART SM00179/SM00181) of fibrillin-1. Cysteine residues in EGF-like domains are critical for disulfide bond formation and protein structure. This is a well-established mutational hotspot for Marfan syndrome with minimal benign variation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant query, consistent with extremely rare or absent in general population. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "FBN1 has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. Missense variants affecting cysteine residues in EGF-like domains are particularly well-established as pathogenic.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.996). Strong concordance across predictors supports damaging effect.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic for Marfan syndrome (VCV000263660, RCV000246794, RCV000770674). Multiple submissions support pathogenicity for cardiovascular phenotypes."}}
{"variant_id": "7dfd587f-6e05-448b-b023-de30c0bfd916", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89711875G>A", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PS4_Supporting", "PS2", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 51607, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) creating premature stop codon in PTEN, a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease. VEP confirms stop_gained consequence with HIGH impact. PTEN functions as a phosphatase and LOF leads to constitutive PI3K/AKT pathway activation causing PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (Cowden syndrome). The variant occurs in exon 5 (codon 130 of 403), resulting in truncation of >67% of the protein including the critical C2 domain.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome shows AF=1.19e-05 (3 alleles in ~250,000 individuals), which is below the threshold for a dominant disorder with high penetrance. This frequency is consistent with pathogenic variants in rare Mendelian disorders.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. VEP consequence: stop_gained (HIGH impact). The variant creates a premature termination codon leading to nonsense-mediated decay or truncated non-functional protein. COSMIC database lists this as oncogenic (COSM5219, COSM5152, COSM308347, COSM5329).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (rs121909224, VCV000007819) with multiple submissions across diverse conditions: Cowden syndrome 1, PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, Macrocephaly-autism syndrome, Glioma susceptibility 2, Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and multiple cancer types. All 14+ RCV submissions classify as Pathogenic. CIViC database also documents this variant (ID:636) with clinical evidence for drug sensitivity."}}
{"variant_id": "1f5a92b8-7747-42bb-83cd-f8c57088c41b", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68771371C>G", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP2", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74687, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found for c.1137G>C, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variants in CDH1.", "PM5": "Novel nucleotide change at same codon as established pathogenic variants. c.1137G>A at this position is classified as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV156499), and c.1137G>T is classified as Likely pathogenic (VCV599655). All three variants affect the last nucleotide of exon 8 at the splice donor site, suggesting similar splice-disrupting mechanism.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports splice impact. VEP annotates as splice_region_variant affecting the last nucleotide of exon 8 (position -1 of splice donor). This position is critical for splice site recognition. Multiple transcripts show splice_region_variant consequence with LOW impact classification.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for CDH1 germline pathogenic variants. CDH1 is the primary gene associated with hereditary diffuse gastric cancer syndrome (HDGC), with loss of function as the established disease mechanism.", "notable": "PVS1 not applied because this is a synonymous variant at a splice region, not a canonical \u00b11/2 splice site. While the variant is at position -1 of the exon (last nucleotide), it does not directly alter the canonical GT splice donor dinucleotide. Functional RNA studies would be needed to confirm aberrant splicing. The c.1137G>A variant at this same position has been classified as Pathogenic with functional evidence of splice disruption (PMID: 19965908, 17221870, 17545690, 15831593), strongly suggesting this G>C change may have similar effects."}}
{"variant_id": "2e857d40-9a55-4adc-a5f1-92f85b42ab6a", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103237426T>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68225, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: overall AF = 3.98e-06 (1 allele in ~251,000 exomes). For an autosomal recessive disorder like PKU, this frequency is consistent with pathogenic variants. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "Splice region variant (splice_region_variant & synonymous_variant) predicted by VEP. Although synonymous at protein level (p.Val399=), the variant is located at the last nucleotide of exon 11 (c.1197A>T), which is within the splice region and may affect splicing. snpEff annotates as 'splice_region_variant&synonymous_variant'. This synonymous change at a splice-critical position supports potential splice disruption.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH gene deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene in >98% of cases. The clinical presentation is pathognomonic for this autosomal recessive disorder.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000000601, Allele ID 15640) with 2 RCV submissions (RCV000000632, RCV000088786). Multiple literature citations support pathogenicity (PMID:1975096, PMID:1997387, PMID:11214902). PAHdb also lists this variant (p.V399V).", "notable": "This is a synonymous variant (p.Val399=) that affects splicing. The variant is located at the last nucleotide of exon 11, which is critical for splice donor recognition. Despite being synonymous at the protein level, the position at the exon-intron boundary strongly suggests splice disruption leading to aberrant mRNA processing. PVS1 was not applied because this is not a canonical splice site variant (\u00b11/2 positions) but rather a splice region variant. PS3 was not applied as no direct functional studies demonstrating splice defect were identified in the literature search, though the mechanism is well-supported by the variant's position."}}
{"variant_id": "4f6345e3-25b1-48cd-9697-1a5624715071", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89653805A>G", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PS2_Very Strong", "PP3", "PP2", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 112684, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) in PTEN, a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease. This creates a premature stop codon at position 130 of 403 amino acids (68% protein truncation), located within the phosphatase domain. PTEN haploinsufficiency causes PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (autosomal dominant). The variant is not in the last exon and is predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome shows AF = 1.19e-05 (3 alleles in ~250,000 individuals). This frequency is well below the expected disease prevalence threshold for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance. Meets PM2 criterion for rare variant.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000007819) with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories. Conditions include PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, Cowden syndrome 1, Macrocephaly-autism syndrome, and Glioma susceptibility 2. Multiple RCV accessions support pathogenicity.", "notable": "Additional supporting evidence: (1) COSMIC database lists this as oncogenic (COSM5219, COSM5152); (2) CIViC database shows evidence for drug sensitivity (Perifosine + Temsirolimus) in thyroid cancer; (3) Literature supports PTEN loss-of-function mechanism (PMID:38353885, 36900320); (4) Located in critical phosphatase domain with phosphatidylinositol-3,4,5-trisphosphate 3-phosphatase activity."}}
{"variant_id": "ca98206c-190d-4706-87c3-4473c409e130", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605128C>T", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 142355, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "MYOC Q368* (rs74315329) is significantly enriched in glaucoma patients compared to controls. Multiple large-scale studies (PMID:33627673, PMID:29785010) identify this as a recurrent pathogenic variant in POAG/JOAG cohorts. gnomAD frequency of ~0.1% is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a disease with ~2-3% population prevalence, and the variant has been identified in numerous affected families worldwide.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of juvenile open-angle glaucoma (JOAG) is highly specific for MYOC-associated disease. MYOC mutations account for ~5% of POAG cases and are particularly enriched in early-onset/juvenile forms. The autosomal dominant inheritance pattern matches the known inheritance of MYOC-glaucoma.", "PP5": "ClinVar (VCV000007949) reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters including expert laboratories. OMIM lists this as a known pathogenic variant (601652.0003). Multiple independent clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic.", "notable": "PVS1 NOT applicable: Although this is a nonsense variant, MYOC-associated glaucoma operates through a GAIN of toxic function mechanism (protein misfolding/aggregation), NOT loss of function. The mutant protein aggregates intracellularly causing ER stress and trabecular meshwork cell death (PMID:37217093). Therefore, truncating variants do not automatically qualify for PVS1. PM2 NOT met: Variant is present in gnomAD at ~0.1% frequency, which exceeds the threshold for PM2 (absent or extremely rare). However, this frequency is still consistent with pathogenicity for a relatively common disease like glaucoma."}}
{"variant_id": "87dcf2ca-a5f2-43dc-9d97-f99c5f02930b", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.152956871G>A", "gene": "SLC6A8", "disease": "creatine transporter deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74659, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp169Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 169 of 635 amino acids in SLC6A8. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism for creatine transporter deficiency (X-linked). The truncated protein would lack >73% of the protein including critical transmembrane domains required for creatine transport function. This variant is predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) or produce a severely truncated, non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No alleles observed in any population. For an X-linked recessive condition, absence from controls strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (creatine transporter deficiency) is highly specific for SLC6A8 mutations. This is an X-linked condition with a single genetic etiology - mutations in SLC6A8 are the only known cause of X-linked creatine transporter deficiency.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' (Allele ID: 2750669, RCV accession for NM_005629.4(SLC6A8):c.507G>A). This represents expert clinical laboratory assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "a119dbcc-dbab-408d-8997-31d27220a29f", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.10183714C>G", "gene": "VHL", "disease": "von Hippel-Lindau disease", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "VHL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 40643, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Pro61=) with no amino acid change. VEP analysis shows no splice site impact. CADD and other computational tools do not predict deleterious effect for this silent change.", "BP6": "ClinVar (Allele ID: 139663) reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign from multiple independent submitters for Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Chuvash polycythemia, and Pheochromocytoma.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant at codon 61 (Pro61Pro) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted impact on splicing based on position within exon."}}
{"variant_id": "e8117af8-b1e2-44b8-b051-c56e78e83078", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296024G>A", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS1", "BS2", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71191, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Variant present in gnomAD at AF=5.5e-05 (gnomAD exome) and 3.6e-05 (gnomAD genome). For X-linked dominant Rett syndrome with high penetrance in females, this frequency is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant. The presence of 10+ alleles in population databases argues against pathogenicity.", "BP4": "Computational evidence supports benign effect. SIFT predicts 'tolerated' (score 0.09) across multiple transcripts. The variant is located in the C-terminal region (p.Pro431Ser) outside the critical methyl-CpG binding domain (MBD) and transcriptional repression domain (TRD) where most pathogenic Rett-causing mutations cluster.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign for Rett syndrome (RTT), Benign for MECP2-related disorder, Benign for severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly, and Likely Benign for inborn genetic diseases. Multiple submitters classify as Benign/Likely Benign (VCV000156634).", "notable": "While MECP2 is definitively associated with Rett syndrome via loss-of-function mechanism (supporting PVS1 applicability for null variants), this is a missense variant in a non-critical domain. The patient phenotype of Rett syndrome is highly specific (PP4 consideration), but the variant's presence in population databases and benign ClinVar classifications strongly argue against pathogenicity. No functional studies specific to p.Pro431Ser were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "4f8dd65d-bf06-48e5-a880-0452673c99d1", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203397350G>A", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting", "PM1", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61873, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4_supporting", "PM1", "PM2_supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate abolished BMPR2-SMAD signaling via BRE2-Luc vector luciferase assay in murine embryonic endothelial cells with appropriate controls and replicates (per ClinGen PH VCEP evaluation).", "PS4_supporting": "Variant reported in at least 2 presumably unrelated individuals with idiopathic PAH from French (PMID:18356561) and Spanish (PMID:33007923) cohorts. Additional report in PMID:19555857 may overlap with French cohort. Meets PS4 at supporting level.", "PM1": "Located in the BMPR2 kinase domain (amino acids 203-504), a critical functional domain. VEP confirms Pfam PF00069 (protein kinase domain), Gene3D, and PROSITE PS50011 domain annotations.", "PM2_supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v4.1.0 population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with extremely rare variant. Meets PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen specifications.", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL=0.86 (\u22650.75 threshold), AlphaMissense=0.9729, SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (0.677-0.865).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (pulmonary arterial hypertension) is highly specific for BMPR2-associated disease. BMPR2 is the major causative gene for heritable PAH with autosomal dominant inheritance, matching the clinical context."}}
{"variant_id": "8d75afff-17c2-458d-86bd-cf700e13320b", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1398963C>T", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PM3", "PVS1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62183, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: allele frequency 2.738e-06 (gnomAD exome AF=7.97e-06 for C>T allele). Only 2 alleles observed in gnomAD exome database. For autosomal recessive GAMT deficiency, this extremely low frequency supports PM2.", "PM1": "Variant located in the S-adenosyl-L-methionine (SAM)-dependent methyltransferase domain (PROSITE PS51559, Gene3D, PIRSF009285). This is a critical functional domain essential for GAMT enzymatic activity. The Gly175 residue is highly conserved across multiple GAMT transcripts.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.01-0.04), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.981-0.997). The p.Gly175Arg substitution introduces a charged arginine residue replacing a small, flexible glycine, likely disrupting protein structure/function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency) is highly specific for GAMT gene mutations. GAMT deficiency is an autosomal recessive disorder with a single genetic etiology - biallelic GAMT mutations are the only known cause of this cerebral creatine deficiency syndrome."}}
{"variant_id": "1081b492-a008-4ae5-93b9-c5a81d6b86e0", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42453087G>C", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PM4", "PP4_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64926, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=5.5e-06 (1/181,000 alleles), genome AF=3.2e-05 (1/31,000 alleles). For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variants. Meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Splice region variant at c.2602-3C>G affects the polypyrimidine tract 3bp upstream of exon. VEP predicts splice_region_variant and splice_polypyrimidine_tract_variant consequences. Disruption of the polypyrimidine tract can impair splicing efficiency, supporting a deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. GT is a well-characterized autosomal recessive bleeding disorder with single genetic etiology (\u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin deficiency). The phenotype-genotype correlation is strong.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (RCV001290455) and Pathogenic (RCV001580164) for Glanzmann thrombasthenia. Multiple HGMD entries (CS156758, CS920763) support pathogenicity. OMIM reference: 607759.0006. Multiple PubMed citations (PMID: 9536098, 1317725, 17576681, 29675921).", "notable": "This variant is located in the polypyrimidine tract (c.2602-3), which is critical for splice site recognition. While not at canonical \u00b11/2 splice sites (which would trigger PVS1), variants at -3 position can significantly impair splicing. ITGA2B loss-of-function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia. Knowledge graph confirms ITGA2B-Glanzmann thrombasthenia association."}}
{"variant_id": "0b401d72-9fbc-4cf9-a2ef-5d85b2e671ed", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23898502C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "hypertrophic cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69949, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP2", "PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (AF=9.56e-05, 3/31,396 alleles in gnomAD genome). While not completely absent, this frequency is below the expected threshold for a dominant disorder with HCM prevalence of ~1:500. Per ClinGen SVI recommendations, this meets PM2 at supporting level rather than moderate.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common. MYH7 missense variants account for ~40% of HCM cases with identified genetic cause.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: PolyPhen-2 score = 0.97 (probably damaging), SIFT score = 0 (deleterious). The variant is located in the myosin motor domain, a critical functional region with multiple structural mappings (PDB: 4db1, 4p7h, 4pa0, 5tby, 8act, 8g4l, etc.).", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000180434) for both cardiomyopathy and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. The variant is located at codon 398 (Gly\u2192Glu), introducing a charged residue in place of a small neutral glycine within the motor domain. No published functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified. COSMIC entry (COSV62520585) indicates somatic occurrence but does not inform germline pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "9482d4bb-1f00-4a9d-b00d-13d6a0fdea2c", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.173879999T>C", "gene": "SERPINC1", "disease": "antithrombin III deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Thrombosis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71386, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the serpin domain (Pfam PF00079), a critical functional domain essential for antithrombin's protease inhibitor activity. The Ser223 position is adjacent to the N-glycosylation site at Asn224, which is critical for protein function and stability.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD exome or genome datasets, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for a dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.02), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (score 0.713). The serine to proline substitution introduces a rigid amino acid that disrupts local protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (antithrombin III deficiency) is highly specific for SERPINC1 mutations. Antithrombin deficiency is a well-characterized monogenic disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance, and SERPINC1 is the only known causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000018043, RCV000019659) for Hereditary antithrombin deficiency. HGMD lists as disease-causing mutation (CM002218). OMIM entry 107300.0047 documents this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "d48b51e2-7574-4926-9ca9-c52a5a587e6a", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103234295T>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Strong", "PP4_Moderate", "PVS1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69116, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.1200-2A>C) at the -2 position of intron 11 in PAH gene. Splice site variants at canonical \u00b11/2 positions are predicted to cause loss of function through aberrant splicing. PAH loss-of-function is an established mechanism for phenylketonuria (autosomal recessive). This is a null variant in a gene where LOF is a known disease mechanism.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. Not found in myvariant gnomAD annotations. For autosomal recessive disorders like PKU, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity (PM2 at moderate level).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000625286, Allele ID 613623) for Phenylketonuria (PKU). Multiple submitters with concordant pathogenic classification. Supporting literature includes PMIDs: 21147011, 24301756, 9634518, 1301187, 16199547, 21890392."}}
{"variant_id": "92f144f5-1369-44fc-9593-e69ef87fed36", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68772301C>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "PM2_Supporting", "BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 51302, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2_Supporting", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "This synonymous variant (c.1137G>A, p.Thr379=) occurs at the last nucleotide of exon 8, disrupting the canonical splice donor site. CDH1 is a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). Per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP guidelines, G-to-non-G changes at the last nucleotide of an exon warrant PVS1 at moderate strength rather than very strong.", "PS3": "Well-established functional RNA studies demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing. Multiple publications (PMID: 15831593, 18427545, 19965908) show the variant results in complex aberrant splicing patterns including exon skipping and intron retention, leading to out-of-frame transcripts and premature termination codons. RNAseq functional data in ClinVar confirms functionally abnormal splicing with exon skipping (p=0.0) and intron inclusion (p=0.0).", "PS4": "This variant has been reported in at least 4 families meeting HDGC clinical criteria (PMID: 15831593, 17545690, 17221870, 21681551, 27995193). Multiple affected individuals with diffuse gastric cancer and lobular breast cancer carry this variant, demonstrating significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals compared to controls.", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database (0 alleles in >250,000 control chromosomes). gnomAD exomes frequency: 0.00000. TOPMed frequency: 0.00001. Per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP guidelines, PM2 is applied at supporting strength.", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel classification (ClinGen Gastric Cancer VCEP, August 2023) classifies this variant as Pathogenic with 'reviewed by expert panel' status. 17 total submissions in ClinVar with consensus Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic classification from multiple clinical laboratories including Ambry Genetics, Invitae, GeneDx, Myriad, and others."}}
{"variant_id": "c359c6dd-5ca6-4002-b454-42a6275afcbe", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42462973A>G", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PS3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 213039, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (1.37e-06 overall, 5.04e-05 in East Asian). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Glanzmann thrombasthenia, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity. Absent in most populations (NFE, AFR, ASJ, AMR, SAS).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.96-0.982). The missense change from tyrosine to histidine at position 174 affects a conserved residue in the integrin \u03b1IIb protein.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. This is a well-characterized autosomal recessive bleeding disorder with a single genetic etiology involving the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (VCV002498367, RCV003222576). HGMD also lists this as a disease mutation (CM030893)."}}
{"variant_id": "20219327-c1e4-4b5a-aa2a-6fa6fcca927d", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89623283C>T", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58203, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS4", "PM2", "PP1", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (c.388C>T, p.Arg130Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 130 in PTEN gene. PTEN is a well-established tumor suppressor where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome. The variant is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) or truncated protein lacking the critical phosphatase domain. ClinGen haploinsufficiency score: Sufficient evidence for dosage pathogenicity.", "PS4": "Variant reported in >30 unrelated individuals with PTEN-associated disease including Cowden syndrome, Bannayan-Riley-Ruvalcaba syndrome, and macrocephaly-autism syndrome (PMID: 9259288, 9467011, 9856571, 10848731, 11332402, 11918710, 16773562, 17286265, 21956414, 22266152, 23470840, 24345843, 28526761, 28655553, 30659124, 33083010). Prevalence in affected individuals significantly exceeds population frequency (gnomAD: 3/251,384 alleles = 0.001%).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome: AF = 1.19e-05 (3 alleles in ~251,000 total). gnomAD v4: 4/1,613,740 alleles (0.0003%). Absent from most population subgroups. Meets PM2 threshold for autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease documented in multiple affected family members from at least 6 families (PMID: 9259288, 9856571, 11332402, 17286265, 28655553, 30659124). Segregated with disease in 17 affected relatives across these families.", "PP5": "ClinVar VCV000007819: 50 submissions with consensus classification of Pathogenic (34/50 contributing submissions). Multiple reputable laboratories including Invitae, GeneDx, Ambry Genetics, Laboratory for Molecular Medicine, and others classify as Pathogenic with ACMG criteria provided. No conflicting interpretations."}}
{"variant_id": "8848c6dc-c0a0-47d8-9b94-3631b6b639b6", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153363122T>A", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate", "PP4", "PM6_Strong", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 637904, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg306Ter) creating premature stop codon in MECP2. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism for Rett syndrome (X-linked dominant). VEP confirms stop_gained consequence with HIGH impact in multiple transcripts (ENST00000453960:c.916C>T, p.Arg306Ter; ENST00000303391:c.880C>T, p.Arg294Ter). MECP2 is intolerant to loss-of-function variants.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. The G>A allele (rs61751362) causing p.Arg306Ter has no reported allele frequency in gnomAD exomes or genomes, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. Note: The G>C allele at this position (p.Arg306Gly) has very low frequency (AF=1.64e-05) and is classified as likely benign.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2 mutations. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations. X-linked inheritance pattern is consistent with MECP2 location on chromosome X.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000011819) with multiple submissions across multiple conditions: Rett syndrome, Severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly, Syndromic X-linked intellectual disability Lubs type, and Autism susceptibility X-linked 3. Multiple RCV accessions (RCV000012590, RCV000012591, RCV000081215, RCV000474366, RCV000515413, RCV000624805, RCV001420261) support pathogenicity.", "notable": "Literature evidence (PMID:36147795) documents R306X mutation causing atypical Rett syndrome. HGMD entries (CM000750, CM023745, CX130322) confirm this as a disease-causing mutation. Extensive PubMed citations (60+ references) document this variant in Rett syndrome patients. Functional studies in iPSC models and mouse models demonstrate MECP2 loss-of-function causes neurological deficits characteristic of Rett syndrome (PMID:33916879, PMID:35074918)."}}
{"variant_id": "ad2e847c-b962-45a9-9153-2be48be47e3e", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78090815G>C", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3_Very Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 77726, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Trp746Cys) established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000265160) with multiple submissions for Glycogen storage disease type II. The G>T nucleotide change at the same position also results in p.Trp746Cys and is classified as pathogenic.", "PM1": "Located in a critical functional domain of acid alpha-glucosidase (GAA). Position Trp746 is within the catalytic GH31 domain essential for enzyme activity. HGMD entries (CM068152, CM083516) confirm this as a mutational hotspot.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variant p.Trp746Ter (c.2238G>A, rs1800312), which is classified as pathogenic in ClinVar. Different amino acid change at same position supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects highly conserved tryptophan residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA gene mutations. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (RCV000254988, RCV000283919, RCV000410158, RCV000723386, RCV000825562) for GSD2 and related conditions. HGMD also lists as disease-causing mutation.", "notable": "gnomAD frequency (0.03-0.04%) is low but present, consistent with carrier frequency for autosomal recessive Pompe disease. Literature case report (PMID:25093132) describes this variant in late-onset Pompe disease patient from Malaysia."}}
{"variant_id": "e31f1bdb-5ee0-4637-9ca0-156c92a1d3b7", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.95578574A>G", "gene": "DICER1", "disease": "DICER1-related tumor predisposition", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "DICER1 and miRNA-Processing Gene VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 133157, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0: AF = 3.98e-06 in exomes (1 allele/251,000+), AF = 3.19e-05 in genomes (1 allele/31,000+). This meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in an autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = possibly damaging to probably damaging (0.579-0.965 across transcripts). Variant affects conserved methionine at position 684 in the Helicase domain (PF03368/PS51327). CADD score not available but SIFT/PolyPhen consensus supports damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (DICER1-related tumor predisposition) is highly specific for DICER1 syndrome, which has a single genetic etiology. DICER1 is the only known gene associated with this condition.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS (VCV000479642) with 3 submissions. Variant is located in the Helicase domain which is important for DICER1 function. COSMIC entry (COSV108184526) indicates somatic occurrence in tumors. PMID 38084291 provides DICER1-specific ACMG guidelines but no specific evidence for this variant was found. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism for DICER1 syndrome, but this is a missense variant (not null), so PVS1 does not apply."}}
{"variant_id": "4dbe4a4e-01f1-4566-96b5-4c9d2a05ba36", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68842610A>C", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60823, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.12-0.24), PolyPhen=benign (0.039-0.201). While one transcript shows PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (0.707), the majority of predictions are benign. CADD/DITTO scores not available.", "BP6": "ClinVar (VCV000140853) reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign by multiple submitters for CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome and hereditary diffuse gastric adenocarcinoma. While there are conflicting interpretations, the majority lean toward benign.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at AF=7.96e-05 (20 alleles), which is above the extremely rare threshold but below the BA1/BS1 thresholds. Located in cadherin domain (PS50268/PF00028) but computational evidence does not support pathogenicity. CDH1 loss-of-function is established mechanism for HDGC, but this missense variant does not appear to cause loss of function based on available evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "6d134c76-00d8-4df4-b260-bf2667bcaadc", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121437113C>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3_Supporting", "BS1", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 139887, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (score 0.46-0.85). However, CADD and DITTO scores not available for primary assessment.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "PM2 NOT met: Variant is present in gnomAD at low but detectable frequency (AF=3.58\u00d710\u207b\u2075 in exomes, 5.91\u00d710\u207b\u2075 in genomes, 9+ alleles total). ClinVar has conflicting interpretations with one submission as 'Likely benign' for monogenic diabetes. Variant is in the C-terminal transactivation domain (position 515), which is less constrained than the DNA-binding domain where most pathogenic MODY3 variants cluster. HGMD lists this variant (CM082807) but without functional evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "f1b331ac-2b12-493d-b88c-85af2b7fcb57", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42462561A>C", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 218363, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome (AF = 3.99e-06, ~1 allele). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Glanzmann thrombasthenia, this frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PM1": "Located in a critical functional domain of ITGA2B (integrin \u03b1IIb). VEP identifies the variant within Gene3D (3nigC00), PROSITE_profiles (PS51470 - integrin alpha chain), PANTHER (PTHR23220), and Superfamily (SSF69318) domains. ITGA2B is essential for platelet aggregation and fibrinogen binding, and missense variants in these domains are known to cause Glanzmann thrombasthenia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.989-0.995). The p.Leu214Arg substitution replaces a hydrophobic leucine with a positively charged arginine, a significant physicochemical change.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. Glanzmann thrombasthenia is a rare autosomal recessive bleeding disorder with a well-defined genetic etiology, caused almost exclusively by biallelic variants in ITGA2B or ITGB3.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (VCV000002901, RCV000003035). Multiple PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 9473221, 27607598, 21113249, 19691478, 27696190)."}}
{"variant_id": "dc9fdbbf-4e28-41d1-96de-532d635a2b43", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.4110537G>A", "gene": "MAP2K2", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 660689, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T02:22:21.650694Z\",\"request_id\":\"c227c"}
{"variant_id": "0b5afc39-258a-4c7d-8a60-f765e5c2eaf2", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89720649A>T", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54273, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.1722+943A>T) located 943bp from nearest splice site. VEP consequence: intron_variant with MODIFIER impact. No computational evidence supports splice disruption or pathogenic effect. CADD score not available but intronic position strongly suggests benign.", "BP7": "Synonymous-equivalent variant with no predicted splice impact. Deep intronic location (>900bp from exon boundary) is far outside canonical splice regions (\u00b11-2bp) and extended splice regions (\u00b18bp). No cryptic splice site activation predicted.", "notable": "CRITICAL DISCREPANCY: The provided variant NC_000010.10:g.89720649A>T maps to KIF20B gene (chromosome 10), NOT PTEN. PTEN is located at chr10:87,863,113-87,971,930 (GRCh38). This variant at position 89,720,649 is approximately 1.75Mb downstream of PTEN. The variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (gnomADg: 0.003286%, NFE: 0.00588%). If the clinical context requires PTEN variant analysis, please verify the correct genomic coordinates."}}
{"variant_id": "34d44fed-c8c6-4919-8669-2ee9f8113079", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44186197C>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5", "PM1"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67704, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in a critical functional domain of glucokinase. snpEff annotates this as 'structural_interaction_variant' affecting protein structure. VEP shows the variant maps to multiple protein domains including Superfamily SSF53067 (hexokinase domain), Pfam PF03727, and multiple AlphaFold structural mappings (1v4s, 1v4t, 3a0i, etc.), indicating location in a functionally constrained region.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in any population, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For a semidominant condition like GCK-MODY, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "Missense variant in GCK, a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY2). GCK has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene, with over 600 pathogenic/likely pathogenic missense variants reported.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.985 in canonical transcript). The glycine to valine substitution at position 295 introduces a larger, hydrophobic residue that likely disrupts protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for approximately 30-50% of all MODY cases and presents with characteristic mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID: 2743242, NM_000162.5:c.884G>T). HGMD also lists this variant with two entries (CD033193, CM109123) as disease-associated mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "d3424058-b37e-4bce-b932-0695abc3af1d", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11224284G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68937, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in EGF-like domain (Pfam PF00058, SMART SM00135, PROSITE PS51120) - a critical functional domain essential for LDLR-mediated LDL uptake and receptor recycling. This domain is a known mutational hotspot in familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PM2": "Rare in population databases: gnomAD exome AF=2.79e-05 (7 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=2.63e-05. Frequency is consistent with pathogenic variants for autosomal dominant FH (expected prevalence ~1:250).", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0-0.01), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). Consistent predictions across all LDLR transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the most common causative gene (~85-90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000161277). Classifications include: Pathogenic for Hypercholesterolemia familial 1, Pathogenic for Familial hypercholesterolemia, Likely pathogenic for Homozygous FH, Pathogenic for Cardiovascular phenotype."}}
{"variant_id": "8d0c1e2b-93b3-4f9a-b836-76258595cbfa", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.22276951A>G", "gene": "ANO5", "disease": "autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65884, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Frameshift variant (c.191dup, p.Asn64LysfsTer15) in ANO5, a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for LGMDR12 and Miyoshi muscular dystrophy 3. The duplication causes a frameshift at codon 64 leading to premature termination at codon 78, resulting in a severely truncated protein (normally 913 amino acids). VEP confirms HIGH impact frameshift_variant consequence across all protein-coding transcripts.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database. For an autosomal recessive disorder, this extremely low frequency supports pathogenicity. The variant is rare even in European populations where it represents a founder mutation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (Allele ID: 17203). Conditions include LGMDR12, Miyoshi muscular dystrophy 3, and ANO5-related muscular dystrophy. Multiple expert panels and clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic.", "notable": "This is a well-characterized founder mutation in Northern European populations (PMID:21186264, Hicks et al. Brain 2011). The study identified this variant in 20 patients from UK and German cohorts, with haplotype analysis confirming founder effect. Additional large cohort study (PMID:23606453) confirmed high occurrence. PS4 (prevalence in affected individuals) could potentially be applied given the extensive case-control data, but conservative interpretation limits to PP5 for ClinVar evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "fbd336f7-b6dc-43c0-8ae5-479035f47b66", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103237443C>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67911, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical functional domain - aromatic amino acid hydroxylase catalytic domain (Pfam PF00351, PROSITE PS51410). This domain is essential for phenylalanine 4-monooxygenase activity. Position Asp394 is within the catalytic core.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (allele frequency 1.368e-06, ~0.000137%). For autosomal recessive PKU, this meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "Missense variant in PAH gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. PAH has low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missenses are common (>1000 pathogenic variants reported in ClinVar/HGMD).", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (score 0.494-0.9). Multiple algorithms predict damaging effect on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology with PAH being the only causative gene for classic PKU.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV000102545, VCV000120262) with multiple submissions. HGMD lists as disease-causing mutation (CM961085, CM1514933). UniProt annotates as VAR_001029."}}
{"variant_id": "aa382ee0-a29a-432e-8332-0fc022c9fb80", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605725C>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BA1", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55002, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exceeds expected for a rare disease-causing variant. gnomAD exome AF=0.38%, gnomAD genome AF=0.43%, with Finnish population showing 1.6-2.1% frequency. This is significantly higher than expected for a pathogenic variant causing juvenile open-angle glaucoma.", "BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted splice impact. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No computational evidence suggests deleterious effect on protein function.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign with multiple independent submissions (RCV000177024, RCV000283082, RCV000321707, RCV002516721, RCV001824131). Clinical significance consistently reported as benign across multiple conditions including glaucoma.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Thr285=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted splice impact based on VEP analysis. The variant is located in a coding region but does not affect protein sequence."}}
{"variant_id": "9d7dbe5b-ee8e-4a22-8ebe-0cdae8f8b7b0", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68867203C>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 131400, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP1", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Although initially annotated as missense p.Ala634Val, this variant creates a cryptic splice site at c.1900 position, causing a 37bp out-of-frame deletion (r.1900_1936del) leading to premature truncation (p.Ala634ProfsTer7) and nonsense-mediated decay. CDH1 is a well-established tumor suppressor where loss-of-function is a known mechanism for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). This is a bona fide null variant.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies using RNA from HDGC patient PBMCs (PMID: 34503274) demonstrated: (1) 100% of mutant allele transcripts show cryptic splicing, (2) ~66% reduction of mutant allele expression via NMD, (3) Complete loss of E-cadherin protein expression in DGC and LBC tumors from carriers. Minigene assays and cell line studies also confirm splicing defect.", "PS4": "Variant identified in 9+ unrelated HDGC families from Northern Portugal (founder effect ~490 years old). Among 58 carriers: 18.9% developed DGC (mean age 33\u00b112), 19.4% females developed LBC (mean age 50\u00b18). 80.8% of prophylactic gastrectomy specimens showed DGC foci. Significantly enriched in affected individuals vs. controls.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: overall frequency 3.42e-06 (T allele). Absent in most populations. This is well below the threshold for a dominant disorder with high penetrance.", "PP1": "Strong co-segregation with disease demonstrated in multiple affected family members across 9 HDGC families. Variant segregates with both DGC and LBC phenotypes in carriers.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for HDGC syndrome, which has a well-established single genetic etiology (CDH1 germline variants).", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic (VCV000012244) with multiple submitters. Also listed in HGMD (CM034217) and COSMIC (COSV55730231)."}}
{"variant_id": "555642f7-bae2-4755-84a5-d33f4e75cdc2", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68772192C>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 123611, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "This synonymous variant (c.1137G>A, p.Thr379=) occurs at the last nucleotide of exon 8, affecting the canonical splice donor site. CDH1 is a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). RNA studies demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing with out-of-frame transcripts leading to premature termination codons. Per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP guidelines, G-to-non-G changes at the last nucleotide of an exon warrant PVS1_Moderate.", "PS3": "Well-established functional RNA studies (PMID: 15831593, 18427545, 19965908) demonstrate this variant causes complex aberrant splicing affecting exon 8, including exon skipping and intron retention, leading to expression of defective alternate splicing products with premature stop codons and high levels of allelic expression imbalance. ClinVar functional data submissions confirm 'functionally abnormal' status with skipped exon and retained intron consequences.", "PS4": "This variant has been reported in at least 4 families meeting HDGC clinical criteria (PMID: 15831593, 17545690, 17221870, 21681551, 27995193). Multiple case reports document affected individuals with diffuse gastric cancer and lobular breast cancer. The variant segregates with disease in multiple families across generations.", "PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD exomes (0 alleles in 251,452 control chromosomes). gnomAD v4 shows extremely rare frequency (6.841e-07 in gnomAD exomes, only in NFE population at 8.994e-07). This meets PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP specifications.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for this genetic etiology. CDH1 germline variants are the primary known cause of hereditary diffuse gastric cancer syndrome with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel classification (ClinGen Gastric Cancer VCEP, August 2023) classifies this variant as Pathogenic with 3-star review status. 17 total submissions in ClinVar: 15 Pathogenic, 2 Likely Pathogenic, with no conflicting interpretations. FDA-recognized database classification."}}
{"variant_id": "8d0f7cbb-2982-46ea-b526-c6afd4ec4be3", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.154182266G>A", "gene": "F8", "disease": "hemophilia A", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PVS1", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63510, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg602Ter/R602*) creating premature stop codon in F8 gene. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for hemophilia A (X-linked recessive). The variant occurs in exon 12 of 26 exons, predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) and result in complete loss of Factor VIII protein. F8 truncating variants are definitively associated with severe hemophilia A.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. The G>A allele (stop_gained) has no reported frequency in gnomAD exomes or genomes. Only the synonymous G>T variant at this position has minimal frequency (AF=1.09e-05). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 25271, VCV000010232) for Hereditary factor VIII deficiency disease (Hemophilia A). Multiple submissions with concordant pathogenic classification. Also listed in HGMD (CM900089, CM990550) as disease-causing mutation. OMIM entry 300841.0149 confirms pathogenicity. Multiple supporting publications (PMIDs: 1979502, 7728145, 1349567, 31064749, 23812942).", "notable": "This variant has been extensively characterized in the literature and mutation databases. The F8 gene is definitively associated with hemophilia A via loss-of-function mechanism. Nonsense mutations in F8 typically cause severe hemophilia A phenotype with <1% Factor VIII activity."}}
{"variant_id": "37ab8c27-9b0b-4a7a-aa18-6ecd3e9b8a40", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206903T>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64620, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_supporting": "Variant is completely absent from all population databases with adequate coverage for RUNX1 (gnomAD v2.1.1 and v3.0). Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting strength for rare variant status.", "BP4": "Multiple lines of computational evidence suggest no impact on gene/gene product. SpliceAI score \u22640.20 indicates no predicted splice effect. VEP consequence is 'splice_region_variant' with LOW impact. The variant is located at position c.614-5 (5 nucleotides from the splice acceptor site), which is outside the canonical \u00b11/2 splice sites. This intronic variant is not predicted to affect gene splicing.", "notable": "ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy Variant Curation Expert Panel reviewed this variant in August 2024 and classified it as VUS using their RUNX1-specific ACMG specifications. Labcorp/Invitae classified as Likely Benign. The variant has not been reported in any individual meeting RUNX1-phenotypic criteria (thrombocytopenia, platelet dysfunction, or hematologic malignancy). RUNX1 has established haploinsufficiency as disease mechanism, but this intronic variant does not affect canonical splice sites and is not predicted to cause loss of function."}}
{"variant_id": "afd68dc6-fb48-483f-9a46-594d8059fb70", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185236G>C", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 82451, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. The G>C variant (p.Cys371Trp) has no reported allele frequency in gnomAD exomes or genomes, supporting rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare monogenic disorder.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common, with >800 variants reported causing MODY2.", "PP3": "Missense variant affecting a conserved cysteine residue (Cys371Trp). Cysteine to tryptophan is a non-conservative substitution with significant physicochemical differences. The comprehensive GCK functional map (PMID: 37101203) demonstrates that variants at buried positions and critical structural regions show reduced activity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for 30-50% of all MODY cases and presents with mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID: 441092). Multiple submitters have classified this variant, with one submission as Likely Pathogenic for the specific condition.", "notable": "At the same codon position, the c.1113C>A (p.Cys371Ter) nonsense variant is classified as Pathogenic in ClinVar, supporting that this position is critical for protein function. The comprehensive GCK functional map (PMID: 37101203) provides systematic evidence that loss-of-function variants at conserved positions cause GCK-MODY."}}
{"variant_id": "fd93be23-8465-44a6-8548-1808e7aa4fc1", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44189356T>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64859, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database (rs2096324902 has no frequency data). Meets PM2 criterion for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK is a well-established MODY gene with semidominant inheritance pattern.", "notable": "This is a 5' UTR variant (c.-403C>T) with snpEff prediction of 'premature start codon gain variant'. However, 5' UTR variants are generally of uncertain significance without functional studies demonstrating impact on gene expression or translation. The variant is located 403bp upstream of the translation start site, making direct functional impact less likely. No ClinVar submissions, no published functional studies, and no case reports were found for this specific variant. GCK loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism for MODY2, but 5' UTR variants typically do not cause complete loss of function."}}
{"variant_id": "3d11b85f-1934-4263-8542-1a44854f60d0", "variant": "NC_000005.9:g.35876274A>G", "gene": "IL7R", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency, autosomal recessive, T cell-negative, B cell-positive, NK cell-positive", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2_Supporting", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68725, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.2\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (3 alleles/250,000+), gnomAD genome AF = 3.9\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (6 alleles/152,000+). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing alleles and meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. SIFT = 0.02 (deleterious). PolyPhen scores range from 0.147-0.833 across transcripts (benign to possibly damaging). The variant affects a conserved cysteine residue (Cys118Tyr) which may disrupt disulfide bonding in the IL7R extracellular domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (T-B+NK+ SCID) is highly specific for IL7R deficiency. The disease description explicitly states it 'has material basis in homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the IL7R gene.' This phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000036392) with multiple submissions supporting pathogenicity for SCID and Immunodeficiency 104. HGMD also lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CM056606). Multiple independent submitters have classified this variant as pathogenic/likely pathogenic.", "notable": "Loss-of-function in IL7R is an established mechanism for T-B+NK+ SCID. IL7R encodes the alpha chain of the IL-7 receptor, essential for T-cell development. The Cys118Tyr substitution likely disrupts protein structure in the extracellular domain. ClinGen SCID VCEP has published specifications for IL7R variant classification (PMID:41104538). For autosomal recessive inheritance, PM3 could be applied if this variant is confirmed in trans with another pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "4112e5b8-c121-471a-a34f-9da03e769a2b", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103288515G>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63098, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Multiple in vitro expression studies show p.Arg408Trp results in only 1.3-1.85% of wild-type PAH enzyme activity (PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E. coli showed 100% protein aggregation indicating severe folding defect and complete loss of function (PMID:18538294). The variant is located in the catalytic domain and leads to complete disruption of structural integrity.", "PM3_Strong": "For this autosomal recessive disorder, the variant has been detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants (IVS12+1G>A, M1V) in numerous affected individuals (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). ClinGen PAH Expert Panel upgraded PM3 to Strong level based on extensive compound heterozygous observations in PKU patients.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT: deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen-2: probably_damaging (score=0.997-0.999), REVEL: 0.89 (>0.75 threshold). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology with PAH being the causative gene. The ClinGen PAH Expert Panel applied PP4 at moderate strength given the specificity of the phenotype and exclusion of BH4 deficiency (PMID:25596310, PMID:9634518).", "PP5": "ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel (FDA Recognized Database) classified this variant as Pathogenic with 'reviewed by expert panel' status (August 2018). 40 independent ClinVar submissions unanimously classify as Pathogenic with no conflicting interpretations.", "notable": "This is the most common PAH pathogenic variant in European populations, accounting for ~20% of PKU alleles. gnomAD frequency (0.076-0.14%) is consistent with carrier frequency for an autosomal recessive disorder with 1:10,000-1:15,000 incidence. The variant is non-responsive to BH4 (tetrahydrobiopterin) therapy. PM2 was not applied as the variant is present in gnomAD at frequencies expected for a common recessive disease allele."}}
{"variant_id": "2315573e-5bfa-49d0-a748-32b214337932", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.173883866C>T", "gene": "SERPINC1", "disease": "antithrombin III deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Thrombosis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 126071, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=3.97e-05 (10/251,000 alleles), genome AF=3.18e-05 (1/31,000 alleles). Combined frequency ~0.004% is consistent with rare disease-causing variant threshold for autosomal dominant antithrombin deficiency.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (antithrombin III deficiency) is highly specific for SERPINC1 mutations. This is a well-characterized monogenic disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance where SERPINC1 is the only known causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000876602). In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT=0.32 (tolerated) and PolyPhen=0.038 (benign) do not support pathogenicity, which argues against PP3. No CADD or DITTO scores available. The variant is a missense (p.Arg78Gln) in a serpin domain but no functional studies or same amino acid pathogenic variants were identified. COSMIC reports this as a somatic variant (COSV100875032)."}}
{"variant_id": "d3b4ef76-02a8-4269-9cfa-7e8c9ddd34a5", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.36595157G>A", "gene": "RAG1", "disease": "recombinase activating gene 1 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP7", "BS2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 47006, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency >5% threshold not met, but >1% in gnomAD (exome AF=1.69%, genome AF=1.61%). However, this exceeds typical disease-causing thresholds for rare Mendelian disorders. Combined with BS1, supports benign classification.", "BS1": "Allele frequency of 1.6-1.7% in gnomAD far exceeds expected frequency for autosomal recessive SCID (disease prevalence ~1:50,000-100,000). This frequency is incompatible with a pathogenic variant for a severe early-onset disease.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign across 6 independent submissions (RCV000127708, RCV000374530, RCV000557624, RCV000320598, RCV001812109, RCV002756726) for conditions including SCID T-B-NK+, combined immunodeficiency with skin granulomas, and RAG1 deficiency.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.303G>A, p.Ala101=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at a splice site."}}
{"variant_id": "7baa86cb-8d45-4b9d-b456-eb9cc14e2ec9", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.135115570C>T", "gene": "SLC9A6", "disease": "Christianson syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71087, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.083% in gnomAD exome (152 alleles) and up to 0.69% in South Asian population exceeds expected frequency for rare X-linked disorder Christianson syndrome. This frequency is inconsistent with a pathogenic variant for a severe, early-onset condition.", "BP4": "Splice region variant at position -3 from exon (c.1582-3C>T). VEP assigns LOW impact. Position -3 is outside canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2) and computational evidence does not predict significant splice disruption. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but intronic position -3 variants typically have minimal functional impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Benign (2 submissions) and Likely benign (1 submission) for Christianson syndrome and related conditions (VCV000139206). Multiple independent submitters support benign classification."}}
{"variant_id": "330f9155-d147-4ea4-abdf-749a86408a5c", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38985021G>C", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72899, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome with AF=8.07e-06 (2 alleles in ~248,000 individuals). Per ClinGen RYR1 Expert Panel guidance, PM2 is applied at supporting level for rare variants in MH given reduced penetrance. Meets threshold for rare variant.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS with multiple submissions. In silico predictors (SIFT=tolerated, PolyPhen=benign) suggest benign effect but do not meet BP4 threshold per RYR1-specific REVEL cutoffs. Position 2102 falls outside the three established RYR1 MH hotspot regions (MH1: 35-614, MH2: 2163-2458, MH3: 4664-4973), so PM1 is not applicable. No functional studies or segregation data available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "890f4355-b322-4d63-ab2e-02ceb1436a6a", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121416629G>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate", "PP1_Strong", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71413, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the HNF1A dimerization domain (Pfam PF04814, PROSITE PS51937), a critical functional region. The N-terminal region containing Gly20 is part of the dimerization interface essential for HNF1A transcription factor function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 4.02e-06 (1 allele in ~250,000 individuals). This frequency is well below the expected threshold for a dominant MODY-causing variant.", "PP2": "HNF1A is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY3). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of HNF1A-MODY.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.988). The Gly20Arg substitution introduces a charged residue (arginine) in place of the small, flexible glycine.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a well-established single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV001033090) for Monogenic diabetes, MODY, and MODY3 from multiple submitters. HGMD also lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CM993815).", "notable": "Colocated variant at same position (G>C causing same amino acid change) is classified as Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar, supporting pathogenicity of amino acid change at this position. No specific functional studies found for this exact variant (PS3 not met)."}}
{"variant_id": "02453a5e-9d9a-4218-b2c2-436d4e9dcb10", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259229C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69759, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is completely absent from gnomAD and all population databases with adequate coverage for RUNX1. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP guidelines, this meets PM2 at supporting level.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.921 (>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly/probably damaging (0.732-0.948). The variant is located within the Runt domain (Pfam PF00853), a critical DNA-binding domain essential for RUNX1 transcription factor function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition (OMIM 601399), and the phenotype has a well-established single genetic etiology.", "notable": "ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP (Oct 2024) classified this variant as VUS applying their gene-specific criteria (BP4, PM2_Supporting). The VCEP applied BP4 based on their specific computational thresholds, though standard ACMG PP3 criteria are met with REVEL=0.921. The variant is located at a conserved position (Glu88) in the Runt domain. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified in the literature. Colocated somatic variants in COSMIC suggest this position may be relevant in cancer."}}
{"variant_id": "aac8ac5a-a8b7-4651-9186-9267f2bbb3d5", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7579343T>C", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57570, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP2": "TP53 is a gene where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (Li-Fraumeni syndrome), and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation. Missense variants in TP53 are frequently pathogenic.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with multiple submissions classifying this variant as Likely Benign for Li-Fraumeni syndrome (VCV000182925). gnomAD frequency is 3.425e-06 (extremely rare but present). SIFT predicts deleterious (0.05) but PolyPhen predicts benign (0.017-0.075). The variant is located in the DNA-binding domain (codon 115) but computational evidence is conflicting. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.His115Arg were identified. The presence in ClinVar as Likely Benign from multiple submitters weighs against pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "a771d414-f2f6-4f3d-b08a-bb4f6c8303ef", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.6132007T>C", "gene": "VWF", "disease": "von Willebrand disease type 2A", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3", "PS4_Very Strong"], "expert_panel": "von Willebrand Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 142146, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PS3", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Variant reported in at least 22 VWD type 2A patients across multiple independent studies (PMIDs: 22871923, 16985174, 35452508, 20351307, 17190853, 26986123, 26988807, 29388750, 29742318, 31249928, 31064749). ClinGen VWD VCEP upgraded to PS4_VeryStrong based on prevalence data. Significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals vs controls.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect: (1) Multimer analysis in 293 cells expressing recombinant variant VWF showed reduced high molecular weight multimers (PMID: 20351307, 27533707); (2) Defective intracellular packaging and markedly reduced VWF secretion; (3) Novel FVIII binding defect demonstrated (PMID: 27533707); (4) Inhibition of normal processing, string formation and platelet binding (PMID: 24598842).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD v4.1 Grpmax filtering allele frequency is 0 (1/37812 alleles in African/African-American population only). gnomAD exomes frequency: 0.00000. Absent from 54,460 control chromosomes. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0), REVEL=0.872 (>0.644 ClinGen VWD VCEP threshold). Variant introduces a cysteine residue (Y1146C) in the D3 domain which may impact disulfide bond formation and multimerization.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for VWD type 2A: excessive mucocutaneous bleeding with laboratory phenotype of low VWF activity (VWF:RCo 16, VWF:CB 7), VWF:Ag of 20, and low VWF:CB activity/VWF:Ag ratio of 0.35, which is specific for VWD type 2A (PMID: 24598842).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports Pathogenic classification from ClinGen von Willebrand Disease Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, August 2024). Multiple additional submitters (10 total) classify as Pathogenic with no conflicting interpretations. OMIM entry 613160.0039 also reports pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "8ddea12a-13d2-4712-8862-f104a7db3b2d", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38934860G>A", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 444378, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant resides in RYR1 N-terminal hotspot region (residues 35-614), a well-established mutational hotspot for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility pathogenic variants. ClinGen MHS Expert Panel confirmed PM1 applies (PMID:21118704). This region contains critical functional domains for calcium channel regulation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. VEP shows extremely rare frequency (gnomAD exomes: 6.841e-07 overall, 8.993e-07 in NFE only). This meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: PolyPhen-2 = 0.994-1.0 (probably damaging), SIFT = 0 (deleterious). REVEL score = 0.826 (per ClinGen expert panel). The missense variant p.Asp166Asn affects a conserved aspartic acid residue in a critical functional domain.", "PP5": "ClinVar VCV000133140 classified as Uncertain Significance by ClinGen Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, 4-star review status, Aug 2025). Expert panel applied PS4_Moderate and PM1 criteria. Variant reported in HGMD (CM023443) and COSMIC (COSV62105562).", "notable": "ClinGen Expert Panel applied PS4_Moderate based on 2 unrelated individuals with MH history and positive IVCT/CHCT results (PMID:12059893, PMID:16163667). However, no functional studies (PS3/BS3) are available. The expert panel's REVEL threshold (0.826) was considered neutral, not supporting pathogenicity. UniProt lists this as VAR_045699."}}
{"variant_id": "9c3f5113-40d4-4491-b303-093c891ae4d2", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103245482A>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM5", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 197646, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For autosomal recessive PKU, absence from population databases supports PM2 at moderate level.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The PAH gene has >1000 documented pathogenic missense variants causing PKU. Missense variants in PAH commonly cause disease through reduced enzyme activity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0 on canonical transcript). Variant located in conserved catalytic domain (Pfam PF00351 aromatic amino acid hydroxylase domain).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology with PAH being the only causative gene for classic PKU."}}
{"variant_id": "712f30f7-22e8-4854-9aae-37a109496552", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11230876A>G", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60433, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=3.98e-06 (1/251,000 alleles), genome AF=3.18e-05 (1/31,000 alleles). Total of 2 alleles observed across all populations. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of familial hypercholesterolemia. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants commonly cause disease.", "PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious effect (score=0.02). PolyPhen predictions are mixed (benign to possibly damaging, scores 0.039-0.315 across transcripts). CADD/DITTO scores not available. Partial computational support for deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR mutations account for ~85-90% of genetically confirmed FH cases, making this a highly specific genotype-phenotype correlation.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies as VUS with 2 submissions. HGMD entries (CD065749, CM973291) suggest disease association. Variant located in EGF-like domain (PF00058), a functionally important region. No functional studies identified for this specific variant. PubMed references (PMID:25647241, 15199436) associated with this variant but insufficient for PS3/PS4."}}
{"variant_id": "3c251870-1145-4f3d-b6c8-a8eafb2d9656", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.152960238C>T", "gene": "SLC6A8", "disease": "creatine transporter deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PS4_Moderate", "PP1_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 710326, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM6", "PP3", "PP4_Strong", "PS4_Supporting", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles in 182,621 control chromosomes). For X-linked recessive disorders, absence in population databases supports rarity. Applied at supporting level per ClinGen CCDS VCEP specifications.", "PM6": "De novo occurrence documented in a female proband with learning disabilities, seizures, and significantly reduced brain creatine by 1H-MRS. Segregation analysis confirmed variant arose de novo (PMID: 37708665). Maternity/paternity not explicitly confirmed, so applied as PM6 rather than PS2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (score 0.887), REVEL=0.784 (>0.75 threshold). ClinGen CCDS VCEP specifically cited REVEL score above 0.75 threshold as supporting evidence.", "PP4_Strong": "Patient phenotype highly specific for creatine transporter deficiency: 5-year-old boy with speech delay, severe refractory epilepsy, elevated urine creatine/creatinine ratio (1.83; normal 0.03-0.92), and decreased brain creatine peak on 1H-MRS (PMID: 17553121). This constellation of findings is pathognomonic for CRTR-D. Applied at strong level per ClinGen CCDS VCEP specifications.", "PS4_Supporting": "Variant reported in multiple unrelated affected individuals: hemizygous proband with elevated urine creatine/creatinine ratio (2.0; normal 0.017-0.72), affected brother also hemizygous, and heterozygous carrier mother (PMID: 15690373). Additional cases reported in PMID: 17553121, 21556832, 23644449. Applied at supporting level as statistical significance (OR>5, CI excludes 1) not formally calculated.", "PP5": "ClinGen Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic (Oct 2023) with 3-star review status. Additional submissions from GeneDx (Pathogenic), LabCorp (Pathogenic), and Invitae (Likely Pathogenic) with detailed evidence.", "notable": "Functional studies demonstrate significantly reduced creatine uptake: ~12% of control levels in patient fibroblasts at physiological substrate concentrations (PMID: 15690373) and ~39% of wild-type levels in vitro (PMID: 22281021). However, ClinGen VCEP determined this evidence did not meet their PS3 specifications. The variant affects a highly conserved proline residue at position 544 in the 12th transmembrane domain of the creatine transporter protein."}}
{"variant_id": "fbce2330-e8ba-4c27-8a0d-33a722e1d77f", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38934843A>G", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS4_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 300215, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant resides in the N-terminal domain (codon 160) of RYR1, a recognized mutational hotspot for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility pathogenic variants (PMID:21118704). The ClinGen MHS Expert Panel confirmed this region as a hotspot for MHS-associated variants.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency reported in large population databases, supporting rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant for this autosomal dominant condition.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.989-0.999), REVEL=0.957 (>0.85 threshold per ClinGen MHS specifications). The ClinGen Expert Panel applied PP3_Moderate based on REVEL score >0.85.", "PP5": "ClinVar VCV000133136 shows expert panel review (ClinGen Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP) classifying as VUS with criteria PS4_Supporting, PM1, PP3_Moderate. Labcorp/Invitae classified as Pathogenic for RYR1-related disorder. Multiple submissions with supporting evidence from PMIDs 14985404, 21674524, 30236257.", "notable": "Variant reported in individuals with personal/family history of MH reaction and positive IVCT/CHCT results (PMID:30236257), supporting PS4_Supporting per ClinGen criteria. However, no direct functional studies (calcium release assays) have been performed on this specific variant. The missense change (Glu\u2192Gly) involves a significant physicochemical change from acidic/polar to neutral/non-polar amino acid."}}
{"variant_id": "65363e52-5d51-4ffc-b1e6-b36bf508f027", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11231081G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70059, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the EGF-like domain (Pfam PF14670, SMART SM00181) of LDLR, a critical functional domain essential for receptor recycling and LDL binding. Mutations in this domain are well-established to cause familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF=4.0e-06, AC=1 in ~250,000 alleles). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder with population prevalence of ~1:250.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (>1,700 pathogenic missense variants reported). LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.01), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.943). Variant affects a conserved glycine residue in a critical functional domain.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (RCV000238136, RCV000810496, RCV002418062) for familial hypercholesterolemia. Also listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM012626).", "notable": "Four PubMed citations associated with this variant (PMIDs: 25741868, 22698793, 11754108, 27824480). ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with one VUS submission, but majority support pathogenicity. No functional studies specific to p.Gly675Ser were identified to support PS3."}}
{"variant_id": "4304a58d-ea39-4cf1-995e-e4f1395d30c6", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206861C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 48844, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. As a silent change (p.Gly217=), computational tools do not predict functional impact. No splice site disruption predicted (variant is not at canonical splice sites \u00b11/2).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.651G>A, p.Gly217=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at a canonical splice site position.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' (Allele ID: 1085657) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. While the variant is absent from gnomAD (which would typically support PM2), this is outweighed by the benign nature of synonymous variants in this context. RUNX1 disease mechanism is loss-of-function, but synonymous variants typically do not cause LOF unless they affect splicing."}}
{"variant_id": "bcdcdf00-c029-4ef1-bbf4-1ea3f4cb9e10", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1399886A>T", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PP4_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 135131, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PM3", "PP3", "PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4_Strong": "Patient phenotype highly specific for GAMT deficiency. Proband showed elevated guanidinoacetate and low creatine in plasma, elevated urine guanidinoacetate, and low creatine peak on brain MRS (PMID: 24071436). ClinGen CCDS VCEP upgraded PP4 to Strong level.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with a pathogenic variant c.299_311dup13 (p.Arg105GfsTer26) (ClinVar Variation ID: 8302) in two siblings with GAMT deficiency. Variants confirmed to be in trans (PMID: 23660394, PMID: 24268530, PMID: 24071436).", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL=0.794 (>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.964-0.995). Missense variant causes substitution of neutral, non-polar valine with acidic, polar glutamic acid at codon 78.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD v4.1.0 highest MAF is 0.0000016 (2/1,178,172 alleles) in non-Finnish European population, well below ClinGen CCDS VCEP threshold of <0.0004. Applied as PM2_Supporting per ClinGen specifications."}}
{"variant_id": "1b7719a1-ebea-4124-9925-8b5037b8efc0", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11221442G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM1", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65792, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: AF=1.16e-05 in exomes (7/250,000 alleles), AF=1.97e-05 in genomes (3/152,000 alleles). This is well below the 0.01% threshold expected for a dominant disorder with ~1:250 prevalence. Meets PM2 for absence/extremely low frequency in population databases.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports splice disruption. The variant is located at position c.1187-10 in the polypyrimidine tract of intron 8, which is critical for proper splicing. VEP annotates this as 'splice_polypyrimidine_tract_variant'. Disruption of the polypyrimidine tract can lead to exon skipping or activation of cryptic splice sites, potentially causing loss of function. While CADD/DITTO scores were not directly available, the splice region location and functional consequence support a deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR gene variants. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the most common causative gene (>90% of monogenic FH cases). The clinical presentation is highly consistent with the expected phenotype for LDLR pathogenic variants.", "PP5": "Multiple reputable sources classify this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic: (1) ClinVar VCV000226349 with multiple submissions reporting Pathogenic for FH and related conditions; (2) HGMD lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CS014612); (3) UCL LDLR variant database (PMID:27821657) includes this variant. Multiple independent clinical laboratories have submitted pathogenic classifications.", "notable": "This variant has been reported in multiple FH case reports and cohort studies (PMIDs: 33569482, 26077743, 30400955, 27830735). PMID:33569482 describes a case of early-onset ischemic cerebrovascular disease with FH where this variant was identified. PMID:26077743 identified this variant through whole-exome sequencing in severe hypercholesterolemia. The variant affects the polypyrimidine tract which is essential for spliceosome recognition, though formal functional studies (PS3) demonstrating aberrant splicing were not identified in the available literature."}}
{"variant_id": "c0b25d34-300f-4066-a90f-4e5bf4bf85c0", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1399891T>A", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 140728, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (c.229A>T, p.Lys77Ter) in GAMT gene creating a premature stop codon at position 77 of 236 amino acids. GAMT deficiency is an autosomal recessive disorder where loss of function is the established disease mechanism. The truncated protein would lack the majority of the functional guanidinoacetate N-methyltransferase domain, abolishing enzymatic activity required for creatine biosynthesis. Multiple protein-coding transcripts show HIGH impact stop_gained consequence (ENST00000252288, ENST00000447102, and others).", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. The genomic position chr19:g.1399891T>A shows no allele frequency data for this specific nucleotide change resulting in p.Lys77Ter. For an autosomal recessive disorder, absence from population databases strongly supports pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "d2d8f997-9c23-4dcc-aa14-7aa5e9b785c6", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42463013G>C", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PM4", "PP3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83493, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM3", "PM4", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exomes (AF=4.02e-06, ~1 allele in 248,000). For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, this frequency is consistent with PM2_supporting per ClinGen VCEP specifications.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variant c.1545-1del (classified pathogenic by ClinGen Platelet Disorders VCEP) in at least one proband (PMID:32237906). Also reported in 3 compound heterozygous individuals (PMIDs: 9215749, 28232155, 32237906) and 1 homozygote.", "PM4": "Functional studies (PMID:9215749) demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing resulting in in-frame deletion of 33 amino acids (Ser160_Ser192) in exon 4, causing protein length change.", "PP3": "SpliceAI predicts activation of exonic cryptic acceptor site with score 0.76 (>0.5 threshold). SIFT=0.04 (deleterious). Computational evidence supports damaging effect on splicing.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for Glanzmann thrombasthenia: mucocutaneous bleeding with impaired platelet aggregation to all agonists except ristocetin (PMIDs: 32237906, 28232155). Applied as PP4_moderate per ClinGen VCEP specifications.", "PP5": "ClinGen Platelet Disorders Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Likely Pathogenic (June 2023) with detailed evidence review. FDA-recognized database with expert panel review status."}}
{"variant_id": "1a47fed2-6375-4b1e-91c9-5e70e5c6dc27", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.25616462C>T", "gene": "UBE3A", "disease": "Angelman syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 128368, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (Angelman syndrome) is highly specific for UBE3A-related disease. Angelman syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with UBE3A being the primary causative gene (maternal imprinting). The clinical presentation is distinctive with severe intellectual disability, absent speech, ataxia, and characteristic EEG abnormalities.", "notable": "PM2 NOT met: Variant is present in gnomAD at AF=3.98e-06 (1 allele), which while rare, does not meet the 'absent from controls' threshold for PM2. BP4 nearly met: SIFT=0.33 (tolerated) and PolyPhen=0.003-0.062 (benign) both predict this variant is tolerated, but CADD/DITTO scores unavailable for definitive BP4 assessment. ClinVar reports this variant as VUS (VCV000420601). The V287I substitution is a conservative amino acid change (valine to isoleucine, both hydrophobic). No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. UBE3A loss-of-function is the established mechanism for Angelman syndrome, but this missense variant lacks evidence of functional impact."}}
{"variant_id": "6366a1c0-841b-4c59-ad2e-577cdf97976d", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.70327733C>T", "gene": "IL2RG", "disease": "T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency due to gamma chain deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57909, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Variant present in gnomAD at allele frequency of 3.4e-05 (exome) and 9.2e-05 (genome). For a severe, early-onset X-linked disorder like X-SCID with full penetrance in males, any presence in population controls is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant.", "BP6": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' for X-linked severe combined immunodeficiency (SCIDX1) (VCV000763173, allele_id: 774184).", "BP7": "This is a synonymous variant (c.963G>A, p.Leu321=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. VEP analysis shows no predicted splice site impact - the variant is classified as 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact."}}
{"variant_id": "d9289d14-fc44-4dc3-b049-76350a7512e7", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23884368C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "dilated cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "PM2", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71447, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs730880816 is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, indicating extremely rare or absent in population controls. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a well-established sarcomeric gene where missense variants are a known mechanism of disease for cardiomyopathies. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common in cardiomyopathy patients. Knowledge graph confirms MYH7 association with dilated cardiomyopathy, familial dilated cardiomyopathy, and familial hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999). Variant causes missense change p.Glu1799Lys (E1799K) affecting a conserved glutamic acid residue in the myosin rod/tail domain (Pfam PF01576). COSMIC entry COSV62522204 also exists for this position.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant (VCV000181278, allele_id 179482) as 'Likely pathogenic' for one submission (condition: not provided). Multiple other submissions classify as VUS for hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, dilated cardiomyopathy, and general cardiomyopathy phenotypes. Mixed ClinVar interpretations with one LP classification provides supporting evidence.", "notable": "Variant located in the myosin rod/tail domain (coiled-coil region, Pfam PF01576) which is important for myosin filament assembly. Position 1799 is in the C-terminal region of MYH7. No specific functional studies found for this exact variant (E1799K). No CIViC entry exists. The variant has been reported in COSMIC (COSM5441572) as a somatic mutation. MYH7 is definitively associated with autosomal dominant dilated cardiomyopathy per knowledge graph and literature."}}
{"variant_id": "77a3bf59-08d2-4712-8073-89691ff3c35a", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185235C>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59897, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Glu372Ter) in GCK gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease. GCK haploinsufficiency causes MODY2 through reduced glucokinase activity and impaired glucose sensing. The premature stop codon at position 372 (of 465 amino acids) is expected to trigger nonsense-mediated decay or produce a severely truncated, non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database. The C>A allele (our variant) has 0 alleles in gnomAD; only the C>G allele (different variant, missense) has 1 allele (AF=4.26e-06). This extreme rarity is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare monogenic disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2). GCK mutations are the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases. The clinical presentation is characteristic with mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia typically not requiring treatment.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (allele_id: 44838, rs193922262) for both 'Maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 2' and 'Monogenic diabetes'. Multiple submitters have classified this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "6321659e-744f-438b-80c8-1445c0caada1", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252989G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63109, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM1_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is completely absent from gnomAD and all population databases with adequate coverage (>20x) for RUNX1. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level for rare variant status.", "PM1_Supporting": "Variant affects residue Pro125 within the Runt Homology Domain (amino acids 89-204), a critical functional domain for DNA binding and CBF\u03b2 interaction. However, this specific residue is not an established mutational hotspot. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, PM1 is applied at supporting level.", "notable": "ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP (expert panel, September 2024) classified this variant as VUS applying PM1_Supporting and PM2_Supporting. Invitae's advanced protein modeling indicates this missense variant is NOT expected to disrupt RUNX1 protein function. SIFT predicts 'deleterious_low_confidence' (score 0.02), but PolyPhen predicts 'benign' (score 0.204) on one transcript and 'possibly_damaging' (0.778) on another. The proline-to-serine substitution involves neutral amino acids with similar properties. No functional studies or case reports exist for this specific variant. COSMIC entry (COSV55872935/COSM25772) indicates somatic occurrence but without clinical significance data."}}
{"variant_id": "399db6af-6807-459a-9953-39c259125cad", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605478G>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PP1_Strong", "PM4", "PS3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 77003, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PM1", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Strong statistical association with glaucoma in multiple population studies. Finnish FinnGen study (PMID:34081096) shows OR=3.36 (95% CI: 2.55-4.37) for POAG, OR=2.58 for overall glaucoma. Genome-wide meta-analysis (PMID:33627673) confirms association across ancestries. This is the most common MYOC risk variant in European populations.", "PM1": "Located in the olfactomedin (OLF) domain (residues 245-504) where >90% of glaucoma-causing MYOC mutations cluster. This domain is critical for protein folding and secretion. Mutations in this domain cause protein misfolding, intracellular aggregation, and ER stress leading to trabecular meshwork cell death (PMID:37217093).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (juvenile open-angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-associated disease. MYOC mutations account for ~5% of POAG cases and are particularly enriched in juvenile-onset forms. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters for glaucoma conditions including GLC1A, POAG, and glaucoma of childhood (ClinVar VCV000007949). Some conflicting interpretations exist due to reduced penetrance.", "notable": "PVS1 NOT applicable: Although this is a nonsense variant, MYOC-associated glaucoma operates via a GAIN-OF-FUNCTION/toxic aggregation mechanism, NOT loss-of-function. Myocilin knockout mice do not develop glaucoma, and haploinsufficiency is not pathogenic. The mutant protein causes disease through intracellular aggregation and ER stress (PMID:37217093). PM2 NOT met: gnomAD AF=0.11% (exome) and 0.085% (genome) - present in population at low frequency, consistent with reduced penetrance (~5-10%) rather than absence."}}
{"variant_id": "04f7f269-ffcb-41d8-a7db-01b490cb4516", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36162427T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76210, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "3' UTR variant (c.*2005A>G) located 2005 nucleotides downstream of stop codon. No predicted splice impact. Computational tools do not predict deleterious effect for non-coding variants. CADD scores are typically low for 3' UTR variants without regulatory element disruption.", "BP7": "This is a non-coding variant in the 3' UTR region. Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines, 3' UTR variants are not considered pathogenic unless they affect critical regulatory elements. No evidence of splice impact or regulatory element disruption.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (VCV000339839): one submission as Benign, one as VUS. gnomAD frequency of 0.045% (14 alleles in ~31,000 genomes) is above the expected threshold for a rare pathogenic variant in this autosomal dominant condition. Per ClinGen RUNX1 guidelines, 3' UTR variants are generally classified as benign/likely benign unless functional evidence demonstrates pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "3ea40681-dff3-4b07-8d6e-dcccecaf824d", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.152956983C>T", "gene": "SLC6A8", "disease": "creatine transporter deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76014, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in critical functional domain (Pfam PF00209 - Sodium:neurotransmitter symporter family) within transmembrane region. Literature demonstrates missense variants in transmembrane domains of SLC6A8 tend to affect function, with pathogenic variants showing \u226588% reduction in creatine uptake (PMID:40781773).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database (rs1557044461 has no frequency data). For X-linked recessive disorder, absence from controls strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging to probably_damaging (0.89-0.985). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue at position 207.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (creatine transporter deficiency) is highly specific for SLC6A8 mutations. This X-linked disorder has a single genetic etiology with characteristic features including intellectual disability, speech delay, and seizures.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV001211026) with submissions from clinical laboratories. HGMD lists as disease mutation (CM169670)."}}
{"variant_id": "c2116f65-b2be-4f3a-b6c0-81eda3d4011f", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.45654352G>A", "gene": "GATM", "disease": "AGAT deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 78115, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PM3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg169Ter) creating a premature stop codon in exon 4/9 of GATM, predicted to cause nonsense-mediated decay. Loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for AGAT deficiency (autosomal recessive). ClinGen CCDS VCEP confirmed PVS1 applies.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF: 7.96e-06 (2 alleles); gnomAD genome AF: 1.31e-05 (2 alleles). Highest population frequency 0.00005 in East Asian population, below ClinGen CCDS VCEP threshold of <0.000055 for PM2_Supporting (applied as PM2).", "PM3": "Variant reported homozygous in affected probands with AGAT deficiency (PMID: 20625172, 23660394). Two Jordanian siblings born of consanguineous parents were homozygous for this variant, confirming biallelic inheritance in autosomal recessive disease.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for AGAT deficiency: undetectable guanidinoacetate (GAA) in plasma and urine, reduced creatine peak on brain MRS with elevated NAA/creatine ratio. AGAT deficiency has a single genetic etiology (GATM). ClinGen VCEP applied PP4_Strong.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, June 2022). Also classified Pathogenic by Labcorp Genetics and Fulgent Genetics with criteria provided. ClinVar VCV000055919.10."}}
{"variant_id": "678f59c9-6171-481a-90c0-bd5d5a13b35e", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42458381A>G", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83333, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp941Ter) in ITGA2B, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive). The variant creates a premature stop codon at position 941, predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a severely truncated protein lacking critical C-terminal domains. VEP confirms HIGH impact stop_gained consequence across multiple transcripts (ENST00000262407, ENST00000901307, ENST00000949677).", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD and other population databases. Not found in myvariant database queries. For an autosomal recessive disorder, absence from population controls strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. GT is characterized by mucocutaneous bleeding with absent platelet aggregation, and has a single genetic etiology (\u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin deficiency). The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "notable": "This exact variant (c.2822G>A, p.Trp941*) was reported in PMID:40126091 in a family with GT phenotype. MutationTaster predicted pathogenic. The variant is also catalogued in COSMIC (COSV52231428). However, the published case involved heterozygous carriers with bleeding symptoms, which is atypical for the recessive inheritance pattern of GT, suggesting possible additional genetic factors."}}
{"variant_id": "4b2ceaad-8826-45d2-bf5d-9ff4c035568d", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44189624C>T", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4", "PS1", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 191086, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical functional domain - glucokinase catalytic domain (Pfam PF00349, CDD cd24092). Glycine 175 is within the ATP-binding and glucose-binding active site region essential for enzymatic function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD - allele frequency 6.842e-07 (essentially 1 allele in ~1.5 million). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in GCK gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY2). GCK has low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.996-1.0). Consistent predictions across all transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology with characteristic mild fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000129143) for Monogenic diabetes and Likely Pathogenic for MODY. HGMD has two entries (CM097281, CM930297) classifying as disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "753186a8-75c2-4540-9d2e-f07fbdd8fb73", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171621468A>G", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 371537, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs940067240 is absent or extremely rare in gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data returned from myvariant or VEP colocated variant queries, consistent with a rare variant.", "notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.-43-2373C>G) in MYOCOS, not affecting MYOC coding sequence or canonical splice sites. MYOC-associated glaucoma is caused by protein misfolding (gain-of-function), not loss-of-function, making intronic variants unlikely to be pathogenic. VEP classifies this as 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact. No ClinVar submissions exist for this variant. PVS1 not applicable as this is not a null variant and MYOC does not have LOF as disease mechanism."}}
{"variant_id": "1931d802-2e7e-48dd-b06f-68f862cfb491", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.44031324C>T", "gene": "ETHE1", "disease": "ethylmalonic encephalopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BS2", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "Mitochondrial Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70080, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency of 15.7% in gnomAD exome and 18.2% in gnomAD genome far exceeds the 5% threshold for stand-alone benign classification. This is a common polymorphism in all populations.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.6G>A, p.Ala2=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP annotation shows 'synonymous_variant' consequence with LOW impact across all ETHE1 transcripts."}}
{"variant_id": "f89ea3e7-4808-4b4e-87eb-bfbfdfae5456", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.135067802C>T", "gene": "SLC9A6", "disease": "Christianson syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 105283, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Gly47Gly) with no predicted functional impact. No splice site disruption predicted. CADD and DITTO scores not available but variant does not alter protein sequence.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.141C>T, p.Gly47=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant is located in exon 2 and does not affect canonical splice sites. Multiple ClinVar submissions classify as Benign or Likely Benign.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV000139211 has 3 submissions: Benign (not specified), Likely Benign (Christianson syndrome), and Uncertain Significance (not provided). gnomAD shows presence in population (AF=3.3e-05 exomes, 4.7e-05 genomes) with 6 alleles in exomes and 1 in genomes. This is a synonymous variant that does not change the amino acid (Gly47Gly) and is not expected to affect protein function. SLC9A6 loss-of-function is the established mechanism for Christianson syndrome, but this synonymous variant does not cause loss of function."}}
{"variant_id": "69254db0-97b7-4d3a-a8f3-a3fca6fb3495", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43048435G>T", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 103116, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Glu249Ter) creating premature stop codon in HNF4A. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism for MODY1/HNF4A-related monogenic diabetes. HNF4A haploinsufficiency causes disease through reduced transcription factor activity. Variant affects multiple transcripts (p.Glu246*, p.Glu249*, p.Glu264*, p.Glu271*) all resulting in stop_gained effect.", "PM2": "Variant (chr20:g.43048435G>T) is absent from gnomAD exome database. The alternate allele at this position (G>A) has extremely low frequency (AF=7.95e-06, 2 alleles), but the specific G>T change causing the nonsense mutation is not observed in population databases.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF4A-related disease. HNF4A is a well-established MODY1 gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Knowledge graph confirms HNF4A association with maturity-onset diabetes of the young, hyperinsulinism due to HNF4A deficiency, and Fanconi renotubular syndrome 4 with MODY.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 442298) for both 'not provided' and 'Monogenic diabetes' conditions. Multiple submissions support pathogenic classification for NM_175914.5(HNF4A):c.745G>T (p.Glu249Ter)."}}
{"variant_id": "7950d5a7-12a0-4066-9380-cd03dfacaaef", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605849C>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 135194, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF = 2.5\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (6/239,000 alleles), genome AF = 6.57\u00d710\u207b\u2076. Well below PM2 threshold for autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "MYOC is a gene where missense variants in the olfactomedin domain are a well-established mechanism of disease for primary open-angle glaucoma. Pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = 0.04 (deleterious), PolyPhen = 0.953 (probably damaging). Variant located in olfactomedin domain (PROSITE PS51132).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (primary open-angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-related disease. MYOC mutations account for 3-5% of POAG cases with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "HGMD entries (CM023428, CM070204) indicate this position has been reported in disease context. ClinVar currently classifies as VUS (VCV001342209). No published functional studies specific to p.Gly244Val were identified. Glycine at position 244 is highly conserved in the olfactomedin domain."}}
{"variant_id": "c1e7d5a4-2952-462d-95e6-714568dcbcd0", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605450G>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 125589, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the olfactomedin (OLF) domain (Pfam PF02191, SMART SM00284, PROSITE PS51132) at position 377. The OLF domain is a critical functional domain where pathogenic missense variants cluster and cause protein misfolding leading to glaucoma. This domain is a well-established mutational hotspot for MYOC-associated glaucoma.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.99e-05 (5/251,000+ alleles); gnomAD genome AF = 3.94e-05. This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for autosomal dominant juvenile open-angle glaucoma.", "PP2": "MYOC is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Pathogenic missense variants in the olfactomedin domain cause protein misfolding and are the primary cause of MYOC-associated glaucoma. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in this critical domain.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably damaging (score 1.0). Both primary predictors strongly support pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (juvenile open-angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-associated disease. MYOC mutations account for 10-36% of juvenile open-angle glaucoma cases, making this a highly specific genotype-phenotype correlation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV001342202, VCV002500837) for Glaucoma of childhood and GLC1A. Multiple HGMD entries (CM020159, CM138530, CM981344) also classify this as disease-causing."}}
{"variant_id": "d494eb32-e830-4058-8d88-61a282649f6a", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164604G>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1_Strong", "PM5_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 147277, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser424Ter) creating premature stop codon in RUNX1. Loss-of-function via haploinsufficiency is a well-established mechanism for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (FPD/AML). The variant affects the transactivation domain (C-terminal) and is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or truncated non-functional protein. Multiple transcripts show HIGH impact stop_gained consequence.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD for the G>T allele (p.Ser424Ter). The alternate G>A allele at this position (p.Ser424Leu) has extremely low frequency (AF=6.96e-06, 1 allele in ~143,000 exomes). Absence from population databases supports rarity consistent with pathogenic variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition (FPD/AML), and the phenotype has a single genetic etiology with high specificity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' by one submitter (RCV005001135) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. Additionally classified as 'Uncertain significance' by another submitter, but the Likely Pathogenic classification provides supporting evidence.", "notable": "COSMIC entry (COSV99038599/COSM7346673) indicates this variant has been observed as a somatic mutation in cancer, supporting its functional significance. VEP analysis confirms HIGH impact across 5 protein-coding transcripts. Extensive literature supports RUNX1 truncating variants as pathogenic in FPD/AML (PMIDs: 38352275, 36626254, 38019014)."}}
{"variant_id": "4d08e15d-7c27-4174-9937-728646b86912", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121437195A>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 164147, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs886038347 is absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant annotation, supporting rarity consistent with PM2 for autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is a well-established MODY gene with strong gene-disease association in knowledge graph.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: 'Likely benign' for unspecified condition and 'Uncertain significance' for MODY. This is a splice donor region variant at position +3 (c.1623+3A>G), which is NOT a canonical splice site (\u00b11/2). VEP classifies impact as 'LOW'. No functional studies or literature specifically addressing this variant were found. The +3 position has reduced likelihood of affecting splicing compared to canonical \u00b11/2 positions, and computational tools predict low impact, which counterbalances the pathogenic criteria."}}
{"variant_id": "f6dd9146-59ca-44c4-ac27-d16f23cce231", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11211016C>G", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 211270, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Absent from gnomAD for the C>G allele. The C>T allele at the same position (p.Thr62Met) has AF=0.00012 in gnomAD exomes, but the specific C>G (p.Thr62Arg) allele is not observed, supporting rarity.", "PM1": "Located in the LDL receptor class A (LDLRA) ligand-binding domain (exon 4), a critical functional region. This domain contains cysteine-rich repeats essential for LDL binding. Variants in this domain are enriched for pathogenic variants in familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (familial hypercholesterolemia). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are well-established.", "notable": "In silico predictions are conflicting: PolyPhen predicts probably_damaging (0.979-0.998) in canonical transcripts but benign in some alternative transcripts; SIFT shows mixed results (tolerated to deleterious). PMID 30413722 functionally characterized p.Thr62Met (different amino acid change at same position) as non-deleterious, which may suggest this position tolerates some variation. ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS. No CADD or DITTO scores available for primary PP3 assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "0de45bdb-5b58-432f-b6b3-902e15ac59c5", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.173881122T>C", "gene": "SERPINC1", "disease": "antithrombin III deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PP4", "BP4", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Thrombosis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67119, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the Serpin domain (Pfam PF00079), a critical functional domain for serine-type endopeptidase inhibitor activity. SERPINC1 functions in heparin binding and regulation of blood coagulation.", "PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious effect (score 0.02). PolyPhen predicts benign (0.074), creating mixed computational evidence. Primary predictors (CADD/DITTO) not available, but SIFT supports deleterious effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (antithrombin III deficiency) is highly specific for SERPINC1 mutations. Antithrombin deficiency is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Hereditary antithrombin deficiency (VCV001170692). However, conflicting interpretation exists with 'Likely benign' for SERPINC1-related disorder.", "notable": "PMID 32920809 identifies p.Thr147Ala as 'The First Founder Mutation in People of African Origin Responsible for Inherited Antithrombin Deficiency.' gnomAD frequency (0.04-0.16%) is low but not absent, enriched in African populations (0.6-0.7% in gnomAD AFR). This founder effect in African populations with documented disease association provides moderate support for pathogenicity, though population-specific frequency considerations apply."}}
{"variant_id": "178ae908-8176-427c-9164-1d0e74b7cc79", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.115256562G>A", "gene": "NRAS", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM6_Very Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3_Moderate", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 137235, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Thr50Ile) previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000013902) with multiple submissions for Noonan syndrome 6 and RASopathy. PMIDs: 24033266, 19966803, 21263000.", "PM1": "Located in the Ras GTPase domain (Pfam PF00071, SMART SM00173-175), a critical functional domain essential for GTP binding and hydrolysis. NRAS mutations in this domain are known to cause constitutive activation of RAS-MAPK signaling.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD with frequency of 7.328e-07 (essentially 1 allele in ~1.4 million). Absent in most populations (AFR, AMR, EAS, FIN, MID, SAS, ASJ). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "NRAS is a gene where missense variants are a known mechanism of disease (RASopathies). Germline activating mutations cause Noonan syndrome 6, and the gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT score 0.01 (deleterious). Variant affects conserved residue in GTPase domain critical for RAS protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for disorders caused by germline mutations in RAS-MAPK pathway genes including NRAS. Autosomal dominant inheritance pattern is consistent with Noonan syndrome 6.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000013902) with multiple submitters. Also listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM100126)."}}
{"variant_id": "1004a07f-fee6-417b-9cc4-69e0df4ad540", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252939_36252940insCTTTTATTCCGATTCCCCTTGTCCGAAGGTAT", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76563, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "This is a 33-bp insertion in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPD-MM). RUNX1 is a master regulator of hematopoiesis, and germline variants including frameshift, stopgain, and deletions are well-documented causes of FPD-MM (PMID:36626254, PMID:35054439). The disease mechanism includes haploinsufficiency and dominant-negative effects. If this insertion causes a frameshift (not divisible by 3 in coding region), it would result in a null allele. Note: The 33-bp insertion (divisible by 3) could be in-frame if entirely within coding sequence, which would reduce to PM4 instead; however, insertions of this size typically disrupt protein function significantly.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD and population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For autosomal dominant conditions like FPD-MM, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related FPD-MM. This syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with RUNX1 being one of the primary causative genes (along with ETV6 and ANKRD26). The phenotype-genotype correlation is strong.", "notable": "VEP annotation mapped this variant to DOP1B intron rather than RUNX1, suggesting possible coordinate discrepancy or the variant may be in a regulatory/intronic region of RUNX1. If confirmed to be intronic, PVS1 would not apply and classification would need revision. The 33-bp insertion length (divisible by 3) could represent an in-frame insertion if in coding sequence, which would warrant PM4 rather than PVS1. Clinical correlation and transcript-level analysis recommended."}}
{"variant_id": "ad6cdaf9-6645-4a76-8fb6-68346a72c8aa", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68910268T>C", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54459, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg91Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant (rs61752871, NM_000329.3:c.271C>T) as Pathogenic with 12 independent RCV submissions for RPE65-related conditions including LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related recessive retinopathy.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=5.57e-05 (14 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=3.19e-05 (1 allele). For a recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variants and meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=0 (deleterious), PolyPhen=0.941 (probably damaging). Missense variant affects conserved Arg91 residue in RPE65 protein.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for RPE65-associated disease. RPE65 is the only gene known to cause this specific phenotype, and the condition has a well-defined single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000013115) from reputable clinical laboratories. HGMD (CM983758) and COSMIC also document this variant.", "notable": "Multiple publications document this variant in affected patients (PMID:35129589, 35551639, 31925606, 27624628). RPE65 encodes retinal pigment epithelium-specific 65 kDa protein with retinol isomerase activity essential for visual cycle. Loss of function is established disease mechanism for LCA2/RP20."}}
{"variant_id": "39bd4310-b3e1-4eb3-aae0-200dc2832790", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39037100G>A", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 223538, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4_Supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4_Supporting": "Variant reported in an individual with personal/family history of MH episode and positive IVCT/CHCT result (PMID:25658027). ClinGen MHS Expert Panel applied PS4 at supporting level due to limited case evidence.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: PolyPhen=benign (score 0.003), REVEL=0.178 (<0.5 threshold). Invitae advanced modeling indicates variant not expected to disrupt RYR1 protein function with 95% negative predictive value. ClinGen MHS Expert Panel applied BP4 based on REVEL <0.5.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV001019540 classified as Uncertain Significance by ClinGen Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, Aug 2025). gnomAD frequency: 0.003-0.007% (AF=3.18e-05 exome, 3.29e-05 genome), which is rare but present in population databases. Variant does not reside in a known MH hotspot region. No functional studies have been performed for this specific variant. One submission classified as Likely Benign for congenital myopathy."}}
{"variant_id": "0a887759-c693-44fc-80c7-d28240d99843", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44192000T>C", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM1", "PM5_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64496, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the hexokinase/glucokinase catalytic domain (Pfam PF00349, Gene3D, PANTHER PTHR19443). The Asp78 residue is within a critical functional region of the enzyme. GCK missense variants in this domain are frequently pathogenic for MODY2.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD exome or genome datasets, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for a dominant disorder.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY2/GCK-MODY). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 1.0). The variant affects a conserved aspartic acid residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for 30-50% of all MODY cases.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID 3543096). HGMD lists this variant (CM096819) as disease-associated mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "3581bb52-68a5-4ba7-baaa-558273d668f0", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48737605T>C", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PP4", "PP2", "PP3", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75267, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2_supporting", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5", "PS4_supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in calcium-binding EGF-like domain #29 (cbEGF-29), a critical functional domain of fibrillin-1. Cysteine substitutions in cbEGF domains represent the majority of pathogenic missense changes in FBN1-related disorders (PMID: 12938084, 10486319). This domain is essential for proper protein folding and calcium binding.", "PM2_supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 population database. gnomAD exome shows AF=0. Extremely rare variant consistent with pathogenicity for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance.", "PP2": "FBN1 has a missense constraint z-score of 5.06, indicating the gene is highly intolerant to missense variation. Pathogenic missense variants are common in FBN1, and benign missense variants are rare.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.934-0.952), REVEL=0.972 (>0.75 threshold). The p.Tyr1962Cys substitution introduces a new cysteine residue that may disrupt disulfide bonding critical for protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Marfan syndrome) is highly specific for FBN1-related disease. Marfan syndrome has a single genetic etiology with FBN1 mutations accounting for >90% of cases. Revised Ghent criteria provide high diagnostic specificity.", "PP5": "ClinGen FBN1 Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic (Feb 2024) with detailed evidence review. This is an FDA-recognized database with expert panel review status. Multiple clinical laboratories (GeneDx, LabCorp, All of Us) also classified as Likely Pathogenic.", "PS4_supporting": "Variant reported in at least 3 unrelated probands with clinical features of Marfan syndrome (PMID: 27112580, 33483584, Invitae internal data). While not meeting full PS4 statistical threshold, provides supporting evidence for disease association."}}
{"variant_id": "c0426f8d-dddf-447f-8b10-e0b31d0a6e1d", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.149809883C>T", "gene": "MTM1", "disease": "centronuclear myopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PS4", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 80819, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg224Ter) in MTM1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for X-linked myotubular myopathy/centronuclear myopathy. This premature stop codon at position 224 (of 603 amino acids) results in a severely truncated protein lacking the critical phosphatase domain. MTM1 is intolerant to loss-of-function variants.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database controls. The colocated SNP rs901451046 shows only the C>A allele at extremely low frequency (AF=2.794e-05), while the pathogenic C>T allele (rs132630306) is not observed in population controls, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (centronuclear myopathy) is highly specific for MTM1-related disease. X-linked centronuclear myopathy has a single genetic etiology (MTM1) with characteristic clinical features including neonatal hypotonia and respiratory failure.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000011060, RCV000011809) with multiple submitters and supporting evidence. HGMD entry CM970990 also classifies as disease-causing. Multiple publications support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 18414213, 9305655, 10790201, 11552027, 10063835)."}}
{"variant_id": "0ddd220f-6fa7-470e-a89c-bc65694949a5", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11200228G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 142864, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PM3", "PP1", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Intronic splice variant (c.1187-10G>A) that activates a cryptic splice acceptor site, leading to retention of 8 nucleotides from intron 8 in the mRNA. This causes a frameshift and premature stop codon (p.Gly396Aspfs*20), resulting in loss of function. LDLR loss-of-function is an established mechanism for familial hypercholesterolemia. RNA studies from homozygous patients confirmed aberrant splicing (PMID: 26077743, 19208450).", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect: (1) RNA assays in EBV-transformed lymphocytes from heterozygous and homozygous patients showed aberrant splicing with retention of 8 nucleotides from intron 8 (PMID: 26077743, 19208450); (2) FACS assays showed 50-75% reduced LDLR activity in heterozygous patients and significantly reduced activity in homozygous patients (PMID: 21865347, 19208450); (3) SpliceAI score of 1.00 predicts complete splice disruption.", "PS4": "Variant identified in \u226510 unrelated individuals with familial hypercholesterolemia across multiple populations (Caucasian, Chinese, Filipino, French) in published literature (PMID: 11668627, 12436241, 16205024, 20145306, 24075752, 26077743, 30512145, 33418990, 33994402). Prevalence in affected individuals significantly exceeds population frequency (gnomAD: 0.002-0.003%).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases: gnomAD exome AF = 2.8e-05 (7/250,138 alleles); gnomAD genome AF = 1.97e-05. Below ClinGen FH VCEP threshold of <0.0002 for PM2.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in compound heterozygous patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia (PMID: 36325061). Also observed in homozygous state in severely affected child with parental confirmation (PMID: 26077743).", "PP1": "Strong co-segregation with disease in multiple families: segregated with hypercholesterolemia in 9 heterozygous individuals and 1 homozygous child in a large Chinese family (PMID: 26077743); \u22656 informative meioses across multiple families (PMID: 26077743, 33569482).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-established single genetic etiology with LDLR being the primary causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar consensus classification: Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic with 24 submissions from reputable clinical laboratories (21 contributing to aggregate classification). Multiple submitters applied ACMG criteria including Mayo Clinic, Invitae/Labcorp, GeneDx, Ambry Genetics, and Laboratory for Molecular Medicine."}}
{"variant_id": "62cd0837-4e16-4f5f-b336-16df4f115be5", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36171774A>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 111577, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "This is an intronic variant (c.806-15T>C) located 15 nucleotides from the splice acceptor site. VEP annotation confirms 'intron_variant' as the most severe consequence with MODIFIER impact. Position -15 is outside the canonical splice region (\u00b11-2) and beyond the extended splice region (\u00b13-8) where splicing effects are typically observed. No predicted splice impact based on distance from splice junction.", "BP6": "ClinVar (Allele ID: 1902242) reports this variant as 'Likely benign' for both 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1' and 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome'. Multiple RCV records support this classification.", "notable": "Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines (PMID:31648317, 35764482), intronic variants outside canonical splice sites require functional evidence of splicing disruption to be considered pathogenic. This variant at position -15 is well outside the critical splice region. RUNX1 loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism for FPD/AML, but this intronic variant does not create a null allele."}}
{"variant_id": "6cfd1468-2fa2-43a0-9727-110981cd0b65", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45367068A>C", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 656937, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T02:50:33.359769Z\",\"request_id\":\"c199b"}
{"variant_id": "81753851-bece-428c-b136-fbf34c30b40e", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78086450G>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 81636, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome (AF = 1.21e-05, 3/248,000+ alleles). For autosomal recessive Pompe disease, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity and meets PM2 threshold.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variant. The p.Arg600Leu (c.1799G>T) variant at the same amino acid position is classified as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic in ClinVar, supporting pathogenicity of this p.Arg600His variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 1.0). Variant affects a conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glycogen Storage Disease Type II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA gene mutations. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic (VCV000370130) with multiple independent submissions. HGMD entries (CM074878, CM990614) also document disease association. Multiple PMIDs support pathogenicity (19862843, 18757064, 24715333, 18995995, 10338092, 21920843, 31130284).", "notable": "The ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP has published GAA-specific ACMG/AMP guidelines (PMID: 37907381) and has curated 243 GAA variants. Loss of function is a known mechanism for Pompe disease (enzyme deficiency). This variant is in the glycoside hydrolase family 31 catalytic domain (Pfam PF01055)."}}
{"variant_id": "aed4706a-e502-48b4-8417-bb5c3aa01461", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.41258494C>T", "gene": "BRCA1", "disease": "BRCA1-related cancer predisposition", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "ENIGMA BRCA1 and BRCA2 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 51628, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5", "PS3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Multiple functional studies demonstrate loss of function. CIViC evidence (EID11131, PMID:20516115) supports loss of function. PMID:21473589 shows impact on BRCT domain phosphopeptide recognition. PMID:22889855 (ENIGMA consortium) demonstrates functional abrogation conferring intermediate cancer risk.", "PM1": "Located in the BRCT domain (Pfam PF00533, SMART SM00292), a critical functional domain essential for phosphopeptide binding and DNA damage response. Multiple structural studies (PDB: 1jnx, 1t15, 3coj, etc.) confirm this residue is within the functional domain.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.39e-05 (6 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 1.32e-05. Well below the 0.01% threshold for dominant disorders.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = possibly/probably damaging (scores 0.61-1.0 across transcripts). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (BRCA1-related cancer predisposition) is highly specific for BRCA1-associated hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome, which has a well-established single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic with multiple submissions from expert laboratories (VCV000037636). Multiple RCV records support pathogenicity for hereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome, familial breast cancer, and BRCA1-related cancer predisposition."}}
{"variant_id": "756eeb9f-e985-4813-90f9-4aa49258e73a", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.108236086C>T", "gene": "ATM", "disease": "ATM-related cancer predisposition", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Very Strong", "PS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54671, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the ATM kinase domain (PI3K-related kinase domain, SMART:SM00146). The p.Arg3008 residue is within a critical functional domain essential for ATM kinase activity. Multiple structural mappings confirm domain location (PDB: 5np0, 5np1, 6k9k, 7ni4-6, 7sic-d, 8oxm-q).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=1.59\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (4 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=1.97\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (3 alleles). Total ~7 alleles in >300,000 individuals, well below PM2 threshold for dominant cancer predisposition.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (score 0.892). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue in kinase domain. COSMIC entries (COSM21642, COSM1561109) indicate somatic occurrence in cancer.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic from multiple submitters (VCV000142187). Classifications include: Pathogenic for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Pathogenic for gastric cancer, Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic for ataxia-telangiectasia, Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic for familial breast cancer, Likely pathogenic for ATM-related cancer predisposition. Multiple RCV accessions support consensus.", "notable": "CIViC evidence (EID2223) indicates R3008C confers resistance to doxorubicin in CLL (PMID:23585524). HGMD mutation entry (CM000656) confirms disease association. Literature identifies this variant in metastatic prostate cancer cohort (PMID:37118955) and gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma (PMID:35078243). ATM is established tumor suppressor where LOF is known disease mechanism for cancer predisposition."}}
{"variant_id": "dc449eb6-2adf-42e5-9acc-d6d8c6d0118b", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38990371G>C", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Moderate", "PM1", "PS3_Moderate", "PS4_Moderate", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83329, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PM2", "PP1", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Functional studies in HEK293 cells and patient myotubes demonstrated increased sensitivity to RYR1 agonists, supporting a damaging effect (PMID: 27586648, 15210166). Applied at moderate strength per ClinGen MHS VCEP specifications.", "PS4": "Variant reported in 5 unrelated individuals with personal or family history of malignant hyperthermia reaction; 4 had positive IVCT/CHCT diagnostic test results (PMID: 12434264, 24433488, 25268394). Applied at moderate strength per ClinGen MHS VCEP.", "PM1": "Located in a mutational hotspot region of RYR1 known to harbor pathogenic variants contributing to malignant hyperthermia susceptibility (PMID: 21118704).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database at time of expert panel interpretation. Variant is extremely rare, consistent with pathogenic status for this autosomal dominant condition.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with malignant hyperthermia susceptibility demonstrated in 6 affected individuals across multiple families (PMID: 12434264, 14641996). Applied at moderate strength per ClinGen MHS VCEP.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably damaging (score 0.998), REVEL=0.905 (>0.85 threshold). Applied at moderate strength per ClinGen MHS VCEP.", "PP5": "ClinGen Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (July 2022) with FDA-recognized database status. PharmGKB Level 1A evidence for drug response (volatile anesthetics, succinylcholine)."}}
{"variant_id": "7b8b8c9c-da02-4129-b0b8-42009c27d9cc", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.229567467C>A", "gene": "ACTA1", "disease": "alpha-actinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Strong", "PVS1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57163, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.990+1G>T) at the +1 position of intron 6 in ACTA1. This is a null variant type (splice donor \u00b11/2) in a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for nemaline myopathy and alpha-actinopathy. ACTA1 splice variants are known to cause aberrant splicing leading to exon skipping or intron retention, resulting in non-functional protein or nonsense-mediated decay.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF = 1.19e-05, 3 alleles total). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal recessive disorder. The variant is absent from most population subgroups (gnomAD genome: AF = 1.97e-05).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic (VCV000464139) with multiple submissions for alpha-actinopathy and actin accumulation myopathy. Multiple independent clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "01e24f51-2715-4a65-be17-9adaa7b8d808", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259326C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75905, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg201Ter) in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease. RUNX1 haploinsufficiency causes familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). The variant creates a premature stop codon at position 201 (or 174 in alternate transcripts), truncating the protein within the critical Runt homology domain (RHD). This is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a severely truncated non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 1.369e-06 (approximately 1 allele in 730,000). This is well below the expected frequency for a pathogenic variant in an autosomal dominant disorder with reduced penetrance. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disorder (FPDMM). This syndrome has a well-established single genetic etiology with RUNX1 germline mutations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000376018). Conditions include: Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1, RUNX1-related disorder, and Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. Supporting PMIDs: 24100448, 10508512."}}
{"variant_id": "8af9da9e-f9d6-4adb-8482-a4870cad8cfc", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39057615C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73560, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Gly2434Arg) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar VCV000012970 reports this exact variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions for MHS1, central core myopathy, and RYR1-related disorders. HGMD entry CM941269 confirms pathogenicity.", "PM1": "Located in the RYR1 gene which encodes the ryanodine receptor 1, a critical calcium release channel in skeletal muscle. The variant affects a conserved glycine residue in a functional domain. RYR1 has well-characterized mutational hotspots associated with malignant hyperthermia.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 0.0001012 (8 alleles/~251,000 total), gnomAD genome AF = 0.00005257 (8 alleles/~152,000 total). This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for a condition with reduced penetrance.", "PP2": "RYR1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation relative to pathogenic missense variants.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. PolyPhen scores range from 0.33-0.858 (benign to possibly damaging across transcripts). SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0). While individual scores are moderate, the consensus across tools supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia susceptibility) is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. MHS1 has a well-defined genetic etiology with RYR1 being the primary causative gene.", "PP5": "Multiple reputable sources report as pathogenic: ClinVar (VCV000012970) with multiple submitters, HGMD (CM941269), PharmGKB (PA166155544). Associated with drug response/toxicity to volatile anesthetics and succinylcholine."}}
{"variant_id": "1d7ecaa8-a3e7-484d-96c5-4e72a6a2ce12", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68896799G>A", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate", "PM3", "PM5", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64648, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=5.57\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (14/251,214 alleles), genome AF=3.19\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (1/31,396 alleles). For autosomal recessive disease, this frequency is consistent with pathogenic variant (well below 0.1% threshold).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.941). Arginine to tryptophan substitution represents significant physicochemical change.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for RPE65-associated inherited retinal dystrophy. RPE65 mutations account for 0.6-6% of RP and 3-16% of LCA/EORD cases, with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with 12 independent submissions (VCV000013115) for multiple RPE65-related conditions including LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. Multiple expert panels and clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic.", "notable": "This variant (p.Arg91Trp) is well-documented in literature across multiple populations (Italian, Chinese, North African, Irish) with consistent pathogenic classification (PMIDs: 35129589, 35551639, 31925606, 27624628). RPE65 gene therapy (voretigene neparvovec/Luxturna) is FDA-approved for patients with biallelic RPE65 mutations, making this an actionable finding."}}
{"variant_id": "d8fabf90-19f4-4693-87f9-0d08b2826ba4", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.70330809G>T", "gene": "IL2RG", "disease": "T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency due to gamma chain deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1", "PP4"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76064, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant not found in gnomAD or other population databases. The genomic coordinates NC_000023.10:g.70330809G>T returned no population frequency data in myvariant or VEP queries, consistent with an extremely rare or private variant. Per ACMG guidelines, absence from population databases supports PM2 for rare disease variants.", "PP3": "While direct computational predictions (CADD, DITTO) could not be retrieved for this specific variant due to coordinate mapping issues, the clinical context of IL2RG variants causing X-SCID strongly suggests functional impact. IL2RG loss-of-function variants are well-established to cause disease through disruption of cytokine receptor signaling essential for lymphocyte development.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency due to gamma chain deficiency is highly specific for IL2RG mutations. X-SCID caused by IL2RG mutations has a single genetic etiology with characteristic T-B+NK- immunophenotype. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established (PMID: 33959125, 39176082, 41164818).", "notable": "PVS1 could not be definitively applied as the specific variant consequence (nonsense, frameshift, splice site) could not be confirmed from the provided genomic coordinates. VEP annotation mapped the coordinates to KIF4A intron rather than IL2RG, suggesting potential coordinate discrepancy. If this variant is confirmed to be a null variant (nonsense, frameshift, or canonical splice site) in IL2RG, PVS1 would apply and upgrade classification to Pathogenic. IL2RG is well-established as a gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease (X-SCID), with extensive literature support (>690 publications in PubMed). Knowledge graph confirms IL2RG association with severe combined immunodeficiency."}}
{"variant_id": "5fe1934d-e35e-4f18-9095-389cc95f3639", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.48244792G>A", "gene": "SGCA", "disease": "autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PM3"], "expert_panel": "Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65382, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.39e-05 (6/251,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 1.31e-05. For an autosomal recessive disorder, this extremely low frequency supports PM2.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. PolyPhen scores range from 0.723 (possibly damaging) to 0.968 (probably damaging) across transcripts. While SIFT predicts tolerated (0.13), the PolyPhen predictions and the variant's location in a conserved functional domain support PP3.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy) is highly specific for SGCA-related sarcoglycanopathy (LGMDR3/LGMD2D). SGCA mutations are a well-established cause of this specific phenotype with characteristic clinical features.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000092301) with multiple submissions: 2 Pathogenic and 1 Likely Pathogenic classification for LGMDR3/LGMD2D. Multiple PubMed citations (11 references) support pathogenicity.", "notable": "Variant is registered in HGMD (CM163140, CM951149) as a disease-causing mutation. The p.Arg34His substitution affects a conserved arginine residue in the extracellular domain of alpha-sarcoglycan. SGCA loss-of-function is an established mechanism for LGMD2D/LGMDR3, though this is a missense variant rather than a null variant, so PVS1 does not apply."}}
{"variant_id": "708cdf45-b52a-42f5-8db0-407c60064452", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68772227G>C", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BS2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65647, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: overall frequency 1.43e-06 (0.000143%), with only East Asian population showing 5.585e-05. This is well below the 0.01% threshold for rare variants in autosomal dominant conditions.", "notable": "ClinVar reports conflicting interpretations (VCV000230669) with most submissions classifying as Uncertain Significance. The same genomic position has a pathogenic nonsense variant (c.76G>T, p.Glu26Ter) but this does NOT support PM5 as PM5 requires a different missense at the same position, not a truncating variant. SIFT (tolerated, 0.32-0.4) and PolyPhen (benign, 0.062-0.177) both predict benign effect. Position 26 is in the signal peptide region which is cleaved during protein maturation, potentially reducing functional impact of missense changes in this region. CDH1 loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism for HDGC, but this missense variant lacks evidence of functional impairment."}}
{"variant_id": "6e8eafc1-1051-447d-8cd5-574da313694e", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121432001C>T", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate", "PVS1", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63502, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases.", "notable": "PM2 not met: Variant present in gnomAD at AF ~4.6e-05 (18 alleles total across exome/genome), which exceeds the extremely low frequency threshold for a dominant disorder with ~1/10,000 prevalence. PP3 not met: SIFT predicts 'tolerated' (0.08-0.12) and PolyPhen predicts 'benign' (0.03-0.26) in most transcripts. CADD/DITTO scores not available. ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations including 'likely_benign' submissions. Variant is in the transactivation domain (PF04812) but no functional studies demonstrate damaging effect."}}
{"variant_id": "9d0aecdb-8e42-4e28-9d7e-d2ed3dc4e264", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78086699G>T", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Strong", "PM5", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 131006, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant not found in gnomAD or other population databases. For autosomal recessive disorders, PM2 is applied at supporting level per ClinGen recommendations. Absence from population databases supports rarity.", "notable": "This is a 5' UTR variant (c.-123C>T) in the GAA gene. 5' UTR variants are generally considered to have lower pathogenic potential compared to coding or canonical splice site variants. The variant is located 46bp upstream of the canonical GAA transcript start site. No functional studies, ClinVar submissions, or literature reports were found for this specific variant. GAA loss-of-function is the established mechanism for Pompe disease, but 5' UTR variants typically do not cause complete loss of function unless they affect critical regulatory elements. ClinVar shows multiple 5' UTR variants in GAA classified as Benign/Likely Benign."}}
{"variant_id": "e5e3150c-8593-41b4-b9c7-ef6ab87624f5", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231663C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BA1", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 40343, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.64% in gnomAD genome (0.19% in exome) exceeds expected frequency for a rare autosomal dominant disorder. Frequency reaches 2.4-2.6% in African populations, far exceeding disease prevalence.", "BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.613+108G>A) located 108 bp from nearest exon boundary. VEP predicts 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact. No splice site disruption predicted. No CADD or DITTO scores available for this non-coding variant, but position and consequence strongly suggest no functional impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (VCV001219872) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome, with additional Likely Benign classification for unspecified conditions. Multiple submissions support benign interpretation."}}
{"variant_id": "aa18502e-2631-4d78-8a48-f05bee4c1509", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.138612974C>T", "gene": "F9", "disease": "hemophilia B", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56034, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exome is 0.068% (677/1,000,000 alleles), which exceeds expected frequency for hemophilia B (disease prevalence ~1:30,000 males). This frequency is too high for a pathogenic variant in a rare X-linked disorder.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (VCV000697610, RCV001830877, RCV000864557) for Hereditary factor IX deficiency disease (Hemophilia B) with multiple submissions supporting benign classification.", "BP7": "This is a synonymous variant (c.51C>T, p.Ile17=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No predicted splice impact - variant is located in exon 2, not near canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions)."}}
{"variant_id": "14304a9f-8fc4-4d51-a274-047d5536a79f", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.45657052G>C", "gene": "GATM", "disease": "AGAT deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PS3_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61283, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3_Supporting": "Functional study (PMID: 27233232) demonstrated <10% of wild-type AGAT enzyme activity via site-directed mutagenesis in HeLa cells. ClinGen CCDS Expert Panel applied PS3 at supporting level due to assay limitations (overexpression system, single study).", "PM2_Supporting": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.1.0: AF = 0.000001695 (2/1,179,822 alleles in European non-Finnish population). Below ClinGen CCDS VCEP threshold of 0.000055 for PM2_Supporting. Consistent with rare autosomal recessive disorder (AGAT deficiency prevalence <1/1,000,000).", "notable": "ClinGen CCDS Expert Panel (April 2025) classified as VUS applying PS3_Supporting, PM2_Supporting, and BP4. Computational predictors (SIFT=0.48 tolerated, PolyPhen=0.031 benign, REVEL=0.04) suggest benign effect (BP4), but functional data showing severely reduced enzyme activity (<10%) provides conflicting evidence supporting pathogenicity. The variant was found in a control individual as heterozygous, which is expected for a recessive condition carrier."}}
{"variant_id": "791488da-e5d8-4596-95b1-53079e87e817", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.138644147T>G", "gene": "F9", "disease": "hemophilia B", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 215669, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the serine protease (SP) domain of F9, a critical functional domain essential for catalytic activity. The Cys435 residue forms a disulfide bond critical for protein structure. Multiple HGMD mutations at this position (CM112729, CM125301, CM960608) indicate this is a mutational hotspot.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for this X-linked recessive disorder.", "PM5": "Three different HGMD mutations (CM112729, CM125301, CM960608) are documented at the same amino acid position (Cys435), indicating that other amino acid substitutions at this position are established as pathogenic.", "PP2": "F9 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (hemophilia B). The serine protease domain has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). The Cys435Gly substitution disrupts a conserved cysteine residue involved in disulfide bond formation.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hemophilia B) is highly specific for F9 gene mutations. Hemophilia B is an X-linked recessive bleeding disorder with a single genetic etiology (F9 gene).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Hereditary factor IX deficiency disease (HEMB). ClinVar allele ID: 3401361."}}
{"variant_id": "e0a2dd66-32dc-4175-a9a7-5c38699e4566", "variant": "NC_000005.9:g.35857120T>C", "gene": "IL7R", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency, autosomal recessive, T cell-negative, B cell-positive, NK cell-positive", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71601, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs2149893604 is absent from gnomAD (frequency = 0 across all populations including gnomAD exomes: AFR, AMR, ASJ, EAS, FIN, MID, NFE, SAS). For an autosomal recessive disorder, absence from population databases supports PM2.", "notable": "This is a deep intronic variant (c.82+61T>C) located 61 bp into intron 1 of IL7R. VEP classifies it as an intron_variant with MODIFIER impact. While IL7R loss-of-function mutations are a known mechanism for T-B+NK+ SCID, this variant is not at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and is not predicted to affect splicing by standard tools. The variant is not in ClinVar. Literature describes pathogenic IL7R variants causing SCID, including synonymous variants affecting splicing (PMID:27833609, PMID:38587703), but these affect exonic splicing enhancers or create cryptic splice sites - mechanisms not applicable to this deep intronic position. Without functional studies demonstrating splice disruption or other pathogenic mechanism, this intronic variant cannot be classified as pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "ee804ee2-6db6-463d-b90d-51e2fd2374f2", "variant": "NC_000013.10:g.20763719A>G", "gene": "GJB2", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5", "PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 87547, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect: (1) Kim et al. 2015 (PMID:26088551) showed significantly reduced biochemical coupling in Cx26-V37I-transfected HEK293T cells; (2) Lin et al. 2019 (PMID:31562289) generated knock-in mouse model recapitulating human phenotype with reduced gap junction plaque length, mild endocochlear potential drop, and compromised cochlear amplification; (3) Chen et al. 2024 (PMID:38831582) confirmed deficient gap junction coupling.", "PS4": "Variant is significantly enriched in affected individuals. Meta-analysis (PMID:28489599) and multiple population studies demonstrate strong association with hearing loss. Kriukelis et al. 2024 (PMID:38486023) found V37I as the most frequent variant in Australian pediatric hearing loss cohort. Multiple case-control studies show significant enrichment in hearing loss patients vs controls.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (nonsyndromic genetic deafness) is highly specific for GJB2-related DFNB1A, which has a well-established single genetic etiology. GJB2 mutations account for ~50% of autosomal recessive nonsyndromic hearing loss.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000017023). Multiple expert panels and clinical laboratories classify as pathogenic, with evidence available for review.", "notable": "PM2 NOT met: gnomAD AF=0.77% (exome) and 0.62% (genome), with up to 7% in East Asian populations - this exceeds typical PM2 thresholds. However, this is consistent with the variant's low penetrance and mild phenotype. BP4 consideration: SIFT predicts 'tolerated_low_confidence' (0.06), but functional studies override computational predictions. The variant demonstrates reduced penetrance and variable expressivity, typically causing mild-to-moderate late-onset hearing loss."}}
{"variant_id": "a4171750-2311-4219-b360-9f6ad59166a1", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14977490T>C", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75157, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency) is highly specific for a disease with single genetic etiology. DCLRE1C mutations are a well-established cause of T-B-NK+ SCID (Artemis deficiency).", "notable": "PM2 not met: Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (1.316e-05 overall, 2.944e-05 in NFE). For autosomal recessive disorders, PM2 requires extremely low frequency or absence. This frequency is borderline but technically present. PVS1 not applicable: This is an intronic variant (ENST00000467536.1:n.66+4870T>C) located deep within an intron (~4.8kb from splice site), not a canonical splice site variant (\u00b11/2). VEP annotates as 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact. PP3 not met: No computational evidence of splice impact or deleterious effect. VEP shows MODIFIER impact with no predicted functional consequence. The variant is located in MEIG1 gene region per VEP annotation, though clinical context suggests DCLRE1C involvement."}}
{"variant_id": "7aade9cf-c2bd-4f71-bc0c-964c6aa7a669", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605813G>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83831, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PP3", "BS3_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP3": "REVEL score = 0.664, within the ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP PP3 range (0.644-0.772), predicting a damaging effect on MYOC function. However, SIFT = 0.07 (tolerated) and PolyPhen = 0.488 (possibly damaging) show mixed predictions.", "BS3_Supporting": "Functional study (PMID: 36579626) demonstrated that Thr256Met protein had similar thermal stability levels compared to wild-type myocilin protein. The assay met the OddsPath threshold for BS3_Moderate (<0.23), indicating this variant did not impact protein function. Applied at Supporting level per standard ACMG framework.", "notable": "ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP (v2.0.0, Dec 2024) classified this variant as Uncertain Significance with score of -1. gnomAD frequency (0.0001559 in East Asian) did not meet PM2_Supporting threshold (\u22640.0001) per VCEP specifications. Variant is located in the olfactomedin domain (Pfam PF02191), a critical functional domain for MYOC. No segregation data or de novo evidence available."}}
{"variant_id": "31011de0-2c21-4068-9234-833617f290cc", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103245512C>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS1", "PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55441, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Multiple in vitro expression studies show p.Arg408Trp results in only 1.3-1.85% of wild-type PAH enzyme activity (PMID:17935162, PMID:25596310). Protein expression studies in E.coli showed 100% protein aggregation indicating severe folding defect and complete loss of function (PMID:18538294). The variant is located in the catalytic domain and leads to complete disruption of structural integrity.", "PM3_Strong": "For this autosomal recessive disorder, the variant has been detected in trans with multiple pathogenic variants (IVS12+1G>A, M1V) in numerous affected individuals (PMID:9634518, PMID:1971147, PMID:1609797). ClinGen PAH Expert Panel applied PM3 at Strong level based on extensive compound heterozygous observations.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT: deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen-2: probably_damaging (score=0.997-0.999), REVEL: 0.89 (>0.75 threshold). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency, which has a single genetic etiology. This is the most common PAH mutation in European populations, consistently associated with classic PKU phenotype. ClinGen PAH Expert Panel applied PP4 at Moderate level.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports Pathogenic classification from ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, Aug 2018) with 40+ concordant submissions. This is an FDA Recognized Database classification. Multiple reputable laboratories (GeneDx, Invitae, Ambry, Mayo Clinic) independently classify as Pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "7ed0a7a6-a85c-4faf-8a42-5ac1a5559d6b", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1399009A>G", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 417415, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs2144636453 (NM_000156.6:c.476T>C, p.Leu159Pro) is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in any population, consistent with an extremely rare variant. For autosomal recessive GAMT deficiency, absence from population databases supports PM2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999). The variant causes a Leu159Pro substitution, introducing a proline residue which disrupts protein secondary structure. The variant is located within a conserved methyltransferase domain (PROSITE PS51559, Gene3D, PANTHER PTHR32379). snpEff annotates this as a structural_interaction_variant affecting protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency) is highly specific for GAMT gene mutations. GAMT deficiency is a well-characterized autosomal recessive disorder with a single genetic etiology. The clinical presentation (intellectual disability, seizures, movement disorders) is pathognomonic for this condition.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV003159214) and Likely Pathogenic (RCV001816225) for GAMT deficiency (VCV001335317). HGMD also catalogs this variant (CM144318). UniProt lists this as VAR_071784. Multiple reputable sources classify this variant as pathogenic/likely pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "326c25fb-e8bf-44cd-83e0-6f57e005411d", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48807599G>A", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PS2_Supporting", "PM1", "PP2", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68411, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Variant identified in 14 affected individuals from 2 unrelated families with Marfan syndrome and aortic aneurysms/dissections (PMID:30485715). Multiple ClinVar submissions report pathogenicity with segregation in affected families.", "PM1": "Located in cbEGF-like domain (calcium-binding EGF domain) of fibrillin-1, a critical functional domain. Cysteine substitutions in cbEGF domains disrupt disulfide bonds essential for domain structure and calcium binding, which is a well-established pathogenic mechanism in FBN1.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for a dominant disorder with ~1:5000 prevalence.", "PP2": "FBN1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Cysteine substitutions in cbEGF domains are particularly pathogenic as they disrupt critical disulfide bonds. Low rate of benign missense variation in this gene.", "PP3": "Computational predictions support deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen = possibly damaging (score 0.719). Arginine to cysteine substitution introduces a reactive thiol group that disrupts normal protein structure.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000016466) with multiple independent submissions for Marfan syndrome and familial thoracic aortic aneurysm/dissection. Also listed in HGMD (CM056956) and OMIM (134797.0047)."}}
{"variant_id": "f9d2ab1b-971b-4536-826d-99d4f2dd7426", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.4101062G>T", "gene": "MAP2K2", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 49029, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency of 47.8% in gnomAD exome and 42.6% in gnomAD genome far exceeds the 5% threshold for stand-alone benign classification. This is a common polymorphism in the general population.", "BP6": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Benign with multiple submissions for RASopathy, Cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome 4 (CFC4), and cardiovascular phenotype (ClinVar allele ID: 49286).", "BP7": "This is a synonymous variant (c.660C>A, p.Ile220=) that does not change the amino acid sequence. VEP analysis shows no predicted splice impact - the variant is located within the coding region (not at splice sites) with consequence 'synonymous_variant' and LOW impact."}}
{"variant_id": "b4cbc77a-3fee-4506-8590-ba240224bdb4", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38990643C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS4_Moderate", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71507, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Gly2434Arg) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000012970). OMIM entry 180901.0007 confirms established pathogenicity.", "PM1": "Located in RYR1 gene where the ClinGen RYR1-MHS Expert Panel has identified mutational hotspots. RYR1 missense variants in critical functional domains are associated with malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. Per ClinGen guidelines, PM1 hotspot criterion has OR of 24:1 for RYR1.", "PM2": "Rare variant in gnomAD: AF=0.0000318 (exome) and AF=0.0000526 (genome). Present at extremely low frequency consistent with pathogenic variant for autosomal dominant condition with reduced penetrance.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. PolyPhen: 0.466-0.858 (possibly damaging). SIFT: deleterious (score 0). Multiple transcripts show consistent damaging predictions.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia susceptibility) is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. RYR1 is the primary gene associated with MHS1, and the phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic from multiple submitters including expert panels. Associated with MHS1, central core myopathy, and RYR1-related disorders. Also classified for drug response (toxicity to volatile anesthetics and succinylcholine)."}}
{"variant_id": "860ebbbe-423f-4462-b5e0-164fffe40652", "variant": "NC_000004.11:g.995305T>C", "gene": "IDUA", "disease": "mucopolysaccharidosis type 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54907, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS3", "PM3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp402Ter) creating premature stop codon in exon 9 of 14 exons in IDUA gene. Loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for MPS I. Predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) as the premature termination codon is located >54 nucleotides upstream of the final exon-exon junction.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate complete loss of IDUA enzyme activity. Transient expression in COS-7 cells showed complete loss of IDUA activity (PMID: 11735025). Knock-in mouse model homozygous for analogous variant (Idua Trp392Ter) showed phenotype closely correlating with human MPS1 features (PMID: 19751987).", "PM3": "For this autosomal recessive disorder, variant has been detected in trans with pathogenic variants in numerous affected individuals. At least 38 homozygotes and 73+ compound heterozygotes reported (PMID: 1301196, 28752568, 11735025, 30809705). This is the most common MPS I variant in multiple populations (US 45%, UK 45%, Germany 50%, Spain 62%).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (mucopolysaccharidosis type 1) is highly specific for IDUA-related disease. MPS I has a single genetic etiology (IDUA gene). Patients reported with detailed clinical features including elevated urine GAGs and deficient IDUA enzyme activity.", "PP5": "Reviewed by ClinGen Lysosomal Storage Disorder Variant Curation Expert Panel (January 2025) as Pathogenic. 30+ submitters in ClinVar unanimously classify as Pathogenic. FDA Recognized Database entry.", "notable": "gnomAD frequency (0.0006-0.001) is higher than typical for pathogenic variants but below BS1 threshold for recessive disorders. ClinGen VCEP determined this does not meet PM2 threshold (<0.00025) but also does not meet BS1 (>0.0025). No homozygotes observed in gnomAD population databases."}}
{"variant_id": "6663dc62-0d62-4323-967d-4431216d3b1f", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11215925C>T", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67490, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in LDL-A repeat/ligand-binding domain (SMART SM00192, Pfam PF00057, PROSITE PS50068) - a critical functional domain essential for LDL binding. This domain contains highly conserved cysteine residues forming disulfide bonds; the R115C substitution introduces an additional cysteine that may disrupt domain structure.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.79e-05 (7/250,714 alleles). This frequency is below the expected threshold for a dominant disorder with high penetrance like familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical domains, and missense variants causing FH are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0-0.04), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.942-0.975). Consistent predictions across all protein-coding transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the most common causative gene (~85-90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely pathogenic/Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000251162). Also catalogued in HGMD (CM055402) as disease-causing mutation.", "notable": "PVS1 not applicable as this is a missense variant, not a null variant. PS1/PM5 not met as no established pathogenic variant at this exact amino acid position was identified. PS3 not met as no specific functional studies for this variant were found, though the domain is well-characterized."}}
{"variant_id": "9f86afbc-b31d-472c-ac5d-ee0799f21c9c", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.66729180T>C", "gene": "MAP2K1", "disease": "cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PM6_Strong", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 654762, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T03:00:37.029730Z\",\"request_id\":\"2ae6d"}
{"variant_id": "2e8e98fe-73fe-4082-9d1e-681d43b94bca", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45367138A>G", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PM3_Supporting", "PM5_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 139076, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PS3", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Although annotated as synonymous (p.Gly477=), functional studies demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing leading to exon 10 deletions (95bp, 155bp, 261bp) and protein truncation. This effectively creates a null allele in ITGB3, where loss of function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive).", "PS3": "Well-established functional study (PMID: 37716584) using minigene splicing assay demonstrated that c.1431C>T causes three types of aberrant splicing events, resulting in protein truncation and significantly declined ITGB3 protein expression. Western blotting confirmed reduced protein levels.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in population controls, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal recessive disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGB3/ITGA2B mutations. This is a well-characterized inherited platelet disorder with a single genetic etiology involving the integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23 complex.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (Allele ID: 3401372, RCV accession: NM_000212.3(ITGB3):c.1431C>T)."}}
{"variant_id": "be1f9e39-8225-4a2c-ab44-d75c12a1681d", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7123978T>C", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66792, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=3.97e-06 (1 allele/251,000), genome AF=6.57e-06. For autosomal recessive VLCADD, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing alleles. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (0.00-0.03), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.971-0.999). Variant affects conserved valine residue at position 87 in Gene3D domain. Meets PP3 threshold.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (VLCADD) is highly specific for ACADVL gene. VLCADD has a single genetic etiology with ACADVL being the only causative gene. Phenotype-genotype correlation supports pathogenicity.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies as VUS (VCV000203570). No functional studies found for this specific variant. For autosomal recessive inheritance, PM3 could be applied if variant is confirmed in trans with another pathogenic variant. ACMG/AMP specifications for ACADVL (PMID:37549443) provide gene-specific guidance."}}
{"variant_id": "e78376c1-7f08-4335-87ea-e4c47d2801ff", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.108119667A>G", "gene": "ATM", "disease": "hereditary breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS1", "BP2_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55631, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD (0.083% genome, 0.016% exome) exceeds expected frequency for a pathogenic ATM variant in hereditary breast cancer. ATM pathogenic variants are typically very rare (<0.01%).", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.09), PolyPhen=benign (0.0). No evidence of deleterious impact on protein function.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports predominantly Benign/Likely benign classifications from multiple submitters for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, ataxia-telangiectasia, familial breast cancer, and ATM-related disorders. Only one VUS submission for breast/ovarian cancer."}}
{"variant_id": "a0d2f8e1-aad3-4fe8-b45c-4e716663a496", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.140477853C>A", "gene": "BRAF", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PS3", "PM2", "PP3", "PP2", "PM6_Strong"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83016, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Leu485Phe) previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000013975) with multiple submissions classifying as Pathogenic for CFC syndrome and RASopathy. HGMD entry CM060880 confirms disease-causing status.", "PM1": "Located in the BRAF protein kinase domain (Pfam PF07714, SMART SM00220, PROSITE PS50011). This is a critical functional domain where germline mutations cause RASopathies including CFC syndrome. The kinase domain is a well-established mutational hotspot for both germline RASopathy and somatic cancer mutations.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD v4.0 population database (frequency = 0 across all populations). This meets the PM2 criterion for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for disorders caused by BRAF germline mutations. BRAF is one of the major genes associated with cardio-facio-cutaneous syndrome (CFC1, OMIM 115150), a well-defined RASopathy with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000013975) with multiple independent submissions from clinical laboratories. Conditions include RASopathy, CFC syndrome, and Noonan syndrome.", "notable": "CIViC evidence (EID7579, PMID:31515458) supports gain-of-function effect. PMID:34108213 specifically identifies L485F as an oncogenic BRAF mutant with R-spine stability affecting RAF inhibitor resistance. SIFT predicts deleterious effect (score 0), though PolyPhen predicts benign (0.006-0.179). The variant is also observed in COSMIC (COSV56396779) as a somatic mutation in cancer, supporting functional significance."}}
{"variant_id": "dc88e22c-bbbf-4aeb-9c2a-0e3babeaaeed", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7578389G>T", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3_Moderate", "BS3_Supporting", "BS2_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71924, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "BS2_Supporting", "BS3_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v4.1.0 population database. Meets PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen TP53 VCEP specifications.", "PP3": "Computational predictors support deleterious effect: BayesDel=0.204 (>0.16 threshold), Align GVGD=Class C65. VEP shows PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.977) for some transcripts. Applied at moderate level per TP53 VCEP specifications.", "BS2_Supporting": "Observed in 3 heterozygous unrelated females with no personal history of cancer prior to age 60 years and no personal history of sarcoma at any age (Ambry SCV000274425.4). This is inconsistent with Li-Fraumeni syndrome which has high penetrance.", "BS3_Supporting": "In vitro functional assays show partially functional transactivation in yeast assays (PMID:12826609) and retained growth suppression activity in human cell lines with no dominant negative effect (PMID:29979965, 30224644). Functional studies indicate variant does not substantially impact TP53 protein function.", "notable": "ClinGen TP53 Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Uncertain Significance (reviewed by expert panel, March 2025). Different missense variants at same position (p.Arg181His, p.Arg181Cys) are pathogenic, indicating importance of arginine at this position. However, the serine substitution appears to retain function. Variant is in the DNA binding domain (Pfam PF00870). COSMIC entries (COSM11090, COSM45475) indicate somatic occurrence."}}
{"variant_id": "efb54c7a-0e93-446d-8d17-c045ae81e10a", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164684T>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 134682, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is essentially absent from gnomAD population databases (AF = 2.124e-06 overall, only observed in NFE at 2.761e-06). This extremely low frequency in >1.5 million alleles supports rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Germline missense variants in RUNX1, particularly in the Runt homology domain and transactivation domain, are known to cause familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation in functional domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict a deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen-2 = probably damaging (score 0.988). The variant affects a conserved glutamine residue in the C-terminal transactivation domain (Pfam PF08504). Note: CADD and DITTO scores were not available for primary assessment.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM/RUNX1-FPD). This syndrome has a well-defined single genetic etiology with RUNX1 as the causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV001035236). The variant is located in the transactivation domain (C-terminal region) of RUNX1, where pathogenic missense variants have been reported. A validated transactivation assay exists for RUNX1 variant classification (PMID: 35026845) that could provide functional evidence. Recent literature (PMID: 38513139) demonstrates that RUNX1 C-terminal mutations impair blood cell differentiation by perturbing enhancer-promoter networks, supporting functional importance of this domain."}}
{"variant_id": "008bf1cc-6bd3-4b37-b73c-b2e339d3b595", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121431974T>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 146749, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the DNA-binding homeodomain (residues 83-279) of HNF1A, a critical functional domain. Multiple protein domains identified: Pfam PF00046 (Homeodomain), PROSITE PS50071, SMART SM00389. Functional studies (PMID:35257744) demonstrate that variants in this domain cause reduced DNA-binding capacity and protein instability.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in gnomAD exome or genome datasets, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in HNF1A, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY3). HNF1A has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical functional domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-1.0). Consistent predictions across all protein-coding transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), a condition with a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Likely Pathogenic (Allele ID: 1318221, VCV001327609) for Monogenic diabetes. Same rsID (rs2135841104) also has Likely Pathogenic classification for the T>C change at this position."}}
{"variant_id": "7b717baa-5df4-4bbc-8132-edfcceb7b495", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185168C>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 74928, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. rs1235227560 has no reported allele frequency, meeting PM2 threshold for rare variant in a gene where loss-of-function causes disease.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene with a low rate of benign missense variation and where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (MODY2). Over 644 GCK mutations have been described, predominantly missense, causing MODY2 through impaired enzyme activity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly_damaging (score 0.64-0.70). snpEff annotates as structural_interaction_variant affecting protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK mutations account for up to 61% of MODY cases in Southern European populations.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS (VCV001522625). Nearby residue Arg392 has been functionally characterized (PMID:22761713) showing reduced enzyme activity (Ia=0.60). The p.Glu395_Arg397del deletion affecting adjacent residues disrupts Arg394 interactions, suggesting this position is structurally important. However, no direct functional studies exist for p.Arg394Leu specifically."}}
{"variant_id": "808f8d7b-6023-415d-bce5-e3b50e3d2a6d", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36161592T>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50300, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "3' UTR variant (c.*2840A>T) with MODIFIER impact. No predicted effect on protein function. VEP consequence: 3_prime_UTR_variant. No computational evidence supports a deleterious effect on gene expression or splicing.", "BP7": "Non-coding variant in 3' UTR region with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not affect canonical splice sites or protein coding sequence.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (VCV000339818): one submission as 'Benign' and one as 'Uncertain significance'. gnomAD frequency of 0.027% (AF=0.00027) indicates the variant is present in population databases, though at low frequency. Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines (PMID:31648317), 3' UTR variants are generally not considered pathogenic unless functional studies demonstrate impact on gene expression."}}
{"variant_id": "8b920c00-cf31-40ef-a263-35e46162f466", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121437325C>T", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS2", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 45692, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency exceeds 5% in African population (gnomAD_AFR: 5.6%). Global frequency is 1.586%. This exceeds the BA1 stand-alone threshold of >5% for benign classification.", "notable": "CRITICAL: This variant (rs115578627) maps to the KDM2B gene (intron variant c.3829+2532G>A), NOT to HNF1A as indicated in the clinical context. The genomic coordinates NC_000012.11:g.121437325C>T do not correspond to the HNF1A gene. If the patient has monogenic diabetes/MODY, this variant is unlikely to be causative. Recommend verifying the variant coordinates or re-sequencing the HNF1A gene."}}
{"variant_id": "4100a15d-d768-4cdf-9f4e-4e4842b7df8b", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.152473878A>T", "gene": "NEB", "disease": "nemaline myopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52658, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exome is 0.12% (1201/100,000), with South Asian population reaching 1.12%. This exceeds expected frequency for autosomal recessive nemaline myopathy (carrier frequency typically <1% for rare recessive disorders). Meets BS1 threshold.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.58-0.70), PolyPhen=benign (0.001-0.017). No CADD/DITTO scores available, but secondary predictors consistently indicate no damaging effect.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (VCV000499052) with 4 RCV submissions all classifying as Benign for nemaline myopathy 2 (NEM2), nemaline myopathy, and unspecified conditions."}}
{"variant_id": "5e699e3c-5574-4272-a29d-28f2b1354654", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23889429C>T", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58629, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for cardiomyopathy. gnomAD exome AF=0.206% (503 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.186% (58 alleles). Combined frequency ~0.2% significantly exceeds the expected disease frequency threshold for autosomal dominant cardiomyopathy (typically <0.01-0.05%).", "BP4": "Synonymous variant (c.3351G>A, p.Glu1117=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No splice site predictions indicate disruption. CADD and other computational tools not applicable for synonymous variants without splice effects.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign by multiple submitters across multiple conditions including Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (Benign), Cardiovascular phenotype (Benign), Cardiomyopathy (Benign), Dilated Cardiomyopathy (Likely benign), and Left ventricular noncompaction cardiomyopathy (Likely benign). ClinVar Allele ID: 52127, rsID: rs45554236.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Glu1117=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. Codon change gaG>gaA maintains glutamic acid. No predicted splice impact based on VEP analysis showing only 'synonymous_variant' consequence."}}
{"variant_id": "776e37b6-c807-4cd8-99c7-ad18dd7a6391", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68867391G>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63130, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exome is 8.75e-05 (0.00875%), with higher frequency in East Asian populations (gnomAD exome EAS: 0.17%, gnomAD genome EAS: 0.12%). For a highly penetrant autosomal dominant cancer predisposition syndrome like HDGC, this frequency exceeds expected disease prevalence, supporting BS1.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign by multiple submitters for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, CDH1-related disorder, and CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome (VCV000184838). While there are conflicting interpretations for HDGC specifically, the predominant classification trend is toward benign.", "notable": "In-silico predictions show mixed results: SIFT predicts deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen predicts possibly damaging (0.604-0.73). However, computational evidence alone is insufficient to override population frequency and ClinVar consensus. The variant is located in the cytoplasmic domain of E-cadherin (amino acid 880), which is less critical than the extracellular cadherin domains for cell adhesion function."}}
{"variant_id": "f8c03fde-6d9e-4d11-b9a5-6e631ce1d8fd", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103238107G>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67062, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Humanized mouse model carrying c.1066-11G>A demonstrates PAH deficiency pathology (PMID:38520741). This in vivo functional study confirms the variant causes loss of PAH function and phenylketonuria phenotype.", "PS4": "Variant extensively reported in PKU patients across multiple populations: Turkey (PMID:35355500), Iran (PMID:37525467), Jordan (PMID:40630137), Portugal (PMID:33465300), Mexico (PMID:34828281), Brazil (PMID:29749107), Romania (PMID:37189584), Italy (PMID:37509538). Prevalence in affected individuals significantly exceeds controls.", "PM2": "Rare in gnomAD: AF=0.000247 in exomes, AF=0.000255 in genomes. For autosomal recessive PKU, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations and supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports splicing impact. VEP identifies splice_polypyrimidine_tract_variant affecting the polypyrimidine tract 11bp upstream of exon 11 acceptor site. This intronic position is critical for spliceosome recognition.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene mutations) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000000607) for phenylketonuria, hyperphenylalaninemia, and inborn genetic diseases. Also listed in HGMD (CS910455), PAHdb, and OMIM (612349.0033)."}}
{"variant_id": "23f45364-22dd-4a0c-acf0-4d8bea0c95ce", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68844136G>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65252, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS2", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS2": "ClinGen Expert Panel reports variant observed in at least 10-22 individuals without diffuse gastric cancer (DGC), signet ring cell (SRC) tumors, or lobular breast cancer (LBC), and whose families do not suggest hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC). This meets BS2 criteria for observation in healthy adults with full penetrance expected.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=0.14 (tolerated), PolyPhen=0.009 (benign). In silico analysis supports that this variant does not alter protein structure/function. Conservative amino acid change (Val\u2192Ile) with similar biochemical properties.", "notable": "ClinGen Gastric Cancer Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Likely Benign (Aug 2023) using CDH1-specific ACMG specifications v3.1, applying BS2 criterion. Multiple clinical laboratories (Ambry, Invitae/Labcorp) also classify as Likely Benign. gnomAD frequency is very low (AF ~0.00001) but this does not support PM2 given the benign evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "f2fc6a36-08b0-4d07-83a2-f60e3aed090e", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7578421G>A", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3_Supporting", "BS2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53753, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg248Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant (rs121912651) as Pathogenic for Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1 with multiple submissions from expert laboratories.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. CIViC evidence (EID10261, PMID:11896595) shows dominant-negative effect. EID7120 (PMID:8099841) supports oncogenicity. R248 is a DNA-contact residue critical for p53 DNA binding function.", "PM1": "Located in the DNA-binding domain of TP53, a critical functional domain. Codon 248 is one of the most frequently mutated hotspot positions in TP53, with extensive structural data (>300 PDB structures mapping to this region). No benign variation observed at this position.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.98e-06 (1 allele in ~251,000 individuals); gnomAD genome AF = 0. This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "TP53 is a gene with a low rate of benign missense variation and where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. Missense variants in the DNA-binding domain are well-established causes of Li-Fraumeni syndrome.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 1.0). The variant affects a critical DNA-contact residue (Arg248) essential for p53 tumor suppressor function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1) is highly specific for TP53 germline pathogenic variants. LFS has a single genetic etiology with TP53 being the causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000012347). Multiple expert laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic for Li-Fraumeni syndrome and hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome."}}
{"variant_id": "1cc8dfc3-b2c0-40fe-8cab-a2e459188d27", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45369703C>T", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60518, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PS3", "PP5", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Although annotated as synonymous (p.Gly477=), functional studies (PMID:37716584) demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing leading to protein truncation. The minigene assay showed three types of alternative splicing: 95bp deletion, 155bp deletion, and 261bp deletion in exon 10, resulting in loss of functional protein. Loss of function is an established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive). Applied at Very Strong level.", "PS3": "Well-established in vitro functional study (PMID:37716584) using minigene splicing assay and protein expression analysis in 293T cells demonstrated: (1) c.1431C>T causes aberrant mRNA splicing, (2) protein truncation, and (3) declined ITGB3 protein expression. This provides strong evidence of damaging effect on gene product.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. Not found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (Allele ID: 3401372, RCV: NM_000212.3(ITGB3):c.1431C>T). Reputable source with supporting evidence.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGB3/ITGA2B mutations. This is a rare autosomal recessive bleeding disorder with a well-defined single genetic etiology involving the integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23 complex."}}
{"variant_id": "b6ea399d-f7a0-4cd2-b814-7e0bd870f57c", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.18023696G>A", "gene": "MYO15A", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS1_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 57151, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for autosomal recessive disorder. gnomAD exome AF=0.000283 (69 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.000702 (22 alleles). Notably elevated in African populations (AFR=0.31%). For a rare recessive disorder like DFNB3, this frequency is higher than expected.", "BP4": "Computational evidence supports benign effect. SIFT=tolerated (0.39), PolyPhen=benign (0.0). Both primary in-silico predictors indicate no damaging effect on protein function.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Benign by multiple submitters (VCV000504629). Four RCV records classify as Likely Benign for nonsyndromic genetic hearing loss, not specified, not provided, and MYO15A-related disorder."}}
{"variant_id": "eb614114-665c-4124-92d9-26b55c1dfc11", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.42984447G>A", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1_Strong", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66372, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Strong": "Start-loss variant (c.3G>A, p.Met1Ile) affecting the initiation codon in HNF4A (NM_175914.5). This variant abolishes the start codon of the pancreatic-specific HNF4A isoform, predicted to cause truncated or absent protein. Loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for HNF4A-MODY (PMID:23348805). ClinGen MDEP applied PVS1_Strong per their gene-specific specifications (v2.0.0).", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. Applied as PM2_Supporting per ClinGen MDEP specifications.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF4A-MODY (MODY1). Published cases include individuals with MODY probability calculator result >50%, negative HNF1A genetic testing, and negative diabetes autoantibodies (PMID:30977832). Applied as PP4_Moderate per ClinGen MDEP specifications.", "notable": "Additional supporting evidence: (1) Variant identified in 2 unrelated individuals with non-autoimmune diabetes (PMID:21683639, PMID:30977832) but insufficient for PS4 threshold; (2) Segregation with diabetes observed in one family with 2 informative meioses (insufficient for PP1); (3) A different variant at the same initiation codon has been classified as likely pathogenic (supports PS1_Supporting per Exeter lab). ClinVar VCV001299751.4 shows expert panel review status with 'Likely Pathogenic' classification (April 2024)."}}
{"variant_id": "39d43aca-1749-4ce4-9fa8-d7ff03c0e481", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11240272A>G", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM5", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 137453, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in exon 17 of LDLR, within a functionally important region of the receptor. LDLR is a well-established gene for familial hypercholesterolemia with loss-of-function as the disease mechanism. The cytoplasmic domain is critical for receptor internalization.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. This meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in a dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. LDLR has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.933-0.998). Consistent predictions across all transcripts support damaging effect on protein function.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (VCV000252340, RCV000237741) for Hypercholesterolemia, familial, 1. HGMD also lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CM045056). Published in PMID:15556094."}}
{"variant_id": "44753df3-3d83-4cd3-b481-507ace59c997", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.45654417T>C", "gene": "GATM", "disease": "AGAT deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 84597, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (7.002e-07 overall frequency, only 1 allele in NFE population at 9.247e-07). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this extremely low frequency supports PM2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=0.03 (deleterious), PolyPhen=0.708 (possibly damaging). Variant is located in splice region and affects the amidinotransferase functional domain (Pfam PF02274). CADD/DITTO scores not available but secondary predictors support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (AGAT deficiency) is highly specific for GATM-related disease. AGAT deficiency is a well-characterized cerebral creatine deficiency syndrome with single genetic etiology (GATM). ClinGen VCEP has established disease-specific criteria for this condition (PMID:38452609).", "notable": "Variant is classified as VUS in ClinVar (VCV000654184). Located in critical amidinotransferase domain. GATM is established as the sole gene causing AGAT deficiency with autosomal recessive inheritance. Loss of function is the known disease mechanism. No functional studies available for this specific variant. ClinGen CCDS VCEP has curated 45 GATM variants with disease-specific guidelines."}}
{"variant_id": "d2f975d0-90d3-4610-83fe-fbdec78fa50d", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7579885C>G", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS2_Supporting", "BS3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 103312, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg175His) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant as Pathogenic (VCV000012374) with multiple independent submissions for Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1 and hereditary cancer syndromes.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. CIViC evidence (EID10527, EID7106, EID7112) shows dominant-negative effect and loss of DNA-binding function. Multiple publications (PMID:10519380, PMID:27589690, PMID:14743206) confirm loss-of-function and gain-of-function oncogenic properties. R175H is a structural mutant that destabilizes the p53 DNA-binding domain.", "PM1": "Located in the DNA-binding domain (DBD) of TP53 at codon 175, a critical mutational hotspot. This residue is essential for zinc coordination and DNA binding. The DBD is a well-established critical functional domain with minimal benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.98e-06 (1/251,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 6.57e-06 (1/152,000+ alleles). Meets PM2 threshold for absence/extremely low frequency in controls.", "PP2": "Missense variant in TP53, a gene with low rate of benign missense variation and where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. TP53 missense mutations in the DBD are well-established causes of Li-Fraumeni syndrome.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Li-Fraumeni syndrome 1) is highly specific for TP53-related disorders. LFS has a single genetic etiology with TP53 germline mutations accounting for >95% of cases.", "PP5": "Multiple reputable sources report as pathogenic. ClinVar: Pathogenic with multiple 3-star and 4-star submissions. HGMD: CM951224, CM062017. OMIM: 191170.003. Classified as oncogenic in COSMIC."}}
{"variant_id": "9a18dc91-2016-4b25-ab42-a9f679412ae8", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.140501333A>G", "gene": "BRAF", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM6", "PM2", "PP3", "PP2"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73154, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Phe247Leu) at this position has been previously established as pathogenic in ClinVar with multiple independent submissions for Noonan syndrome 7, Cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome 1, and RASopathy conditions.", "PS3": "CIViC database reports functional evidence (EID7576, PMID:31515458 - Yaeger et al., 2019) demonstrating gain-of-function effect for BRAF F247L. BRAF germline mutations in RASopathies are known to cause constitutive activation of the RAS-MAPK signaling pathway.", "PM1": "Located in the BRAF kinase domain, a critical functional region. BRAF is a serine/threonine protein kinase with well-established protein kinase activity, ATP binding, and scaffold protein binding functions. Mutations in this domain are known to cause RASopathies through aberrant MAPK pathway activation.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance.", "PP2": "BRAF is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for RASopathies (Noonan syndrome, CFC syndrome). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for disorders caused by BRAF germline mutations. BRAF is one of the core genes associated with cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome and Noonan syndrome 7, which are RASopathies with distinct clinical features.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic by multiple submitters for Noonan syndrome 7 (NS7), Cardiofaciocutaneous syndrome 1 (CFC1), RASopathy, and Noonan syndrome-related conditions. ClinVar Allele ID: 179102."}}
{"variant_id": "a44cfe6c-ef76-446d-a02b-a1a8d750e63a", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39051868A>G", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 610034, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T03:09:04.089868Z\",\"request_id\":\"ea053"}
{"variant_id": "053bd356-b996-4fb7-a0af-2f676b65c584", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78086403G>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 72885, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical functional domain (Pfam PF01055 - Glycosyl hydrolase family 31). The Arg600 residue is within the catalytic domain of acid alpha-glucosidase, essential for enzyme function. Multiple protein structure mappings confirm this region's functional importance.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF = 1.21e-05, 3 alleles in ~250,000 individuals). For autosomal recessive Pompe disease, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same amino acid position as established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports p.Arg600Leu (c.1799G>T) as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic for the same condition, demonstrating that amino acid changes at this position cause disease.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 1.0). Consistent predictions across all transcripts analyzed.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (glycogen storage disease II/Pompe disease) is highly specific for GAA gene mutations. Pompe disease has a single genetic etiology with GAA being the only causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV000521900, RCV000408964) with multiple submitters. ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases Variant Curation Expert Panel has established GAA-specific classification guidelines (PMID: 37907381)."}}
{"variant_id": "8f8031f9-e04c-47ce-b028-62c2efb3ddcd", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78086424C>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM3_Supporting", "PM2", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67370, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser601Ter) creating premature stop codon in GAA gene. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for Pompe disease (glycogen storage disease type II). The variant truncates the 952 amino acid protein at position 601, removing critical catalytic domains of acid alpha-glucosidase. VEP confirms 'stop_gained' consequence with HIGH impact.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (AF = 2.054e-06 overall, 2.698e-06 in NFE population). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Pompe disease, this frequency is consistent with pathogenic variants. Absent in most populations (EAS, AFR, SAS, AMR, FIN, ASJ, MID all show 0 frequency).", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000593486, VCV000194154) for Glycogen storage disease type II. Multiple submitters with concordant pathogenic classifications. Also listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM070140, CM114936, CM120529). ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP has established expert-curated GAA variant classifications."}}
{"variant_id": "415eb198-9c77-492e-9e2a-3731e09e3cd4", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44184816G>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "PM2_Supporting", "BP2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52133, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. No computational evidence suggests splice disruption. CADD score not available but synonymous variants typically have low scores.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Ile439=) with no amino acid change. Not located at a canonical splice site (\u00b11/2 positions). VEP shows no splice-altering consequences. The variant does not affect protein sequence."}}
{"variant_id": "6a881023-2757-489b-8156-5057a9bfb710", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.26688863C>T", "gene": "OTOF", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65327, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for autosomal recessive disorder. gnomAD exome AF=0.00035 (88 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.00127 (40 alleles). African population shows enrichment at ~0.5%. For a rare recessive disorder like DFNB9, carrier frequency >0.1% is higher than expected.", "BP4": "Computational evidence is mixed but leans benign when considering ClinVar consensus. While SIFT=deleterious and PolyPhen=possibly/probably damaging, the variant has been classified as Likely Benign by 4 independent ClinVar submitters. CADD score not available but ClinVar consensus overrides individual in-silico predictions.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV000048238 has 4 submissions all classifying as Likely Benign for OTOF-related disorder and nonsyndromic genetic hearing loss. The variant is a missense (p.Asp1528Asn) in a C2 domain. OTOF is known to cause DFNB9 via loss-of-function, but missense variants require functional evidence for pathogenicity assessment."}}
{"variant_id": "4c246b57-b8f9-46e2-9635-feb7be75d20c", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259145A>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64467, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the Runt homology domain (RHD), a critical functional domain of RUNX1 responsible for DNA binding and CBF\u03b2 interaction. VEP annotation confirms location in Pfam domain PF00853 (Runt domain). The RHD is a well-established mutational hotspot for pathogenic RUNX1 variants in familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant annotation. For an autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance like RUNX1-related thrombocytopenia/cancer predisposition, absence from population databases supports rarity consistent with pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT scores 0.00-0.02 (deleterious_low_confidence across all transcripts), PolyPhen-2 scores 0.968-0.992 (probably_damaging). The variant affects a highly conserved phenylalanine residue (Phe116/Phe89 depending on transcript) within the Runt domain. COSMIC reports this position as a somatic mutation site (COSV55895100/COSM6022396).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM/RUNX1-FPD). This is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance, and RUNX1 is the only known causative gene for this specific phenotype."}}
{"variant_id": "80e8890a-cea6-43c9-bf91-9278337c5786", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164656A>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70680, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD v4 shows allele frequency of 1.326e-05 (0.001326%) overall, with only the G allele (different nucleotide change) observed at very low frequency. The T allele (p.Tyr407Asn) is absent or at extremely low frequency, meeting PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants are a known mechanism of disease. Germline RUNX1 missense mutations in the Runt homology domain and transactivation domain are well-established causes of familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation in functional domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT score = 0 (deleterious), PolyPhen score = 0.992 (probably_damaging). The variant affects a conserved tyrosine residue at position 407 in the C-terminal transactivation domain (Pfam PF08504). The Y>N substitution introduces a polar asparagine in place of an aromatic tyrosine.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder (FPDMM), which has a single genetic etiology. This phenotype-genotype correlation strongly supports pathogenicity.", "notable": "ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV001338109). The variant is located in the RUNX1 transactivation domain (C-terminal region), where pathogenic missense mutations have been reported to impair transcriptional activity. RUNX1 C-terminal mutations have been shown to impair blood cell differentiation (PMID:38513139). However, no functional studies or case reports specific to p.Tyr407Asn were identified. Loss-of-function/haploinsufficiency is the established disease mechanism for RUNX1-FPDMM."}}
{"variant_id": "aa730450-8f23-4731-99be-572edc912052", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89725122G>A", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "BS3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64452, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) in PTEN, a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease. This creates a premature stop codon at position 130 of 403 amino acids, resulting in truncation of >67% of the protein including critical phosphatase domains. PTEN haploinsufficiency causes PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (Cowden syndrome). VEP confirms HIGH impact stop_gained consequence across all protein-coding transcripts.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 2.737e-06 (approximately 3 alleles in ~1.1 million total alleles). This is well below the threshold expected for a dominant disorder with high penetrance. Meets PM2 criterion for absence/extremely low frequency in controls.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome) is highly specific for PTEN-related disease. PHTS has a single genetic etiology (PTEN mutations) with characteristic features including hamartomas, macrocephaly, and increased cancer risk. The phenotype-genotype correlation strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (14+ RCV accessions) from reputable clinical laboratories for Cowden syndrome 1, PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, macrocephaly-autism syndrome, glioma susceptibility, and hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. Allele ID: 22858. No conflicting interpretations for the C>T change.", "notable": "Literature evidence: PMID 38353885 reports this exact variant (c.388C>T) in a patient with Cowden syndrome and multiple bronchial carcinoids. CIViC database (variant ID 636) documents R130* with evidence for drug sensitivity to Perifosine + Temsirolimus in thyroid cancer (EID1627). COSMIC identifies this as a somatic oncogenic variant (COSM5152, COSM5219). The variant is located within the phosphatase domain critical for PTEN tumor suppressor function."}}
{"variant_id": "bda540d2-f8f0-4520-bf4a-f111b5cb9d1b", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11222296G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62732, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD exome (AF = 1.14e-05, 2 alleles in ~175,000 individuals). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "notable": "CRITICAL DISCREPANCY: The provided coordinates (NC_000019.9:g.11222296G>A / rs1294806884) map to the DOCK6 gene (intron variant c.3241-48C>T), NOT the LDLR gene as stated in clinical context. LDLR is located at chr19:11,089,362-11,133,830 (GRCh38), while this variant is at position 11,222,296. This is a deep intronic variant (48bp from splice site) with no predicted functional impact. No ClinVar submissions found. No pathogenic evidence available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "1bf87321-26f3-4002-89f6-676c672578d4", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203395675G>A", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 77565, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP2", "PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 and v4.1 (0 alleles). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PM1": "Located in the serine/threonine kinase domain (Pfam PF00069) of BMPR2, a critical functional domain essential for receptor signaling. This domain is a mutational hotspot for PAH-causing variants.", "PP2": "BMPR2 has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common in pulmonary arterial hypertension. Gene is highly constrained.", "PP3": "SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0.01). Variant also affects splice region. PolyPhen predicts benign (0.031-0.132), creating mixed computational evidence. CADD/DITTO scores not available but SIFT deleterious supports PP3 at supporting level.", "notable": "ClinVar has conflicting interpretations: Pathogenic for FOP (different phenotype) and VUS for PAH. The G>T variant at same position (p.Glu376Ter, nonsense) is classified Pathogenic by ClinGen VCEP for PAH, supporting functional importance of this residue. HGMD entry CM1513949 exists. Variant is in splice region which may affect splicing."}}
{"variant_id": "94a782c6-4723-40bc-9cdd-65893ca3e404", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171621721A>G", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 196844, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs1653382463 is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant query, supporting rarity consistent with PM2 for autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (primary open-angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-related disease. MYOC is a well-established gene for autosomal dominant POAG (GLC1A), with strong gene-disease association confirmed in knowledge graph.", "notable": "Computational predictions are benign (SIFT=0.83 tolerated, PolyPhen=0.0 benign), which argues against pathogenicity but does not meet BP4 threshold without CADD/DITTO scores. Variant is located in signal peptide region (amino acid 11), not in the critical olfactomedin domain (residues 244-504) where most pathogenic MYOC variants cluster. ClinVar classifies as VUS with 3 submissions. No functional studies or literature reports specific to this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "96eaf4a9-6ebf-43f2-8ad1-f4cfcb76ac71", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43047083C>T", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 49194, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.88+142563G>A) located >142kb from the nearest splice site. No predicted splice impact. VEP consequence: intron_variant with MODIFIER impact. No computational evidence supports a deleterious effect.", "BP7": "Intronic variant with no predicted splice impact. Located far from canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and not predicted to create cryptic splice sites.", "notable": "CRITICAL FINDING: VEP annotation indicates this variant (chr20:43047083C>T, rs1187713149) is located in the PTPRT gene, NOT HNF4A. The variant is a deep intronic variant with no functional consequence. gnomAD frequency: 3.29e-05 overall (rare but present in population). HNF4A is confirmed to be associated with MODY1 (maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 1) via autosomal dominant inheritance with loss-of-function mechanism, but this variant does not appear to affect HNF4A."}}
{"variant_id": "14bfab84-c1df-4ad7-9174-144dd0143409", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43249693T>C", "gene": "ADA", "disease": "adenosine deaminase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64121, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (adenosine deaminase deficiency) is highly specific for ADA gene mutations with single genetic etiology. ADA-SCID is a well-characterized autosomal recessive disorder caused by biallelic ADA mutations.", "notable": "PM2 not met: Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=7.95e-05 exome, 3.19e-05 genome), which is consistent with carrier frequency for a rare recessive disorder but does not meet 'absent from controls' threshold. PP3 not met: CADD=10.95 (<15 threshold), REVEL=0.241 (<0.75), SIFT=tolerated, PolyPhen=benign - computational evidence does not support deleterious effect. ClinVar reports this variant as VUS for ADA-SCID (allele_id: 886149). No literature evidence found for this specific variant (p.Asp314Gly)."}}
{"variant_id": "50f91390-6424-47ba-a587-3d70328e4353", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.215847445T>G", "gene": "USH2A", "disease": "Usher syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55194, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM3", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=0.000969 (243/250,000+ alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.000956 (30/31,000+ alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Usher syndrome type 2A, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations and meets PM2 threshold for extremely low frequency.", "PM3": "This variant (c.2276G>T) is well-documented in compound heterozygous state with other pathogenic USH2A variants in multiple affected individuals with Usher syndrome and retinitis pigmentosa. Literature evidence (PMID:37287646, PMID:33452396, PMID:34948090, PMID:38347443) demonstrates detection in trans with other pathogenic variants in affected patients.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999-1.0). The cysteine at position 759 is highly conserved and located within a Laminin G-like domain (PF00053), critical for protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Usher syndrome) is highly specific for USH2A-related disease. USH2A is the most common cause of Usher syndrome type 2, accounting for ~80% of cases. The combination of sensorineural hearing loss and retinitis pigmentosa is characteristic.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000002356). Conditions include Usher syndrome type 2A, Retinitis pigmentosa 39, and USH2A-related disorder. Multiple expert panels and clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic.", "notable": "This variant is also listed in HGMD (CM001372) and COSMIC (COSV99048434). Extensive literature support with 36+ PubMed citations documenting this variant in affected patients. The p.Cys759Phe substitution affects a conserved cysteine residue in the Laminin G-like domain, likely disrupting disulfide bond formation critical for protein folding and function."}}
{"variant_id": "c400a0f9-d38a-4d2e-9b96-5829547c6b19", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.107312690G>T", "gene": "SLC26A4", "disease": "Pendred syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Moderate", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4", "PP3", "PM3_Very Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61744, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5", "PS4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Variant is significantly enriched in affected individuals. ClinVar reports multiple independent submissions (7 RCV records) classifying this variant as pathogenic for Pendred syndrome and DFNB4. HGMD lists two independent disease-associated entries (CM087094, CM981497). Over 33 publications in PubMed reference this variant in disease context.", "PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=0.000175 (44 alleles/251,000+), gnomAD genome AF=0.0000640 (2 alleles/31,000+). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with expected carrier frequency and meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect. SIFT=deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.983). The missense change Val138Phe affects a conserved residue in the Pfam domain PF13792 (sulfate transporter domain).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Pendred syndrome) is highly specific for SLC26A4-related disease. Pendred syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with SLC26A4 being the primary causative gene, characterized by sensorineural hearing loss, enlarged vestibular aqueduct, and thyroid dysfunction.", "PP5": "Multiple reputable sources report this variant as pathogenic. ClinVar has 7 independent submissions all classifying as Pathogenic for Pendred syndrome, DFNB4, and related hearing loss conditions. HGMD Professional database lists this as a disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "042a61fa-0733-4208-9bcf-82ea00d74c79", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.42676699C>T", "gene": "CAPN3", "disease": "autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP1", "PP4_Moderate", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 58292, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg110Ter) in CAPN3 creates premature stop codon at amino acid 110 of 821 (86.6% protein truncation). CAPN3 loss-of-function is an established mechanism for autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy (LGMDR1). This null variant is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or severely truncated non-functional protein lacking critical calpain protease domains.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database with allele frequency of 3.97712e-06 (1 allele in ~251,000 total alleles). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare recessive disorder.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000017615) with multiple submissions for LGMDR1 (autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2A) and LGMDD4. Variant is also catalogued in HGMD (CM950189) and COSMIC (COSV58826545). Multiple supporting publications (PMIDs: 7720071, 10330340, 15689361, 16141003, 18854869, 16542520, 26677118, 30028523, 31931849, 25135358)."}}
{"variant_id": "0db8711c-7233-4fac-93bc-9e2eee4954ab", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11224299T>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68719, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical EGF-like domain (Pfam PF00058, SMART SM00135) of LDLR. This domain is essential for receptor recycling and LDL binding. Mutations in this region are known to disrupt LDLR function and cause familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.0 (allele frequency 1.369e-06, ~1 in 730,000 alleles). Only observed in NFE population at 1.8e-06. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in dominant disorder.", "PP2": "Missense variant in LDLR, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease (familial hypercholesterolemia). LDLR has low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are well-established cause of FH.", "PP3": "Computational evidence strongly supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.999-1.0). Consistent predictions across all 20+ transcripts analyzed.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (2 submissions) and Likely Pathogenic (2 submissions) for familial hypercholesterolemia (VCV000251847). Evidence includes PMIDs 16250003 and 9039985. Also listed in HGMD (CM172540, CM950766).", "notable": "This variant affects a highly conserved tryptophan residue (Trp483) in the EGF-like domain. The W\u2192R substitution introduces a charged residue in place of a hydrophobic aromatic residue, likely disrupting protein structure. COSMIC also reports this variant (COSV108771464), though somatic significance is unclear."}}
{"variant_id": "5254a3a7-a1c1-442e-9626-0f05a68c4437", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252853C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70836, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.508+1G>C) at the invariant +1 position in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome (FPDMM). VEP confirms HIGH impact splice_donor_variant affecting multiple protein-coding transcripts. Splice site disruption at canonical \u00b11/2 positions is expected to cause aberrant splicing leading to nonsense-mediated decay or truncated protein.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in any population, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For an autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance, absence from population databases strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant (NM_001754.5:c.508+1G>C, Allele ID 1289539) as Likely Pathogenic for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome. Additionally, other nucleotide substitutions at the same position (c.508+1G>T and c.508+1G>A) are classified as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic, providing strong supporting evidence for pathogenicity of any variant disrupting this canonical splice site.", "notable": "COSMIC entries (COSV55869348, COSV55878661) and HGMD entries (CS1312704, CS1612378) at this position indicate somatic and germline pathogenic variants. Extensive literature (PMID:38352275, PMID:36626254, PMID:38019014) establishes RUNX1 germline mutations as causative for familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy predisposition through haploinsufficiency mechanism."}}
{"variant_id": "1f8ff66d-e0d4-47ed-af0f-b63b943b5e33", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11213463G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PVS1_Strong", "PP4", "PS3_Moderate", "PM2", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53178, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.313+1G>A) at the +1 position of intron 3 in LDLR. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for familial hypercholesterolemia (OMIM 606945). Splice donor variants at +1 position are expected to cause exon skipping or intron retention, resulting in null allele.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.78e-05 (7 alleles total). This frequency is well below the expected disease prevalence threshold for familial hypercholesterolemia (~1:250), supporting rarity criterion.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000003736, allele_id 18775) for familial hypercholesterolemia 1, homozygous FH, and related conditions. Multiple HGMD entries (CS941506, CS961609, CS971791) also support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "d000f4f9-fefb-4a45-9939-a12016651e14", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.6155892G>A", "gene": "VWF", "disease": "von Willebrand disease type 2N", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PS3", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "von Willebrand Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 144056, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "This variant (p.Arg854Gln) is located in the D' domain of VWF, which is the critical Factor VIII binding domain. Type 2N VWD is characterized by defective FVIII binding. Multiple functional studies have demonstrated that mutations in this region impair VWF-FVIII interaction. The variant is listed in HGMD (CM910395) and has been extensively characterized in functional assays showing reduced FVIII binding capacity.", "PM1": "Located in the D' domain (residues 764-866) of VWF, which is a critical functional domain responsible for Factor VIII binding. This domain is a mutational hotspot for type 2N von Willebrand disease with minimal benign variation. Structural studies (PDB: 2mhp, 2mhq, 6n29, 7kwo, 7pmv) confirm this residue is within the FVIII binding interface.", "PP3": "Computational predictions support deleterious effect: SIFT score = 0 (deleterious), PolyPhen score = 0.883 (possibly damaging). The missense variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue at position 854.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (von Willebrand disease type 2N) is highly specific for VWF gene mutations affecting the D' domain FVIII binding region. Type 2N VWD has a single genetic etiology with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern matching the clinical context.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (VCV000000296) with multiple submissions across 11 RCV records. Conditions include VWD type 2N, VWD type 1, VWD type 2, VWD type 3, and hereditary VWD. Extensive literature support with 28 PubMed citations including PMIDs: 1581215, 1832934, 1906877, 1918030, 8500791, 15461624, 16953269, 16985174, 21371195, 22875612, 23426949, 23636243, 24029428, 24033266, 25306238, 26105150, 27716216, 28916584, 31019283, 31249928, 31985870, 35046417, 35337356, 35405740, 35552711, 37845247, 20409624, 22197721."}}
{"variant_id": "38ffddfb-a26c-4455-8f41-51c322a384e3", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121426679C>T", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63642, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln124Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 124 of 631 amino acids in HNF1A. Loss-of-function via haploinsufficiency is a well-established mechanism for MODY3 (HNF1A-MODY). Truncation occurs in exon 2, early in the protein, and is predicted to trigger nonsense-mediated decay. VEP impact: HIGH.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for HNF1A-MODY (MODY3), which has a single genetic etiology. HNF1A is the most common cause of MODY, accounting for 30-50% of cases. Knowledge graph confirms strong gene-disease association.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic (VCV000586791) with multiple submissions: Pathogenic for 'not provided', Pathogenic for 'Maturity onset diabetes mellitus in young (MODY)', and Likely pathogenic for 'Monogenic diabetes'. Also documented in HGMD (CM052919)."}}
{"variant_id": "f99e041c-8dcd-4b30-a4bd-cf14e519da75", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605475A>G", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 2627987, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PS4_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles across all populations), meeting the \u22640.0001 threshold for PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP specifications.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.872 (\u22650.7 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (0.01), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (0.905). Variant located in the olfactomedin (OLF) domain (Pfam PF02191), a critical functional domain for myocilin.", "PS4_Supporting": "Two probands with primary open-angle glaucoma (POAG) have been reported carrying this variant (PMIDs: 15534471, 28564705), meeting the \u22652 probands threshold for PS4 at supporting level.", "notable": "ClinGen Glaucoma Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as VUS (Nov 2022) with a score of 3. Only 2 segregations reported in families with POAG, not meeting the \u22653 threshold required for PP1. No functional studies available to assess impact on myocilin protein function. MYOC pathogenic variants cause disease through a gain-of-function/dominant-negative mechanism involving protein misfolding, not loss-of-function, so PVS1 is not applicable for missense variants."}}
{"variant_id": "9fe505f4-9287-4671-ac7c-48bfe0745003", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185193G>C", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 194995, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PP1_Strong", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Variant identified in at least 13 unrelated individuals with hyperglycemia/MODY (PMID:19790256, ClinGen MDEP internal lab contributors). Prevalence in affected individuals significantly exceeds controls, meeting PS4 threshold.", "PP1_Strong": "Variant segregated with hyperglycemia in multiple families with at least 5 informative meioses (ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes VCEP, April 2024). Upgraded to Strong per ClinGen MDEP specifications.", "PP2": "GCK is defined by ClinGen MDEP as a gene with low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants as a common mechanism of disease. Missense variants in GCK are well-established cause of GCK-MODY (MODY2).", "PP3": "REVEL score 0.745 exceeds ClinGen MDEP VCEP threshold of 0.70. PolyPhen predicts 'probably_damaging' (score 0.97-0.981 across transcripts). Computational evidence supports deleterious effect.", "PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles). gnomAD exome frequency 6.879e-07 (extremely rare). Applied as Supporting per ClinGen MDEP specifications for rare variant.", "notable": "ClinVar expert panel classification: Pathogenic (reviewed by ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes VCEP, April 2024). This variant (NM_000162.5:c.1156C>G, p.Leu386Val) causes a conservative amino acid substitution (leucine to valine) at codon 386 in the glucokinase enzyme. Multiple publications support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 19790256, 27269892, 29510678, 30257192, 31197960, 32375122, 33129248)."}}
{"variant_id": "81bf904b-5556-4b47-ba79-6886da6d4fe7", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36421171G>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 180646, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser9Ter) in RUNX1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease. This creates a premature stop codon at position 9, resulting in a severely truncated protein (8 amino acids vs 453 in full-length protein) that would be subject to nonsense-mediated decay. RUNX1 haploinsufficiency causes familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). Multiple publications (PMID:36626254, PMID:38019014, PMID:36741355) confirm LOF as the disease mechanism.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in any population, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant. For an autosomal dominant disorder with reduced penetrance, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "notable": "ClinVar currently lists this variant as VUS (VCV002876217), but this appears to reflect limited submission data rather than conflicting evidence. The variant creates a stop codon at position 9, which would produce a non-functional protein. PP4 was considered but not applied as the phenotype, while highly suggestive, is not exclusively caused by RUNX1 mutations (ETV6, ANKRD26 can cause similar phenotypes)."}}
{"variant_id": "0296c915-483d-450c-bd77-48afc65e46a6", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206807G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66339, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted splice impact. VEP analysis shows 'synonymous_variant' consequence with LOW impact across all transcripts. No canonical splice site involvement (not at \u00b11/2 positions). RUNX1-specific ClinGen MM-VCEP guidelines indicate synonymous variants without splice effects are generally benign.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.705C>T, p.Ala235=) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. No evidence of cryptic splice site creation or disruption of exonic splicing enhancers/silencers based on computational predictions.", "notable": "ClinVar has 3 submissions classifying as Likely Benign and 1 as VUS. Variant is present at very low frequency in gnomAD (AF ~1.3e-05 genome, ~4e-06 exome), which is below PM2 threshold but indicates the variant has been observed in population controls. Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines, synonymous variants outside splice regions are typically classified as Likely Benign."}}
{"variant_id": "32b2080b-fd41-479b-889b-7eb2809aed48", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259321G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 2311936, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant (RUNX1 c.170C>T, p.Pro57Leu) has been reviewed by the ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy Variant Curation Expert Panel (July 2024) and classified as Uncertain Significance with NO ACMG/AMP criteria met. The variant is located outside the critical Runt homology domain (RHD, residues 50-177 in some isoforms, but Pro57 is in the N-terminal region before the core DNA-binding domain). gnomAD shows presence at low frequency (AF=8.64e-06 overall, 0.0029% in Latino population), which does not meet PM2 threshold per ClinGen specifications. In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT=deleterious_low_confidence (0.02), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.999), but multiple submitters note contradictory computational results. One ClinVar submitter (Labcorp/Invitae) classified as Benign. The proline to leucine substitution involves amino acids with similar hydrophobic properties. No functional studies exist for this specific variant. The ClinGen expert panel explicitly stated 'does not meet any ACMG/AMP criteria' using their RUNX1-specific specifications."}}
{"variant_id": "00a30de2-3561-484a-917d-1e97db73fbed", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38976319T>C", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 2500399, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant not found in gnomAD or major population databases. Per ACMG guidelines, absence from population databases supports rarity consistent with pathogenic variants for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility (PM2_Supporting upgraded to PM2 per RYR1-MH Expert Panel recommendations).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia of anesthesia) is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. RYR1 is the primary gene associated with malignant hyperthermia susceptibility (MHS), accounting for ~70% of cases. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "notable": "CRITICAL COORDINATE ISSUE: The provided HGVS (NC_000019.9:g.38976319T>C) uses GRCh37 reference sequence but clinical context specifies GRCh38. VEP annotation maps this position to FBXO17 gene region, not RYR1. Verification of correct genomic coordinates is essential before clinical use. RYR1-MH ClinGen Expert Panel (PMID:33767344) recommends REVEL \u22650.85 for PP3 and has defined three mutational hotspots (MH1: aa35-614, MH2: aa2129-2458, MH3: aa4631-4991) where PM1 can be applied at moderate strength. Functional studies using caffeine/halothane contracture testing or HEK293 transfection assays are considered gold standard for PS3/BS3 evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "f64ddf8e-9c09-431c-9298-763d97eddeab", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42461711C>G", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 2483638, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD and population databases. For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from controls supports pathogenicity. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.989-0.995). The p.Gly287Arg substitution introduces a charged arginine residue in place of the small, flexible glycine in the \u03b1IIb \u03b2-propeller domain, predicted to disrupt protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. GT is a well-characterized autosomal recessive disorder with a single genetic etiology involving \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin defects.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (allele_id: 1935804). The variant is colocated with HGMD mutation CM093511, suggesting prior disease association. Literature extensively documents that missense mutations in the ITGA2B \u03b2-propeller domain (where G287 resides) commonly cause type I or type II GT by impairing \u03b1IIb\u03b23 complex formation or trafficking."}}
{"variant_id": "5204118a-53a9-43ef-b4e2-8860171d70c2", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259309G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 2300786, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD. gnomAD exome shows AF=2.17e-05 (5 alleles total), gnomAD genome shows AF=1.31e-05. This is well below the expected frequency for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants in critical domains are a known mechanism of disease. Germline RUNX1 mutations cause familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). The RUNX1db and multiple publications (PMID:35764482, PMID:34233450) document that missense variants, particularly in the Runt homology domain, are pathogenic. This variant (p.Pro61Leu) is a missense in a gene with established pathogenic missense variants.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder (FPDMM). This syndrome has a well-established single genetic etiology with RUNX1 germline mutations. Knowledge graph confirms RUNX1 is directly associated with 'hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with runx1'.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant (VCV000532655) as Uncertain Significance across 4 RCV records. The variant is located outside the critical Runt homology domain (RHD spans residues 50-177 in canonical transcript, but p.Pro61 is in the N-terminal region before the DNA-binding core). SIFT predicts 'deleterious_low_confidence' (score 0.03) while PolyPhen predicts 'benign' (score 0.12), showing discordant computational predictions. No functional studies specific to p.Pro61Leu were identified. COSMIC reports this variant (COSV104611427) as a somatic mutation, suggesting potential oncogenic relevance."}}
{"variant_id": "98f9e021-9647-43a8-b893-7dcc62cd7111", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36171767G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50789, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Computational evidence suggests no significant impact. VEP predicts LOW impact for this splice region variant at position -8 from the splice acceptor. This is outside the canonical \u00b11/2 splice sites. The variant affects the polypyrimidine tract but is not predicted to significantly alter splicing based on consequence annotation.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Benign (VCV001096171) with two independent submissions (RCV004595600, RCV001417312) both classifying as Likely Benign for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome.", "notable": "While the variant is rare in gnomAD (AF ~4-6e-06), it is present in population databases, which combined with the Likely Benign ClinVar classification argues against pathogenicity. RUNX1 is a gene where LOF is a known disease mechanism, but this intronic variant at position -8 is not predicted to cause loss of function. No functional studies or case reports were found for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "1d7393bb-e854-4e1d-a9a0-36a72f7d1c3b", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42463476G>C", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 141432, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4_Strong", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles). Per ClinGen Platelet Disorders VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level for rare recessive disorders.", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL=0.809 (>0.7 ClinGen PD VCEP threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). Variant located in functional integrin domain (Gene3D, SMART SM00191, Superfamily SSF69318).", "PP4_Strong": "Patient phenotype highly specific for Glanzmann thrombasthenia: mucocutaneous bleeding, impaired platelet aggregation with all agonists except ristocetin, \u03b1IIb\u03b23 surface expression <1% by flow cytometry, <1% PAC-1 binding. ITGA2B/ITGB3 are the only genes causing this phenotype. Per ClinGen PD VCEP specifications, this meets PP4 at strong level.", "PP5": "ClinGen Platelet Disorders Variant Curation Expert Panel (FDA-recognized database) classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic (reviewed by expert panel, June 2023). Classification based on PP4_Strong + PM2_Supporting + PP3.", "notable": "Patient GE reported in PMID:21113249 is compound heterozygous for this variant and Leu684Arg (VUS). PM3 not met because trans phase not confirmed and second variant classified as VUS. HGMD entry CM125428 exists for this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "fabb44c4-f72c-4054-ac93-c7938f486121", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11222314G>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "PM2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71351, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant c.1187-10G>C is absent from gnomAD. The G>A variant at this position has extremely low frequency (AF=2.8e-05 in gnomAD exome, 2.0e-05 in genome). The G>C substitution is not observed in population databases, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variants in LDLR.", "PM5": "Novel nucleotide change (G>C) at the same position as established pathogenic variant c.1187-10G>A (ClinVar: Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic, VCV000226349). Both variants affect the polypyrimidine tract at position -10 from exon 9, suggesting similar functional impact on splicing.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense and splice variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign variation, and pathogenic variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia (>2000 pathogenic variants reported).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of familial hypercholesterolemia is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR mutations account for ~85-90% of genetically confirmed FH cases, making this a single-gene etiology phenotype.", "notable": "The c.1187-10G>A variant at this exact position is classified as Pathogenic in ClinVar with multiple submissions (PMID: 26077743, 27830735, 30400955). The G>C variant affects the same polypyrimidine tract and is predicted to similarly disrupt splicing. HGMD entry CS014612 exists for this position. However, no direct functional studies for the G>C substitution were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "1b4f0fbc-a84a-4f48-aa0f-7ba01610c065", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11227594G>T", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2", "BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 272486, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in EGF-like domain (PROSITE PS51120, Pfam PF00058, SMART SM00135) - a critical functional domain for LDLR receptor recycling and LDL binding. This domain is essential for acid-dependent ligand release in endosomes.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. The G>T allele (p.Asp589Tyr) has no reported allele frequency in gnomAD exomes or genomes, while other alleles at this position (G>A, G>C) are present at extremely low frequencies (AF ~8.35e-05 and ~3.98e-06 respectively).", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for familial hypercholesterolemia. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2 = probably_damaging (score 0.992-0.998 across transcripts). The amino acid change from Asp (acidic) to Tyr (aromatic) represents a significant physicochemical change.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR mutations account for ~85-90% of genetically confirmed FH cases, making this a single-gene etiology phenotype.", "notable": "HGMD entries (CM055370, CM151096) suggest disease association but without accessible functional evidence. Other missense variants at the same codon (D589N, D589H) are classified as VUS in ClinVar, which does not support PM5 but suggests this is a potentially important residue. ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000441222)."}}
{"variant_id": "c0ea2cde-0642-4dcb-acf2-a4b234a5f4a9", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43052700G>A", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PM2_Supporting", "PP1_Strong", "PP3", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55226, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the ligand-binding domain (LBD) of HNF4A, a critical functional domain. VEP shows multiple protein domain annotations including Pfam PF00104 (nuclear hormone receptor ligand-binding domain), SMART SM00430, and Gene3D. The LBD is essential for HNF4A transcriptional activity and dimerization.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome shows AF=4.03e-06 (1 allele in ~248,000 alleles), well below the threshold for autosomal dominant MODY1 (expected prevalence ~1:100,000). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare dominant disorder.", "PP2": "HNF4A is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY1). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene. The p.Arg290His substitution affects a conserved arginine residue.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: PolyPhen-2 scores 0.94-0.999 (probably damaging) across all transcripts; SIFT score=0 (deleterious). The missense variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the ligand-binding domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for MODY, which has a well-defined single genetic etiology. HNF4A is one of the established MODY genes (MODY1), and the clinical presentation aligns with HNF4A-related disorder.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (Allele ID: 793843) with multiple submissions for MODY1, monogenic diabetes, and HNF4A-related disorder. Multiple RCV accessions (RCV000992167, RCV001248988, RCV004527405, RCV003317408, RCV003413778) support pathogenicity. HGMD also lists this variant (CM064050, CM082881)."}}
{"variant_id": "9561d864-f780-45f5-9c16-4aa77affe375", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259398G>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 202251, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=4.37e-06 (1 allele), genome AF=6.57e-06 (1 allele). Combined frequency ~1 in 150,000 individuals. This is well below the threshold for a rare autosomal dominant disorder with reduced penetrance. Meets PM2 criterion for rarity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition, and the phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established. The knowledge graph confirms RUNX1 is directly associated with 'hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with runx1'.", "notable": "This is a splice region variant (c.98-5C>G) located 5 nucleotides upstream of exon 2 in the splice polypyrimidine tract. VEP annotates it as 'splice_region_variant' and 'splice_polypyrimidine_tract_variant' with LOW impact. ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (1 submission from Labcorp/Invitae). The variant is also present in COSMIC (COSV100278438), suggesting somatic occurrence in cancer. RUNX1 haploinsufficiency is a well-established mechanism for FPDMM, and splice-site mutations are recognized as pathogenic in this gene. However, this variant is at position -5 (not canonical \u00b11/2), so PVS1 does not apply. RNA studies from the NIH FPDMM cohort (PMID:38019014) demonstrate that splice-region mutations in RUNX1 can cause aberrant splicing, but functional data for this specific variant is lacking. PP3 was not applied because this is an intronic/splice region variant where standard missense predictors (SIFT, PolyPhen) are not applicable, and no CADD/DITTO scores were available in the annotation data."}}
{"variant_id": "f68ccdb6-5117-44a9-8f96-ac5051095ffd", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605461C>T", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 298612, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PS4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln368Ter/Q368X) creating a premature stop codon in MYOC exon 3. MYOC-associated glaucoma operates via a toxic gain-of-function mechanism where mutant myocilin misfolds and aggregates intracellularly in the trabecular meshwork, causing ER stress and cell death. While this is not a classical loss-of-function mechanism, the variant creates a truncated protein that lacks the critical C-terminal olfactomedin (OLF) domain where >90% of pathogenic mutations cluster. The truncated protein causes intracellular aggregation and is not secreted, consistent with the established pathogenic mechanism for MYOC variants.", "PM2": "Rare variant in gnomAD: exome AF = 0.00111 (0.11%), genome AF = 0.00085 (0.085%). While present in population databases, this frequency is consistent with the known incomplete penetrance of this variant (5.2-9.6% penetrance per FinnGen study PMID:34081096) and is below the threshold expected for a dominant glaucoma-causing variant.", "PS4": "Strong case-control association demonstrated in large population studies. FinnGen study (PMID:34081096, n=218,792) showed OR=3.36 (95% CI: 2.55-4.37) for primary open-angle glaucoma, OR=2.58 (95% CI: 2.12-3.13) for overall glaucoma, and OR=5.45 (95% CI: 2.95-9.28) for glaucoma-related operations. Multiple genome-wide association studies confirm this variant as a significant glaucoma risk allele (PMID:33627673, PMID:36450729).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic with multiple submissions: Pathogenic for Glaucoma of childhood, Likely Pathogenic for Primary open angle glaucoma (POAG), Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic for 'not provided' condition. HGMD entry CM971023 and OMIM 601652.0003 also document this as a disease-causing variant. Over 40 PubMed citations support pathogenicity.", "notable": "Extensive functional studies support pathogenicity: (1) Myocilin misfolding review (PMID:37217093) establishes that MYOC mutations cause glaucoma via toxic gain-of-function with intracellular aggregation; (2) Thermal stability studies (PMID:36579626) demonstrate pathogenic variants have Tm <47\u00b0C cutoff; (3) This is the most common MYOC variant in European populations and accounts for ~5% of POAG cases. The variant shows incomplete penetrance (5.2-9.6%), explaining its presence in population databases."}}
{"variant_id": "13302787-d703-433f-9904-a20fb6beb318", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1399858C>T", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 91338, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp87Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 87 of 236 amino acids in GAMT. Loss of function is an established mechanism for GAMT deficiency (autosomal recessive). The truncated protein would lack >60% of the functional enzyme including critical methyltransferase domains. VEP confirms HIGH impact stop_gained consequence across multiple transcripts.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome: AF = 4.36e-06 (1 allele in ~230,000 alleles). gnomAD genome: AF = 6.57e-06. For autosomal recessive disorders, this extremely low frequency strongly supports pathogenicity as it is well below the expected carrier frequency threshold.", "notable": "ClinVar reports conflicting interpretations (VCV000849693) with one submission as Likely Pathogenic for GAMT deficiency and one as VUS for cerebral creatine deficiency syndrome. The variant is located in a well-characterized methyltransferase domain. GAMT deficiency is a treatable disorder with creatine supplementation, making accurate classification clinically important."}}
{"variant_id": "824bc12b-2cd6-4821-b672-849f3748f174", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.1399792C>T", "gene": "GAMT", "disease": "guanidinoacetate methyltransferase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Very Strong", "PP4_Strong", "PS3"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 232249, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice donor variant (c.327+1G>A) at the +1 position of intron 3 in GAMT. VEP confirms splice_donor_variant consequence with HIGH impact. GAMT deficiency is an autosomal recessive disorder where loss of function is a well-established disease mechanism. Null variants (including canonical splice site variants at \u00b11/2 positions) are expected to cause complete loss of enzyme function through aberrant splicing leading to nonsense-mediated decay or non-functional protein.", "PM2": "Variant is present at extremely low frequency in gnomAD: exome AF=0.000185 (32/173,000 alleles), genome AF=0.000191 (6/31,400 alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this carrier frequency (~1:5,400) is consistent with the rare disease prevalence. Meets PM2 threshold for recessive disorders where low frequency (not complete absence) is expected for pathogenic variants.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 33917) with multiple submissions for GAMT deficiency/Cerebral creatine deficiency syndrome (CCDS). Multiple independent clinical laboratories have classified this variant as pathogenic.", "notable": "Literature evidence (PMID:37808418) documents c.327G>A in GAMT deficiency cases. The variant affects the last nucleotide of exon 3 and disrupts the canonical GT splice donor site, predicted to cause exon skipping or intron retention. GAMT encodes guanidinoacetate methyltransferase essential for creatine biosynthesis; loss of function leads to cerebral creatine deficiency with intellectual disability, seizures, and movement disorders."}}
{"variant_id": "5cac839b-0aa8-4bba-a418-43fd4ef9ded8", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121416357A>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 132372, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants, supporting rarity consistent with PM2 for a rare disease variant.", "notable": "This is a 5' UTR variant (c.-215A>G) in the promoter/regulatory region of HNF1A. ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Uncertain significance' for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID: 3227825). HNF1A is well-established as a MODY3 gene with autosomal dominant inheritance and loss-of-function mechanism. However, 5' UTR variants have uncertain functional impact without specific functional studies demonstrating effect on transcription/translation. PVS1 does not apply as this is not a null variant (not nonsense, frameshift, or canonical splice site). PP3 cannot be applied as computational predictors (SIFT, PolyPhen, CADD) are not designed for non-coding 5' UTR variants. No functional studies (PS3/BS3) or segregation data (PP1/BS4) available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "a532eae1-862f-4d90-b69e-5e590a9f7512", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103260419C>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 118424, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM3", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD exome and genome databases for the C>G allele (p.Arg155Pro). The C>T allele (p.Arg155His) has extremely low frequency (gnomAD exome AF=1.99e-05, genome AF=3.18e-05), but the specific C>G change causing p.Arg155Pro is not present in population databases. ClinGen PAH Expert Panel confirmed absence from ExAC, gnomAD, 1000G, and ESP.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variant R408W in a patient with classic PKU (PMID:10679941). This provides evidence for compound heterozygosity in an autosomal recessive disorder.", "PM5": "Novel missense change at the same amino acid position (Arg155) where a different pathogenic missense variant (p.Arg155His, c.464G>A) has been established as pathogenic. Additionally, p.Arg155Cys (c.463C>T) at this codon is also classified as pathogenic, supporting the critical functional importance of this residue.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2=probably_damaging (score 0.992-0.999), REVEL=0.967 (>0.75 threshold). The amino acid change from arginine (basic, polar) to proline (neutral, non-polar) is non-conservative and likely to disrupt protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (classic phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a well-established single genetic etiology (autosomal recessive PAH mutations) with cofactor deficiency excluded in the reported case (PMID:10679941).", "PP5": "ClinGen PAH Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic (August 2018) with reviewed by expert panel status. Multiple clinical laboratories (Labcorp/Invitae, LabCorp Women's Health) have independently classified this variant as Pathogenic. ClinVar VCV000102687 shows expert panel consensus."}}
{"variant_id": "ca60e11b-5cae-4602-9e96-ed937a93a20e", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42462933A>G", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 95566, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (overall AF=2.085e-06, ~0.0002%). For an autosomal recessive disorder like Glanzmann thrombasthenia, this frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic allele. Meets PM2 threshold.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. GT is caused almost exclusively by biallelic mutations in these two genes encoding the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "notable": "ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000891157). In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT=0.79 (tolerated) and PolyPhen=0 (benign) suggest the variant may be tolerated, which argues against pathogenicity. The variant is located in the \u03b2-propeller domain of \u03b1IIb where pathogenic missense mutations have been reported, but computational evidence does not support a deleterious effect. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.Val187Ala were identified in the literature."}}
{"variant_id": "425dc324-2478-4987-b039-5a6755df655e", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.36615034G>A", "gene": "RAG2", "disease": "recombinase activating gene 2 deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PP1", "PP4", "PM3_Strong", "PM1_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 216953, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PM3", "PP1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Functional study (PMID: 29772310) demonstrated recombination activity of 10.5% compared to wildtype RAG2, well below the ClinGen SCID VCEP threshold of <25% for damaging effect. This establishes functional impairment of V(D)J recombination.", "PM1": "Variant located in RAG2 core domain (amino acids 1-383), which is essential for V(D)J recombination activity and defined as a critical functional domain by ClinGen SCID VCEP (PMID: 26996199).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases: gnomAD exome AF = 3.98\u00d710\u207b\u2076 (1 allele), gnomAD genome AF = 6.57\u00d710\u207b\u2076. No homozygotes observed. Below ClinGen SCID VCEP threshold (<0.0000588) for PM2_Supporting.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in multiple probands. At least 9 probands reported: 8 homozygous, 1 compound heterozygous with confirmed phase (Arg229Trp/Gly95Arg). Upgraded to PM3_Strong per ClinGen SCID VCEP specifications.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease in affected family members documented (Proband 30a and 30b, PMID: 11133745). Variant segregates with SCID phenotype in multiple affected individuals.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.999). Invitae modeling predicts disruption of RAG2 function with 95% positive predictive value.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for RAG2 deficiency: T-B-NK+ lymphocyte subset profile consistent with SCID/Leaky SCID/Omenn syndrome diagnostic criteria (PMID: 11133745).", "PP5": "ClinGen SCID Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (April 2024) with detailed evidence review. Multiple clinical laboratories (Invitae, Baylor Genetics, Revvity) also classify as Pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "347868b5-7cc2-4bd0-ba83-bc69847e7691", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.12647694A>G", "gene": "RAF1", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 122961, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Splice region variant at position +6 from exon boundary (c.680+6T>C). This position is outside the canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2) and computational evidence does not predict significant splice impact. The variant is annotated as 'splice_region_variant&intron_variant' by snpEff, indicating low functional impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign by multiple submitters for RASopathy-related conditions (LEOPARD syndrome 2: Benign; RASopathy: Likely benign; not provided: Likely benign). Only one submission classified as VUS for Noonan syndrome 5.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (exome AF=0.000143, 36 alleles; genome AF=0.000127, 4 alleles). While rare, presence in population controls argues against pathogenicity. RAF1-related RASopathies are caused by gain-of-function missense mutations, not splice variants. PVS1 is not applicable as LOF is not a known disease mechanism for RAF1."}}
{"variant_id": "39f1f763-d020-4c98-b299-b417769cbe17", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11200008C>T", "gene": "N/A", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS3_Supporting", "BA1"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 81593, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BS3_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency exceeds 1% in African/African American population (FAF=1.016% in gnomAD v4.0.0). This stand-alone criterion is sufficient for Benign classification per ACMG guidelines.", "BS3_Supporting": "Functional study (PMID:10484771) using luciferase assays in HepG2 cells demonstrated 160% gene expression, indicating no damaging effect on LDLR promoter activity. ClinGen FH Expert Panel classified this as Level 3 assay evidence supporting benign interpretation.", "notable": "This variant is located in the LDLR promoter region (c.-217C>T) and has been reviewed by the ClinGen Familial Hypercholesterolemia Variant Curation Expert Panel (November 2023), which classified it as Benign. Multiple clinical laboratories (Color Health, Quest Diagnostics, Invitae/Labcorp, GENinCode) have submitted concordant Benign/Likely Benign classifications."}}
{"variant_id": "9e2391e6-ef25-444d-bbd9-ab1c5dcaa579", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121434531C>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 205082, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (AF=3.99e-06, 1 allele in East Asian, 0 in European non-Finnish). Meets ClinGen MDEP PM2_Supporting threshold (ENF Popmax FAF <0.000003 and \u22642 copies in ENF and \u22641 copy in any other subpopulation).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.8949 (>0.70 MDEP threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably damaging (0.947-0.996). Variant located in transactivation domain (Pfam PF04812).", "notable": "ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes Expert Panel classified as VUS (July 2023) with PP3 and PM2_Supporting. Two other missense variants at same codon (p.Ser432Phe, p.Ser432Tyr) also classified as VUS, precluding PM5. HGMD entries (CM133574, CM993817) exist at this position. HNF1A has sufficient evidence for haploinsufficiency (ClinGen), supporting LOF as disease mechanism. Variant identified in individual with diabetes (PMID:10588527) but insufficient clinical data for PP4."}}
{"variant_id": "a1c916ee-23f8-4c0b-94fd-62a0c4d2a5ce", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259343C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 725520, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is completely absent from all population databases including gnomAD with adequate coverage (>20x) for RUNX1. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level rather than moderate.", "notable": "Computational predictions show mixed results: PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0), SIFT=deleterious_low_confidence (score 0.02). However, Invitae's advanced modeling did not meet statistical confidence thresholds to predict impact on RUNX1 protein function. The variant is located at position 50, which is at the N-terminal boundary of the Runt homology domain. No functional studies or case reports exist for this specific variant. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy Expert Panel (January 2025) classified this as VUS with only PM2_Supporting applied."}}
{"variant_id": "9ef50f54-c7d6-4c30-b587-2881accce97f", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259342C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 108776, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (allele frequency 7.592e-06 overall, 8.995e-06 in NFE). This is well below the threshold for a rare dominant disorder with reduced penetrance. Meets PM2 criterion for absence/extremely low frequency in population databases.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.01), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). The glycine to aspartic acid substitution introduces a charged residue at a conserved position. CADD/DITTO scores not available, but secondary predictors consistently support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder (FPDMM). This condition has a well-established single genetic etiology with RUNX1 being the causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS from 2 submitters (Ambry Genetics, Labcorp/Invitae). RUNX1 has established haploinsufficiency as disease mechanism per ClinGen. The variant is a missense change, not a null variant, so PVS1 does not apply. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified. No pathogenic variants at the same amino acid position (Gly50) were found to support PM5."}}
{"variant_id": "f917bdb7-1478-404f-af75-1f77ec88b40f", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231794A>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 279648, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1_supporting", "PM2_supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1_supporting": "Variant located within the Runt homology domain (residues 89-204) of RUNX1, a critical functional domain for DNA binding and transcriptional regulation. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP defines this region as a critical functional domain (PMID:31648317). Applied at supporting level per ClinGen MMVCEP specifications.", "PM2_supporting": "Variant is completely absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 and v3.1.2 population databases with adequate coverage (>20x). Applied at supporting level per current ACMG/ClinGen recommendations for rare variants.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.953 (\u22650.88 threshold per ClinGen MMVCEP), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.982), SIFT=deleterious (score 0). The high REVEL score strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this autosomal dominant condition with well-established gene-disease relationship.", "notable": "ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP (expert panel, May 2025) classified this variant as VUS applying PM1_supporting, PM2_supporting, and PP3. RUNX1 has sufficient evidence for haploinsufficiency per ClinGen dosage sensitivity curation. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified in the literature."}}
{"variant_id": "f462708c-29cd-4edc-b166-f6a832cee349", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231860A>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 482790, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the RUNX1 Runt homology domain (RHD), a critical DNA-binding domain (residues 50-177). VEP annotation confirms variant is within Pfam domain PF00853 (Runt domain). The Runt domain is a well-established mutational hotspot for pathogenic variants in RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM). Literature (PMID:36090034) confirms that missense mutations in this domain at the DNA-binding interface (including nearby residues R142, D171, R174, R177) are recurrently associated with AML and disrupt DNA binding.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases. The rsID (rs2146236679) exists in dbSNP but no population frequency data is available, indicating extreme rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant for this autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT score = 0 (deleterious_low_confidence across all transcripts). PolyPhen-2 = 0.994 (probably_damaging) for transcript ENST00000399240. The variant is annotated as 'structural_interaction_variant' by snpEff, suggesting impact on protein-DNA interactions. The Leu175 residue is located within the conserved Runt domain at the DNA-binding interface.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM/RUNX1-FPD). This is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance, and RUNX1 is the only known causative gene for this specific phenotype."}}
{"variant_id": "25c4af2f-d04a-4400-ad30-4d12c850bf10", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103237511T>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PM2", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 90847, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate complete ablation of PAH enzyme activity. R408W results in 0% residual enzymatic activity despite normal protein expression levels (PMID:33493163). Multiple in vitro and in vivo studies in porcine and mouse models confirm loss of function. The variant affects conformational stability of the PAH protein (PMID:35987969).", "PS4": "R408W is the most common PKU-causing mutation worldwide, present in 40-70% of PKU patients depending on nationality (PMID:33493163). The variant is strongly associated with classic/severe PKU phenotype. Multiple population studies confirm significant enrichment in affected individuals compared to controls.", "PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=0.00076 (191/251,000 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.0019 (61/31,400 alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder with carrier frequency expectations, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing status and meets PM2 threshold.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). The variant is classified as missense_variant affecting a critical residue in the PAH catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU is a well-characterized autosomal recessive disorder with a single genetic etiology (PAH gene mutations). The clinical presentation is pathognomonic for this condition.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000000577, allele_id 15616). Multiple RCV records confirm pathogenic classification for phenylketonuria (PKU), PAH-related disorder, and inborn genetic diseases."}}
{"variant_id": "09daa9d6-a08a-4438-8e98-82f288bebeee", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7124146C>A", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Moderate", "PM3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 99262, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (AF=6.841e-07 overall, 8.993e-07 in NFE). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this extremely low frequency supports PM2 at moderate strength.", "PP3": "Computational predictions show mixed but predominantly damaging results: PolyPhen scores range from 0.499 (possibly_damaging) to 0.994 (probably_damaging) across transcripts. SIFT shows deleterious prediction (score 0.03) in canonical transcript ENST00000584103. The variant affects a conserved phenylalanine residue in the acyl-CoA dehydrogenase domain (Pfam PF02771).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (VLCADD) is highly specific for ACADVL gene mutations. VLCADD is a well-characterized autosomal recessive metabolic disorder with ACADVL as the sole causative gene, meeting PP4 criteria.", "notable": "HGMD lists this variant (CM118334) as a disease mutation. ClinVar currently classifies as VUS. The variant is located in a functional domain (acyl-CoA dehydrogenase, Pfam PF02771) critical for enzyme activity. No functional studies (PS3) or segregation data (PP1) available for this specific variant. For recessive disorders, PM3 would require confirmation of trans configuration with another pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "53cbd66e-e2c9-4428-aaa3-8762fa9dd6ea", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121437090C>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73677, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect. CADD scores for synonymous variants are typically low. No evidence of splice site disruption - variant is at codon position 3 (c.1521C>A), not near canonical splice sites.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Pro507=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at a canonical splice site (\u00b11/2 positions). VEP annotation confirms 'synonymous_variant' as most severe consequence."}}
{"variant_id": "bfdfbf81-6f26-43f8-aa4b-bbb17ebaf54a", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89720813A>T", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75173, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 130 of 403 amino acids in PTEN, a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (Cowden syndrome). This truncation removes >67% of the protein including critical phosphatase domain residues.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 1.19e-05 (3 alleles total). Absent from gnomAD in multiple populations (AFR, EAS, SAS, MID). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome) is highly specific for PTEN-related disease with single genetic etiology. PTEN variants are the only known cause of this syndrome.", "PP5": "Multiple ClinVar submissions classify this variant as Pathogenic for Cowden syndrome 1, PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, Macrocephaly-autism syndrome, Glioma susceptibility 2, and hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome (VCV000007819). OMIM entry 601728.0007 also documents this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "89ab6f7a-953d-4c05-87b9-3d5f4d37345b", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206753C>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55755, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP7", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.759G>A, p.Leu253=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact. The variant does not affect canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions) and is located within an exon, not at splice junctions.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as 'Likely benign' (VCV001121120) for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1. Two RCV submissions (RCV004595605, RCV001451313) support this classification.", "notable": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases, which would typically support PM2 for rare variants. However, for synonymous variants without splice impact, rarity alone does not indicate pathogenicity. COSMIC entry (COSM444412) indicates somatic occurrence in cancer, but this does not establish germline pathogenicity. RUNX1 loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism for FPDMM, but synonymous variants do not cause loss-of-function unless they affect splicing."}}
{"variant_id": "a73c7ac4-5d9a-4c83-8aab-e4fea34cea32", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7579543G>T", "gene": "TP53", "disease": "Li-Fraumeni syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "TP53 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 81279, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (AF = 1.368e-06, ~1 in 730,000 alleles). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in population databases.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Li-Fraumeni syndrome) is highly specific for TP53 germline variants. TP53 is the only known gene associated with classic Li-Fraumeni syndrome.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: 'Likely benign' for Li-Fraumeni syndrome specifically, but 'Conflicting interpretations' for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. Computational predictors (SIFT=tolerated, PolyPhen=benign) uniformly predict benign effect, which would support BP4 but is counterbalanced by PM2. Variant is in the transactivation domain (TAD) but not in a known mutational hotspot. No functional studies available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "e6b07542-2171-4ef9-8c9a-917e08344fb9", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185330C>G", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS1_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73442, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PS1_Supporting", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.1020-1G>C) at the -1 position of intron 8 in GCK. This variant removes a canonical splice acceptor site and is predicted to cause skipping of exon 9 of 10, resulting in deletion of >10% of the protein. GCK loss-of-function is an established mechanism for MODY2/monogenic diabetes (haploinsufficiency). VEP confirms HIGH impact splice_acceptor_variant across all GCK transcripts.", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles). Per ClinGen MDEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level for rare variant status.", "PS1_Supporting": "The c.1020-1G>A variant at the same canonical splice site nucleotide has been classified as pathogenic for monogenic diabetes by ClinGen MDEP. Both variants (G>C and G>A) have similar predicted splice impact by SpliceAI (0.99 for Acceptor Loss). Per ClinGen MDEP specifications, this supports PS1 at supporting level.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK is definitively associated with maturity-onset diabetes of the young, neonatal diabetes mellitus, and hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia in the knowledge graph.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV000036170.4 shows this variant classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Monogenic Diabetes Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, March 2024). One individual with hyperglycemia reported in literature (PMID:18248649), but insufficient for PS4 statistical threshold per ClinGen MDEP criteria."}}
{"variant_id": "50413a95-4bb5-4541-8121-2efb05178517", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.50649239A>T", "gene": "SOS2", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS2", "PS4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 100973, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Met267Lys) at this position is established as pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000209092). The variant c.800T>A (p.Met267Lys) has multiple ClinVar submissions classified as Pathogenic for Noonan syndrome 9 (NS9). Additionally, a different nucleotide change at the same codon (c.800T>C, p.Met267Thr) is also classified as Pathogenic, demonstrating this is a critical residue.", "PM1": "Located in the Dbl homology (DH) domain of SOS2 (Pfam PF00621), a critical functional domain for guanyl-nucleotide exchange factor activity. VEP annotation confirms the variant affects multiple protein domains including Gene3D, SMART SM00325, and CDD cd00160. SOS2 DH domain mutations are known to cause gain-of-function activation of RAS-MAPK signaling.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants for this specific variant, consistent with an extremely rare pathogenic variant. The rsID rs797045167 exists but represents multiple alleles at this position, none with population frequency data.", "PP3": "SIFT prediction: deleterious_low_confidence (score=0). The variant affects a highly conserved methionine residue at position 267. Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RASopathy) is highly specific for disorders caused by SOS2 mutations. SOS2 is an established RASopathy gene causing Noonan syndrome 9 (OMIM 616559). The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (RCV000191031, RCV001250768) and Likely Pathogenic (RCV004732469) by multiple submitters. HGMD entries (CM1511145, CM154932) also document this variant. Published case report (PMID:30707178) describes a patient with Noonan syndrome 9 with this exact variant (c.800T>A, p.Met267Lys)."}}
{"variant_id": "7f8bf0db-1204-4240-937b-b8fb10254549", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.18631362A>G", "gene": "CDKL5", "disease": "CDKL5 disorder", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BS2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67276, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: SIFT=Tolerated (0.068), PolyPhen-2=Benign (0.429), REVEL=0.205 (<0.75), MetaSVM=Tolerated, MetaLR=Tolerated. While CADD=21.8 exceeds threshold, the consensus of other predictors supports benign classification.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign by multiple submitters for CDKL5 disorder (allele_id: 191662). Two independent submissions classify as Benign for DEE2/Angelman syndrome-like and CDKL5 disorder specifically.", "notable": "Variant is present in gnomAD (combined AF ~5e-05, 11 total alleles) which does not meet PM2 rarity threshold. Located in C-terminal region (residue 748) outside the critical kinase domain (residues 13-297). CDKL5 deficiency disorder is caused by loss-of-function variants, but this missense is in a non-catalytic region with benign computational predictions."}}
{"variant_id": "3a30f66d-ebfc-4ef5-95fc-fb852e05df8a", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.31349945C>T", "gene": "COCH", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54322, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency of 0.091% in gnomAD exome (229/250,000+ alleles) and 0.077% in gnomAD genome (24/31,000+ alleles) exceeds expected frequency for rare autosomal dominant hearing loss disorder DFNA9. This frequency is inconsistent with a pathogenic variant for a penetrant dominant condition.", "BP6": "ClinVar (VCV000281981) reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign across 5 submissions from multiple laboratories for DFNA9, nonsyndromic hearing loss, and COCH-related disorders. Consensus classification supports benign interpretation."}}
{"variant_id": "296222b4-2b23-4455-8916-41dc7d49aa17", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11221415G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2", "PM5_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76681, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical EGF-like domain (SMART SM00179/SM00181, PROSITE PS50026/PS01186) of LDLR. This domain is essential for receptor recycling and LDL binding. Mutations in this region are known to cause receptor dysfunction.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (6.842e-07 overall frequency, 8.993e-07 in NFE). Essentially absent from population databases, consistent with pathogenic variant for a dominant disorder.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.969-1.0). Consistent damaging predictions across all transcripts.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. FH has a well-defined genetic etiology with LDLR being the primary causative gene (~85-90% of monogenic FH cases).", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely pathogenic/Pathogenic (VCV000251606, VCV000440618) with multiple independent submissions. Also listed in HGMD as disease mutation (CM022813, CM091468). PubMed citations: 25741868, 12436241, 18718593, 18757057."}}
{"variant_id": "fdc19ad4-b777-4a35-ba3f-cd4be7bac239", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171607754C>T", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60881, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM4", "PP1", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. PMID:16466712 showed Gln368Ter protein has reduced secretion levels compared to wild-type myocilin. PMID:19023451 demonstrated heterozygous expression increases secretion of mutant protein and reduces extracellular processed myocilin. PMID:15069026 showed pathogenic MYOC variants cause protein misfolding, ER accumulation of insoluble aggregates, and apoptosis via unfolded protein response. ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP applied PS3_Moderate based on OddsPath threshold >4.3.", "PS4": "Significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals. 23+ probands with juvenile or primary open angle glaucoma (JOAG/POAG) reported carrying this variant (PMIDs: 11535458, 11004290, 10815160, 22736945, 11803488, 12189160). ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP confirmed PS4 threshold met (\u226515 probands). Variant identified in 107 patients with POAG/ocular hypertension across multiple studies.", "PM4": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln368Ter) causes premature termination, deleting \u226510% of protein (137 amino acids) within the conserved olfactomedin domain. ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP confirmed PM4 is met. The truncation disrupts a critical functional domain essential for myocilin function.", "PP1": "Strong co-segregation with disease in multiple families. 52 segregations in 10 families with JOAG or POAG reported (PMIDs: 11004290, 10815160, 11535458). ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP applied PP1_Strong (\u22657 meioses in >1 family). Founder effect identified in 15 Australian families sharing common disease haplotype (PMID:12522550).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (juvenile open angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-related disease. MYOC is the primary gene associated with autosomal dominant juvenile/primary open angle glaucoma (GLC1A, OMIM 137750). The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "PP5": "ClinGen Glaucoma Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (reviewed by expert panel, March 2022). Multiple ClinVar submissions (15 total) with majority classifying as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic. OMIM entry 601652.0003 documents this as established pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "04e75931-7e04-49cd-8465-eec168b78e7d", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42460929G>A", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 308411, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (c.2822G>A, p.Trp941Ter) creating a premature stop codon in ITGA2B. Loss of function is a well-established mechanism for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (autosomal recessive). The variant truncates the protein at position 941 of 1039 amino acids, removing the transmembrane and cytoplasmic domains critical for integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23 function. VEP confirms HIGH impact stop_gained consequence.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No alleles found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants from gnomAD. For an autosomal recessive disorder, absence from population databases strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. Glanzmann thrombasthenia is a rare inherited bleeding disorder with a single genetic etiology (mutations in genes encoding integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23). Knowledge graph confirms ITGA2B is directly associated with Glanzmann thrombasthenia.", "notable": "Case report (PMID: 40126091) describes this exact variant (ITGA2B c.2822G>A) as a novel mutation causing Glanzmann thrombasthenia in a twin pregnancy patient. This provides supporting clinical evidence but does not meet PS4 threshold for statistical significance. COSMIC entry (COSV52231428) indicates somatic occurrence at this position."}}
{"variant_id": "ea96a10a-ffb9-4798-9c3f-ae0c2393f5e8", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45384849G>T", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PP3", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56241, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (overall frequency 6.575e-06, ~1 in 152,000 alleles). Present at low frequency in African population (2.414e-05). For autosomal recessive disorders, PM2 is applied at supporting level when variant is present at very low frequency rather than completely absent.", "notable": "This variant (rs1020586550) is located in an intergenic/regulatory enhancer region (ENSR17_C6HL3), NOT within the ITGB3 coding sequence. The consequence is classified as 'regulatory_region_variant' with MODIFIER impact. No functional studies exist demonstrating this enhancer variant affects ITGB3 expression. Glanzmann thrombasthenia is typically caused by coding mutations (missense, nonsense, frameshift, splice site) in ITGA2B or ITGB3 that directly disrupt integrin \u03b1IIb\u03b23 function. Regulatory variants causing this condition would be exceptionally rare and would require functional evidence of reduced ITGB3 expression."}}
{"variant_id": "401b2623-4bfa-4dbd-a63a-31faac533f32", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45361830T>G", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP4_Strong", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 78767, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD and population databases. For autosomal recessive Glanzmann thrombasthenia, absence from controls supports pathogenicity.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.934 in ENST00000571680). The variant affects a conserved isoleucine residue in the PSI (plexin-semaphorin-integrin) domain of \u03b23 integrin.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Glanzmann thrombasthenia) is highly specific for ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations. GT is a well-characterized inherited platelet disorder with a single genetic etiology involving the \u03b1IIb\u03b23 integrin complex.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely pathogenic' for Glanzmann thrombasthenia (Allele ID: 3550493, NM_000212.3:c.383T>G p.Ile128Ser)."}}
{"variant_id": "1e8ae32a-d97c-4b55-8bad-887ebc9ccd35", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206756G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67819, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant (p.Ser252=) with no predicted impact on protein function. CADD and DITTO scores not available, but synonymous variants that do not affect splicing are computationally predicted to be benign by default.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.756C>T, p.Ser252Ser) that does not alter the amino acid sequence. Position c.756 is not at a canonical splice site (\u00b11/2 positions from exon-intron boundary). No evidence of cryptic splice site activation or splicing disruption in literature.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (Likely benign vs VUS) from different submitters. Variant is absent from gnomAD population databases, which would typically support PM2 for rare variants, but for synonymous variants without splice impact, rarity alone does not indicate pathogenicity. RUNX1 loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism, but synonymous variants do not cause loss of function unless they affect splicing."}}
{"variant_id": "b03c2ddf-8ac7-4851-91b1-243831593c98", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121416285G>A", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 198664, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database (rs2135818764 has no frequency data). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "notable": "This is an upstream/promoter variant (c.-287G>A) located 61-287 bp upstream of HNF1A transcription start site. ClinVar classifies as VUS for monogenic diabetes (VCV001342946). HGMD lists as CR133587 (regulatory mutation). PVS1 not applicable as this is not a null variant (nonsense, frameshift, or canonical splice). PP3 not applicable as computational predictors (SIFT, PolyPhen, CADD) are designed for coding variants and do not reliably predict effects of promoter variants. No functional studies demonstrating impact on HNF1A expression or transcription factor binding. HNF1A-MODY is caused by loss-of-function through haploinsufficiency, but upstream variants require functional evidence to establish pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "9b807b63-4df0-4550-998d-e8fc863076fc", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252940_36252941insGTTG", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 223481, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant not found in gnomAD or other population databases. Absent from controls supports rarity consistent with pathogenic variants in RUNX1-associated FPD-MM.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-associated familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPD-MM), which has a well-established single genetic etiology.", "notable": "CRITICAL ANNOTATION DISCREPANCY: VEP annotation maps NC_000021.8:g.36252940_36252941insGTTG to DOP1B gene as an intronic variant (c.5122-832_5122-831insGTTG), NOT to RUNX1. The provided genomic coordinates (chr21:36252940) appear to be outside the canonical RUNX1 gene region (chr21:34,787,801-36,004,667 in GRCh38). If this variant is truly within RUNX1 coding sequence and causes a frameshift, PVS1 would apply (RUNX1 loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for FPD-MM). Recommend verification of variant coordinates and transcript annotation before clinical action."}}
{"variant_id": "5b450859-2bbb-4ce1-8af2-dc8931047aca", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42449795G>A", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59094, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "SpliceAI predicts no impact on splicing. PhyloP score of 1.44 indicates the nucleotide is not highly conserved. Computational evidence suggests no deleterious effect on splicing or protein function.", "BP7": "This is an intronic variant (c.3061-4C>T) located at position -4 from the splice acceptor site, outside the canonical \u00b11/2 splice sites. No predicted splice impact by SpliceAI, and the nucleotide is not highly conserved (phyloP 1.44).", "notable": "PM2_Supporting was noted by ClinGen VCEP (gnomAD v4.1.0 MAF 0.00006687 in East Asian population, below 0.0001 threshold), but this supporting pathogenic criterion is outweighed by two benign supporting criteria (BP4, BP7). The variant was observed in healthy individuals during predisposition screening with no cases found in Glanzmann thrombasthenia patients in the literature."}}
{"variant_id": "a0869fac-ff3d-4379-932a-5fbf8fe43c63", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36206901A>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63059, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant chr21:g.36206901A>T (c.614-3T>A) is absent from gnomAD for this specific nucleotide change (A>T). The rsID rs762247645 shows the A>G change at extremely low frequency (AF=4.0e-06 exome, 1.3e-04 genome), but the A>T change queried here has no gnomAD entries, supporting rarity consistent with PM2.", "PP3": "Splice region variant at position -3 from exon boundary. SnpEff annotates as 'splice_region_variant&intron_variant' (c.614-3T>A). While not at canonical \u00b11/2 positions, position -3 is within the extended splice region and may affect splicing efficiency. Computational tools predict splice region impact.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition (OMIM 601399), and the phenotype has a well-established single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "RUNX1 is a well-established gene where loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism (haploinsufficiency causes familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy). However, PVS1 cannot be applied because this is a splice region variant at position -3, not a canonical splice site (\u00b11/2). ClinVar currently classifies this variant as VUS (Allele ID: 1348351). No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. The variant affects the RUNX1 gene which has strong gene-disease association with the patient's phenotype."}}
{"variant_id": "dfed8be2-fb3d-47be-ad3d-f6822f70faec", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38973951G>A", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "RYR1-related myopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3"], "expert_panel": "Congenital Myopathies VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 142407, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD: exome AF=1.2e-05 (2/166,892 alleles), genome AF=3.2e-05 (1/31,358 alleles). Combined frequency ~0.02% is well below the 1% threshold for autosomal dominant RYR1-related myopathy. Meets PM2 for rare variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: PolyPhen=probably_damaging (0.998), SIFT=deleterious (0.0). Missense variant affecting conserved alanine residue at position 1577 in a critical calcium channel protein.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports one submission as Pathogenic (VCV000065923) for Central core myopathy (CMYO1A). HGMD lists as disease-causing mutation (CM064217). Three PubMed citations (PMID:17365175, 16940308, 20301565) support pathogenicity.", "notable": "ClinVar has conflicting interpretations with 5 VUS submissions vs 1 Pathogenic submission. The variant is located in a non-cytoplasmic domain of the RYR1 calcium release channel. RYR1 is well-established as causative for central core myopathy and malignant hyperthermia susceptibility with autosomal dominant inheritance. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "fbe6b9cc-48c6-4253-b120-123974da4a50", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78092020G>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 144036, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is rare in gnomAD v2.1.1 with highest population MAF of 0.00019 (3/16178 alleles in African population), which is below the ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP threshold of <0.001 for PM2_Supporting. gnomAD exome AF: 2.4e-05; gnomAD genome AF: 3.9e-05. This meets PM2 at supporting level per disease-specific guidelines.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably damaging (score 0.988), REVEL=0.845 (above 0.7 threshold). The ClinGen expert panel confirmed PP3 is met based on REVEL score >0.7.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV000284232 has 9 submissions all classifying as VUS, including ClinGen Lysosomal Storage Disorder VCEP expert panel review (October 2023). The variant has been detected in at least 3 individuals but not in trans with a pathogenic variant and without Pompe disease symptoms, so PM3 and PP4 are not met. This is a missense variant (not null), so PVS1 is not applicable. No functional studies available (PS3 not met). No de novo evidence (PS2/PM6 not met). No segregation data (PP1 not met)."}}
{"variant_id": "38636142-e1fa-48a5-bfb1-682a7a505a4d", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.25616912A>G", "gene": "UBE3A", "disease": "Angelman syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 138994, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP colocated variants. For a dominant disorder with paternal imprinting like Angelman syndrome, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "UBE3A is a gene where missense variants are a known mechanism of disease. Bossuyt et al. (2021, PMID:33607653) demonstrated that 55% of AS-linked UBE3A missense mutations cause mislocalization and 29% cause loss of E3 ligase activity. Pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). The Cys137Arg substitution replaces a cysteine with arginine, a significant physicochemical change.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Angelman syndrome) is highly specific for UBE3A dysfunction. Angelman syndrome has a well-defined clinical presentation and UBE3A is the primary causative gene (~10% of cases due to point mutations).", "PP5": "ClinVar (VCV000156120) has one submission classifying this variant as 'Likely pathogenic'. HGMD also lists this variant (CM1516615) as disease-associated.", "notable": "This variant affects Cys137, located in the N-terminal region of UBE3A. Bossuyt et al. (2021) showed that N-terminal mutations can affect both subcellular localization and catalytic activity. The specific p.Cys137Arg variant was not directly tested in their functional screen, but the study provides strong mechanistic support for pathogenicity of UBE3A missense variants in this region."}}
{"variant_id": "d259092e-4ec8-4e34-9b36-8d548c8e4f7e", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23902341G>A", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61730, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg403Gln) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports NM_000257.4(MYH7):c.1208G>A (p.Arg403Gln) as Pathogenic with multiple submissions for Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy 1 (rs121913624). This is the canonical R403Q mutation first identified in HCM.", "PS3": "Extensive functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. Multiple publications (PMID:37771571, PMID:34634306, PMID:40463011) show R403Q causes hypercontractility, altered myosin relaxed states, and abnormal mechanotransduction. This is one of the most well-characterized HCM mutations with in vitro and in vivo functional evidence.", "PM1": "Located in the myosin motor domain (residue 403), a critical functional region. VEP shows multiple protein domain mappings including myosin motor domain (Pfam PF00063), SMART SM00242, and structural interaction variant annotations. The motor domain is a mutational hotspot for HCM with minimal benign variation.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exomes shows frequency of 6.84e-07 (essentially absent), with only 8.993e-07 in NFE population. This meets PM2 threshold for absence from controls.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Pathogenic missense variants are common in MYH7, and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). All transcript consequences show MODERATE impact with consistent damaging predictions across all 40+ transcripts.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000014087). Listed in HGMD (CM930503, CM900168) as disease-causing mutation. OMIM references 160760.0001 and 160760.0014."}}
{"variant_id": "735a8cdc-ae26-4fbf-b706-49da306cefca", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164907G>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 140579, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_supporting": "Variant c.968C>G (p.Thr323Arg) is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 and v3.1.2 population databases. The related variant at same position (c.968C>T) has extremely low frequency (AF=6.989e-07, 1 allele), but the specific G>C change is not observed. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this supports PM2 at supporting level.", "BP4": "Multiple computational predictors suggest benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (0.08-0.48), PolyPhen=benign (0.0). The variant is located at amino acid 323, which is OUTSIDE the critical Runt Homology Domain (RHD, residues 89-204). REVEL score for similar variants at this position is <0.50 (0.04-0.074). SpliceAI delta scores \u22640.20 indicate no significant splice impact despite being annotated as splice_region_variant.", "notable": "ClinVar VCV002076125 classifies this variant as Uncertain Significance. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP has evaluated similar variants at codon 323 (p.Thr323Met, p.Thr323Lys) and classified them as VUS with BP4 applied. RUNX1 is a well-established haploinsufficiency gene with sufficient evidence for dosage pathogenicity per ClinGen. However, pathogenic missense variants in RUNX1 are predominantly located within the RHD (residues 89-204), and this variant falls outside that critical domain. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.Thr323Arg were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "4e5e2b9c-9621-4b54-b6c4-650cc1dd3827", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48744786G>A", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PP4", "PP2", "PP3", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66608, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in calcium-binding EGF-like domain (cbEGF, Pfam PF07645, SMART SM00179/SM00181) of FBN1. This is a critical functional domain where pathogenic missense variants cluster. Cysteine substitutions and calcium-binding mutations in cbEGF domains are well-documented to cause Marfan syndrome and related fibrillinopathies (PMID: 35237611, 36035136).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 7.96e-06 (2 alleles), gnomAD genome AF = 6.37e-05 (2 alleles). This frequency is consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for an autosomal dominant disorder with estimated prevalence of 1:5,000-10,000.", "PP2": "FBN1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The majority of pathogenic FBN1 variants causing Marfan syndrome are missense mutations, particularly those affecting cysteine residues or calcium-binding domains. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.916-0.979). The p.Arg1840Cys substitution introduces a cysteine residue which can disrupt disulfide bonding patterns critical for EGF-like domain structure.", "PP5": "ClinVar (VCV000519783) reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters for Marfan syndrome and thoracic aortic aneurysm/dissection. HGMD (CM154844) lists as disease-causing mutation. Three independent ClinVar submissions classify as Likely Pathogenic (RCV001584440, RCV003106002, RCV002313269).", "notable": "The p.Arg1840Cys substitution creates a novel cysteine residue in the cbEGF domain. Cysteine residues are critical for disulfide bond formation that maintains EGF-like domain structure. Arginine-to-cysteine substitutions in FBN1 cbEGF domains have been associated with severe phenotypes including ectopia lentis and aortic complications. Two PubMed references (29357934, 25652356) are associated with this variant in ClinVar."}}
{"variant_id": "9b84fa8c-1789-41fa-a192-056f88af3907", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296882G>A", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS2_Very Strong", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67683, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg270*) in MECP2 creates premature termination codon at position 270 of 486 amino acids. MECP2 loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of Rett syndrome (X-linked dominant). The truncation occurs before the C-terminal domain, removing critical functional regions. VEP confirms HIGH impact stop_gained consequence.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. The G>A (nonsense) allele has zero observations in gnomAD exome/genome data. Only the G>C (missense) variant at this position has extremely rare frequency (AF=9.1\u00d710\u207b\u2077). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2 mutations. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations. The clinical presentation strongly supports pathogenicity.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (Allele ID: 26854). Classified as pathogenic for Rett syndrome (RTT), severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly, X-linked intellectual disability syndromes, and MECP2-related disorders. Also catalogued in HGMD (CM000749, CD002178)."}}
{"variant_id": "3cb94032-782f-4eb2-b705-a27547228f7e", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11222196A>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP1", "PP4", "PM5", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 77572, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP1", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 (0 alleles observed). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variant. p.Asp356Tyr (ClinVar ID 226345) is classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen FH Expert Panel. Additional variants at this codon: p.Asp356His (Likely Pathogenic), p.Asp356Val (Likely Pathogenic).", "PP1": "Variant co-segregates with FH phenotype in 2 informative meioses in 1 family (Centre de Genetique Moleculaire et Chromosomique, APHP Sorbonne Universite). Two affected family members carry the variant.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.947 (>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably damaging (score 0.96-0.977). Variant located in critical EGF-like domain (PS50026, PF07645).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for familial hypercholesterolemia. Variant identified in index case meeting clinical diagnostic criteria for FH after alternative causes of hypercholesterolemia were excluded."}}
{"variant_id": "d4a0cf35-7f65-4d8f-bcc2-3fe95327fb23", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164879G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67685, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.996C>T, p.Asp332=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions). VEP analysis shows no splice-altering consequences for RUNX1 transcripts.", "notable": "PM2 was considered but not applied: While the variant is absent in gnomAD (AF=0.0), the ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines recommend caution with PM2 for synonymous variants. ClinVar has conflicting interpretations (Likely benign from one submitter, VUS from another). The variant is located in the transactivation domain (TAD) region of RUNX1, but synonymous variants in this region without splice effects are generally considered benign."}}
{"variant_id": "317fdec6-df8d-4c37-90c0-0c5ae79cb5ad", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.138643725G>A", "gene": "F9", "disease": "hemophilia B", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM1", "PS3_Supporting", "PS4_Very Strong", "PP1", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59928, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "CRITICAL DISCREPANCY: The provided variant NC_000023.10:g.138643725G>A (using GRCh37/hg19 reference NC_000023.10) maps to FGF13 gene, NOT F9. VEP annotation shows this is a deep intronic variant (c.244-8070G>T in FGF13) with consequence 'intron_variant' and MODIFIER impact. The variant has an rsID (rs989758466) with extremely low gnomAD frequency (1.793e-05 overall, 0.0001912 in AMR population). F9 gene is located at Xq27.1 (approximately chrX:139,530,000-139,563,000 in GRCh38), which is different from the provided coordinates. If this variant is truly in F9, please verify the correct genomic coordinates. As annotated, this deep intronic variant in FGF13 has no predicted functional impact and does not meet criteria for pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "95de2f87-f28a-4d45-9c43-3ed5dc16733c", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252908T>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76921, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the Runt homology domain (RHD), a critical DNA-binding domain of RUNX1 (amino acids 50-177). The RHD is essential for transcription factor function and DNA binding. VEP annotations confirm the variant affects multiple protein domains including Pfam PF00853 (Runt domain), PROSITE PS51062, and structural interaction regions. Literature (PMID:36090034) confirms missense mutations in the RHD impair DNA binding and are recurrently associated with AML.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data found in myvariant or VEP annotations. For a rare autosomal dominant disorder like RUNX1-FPD, absence from population databases supports pathogenicity.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants in the Runt domain are a well-established mechanism of disease. Literature (PMID:33692461, PMID:36626254) confirms that missense variants in RUNX1, particularly in the RHD, cause familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPD/AML). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in this critical domain.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT score = 0 (deleterious_low_confidence) across all transcripts. PolyPhen = 0.968-0.997 (probably_damaging) in evaluated transcripts. snpEff annotates as 'structural_interaction_variant' indicating impact on protein structure. The variant affects a conserved lysine residue (K152/K125 depending on isoform) in the DNA-binding interface.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder (FPD/AML, OMIM #601399). This is a well-characterized single-gene disorder with autosomal dominant inheritance, matching the clinical presentation.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant (NM_001754.5:c.454A>C, p.Lys152Gln) as VUS with 2 submissions for 'not provided' and 'Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome'. COSMIC database shows colocated somatic variants (COSV55874586, COSV55888716) at this position, suggesting the residue is recurrently mutated in cancer. No specific functional studies for K152Q were identified, but in silico modeling (PMID:36090034) of RUNX1 RHD mutations demonstrates that mutations at DNA-binding interface residues reduce DNA association. Loss-of-function is an established mechanism for RUNX1-FPD (PMID:36741355, PMID:36626254)."}}
{"variant_id": "2a06ba5b-9a33-453f-9155-c4652c7b97b3", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68903911G>T", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PP1_Strong", "PM3", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 78060, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PP1_Strong", "PM3", "PP4", "PS3", "PM2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP1_Strong": "Variant segregates with childhood-onset severe retinal dystrophy in multiple families with at least 3 affected members (PMID: 9326941, 26352687). ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP upgraded to PP1_Strong based on segregation data.", "PM3": "Detected in homozygous state in at least two probands affected with Leber congenital amaurosis or early onset severe retinal dystrophy (PMID: 9326941, 26352687). For autosomal recessive RPE65-related retinopathy, homozygosity in affected individuals supports pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. ClinGen VCEP applied PP4_Moderate based on: reduced/nondetectable rod ERG, decreased central visual acuity, symptomatic onset between birth and age 5 years, cone involvement on ERG, light staring, nyctalopia, and positive response to RPE65 gene therapy.", "PS3": "In vitro isomerohydrolase activity assay in adenovirus-infected 293A-LRAT cells showed p.Pro363Thr mutant exhibits complete loss of 11-cis-retinol production relative to wild-type RPE65 control (PMID: 16828753). ClinGen VCEP applied as PS3_Supporting.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD v2.1.1 Popmax Filtering AF is 0.00004443 (4/30608 alleles) in South Asian population, below ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP threshold (<0.0002). gnomAD exome overall AF: 1.59e-05.", "PP3": "REVEL score 0.702 exceeds ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP threshold (>0.644). VEP reports SIFT=tolerated (0.18) and PolyPhen=benign (0.247), but REVEL meta-predictor is prioritized per VCEP specifications.", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel (ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP) reviewed and classified as Pathogenic (Dec 2023). Multiple clinical laboratories (Baylor Genetics, Invitae/Labcorp, Fulgent, MGZ) independently classified as Pathogenic with criteria provided."}}
{"variant_id": "2c4f9e62-f097-4573-acc3-06b1eecaf9f0", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164558G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50197, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Computational evidence supports no deleterious effect. Splice site prediction tools (SSF, MES) predict either an increase in canonical splice site score or decrease by no more than 10%, with no cryptic splice sites created. PhyloP conservation score is -0.44 (not conserved, threshold <0.1). VEP annotates this as LOW impact synonymous variant.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Ser439=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and splice prediction algorithms indicate no effect on splicing. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifically evaluated and applied BP7.", "notable": "PM2_supporting was applied by ClinGen VCEP (variant absent from gnomAD with adequate coverage), but this is downgraded to supporting level per ClinGen specifications and does not outweigh benign evidence. gnomAD exomes frequency: 0.00000; TOPMed: 0.00001. ClinVar has expert panel review (3-star) classifying as Likely Benign with consensus from ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP (Aug 2024), Labcorp Genetics, and Ambry Genetics."}}
{"variant_id": "c81e9cbb-091f-4bd8-8799-a865c5999243", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.7128194G>A", "gene": "ACADVL", "disease": "very long chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "ACADVL VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69964, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp606Ter) in ACADVL gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for VLCAD deficiency. This creates a premature stop codon at position 606 of 655 amino acids, predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a severely truncated non-functional protein. ACADVL is an autosomal recessive disorder where biallelic loss-of-function variants cause disease.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 6.841e-07 (approximately 1 in 1.5 million alleles). Only detected in NFE population at 8.993e-07. This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal recessive disorder.", "PP5": "Reported as Pathogenic in ClinVar (VCV000932836) with multiple RCV submissions for VLCAD deficiency. Also catalogued in HGMD (CM1512126) as a disease-causing mutation. Associated literature includes PMID:26385305 and PMID:10431122."}}
{"variant_id": "8ab7cf89-4df9-4ee4-ac6a-8b22d634ebb3", "variant": "NC_000018.9:g.53128285T>C", "gene": "TCF4", "disease": "Pitt-Hopkins syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP4", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68682, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant not found in gnomAD or any population database. Absent from myvariant and VEP colocated variant databases. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of Pitt-Hopkins syndrome is highly specific for TCF4 pathogenic variants. PTHS has a single genetic etiology (TCF4 haploinsufficiency) with characteristic features including severe intellectual disability, breathing abnormalities, and distinctive facial features.", "notable": "CRITICAL COORDINATE DISCREPANCY: The provided genomic coordinates (NC_000018.9:g.53128285T>C) map to the DCC gene, NOT TCF4, according to VEP annotation. NC_000018.9 is the GRCh37/hg19 reference sequence, but GRCh38 was specified. TCF4 is located at chr18:52,889,562-53,332,018 (GRCh38). This variant requires coordinate verification before clinical interpretation. Additionally, VEP shows this is an intronic variant (c.1063-29071T>C in DCC), which would not support PVS1 if confirmed in TCF4. Literature strongly supports TCF4 haploinsufficiency as the mechanism for PTHS (PMID:34748727, PMID:33414364), with loss-of-function mutations including nonsense, frameshift, splice-site, and missense mutations in the bHLH domain causing disease."}}
{"variant_id": "47b30ecd-c4eb-470e-bd81-0bba893f6f40", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.23896915G>A", "gene": "MYH7", "disease": "cardiomyopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Cardiomyopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 64492, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg453Cys) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar reports this exact variant (rs121913625, c.1357C>T) as Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic for hypertrophic cardiomyopathy 1 with multiple submissions (VCV000014089). Additionally, different nucleotide changes at this position (c.1357C>A causing p.Arg453Ser) are also classified as Pathogenic.", "PM1": "Located in the myosin motor domain (head region) of MYH7, a critical functional domain. Position R453 is within the highly conserved myosin ATPase motor domain. Multiple pathogenic variants cluster at this position (R453C, R453S, R453H). VEP shows multiple protein structure mappings (PDB: 4db1, 4p7h, 4pa0, 5tby, 8act, 8g4l, etc.) confirming location in structured functional domain.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD. VEP colocated variant data shows gnomAD exome frequency of 3.42e-06 (3.4 per million) and gnomAD genome frequency of 6.57e-06. This is well below the 0.01% threshold for autosomal dominant hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.", "PP2": "MYH7 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. Pathogenic missense variants are common in MYH7 (one of the most frequently mutated genes in HCM), and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=0 (deleterious), PolyPhen=1.0 (probably_damaging). The variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in the myosin motor domain.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic by multiple submitters including clinical laboratories. Multiple RCV accessions (RCV000015145, RCV000035717, RCV000154254, RCV000158799, RCV000230258, RCV000618958, RCV001170514, RCV001375645, RCV001618214) with consensus Pathogenic classification.", "notable": "Extensive functional evidence exists: PMID:38862020 demonstrates MYH7 R453C induces cardiac remodelling via TGF-beta/Smad2/3, ERK1/2 and Nox4/ROS/NF-kappaB signalling pathways. PMID:36948619 reports case series of end-stage HCM with advanced heart failure in patients carrying MYH7 R453 variants. PMID:38642550 shows myosin inhibitor reverses HCM phenotype in iPSC-cardiomyocytes with this variant. Over 35 PubMed citations support pathogenicity. OMIM entries 160760.0043 and 160760.0003 document this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "ecff39ce-d1a1-46c9-befc-b352b0e30c5b", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605731C>T", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 117945, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted deleterious effect on protein function. MYOC disease mechanism is gain-of-function (protein misfolding), not loss-of-function, making synonymous variants unlikely to be pathogenic.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.849G>A, p.Glu283=) with no predicted splice impact. Variant is located in exon 3 at codon position 849, not near canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2). VEP consequence is 'synonymous_variant' with LOW impact.", "notable": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD (6.849e-07, ~1 allele in 1.5M), which would typically support PM2. However, for synonymous variants in a gain-of-function gene, rarity alone does not suggest pathogenicity. ClinVar classifies as VUS (VCV002442267). MYOC-associated glaucoma is caused by protein misfolding/aggregation (gain-of-function), not haploinsufficiency, making synonymous variants very unlikely to cause disease."}}
{"variant_id": "934a786c-fbe9-425c-a5bb-904d238bc687", "variant": "NC_000014.8:g.29237157C>G", "gene": "FOXG1", "disease": "FOXG1 disorder", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 43491, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BP4", "BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP4": "Synonymous variant with no predicted functional impact. CADD score not available but VEP impact is LOW. No splice site disruption predicted. Multiple computational tools indicate no deleterious effect.", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Gly224=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant does not alter the amino acid sequence and is not located at a canonical splice site.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with 2 Benign, 1 Likely Benign, and 1 Conflicting submission (VCV000158597). gnomAD exome frequency is 0.0188% (47/250,000+ alleles), which is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant in a rare dominant disorder. FOXG1 syndrome is caused by loss-of-function variants (haploinsufficiency), but this synonymous variant does not cause protein truncation or splice disruption."}}
{"variant_id": "faeecf67-a17e-4c56-b8d5-d7eabea68354", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185213G>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PP1_Moderate", "PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65967, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database with allele frequency of 3.98e-06 (1 allele in ~251,000 alleles). This is well below the expected frequency for GCK-MODY (prevalence ~1:10,000) and meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in this gene. This missense variant (p.Glu256Lys) fits the disease mechanism.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (scores 0.68-0.99 across transcripts). The variant affects a structurally important residue with 'structural_interaction_variant' annotation in snpEff, indicating involvement in protein structural interactions.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK is the causative gene for MODY2, and the clinical presentation aligns with this diagnosis.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000421063, allele_id 259865). The variant is classified as Pathogenic for multiple conditions including: Maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 2, Monogenic diabetes, MODY, Permanent neonatal diabetes mellitus, and Type 2 diabetes mellitus. HGMD also lists this variant (CM930301, CM096796).", "notable": "Comprehensive functional study (PMID:37101203) created a complete map of GCK variant activity using multiplexed yeast complementation assay. This study established that GCK missense variants causing MODY show reduced enzyme activity, and activity scores correlate with fasting glucose levels in carriers. The E256 position is located in a functionally important region of the glucokinase enzyme. Additionally, a different nucleotide change at the same position (c.766G>C, p.Glu256Gln) is classified as Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar, supporting pathogenicity of variants at this residue (supports PM5 concept though not formally applied as it's not the same amino acid change)."}}
{"variant_id": "b93876af-b0e4-4344-ba93-9faae71b0273", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68910225T>G", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 73246, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.98e-06 (1 allele), gnomAD genome AF = 6.57e-06. For a recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with pathogenicity (well below expected carrier frequency for RPE65-related disease).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen-2 = probably damaging (score 0.957). The variant is also listed in HGMD (CM078251) as a disease-causing mutation.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (RPE65-related recessive retinopathy) is highly specific for a disease with a single genetic etiology. RPE65 mutations account for 3-16% of LCA/EORD cases, and the phenotype-genotype correlation is well-established.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000870346) for LCA2, RP20, and RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. Associated with PMIDs 17964524 and 20079931.", "notable": "This missense variant (p.Thr162Pro) affects a conserved threonine residue in the RPE65 protein, which functions as a retinoid isomerohydrolase essential for the visual cycle. The proline substitution may disrupt local protein structure. RPE65 is a well-established gene for autosomal recessive inherited retinal dystrophies with FDA-approved gene therapy (Luxturna). No functional studies specific to this variant were identified (PS3 not met). PM3 could potentially be applied if confirmed in trans with another pathogenic variant."}}
{"variant_id": "8e911e71-3693-4daf-b9ae-6cb15e45c36a", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68910277G>A", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67851, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Strong", "PM5", "PP1", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3_Supporting": "Functional studies demonstrate complete loss of RPE65 enzymatic activity (0% isomerohydrolase activity in retinoid isomerase assay vs wild-type, PMID:16754667). Additional studies show decreased protein expression and accelerated degradation (PMID:25752820). Meets PS3_Supporting threshold per ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP specifications.", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant present in gnomAD v4.1.0 at extremely low frequency (GrpMax AF=0.0001329 in African/African-American population; overall AF=5.57e-05 in exomes, 3.19e-05 in genomes). Below ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP PM2_Supporting threshold of <0.0002.", "PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in multiple unrelated probands: compound heterozygous with c.11+5G>A and c.272G>A (p.Arg91Gln) in at least 2 probands (PMIDs:35129589, 33952291). Also reported homozygous in at least 4 unrelated probands with early-onset severe retinal dystrophy (PMIDs:35129589, 18722466). Meets PM3_Strong threshold.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variants: p.Arg91Gln (ClinVar VCV000098857) and p.Arg91Pro (ClinVar VCV000098858) are both classified as pathogenic for RPE65-related retinopathy.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease demonstrated in multiple affected family members. Variant segregated with childhood-onset severe retinal dystrophy through proband plus 2 similarly affected relatives in homozygous state (PMID:31925606). Meets PP1_Moderate per ClinGen VCEP.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.941), REVEL=0.852 (above ClinGen threshold of \u22650.773), SpliceAI=0.22 (above threshold of \u22650.2 predicting splice impact).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy. Clinical features include congenital onset, abnormal visual acuity, extinguished scotopic and photopic ERG responses, bone spicule pigmentation, white/yellow fundus dots, and nystagmus - collectively highly specific for this single-gene disorder (PMID:31925606).", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel classification: Reviewed by ClinGen Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early Onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP (July 2024) as Pathogenic with 3-star review status. 22 total ClinVar submissions, all concordant for Pathogenic classification. FDA Recognized Database entry."}}
{"variant_id": "654428f7-dc77-4baf-9a5f-7ebaa256f704", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.14976471G>A", "gene": "DCLRE1C", "disease": "severe combined immunodeficiency due to DCLRE1C deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 665216, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T04:25:08.995050Z\",\"request_id\":\"df299"}
{"variant_id": "86306b55-3d7f-4eb7-885d-46f107384d83", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.68910339G>A", "gene": "RPE65", "disease": "RPE65-related recessive retinopathy", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Leber Congenital Amaurosis/early onset Retinal Dystrophy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56752, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Strong", "PM5", "PP1_Moderate", "PP3_Moderate", "PP4_Moderate", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3_Supporting": "Functional studies demonstrate 0% enzymatic activity in retinoid isomerase assay relative to wild-type control (PMID: 16754667). Additional studies show decreased protein expression, abnormal cytoplasmic localization (vs normal membrane association), and accelerated degradation (Takahashi et al., 2006; Li et al., 2015).", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant present in gnomAD v4.1.0 at extremely low frequency: GrpMax AF = 0.0001329 (16/74,990 alleles in African/African-American population). gnomAD exome AF = 5.57e-05, gnomAD genome AF = 3.19e-05. Below ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP PM2_Supporting threshold of <0.0002.", "PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in multiple unrelated probands: compound heterozygous with c.11+5G>A or c.272G>A (p.Arg91Gln) in at least 2 probands (PMIDs: 35129589, 33952291). Also reported homozygous in at least 4 unrelated probands with early-onset severe retinal dystrophy (PMIDs: 35129589, 18722466).", "PM5": "Another pathogenic missense variant at the same codon, NM_000329.3(RPE65):c.272G>A (p.Arg91Gln), has been classified as pathogenic for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy by ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP.", "PP1_Moderate": "Variant segregates with childhood-onset severe retinal dystrophy in proband plus 2 similarly affected relatives in homozygous state (PMID: 31925606).", "PP3_Moderate": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL = 0.852 (above ClinGen threshold \u22650.773), SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 0.941), SpliceAI = 0.22 (above threshold \u22650.2 predicting splicing impact).", "PP4_Moderate": "Patient phenotype highly specific for RPE65-related recessive retinopathy: congenital onset, abnormal visual acuity, extinguished scotopic and photopic ERG responses, bone spicule pigmentation, white/yellow fundus dots, nystagmus (9 total phenotype points per ClinGen scoring, PMID: 31925606).", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel (ClinGen LCA/eoRD VCEP) reviewed and classified as Pathogenic (July 2024). 22 total ClinVar submissions, all concordant for Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic. FDA Recognized Database entry."}}
{"variant_id": "196b22b0-f2f5-4fc6-a399-b9c89bb23124", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171621387C>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "juvenile open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 125032, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is extremely rare in gnomAD v4.1.0: highest MAF = 0.00008329 in Admixed American population (5/60,032 alleles), meeting the \u22640.0001 threshold for PM2_Supporting per ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP specifications.", "BP4": "Multiple computational predictors suggest benign effect: REVEL = 0.062 (within 0.017-0.183 benign range per ClinGen Glaucoma VCEP), PolyPhen = 0.003 (benign). While SIFT = 0.04 (deleterious), the overall computational evidence supports no functional impact. ClinGen Glaucoma Expert Panel applied BP4_Moderate.", "notable": "This variant was reviewed by the ClinGen Glaucoma Variant Curation Expert Panel (Nov 2025) and classified as VUS with a score of -1 (BP4_Moderate + PM2_Supporting). The variant is located at position 122, outside the critical olfactomedin domain (residues 244-504) where most pathogenic MYOC variants cluster. Only 1 proband with JOAG has been reported, not meeting the \u22652 probands threshold for PS4_Supporting. MYOC-associated glaucoma is caused by gain-of-function (protein misfolding), not loss-of-function."}}
{"variant_id": "e10d0c3d-b478-421d-9e3f-919a9e7ff2eb", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246591A>T", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Strong", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67473, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PM2", "PM3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "Deep intronic variant c.1199+502A>T causes aberrant splicing with pseudo-exon inclusion, leading to loss of function of PAH. While not a canonical splice site variant, functional studies demonstrate it disrupts normal splicing. Applied at moderate strength as deep intronic variant with demonstrated splice effect.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies (minigene assays) in Jin et al. 2022 (PMID: 34747549) and Zhang et al. 2023 (PMID: 37237386) demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing through pseudo-exon activation, leading to non-functional PAH protein.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. Not found in any population controls, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variant for autosomal recessive PKU.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with known pathogenic PAH variants in multiple PKU patients. Zhang et al. 2023 documented 18 patients with this variant in compound heterozygous state with other pathogenic variants (c.728G>A, c.1238G>C, c.1199G>A, c.782G>A, c.526C>T, etc.).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlation.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV001120176) for Phenylketonuria. Multiple independent submissions support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "a5b1509f-a41a-4e1f-8abf-f00dfd44bcf5", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231763G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia with normal platelets-hematological cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP4", "BP2", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 45225, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency significantly higher than expected for a rare autosomal dominant disorder. gnomAD genome AF = 0.59% (0.00586), gnomAD exome AF = 0.32% (0.0032). Finnish population shows enrichment up to 3.4%. This frequency is incompatible with a highly penetrant pathogenic variant for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder.", "BP4": "Computational evidence suggests no significant impact. VEP classifies this as LOW impact splice_region_variant located at position +8 from splice donor site (c.613+8C>T). Intronic variants at position +8 are outside the canonical splice site (\u00b11/2) and typically do not disrupt splicing. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but the intronic location and VEP LOW impact classification support benign interpretation.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign (VCV000339876) with multiple submissions supporting benign classification. While RUNX1 loss-of-function is a known disease mechanism for FPDMM, this intronic variant at +8 position is unlikely to cause significant splicing disruption. No literature evidence was found specifically linking this variant to disease."}}
{"variant_id": "520e26f1-fc70-45b8-be82-bedb61fe0eb6", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164634T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 316125, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant was reviewed by the ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy Variant Curation Expert Panel (Oct 2024) who determined it does not meet any ACMG/AMP criteria. The variant is a missense change (p.Tyr414Cys) in the transactivation domain of RUNX1. While RUNX1 is associated with hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome with haploinsufficiency as a mechanism, this specific missense variant lacks functional evidence. gnomAD shows 1 allele (AF=6.29e-06), which is extremely rare but present, preventing PM2 from being applied. Computational predictions are conflicting (SIFT: deleterious_low_confidence; PolyPhen-2: probably_damaging 0.997), but the expert panel did not apply PP3. The tyrosine at position 414 is highly conserved with a large physicochemical difference to cysteine, but no functional studies or case reports exist for this specific variant. The variant is located in the Pfam domain PF08504 (RUNX inhibition domain), but without evidence of pathogenic variants clustering at this position or functional impact data, PM1 cannot be applied."}}
{"variant_id": "dc825edb-4862-4de0-b847-29928bc5af09", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.23646996C>T", "gene": "PALB2", "disease": "hereditary breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "BP1"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 53884, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Trp1038Ter) creating premature stop codon in PALB2, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary breast cancer. The variant occurs in exon 9 of 13 exons and is predicted to undergo nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) or produce a truncated protein lacking the critical C-terminal WD40 domain required for BRCA2 interaction. PALB2 functions in homologous recombination DNA repair pathway.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 5.97e-05 (15/251,000 alleles); gnomAD genome AF = 6.37e-05 (2/31,400 alleles). This frequency is well below the expected threshold for a pathogenic variant in a dominant cancer predisposition gene with incomplete penetrance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000126711) for: Familial cancer of breast, Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, Hereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome, BROVCA5. Clinical significance is consistent across 12+ RCV records. Also listed in HGMD (CM070242) and OMIM (610355.0013).", "notable": "Extensive literature support: PMID:28779002 (PALB2 truncating variants associated with increased breast cancer risk), PMID:26484312 and PMID:27621404 specifically cite c.3113G>A/p.W1038X as pathogenic. COSMIC entries (COSM9496586, COSM6394884) indicate somatic occurrence in tumors. The variant is located in the WD40 repeat domain critical for BRCA2 binding and DNA repair function."}}
{"variant_id": "be2964af-17d7-41a7-9c33-7afda47fa9fa", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.154182236G>A", "gene": "F8", "disease": "hemophilia A", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4", "PS2", "PP1_Strong", "PP4_Moderate", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Coagulation Factor Deficiency VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 126709, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the A2 domain of Factor VIII, a critical functional domain. The A2 domain is essential for Factor VIII cofactor activity and contains multiple pathogenic missense variants. Codon 612 is within a conserved region important for protein function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 2.18e-05 (4 alleles total). For an X-linked recessive disorder like hemophilia A, this frequency is consistent with disease-causing variants given the disease prevalence (~1:5000 males).", "PP2": "F8 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (hemophilia A). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common causes of mild-to-moderate hemophilia A.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.999). The arginine to cysteine substitution introduces a reactive thiol group that may disrupt protein structure or function.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000010236) with 5 RCV submissions from multiple submitters. HGMD has two entries (CD123883, CM910133). Multiple PubMed citations support pathogenicity (PMIDs: 7728145, 1301932, 1908096, 8281136, 31064749, 27943580, 19548904).", "notable": "This variant has been reported in COSMIC (COSV64269271) as a somatic mutation, though F8 is not a canonical cancer gene. The variant is associated with multiple conditions in ClinVar including hereditary factor VIII deficiency (hemophilia A), thrombophilia X-linked, and familial aortopathy."}}
{"variant_id": "59922c1f-f11d-4a37-947e-cbd65fe16ee8", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.45654310G>C", "gene": "GATM", "disease": "AGAT deficiency", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 83119, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "low", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant NC_000015.9:g.45654310G>C is absent from gnomAD and all major population databases. Given the rarity of AGAT deficiency (only 16 individuals reported worldwide), absence from population databases supports PM2 for this autosomal recessive disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of AGAT deficiency is highly specific for GATM-related disease. AGAT deficiency is a rare autosomal recessive disorder with characteristic biochemical findings (low guanidinoacetate in urine/plasma/CSF, low creatine levels) and clinical features (developmental delay, intellectual disability, muscle weakness). Per ClinGen CCDS VCEP guidelines (PMID: 38452609), PP4 can be applied using a points system based on biochemical and clinical findings.", "notable": "CRITICAL LIMITATION: VEP annotation indicates the provided coordinates (chr15:45654310) map to an intronic region of the SQOR gene, not GATM. GATM is located at 15q21.1 (approximately chr15:45,369,000-45,402,000 in GRCh38). The provided variant coordinates may be incorrect or use a different reference sequence version. This significantly limits the ability to assess variant-specific criteria (PVS1, PP3, PM1, etc.). Verification of the correct genomic coordinates is essential before clinical use of this classification. Additionally, no ClinVar entries or literature reports were found for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "ff550456-5053-40d7-86de-84e32f5b1636", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.39003004C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62777, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Functional study in mouse knock-in model (G2435R, equivalent to human G2434R) demonstrated bioenergetic defects in muscle fibers associated with malignant hyperthermia (PMID:32826313). This provides well-established in vivo functional evidence of a damaging effect.", "PS4": "Variant is documented in multiple affected individuals with malignant hyperthermia susceptibility across multiple ClinVar submissions (RCV000013837, RCV000119698, RCV000551243, RCV000612258, RCV001787719-25, RCV002288488, RCV002513026, RCV005025050). OMIM entry 180901.0007 establishes this as a known pathogenic variant. PMID:36751502 reports this variant in MH/rhabdomyolysis patients.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: AF = 3.18e-05 (exome), 5.26e-05 (genome). This is well below the expected frequency for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance like MHS1 (<0.01%). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = possibly damaging (0.466-0.858). Glycine to Arginine substitution introduces a large, positively charged residue in place of the smallest amino acid, likely disrupting protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (malignant hyperthermia susceptibility) is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. MHS1 has a well-established single genetic etiology with RYR1 being the primary causative gene.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from expert laboratories. HGMD entry CM941269 and OMIM 180901.0007 further support pathogenicity. PharmGKB (PA166155544) documents drug response associations."}}
{"variant_id": "63503e61-4aae-421e-be03-6666cab6c331", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.42460932C>A", "gene": "ITGA2B", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75756, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_supporting", "PM3_supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v4.0 (0 alleles in >1,500,000 total alleles). For autosomal recessive disorders, absence from population databases supports PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen recommendations.", "PM3_supporting": "Variant observed in homozygosity in one individual (GT28) with Glanzmann thrombasthenia phenotype (PMID: 16463284). For recessive disorders, homozygosity in an affected individual provides supporting evidence for PM3.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0), REVEL=0.853 (exceeds VCEP threshold of \u22650.7). Variant located in integrin alpha chain domain (PROSITE PS51470).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype is highly specific for Glanzmann thrombasthenia: history of bleeding, impaired platelet aggregation to multiple agonists, but normal/mildly reduced ristocetin agglutination. GT has a well-defined genetic etiology (ITGA2B/ITGB3 mutations). ClinGen VCEP applied PP4 at moderate strength.", "notable": "ClinGen Platelet Disorders VCEP (expert panel, April 2024) classified this variant as VUS using their disease-specific criteria. Another missense at same codon (p.Gly380Asp) also classified as VUS. HGMD lists this variant (CM021108, CM061067). No functional studies available to confirm pathogenicity (PS3 not met). PVS1 not applicable as this is a missense variant, not a null variant."}}
{"variant_id": "26cea1af-9453-4d25-8531-cb770a0f706d", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103237523A>G", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70732, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: allele frequency 1.368e-06 overall (1 allele in ~730,000). Only observed in NFE population at 1.799e-06. For autosomal recessive PKU, this meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The PAH gene has >900 reported pathogenic missense variants causing PKU, and benign missense variation is uncommon. This missense variant (p.Leu367Pro) in a gene with low rate of benign missense supports PP2.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.974-0.997). The variant introduces a proline substitution at a conserved leucine residue in the catalytic domain, which is predicted to disrupt protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with autosomal recessive inheritance, making this phenotype highly specific for the disease.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as VUS (VCV000102525). Two HGMD entries exist at this position (CM101160, CM993959). The variant is located in the aromatic amino acid hydroxylase catalytic domain (Pfam PF00351). No functional studies specifically for p.Leu367Pro were identified in literature. The proline substitution may disrupt local secondary structure."}}
{"variant_id": "5bdf0667-75ca-4f68-afd0-9746a380e787", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36171700C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 121174, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF = 3.98e-06, 1 allele observed). For an autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance like RUNX1-FPD, this frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant. Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants are a known mechanism of disease. The ClinGen MM-VCEP has established that missense variants in RUNX1, particularly in the transactivation domain (TAD), can cause familial platelet disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy (RUNX1-FPD). The variant p.Gly289Arg is located in the transactivation domain (amino acids 291-371 per ClinGen specifications, though position 289 is at the boundary region).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-FPD, which has a well-established single genetic etiology (germline RUNX1 variants). This phenotype-genotype correlation strongly supports pathogenicity.", "notable": "This variant (c.865G>C, p.Gly289Arg) is classified as VUS in ClinVar (VCV000532657) by multiple submitters. The position is in the transactivation domain (TAD) region of RUNX1. SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0), though with low confidence. The same genomic position has COSMIC entries (COSM5858582, COSM4385166) indicating somatic occurrence in cancer. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. PM1 was not applied as position 289 is at the boundary of the TAD critical region (291-371) per ClinGen RUNX1-specific guidelines."}}
{"variant_id": "32174cab-38f2-4ca9-816b-e98c24809005", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.18622608T>G", "gene": "CDKL5", "disease": "CDKL5 disorder", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS1", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 55622, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Variant present in gnomAD at allele frequency higher than expected for CDKL5 disorder: gnomAD exome AF=1.09e-05 (2 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=9.18e-05 (2 alleles). Combined frequency exceeds expected for a rare X-linked disorder with severe phenotype and reduced reproductive fitness.", "BP4": "Multiple computational tools predict benign effect: PolyPhen=benign (score 0.01), SIFT=deleterious_low_confidence (score 0.03, borderline). The variant is a conservative Leu>Val substitution (both hydrophobic amino acids) located outside the catalytic kinase domain (residue 522 is in the C-terminal region). No CADD or DITTO scores available, but PolyPhen strongly supports benign classification.", "notable": "ClinVar has multiple submissions for this variant (VCV000434664): 1 Benign (for CDKL5 disorder), 2 Likely Benign (for DEE2 and not provided), 1 Uncertain Significance (for not specified). The variant is located in a MobiDB-annotated disordered region, not in a critical functional domain. The amino acid change (Leu522Val) is conservative, preserving hydrophobic character."}}
{"variant_id": "0696ef53-ca1c-4130-8c3a-ded2439659dd", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38991277G>C", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PM1_Supporting", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 225810, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. The G>C change (p.Arg2452Pro) has no reported allele frequency, supporting rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant for this autosomal dominant condition.", "PM5": "Novel missense change at the same amino acid position (Arg2452) as an established pathogenic variant. The p.Arg2452Gln (c.7355G>A) variant at this position is classified as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic in ClinVar for RYR1-related disorders, supporting that amino acid changes at this position are disease-causing.", "PP2": "RYR1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for malignant hyperthermia susceptibility. The ClinGen RYR1-MHS Variant Curation Expert Panel has classified numerous missense variants as pathogenic, and the gene has a low rate of benign missense variation relative to pathogenic missense variants.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict a deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.992-0.999). The arginine to proline substitution introduces a helix-breaking residue that likely disrupts local protein structure.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of malignant hyperthermia susceptibility is highly specific for RYR1-related disease. MHS has a well-defined genetic etiology with RYR1 being the primary causative gene (>70% of cases)."}}
{"variant_id": "45d8759d-7438-4066-a6cc-7193f6524fdb", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203424500G>A", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 52786, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH). gnomAD exome AF=0.000263 (66 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.000191. Notably enriched in Ashkenazi Jewish population (gnomAD exome ASJ=0.0059, gnomAD genome ASJ=0.0066). PAH prevalence is ~15-50 per million; this frequency is higher than expected for a highly penetrant dominant disease-causing variant.", "BP4": "Computational evidence suggests benign effect. SIFT=0.12 (tolerated), PolyPhen=0.335 (benign). The variant is located in the cytoplasmic tail domain (position 983), which is outside the critical kinase domain (residues 203-502). No CADD or DITTO scores available, but both available predictors indicate tolerated/benign.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: VCV000333652 with submissions of 'Uncertain significance', 'Likely benign', and 'Conflicting interpretations of pathogenicity'. The variant p.Arg983Gln is in the C-terminal cytoplasmic tail domain, which is less functionally constrained than the kinase domain. BMPR2 is definitively associated with heritable PAH via loss-of-function mechanism, but this missense variant in the tail domain with benign computational predictions and elevated population frequency does not support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "03f19343-ea6f-460e-b6f5-a18145f32513", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68845762G>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS3", "PS4", "PVS1_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67710, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1_Moderate", "PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP1", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1_Moderate": "This synonymous variant (c.1137G>A, p.Thr379=) occurs at the last nucleotide of exon 8, adjacent to the canonical splice donor site. RNA studies demonstrate it causes aberrant splicing with out-of-frame transcripts leading to premature termination codons. CDH1 loss-of-function is an established mechanism for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer. Applied as PVS1_Moderate per ClinGen CDH1 VCEP guidelines for G-to-non-G changes at last nucleotide of exon.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate this variant causes aberrant splicing. Multiple publications (PMID: 15831593, 18427545, 19965908) show RNA analysis reveals complex aberrant splicing patterns affecting exon 8, producing defective alternatively spliced transcripts with premature stop codons and high levels of allelic expression imbalance. RNAseq data confirms exon skipping and intron retention (p=0.0).", "PS4": "Variant reported in at least 4+ families meeting HDGC clinical criteria (PMID: 15831593, 17545690, 17221870, 21681551, 27995193, 32362280). Multiple affected individuals with diffuse gastric cancer and lobular breast cancer carry this variant. Segregation with disease observed across multiple generations in multiple families.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database (gnomAD exome frequency: 6.84e-07, essentially absent). TOPMed frequency: 0.00001. Variant is extremely rare in control populations, consistent with pathogenic variant in a highly penetrant cancer syndrome.", "PP1": "Co-segregation with disease documented in multiple families. In PMID: 32362280, variant segregated with HDGC through multiple generations (index patient, father, brother, aunt all carriers with gastric cancer). In PMID: 15831593, segregation observed through two generations with gastric cancer and cleft lip/palate phenotypes.", "PP5": "ClinVar expert panel classification: Pathogenic (reviewed by ClinGen Gastric Cancer Variant Curation Expert Panel, August 2023). 17 total submissions to ClinVar, all classifying as Pathogenic (16) or Likely Pathogenic (1). FDA Recognized Database. OMIM entry 192090.0020 lists as pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "b30414dc-92da-4197-a2c6-586d93ddce23", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164684T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 204109, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BP7"], "aiva_evidence": {"BP7": "Synonymous variant (c.1191A>G, p.Gln397=) with no predicted splice impact. The variant is located at position c.1191 which is not near canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2 positions). ClinVar reports this variant as 'Likely benign' for the associated RUNX1 syndrome (Allele ID 2920297).", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations: 'Likely benign' from one submitter for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematological cancer predisposition syndrome associated with RUNX1, and 'Uncertain significance' from another submitter for the same condition. The variant is absent from gnomAD population databases, which would typically support PM2 for rare variants, but this is insufficient to overcome the benign evidence for a synonymous variant without splice impact. Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines (PMID:31648317), synonymous variants without predicted splice effects are generally classified as likely benign."}}
{"variant_id": "0a3b6aa8-ca64-4f5b-bf58-e79930be9a9f", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89623251G>A", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2_Supporting", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59855, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) in PTEN, a well-established tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (PHTS)/Cowden syndrome. This variant creates a premature stop codon at position 130, resulting in a truncated protein lacking the critical phosphatase domain. PTEN functions as a lipid and protein phosphatase regulating the PI3K/AKT pathway; haploinsufficiency causes disease.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome shows AF = 1.19339e-05 (3 alleles in ~250,000 individuals), well below the 0.01% threshold for dominant disorders. This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant condition.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome) is highly specific for PTEN-related disorders. PHTS has a single genetic etiology (PTEN mutations) and the clinical presentation strongly supports this diagnosis.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (14 RCV records) for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, Cowden syndrome 1, Macrocephaly-autism syndrome, Glioma susceptibility 2, and hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome. All submissions consistently classify as Pathogenic.", "notable": "CIViC database (EID1627) documents this variant with evidence for sensitivity to Perifosine + Temsirolimus combination therapy in thyroid cancer (Level D evidence). Literature (PMID:38353885) reports this specific variant in a patient with Cowden syndrome and multiple bronchial carcinoids. Functional studies (PMID:34649609) demonstrate that PTEN nonsense mutations result in complete loss of phosphatase activity."}}
{"variant_id": "c3388a6a-bb70-404d-9071-818cc4259294", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43048453C>T", "gene": "HNF4A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS4_Moderate", "PM2_Supporting", "PP1_Strong", "PP4", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67093, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln255*) in HNF4A creating premature stop codon. HNF4A is a well-established gene where loss-of-function is a known mechanism of disease for MODY1 (maturity-onset diabetes of the young type 1). The variant affects multiple transcripts (ENST00000316673, ENST00000457232, ENST00000609795, ENST00000894460) and is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or truncated protein lacking critical C-terminal domains.", "PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in myvariant annotation, indicating extremely rare or absent in general population. This supports rarity consistent with pathogenic variant for autosomal dominant MODY.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for HNF4A-related MODY1. HNF4A is one of the established MODY genes with well-characterized clinical presentation including early-onset diabetes, autosomal dominant inheritance, and sulfonylurea responsiveness.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (rs137853334, Allele ID: 24249) with multiple submissions for MODY1 and Monogenic diabetes. HGMD also lists this variant (CM961363) as disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "c77e2294-e05e-49f2-a917-7266c296dfaa", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.121426697C>G", "gene": "HNF1A", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 663465, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T04:32:56.832071Z\",\"request_id\":\"3c4db"}
{"variant_id": "b84cf0fd-d40e-4407-96af-74368d614b6e", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48905266T>C", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP4", "PS4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 69143, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in FBN1 cbEGF-like domain region. Cysteine substitutions in cbEGF-like domains are associated with severe phenotypes including Marfan syndrome (PMID: 35237611). The variant introduces a novel cysteine (p.Tyr63Cys) which may disrupt critical disulfide bonding patterns essential for fibrillin-1 structure.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD (AF=4.0e-06, 1 allele in ~250,000). This frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder like Marfan syndrome (prevalence ~1:5,000).", "PP2": "FBN1 has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are a well-established mechanism of Marfan syndrome. Approximately 60% of pathogenic FBN1 missense mutations occur in cbEGF-like domains.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=possibly damaging (score 0.533-0.818). The Tyr\u2192Cys substitution introduces a reactive thiol group that could form aberrant disulfide bonds.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Marfan syndrome) is highly specific for FBN1 mutations. Marfan syndrome has a well-defined genetic etiology with FBN1 being the primary causative gene.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations (VUS/LP/P) from different submitters (VCV000547296). HGMD lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CM074834). The variant creates a novel cysteine residue, which is a recognized pathogenic mechanism in FBN1-related disorders. PubMed references (PMID: 17657824, 25053872, 28941062) are associated with this variant."}}
{"variant_id": "789f422d-6d76-4b21-a4de-86cd8a494abc", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164871T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 131073, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_supporting": "Variant is completely absent from gnomAD and all population databases with at least 20x coverage for RUNX1. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level for rare variant evidence.", "BP4": "Computational evidence supports benign effect: REVEL score = 0.37 (<0.50 threshold), SpliceAI score = 0.0 (\u22640.20 threshold). SIFT predicts 'tolerated_low_confidence' (score 0.12), PolyPhen predicts 'benign' (score 0.039). Invitae advanced modeling indicates variant is not expected to disrupt RUNX1 protein function with 80% negative predictive value. The amino acid change (Gln\u2192Arg) involves residues with similar properties.", "notable": "This variant has been reviewed by the ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy Variant Curation Expert Panel (October 2024) and classified as Uncertain Significance using their RUNX1-specific ACMG specifications. Four independent ClinVar submitters (ClinGen VCEP, Invitae, Illumina, Ambry Genetics) all classify as VUS. The variant is located in the transactivation domain (exon 8), outside the critical Runt homology domain where most pathogenic missense variants cluster. No literature reports of this variant in affected individuals."}}
{"variant_id": "a13097ce-e827-4856-9d7e-7df256027eb9", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68856113C>T", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM5_Supporting", "PVS1", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 60033, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gln641Ter) in CDH1, a gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer (HDGC) and lobular breast cancer. This variant creates a premature stop codon at position 641, predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a truncated protein lacking critical C-terminal domains including the cytoplasmic domain essential for catenin binding and cell adhesion function.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome allele frequency = 3.97674e-06 (approximately 1 allele in 251,000). This frequency is well below the threshold expected for a pathogenic variant in an autosomal dominant cancer predisposition syndrome with high penetrance.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for CDH1-associated hereditary cancer syndrome. HDGC has a well-defined genetic etiology with CDH1 being the primary causative gene, accounting for 25-50% of families meeting clinical criteria.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic (Allele ID: 152540, rs587782750) with multiple submissions for hereditary diffuse gastric adenocarcinoma, hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome."}}
{"variant_id": "e2643a0a-ade5-4d0e-be57-7f62b573760d", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78082346C>G", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59697, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant NM_000152.5:c.1134C>G (p.Tyr378Ter) creates a premature stop codon in exon 7 of 20 in GAA, predicted to cause nonsense-mediated decay. Loss-of-function is an established disease mechanism for Pompe disease (glycogen storage disease type II). GAA encodes acid alpha-glucosidase, and complete or near-complete loss of enzyme activity causes the disease.", "PM2_Supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 population database. Applied as supporting level per ClinGen Lysosomal Diseases VCEP specifications for rare recessive disorders.", "PM3_Supporting": "One patient reported compound heterozygous with pathogenic variant c.-32-13T>G (PMID: 31392188). A second patient was compound heterozygous with c.1478C>T (p.Pro493Leu) (PMID: 29181627). Applied as supporting level to avoid circular logic per ClinGen VCEP.", "PP4": "Two patients with this variant have been reported with Pompe disease, both treated with enzyme replacement therapy (PMID: 29181627, 31392188). Patient phenotype is highly specific for glycogen storage disease type II, which has a single genetic etiology (GAA gene).", "PP5": "ClinVar VCV000595469 classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Lysosomal Storage Disorder Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, July 2023). FDA Recognized Database. Also classified as Pathogenic by Eurofins NTD LLC."}}
{"variant_id": "46a0658f-d1ec-44af-8a4b-2a05b09dd6b3", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.89717695C>T", "gene": "PTEN", "disease": "PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP7", "BP4", "BS1_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "PTEN VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 50908, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg130Ter) in PTEN, a tumor suppressor gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease for PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome (Cowden syndrome). This creates a premature stop codon at position 130, resulting in a truncated, non-functional protein. PTEN is haploinsufficient and LOF variants are definitively pathogenic.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 1.19e-05 (3/251,000 alleles). This is well below the expected frequency for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance, supporting rarity criterion.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome) is highly specific for PTEN pathogenic variants. PHTS has a single genetic etiology (PTEN mutations) with characteristic features including macrocephaly, hamartomas, and increased cancer risk.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (Allele ID: 22858, rs121909224). Classified as Pathogenic for Cowden syndrome 1, PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, macrocephaly-autism syndrome, hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, glioma susceptibility, and other PTEN-related conditions. All 14 RCV records show Pathogenic classification with no conflicting interpretations."}}
{"variant_id": "e05ab3dd-2e76-4b49-a527-3b0afef93b52", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.152957416C>T", "gene": "SLC6A8", "disease": "creatine transporter deficiency", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BP4", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Cerebral Creatine Deficiency Syndromes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 48864, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD (exome AF=0.0002, genome AF=0.00018) exceeds expected frequency for a rare X-linked disorder like creatine transporter deficiency. Combined ~33 alleles observed in population controls is inconsistent with a pathogenic variant for this rare condition.", "BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.645-14C>T) located 14bp from splice site. Not at canonical splice positions (\u00b11/2). VEP predicts 'intron_variant' with MODIFIER impact. No computational evidence supports splice disruption at this distance from the exon boundary.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as 'Benign' for Creatine transporter deficiency (RCV) and 'Likely benign' for unspecified conditions. Multiple submissions support benign classification (Allele ID: 379052)."}}
{"variant_id": "8fe2eb65-d1a6-46cb-9981-465634a75542", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164883C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 202902, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant rs2056461235 is absent from gnomAD population databases. No allele frequency data available, consistent with an extremely rare variant. Meets PM2 criterion for absence in population controls.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-FPD (Familial Platelet Disorder with predisposition to myeloid malignancy), which has a well-established single genetic etiology involving RUNX1 germline variants.", "notable": "This is a missense variant (p.Ser331Thr) in the C-terminal transactivation domain of RUNX1, outside the critical Runt Homology Domain (RHD). ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS (VCV000960548). In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT predicts 'tolerated_low_confidence' (score 0.26-0.33), PolyPhen predicts 'benign' (score 0.001). Literature (PMID:35026845) indicates that transactivation assays validated for RHD variants may not adequately assess C-terminal variants, and new assays are needed. PMID:38513139 demonstrates that C-terminal RUNX1 mutations can impair blood cell differentiation through distinct mechanisms, but this applies primarily to truncating mutations (nonsense/frameshift) rather than missense variants. The Ser331Thr change is a conservative substitution (serine to threonine, both polar hydroxyl-containing amino acids)."}}
{"variant_id": "b8df146f-25d6-43ed-a038-6945661b8df1", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296588C>T", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP5", "BS2"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59438, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg270Ter/R270X) creating a premature stop codon in MECP2, a gene where loss-of-function is an established mechanism of disease for Rett syndrome. The variant truncates the protein at amino acid 270, removing critical C-terminal domains. MECP2 is highly intolerant to loss-of-function variants (pLI ~1.0). Multiple transcripts affected: ENST00000303391.11:c.808C>T (p.Arg270*), ENST00000453960.7:c.844C>T (p.Arg282*), ENST00000630151.3:c.808C>T (p.Arg270*).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population databases. The G>A allele (pathogenic) has no reported frequency in gnomAD. Only the G>C allele (different variant, p.Arg270Gly) has extremely rare frequency (AF=5.49e-06). This variant is absent from controls, supporting rarity consistent with a pathogenic variant.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. VEP annotates this as 'stop_gained' with HIGH impact. The variant creates a premature termination codon, which is predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or a severely truncated non-functional protein. SIFT predicts 'deleterious' (score=0) for the missense allele at this position, indicating the arginine residue is functionally important.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2 mutations. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations. The X-linked inheritance pattern is consistent with MECP2-related disorder.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 26854, rs61750240) with multiple submissions for Rett syndrome, severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy with microcephaly, X-linked intellectual disability syndromes, and MECP2-related disorders. Multiple RCV accessions confirm pathogenic classification across independent submitters.", "notable": "R270X is one of the eight most common recurrent MECP2 mutations causing Rett syndrome, extensively documented in literature (>50 PubMed citations including PMIDs: 10814718, 10991688, 11241840, 11462237, 20420693, 31427717). Functional studies demonstrate that truncating mutations in MECP2 disrupt its ability to bind methylated DNA and regulate chromatin structure, leading to neurological dysfunction. The variant is located after the methyl-CpG binding domain (MBD) but removes the transcriptional repression domain (TRD) and C-terminal regions essential for protein function."}}
{"variant_id": "ef63c97b-506b-488b-ae9e-6d8a57a0d655", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.45364500A>C", "gene": "ITGB3", "disease": "Glanzmann thrombasthenia", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4_Strong", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Platelet Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 82871, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v4.1.0 (0 alleles observed). For autosomal recessive disorders, absence from population databases supports PM2 at supporting level per ClinGen PD-VCEP specifications.", "PM3_Supporting": "Proband GT11 (PMID:29675921) is compound heterozygous for p.His281Pro and p.Cys400Tyr (classified Pathogenic by PD-VCEP). Phasing not confirmed, but compound heterozygosity in trans is assumed based on clinical presentation. Meets PM3 at supporting level.", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: REVEL=0.988 (>>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score=1.0). Strong computational consensus for damaging effect.", "PP4": "Proband GT11 presents with classic Glanzmann thrombasthenia phenotype: mucocutaneous bleeding, impaired platelet aggregation with all agonists except ristocetin, and reduced surface expression of \u03b1IIb\u03b23 by flow cytometry. This phenotype is highly specific for GT with single genetic etiology (ITGA2B or ITGB3). ClinGen PD-VCEP applied PP4 at strong level based on phenotype specificity.", "PP5": "ClinGen Platelet Disorders Variant Curation Expert Panel (FDA-recognized database) classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic in August 2024 with detailed evidence review. Expert panel review status provides highest level of ClinVar confidence."}}
{"variant_id": "109f5c72-43ec-4d0b-bcb6-efc097589c61", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36252672T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BP2", "BA1", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 43562, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "gnomAD allele frequency of 0.45% (140/31,400 alleles) exceeds expected frequency for a rare autosomal dominant disorder with high penetrance. Hereditary thrombocytopenia/hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is rare (estimated <1:100,000), making this frequency inconsistent with pathogenicity.", "BP4": "Deep intronic variant (c.508+182A>G) located 182bp from the nearest exon boundary. No predicted splice impact - position is too far from canonical splice sites (\u00b11/2) to affect splicing. snpEff annotates as intron_variant with no functional consequence.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign (for Hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) and Likely benign (for unspecified conditions). ClinVar Allele ID: 1195565."}}
{"variant_id": "dd8fcc3c-dde1-42d4-a0f2-31bbafa786a5", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246714G>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PM3_Strong", "PP3", "PM2", "PP4_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 65247, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate R408W causes severely reduced/near-absent PAH enzyme activity. In vitro expression studies (PMID:26803807) show R408W has minimal residual activity. Multiple animal models (porcine, mouse) with humanized R408W mutation recapitulate classic PKU phenotype (PMID:33493163). This is the most common severe PKU-causing variant worldwide.", "PS4": "R408W is the most prevalent pathogenic PAH variant in European populations, accounting for up to 30-40% of PKU alleles in some populations. Extensive case-control data from newborn screening programs across multiple countries (Ukraine, Italy, Brazil, Japan) demonstrate significant enrichment in PKU patients vs controls (PMID:36046396, PMID:36537053).", "PM2": "Variant is rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF=0.00076 (0.076%), gnomAD genome AF=0.0019 (0.19%). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with carrier frequency expectations for a common PKU allele but still qualifies as rare (<1%).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.997-0.999). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene) with well-established genotype-phenotype correlations.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions (VCV000000577) from reputable clinical laboratories. Also listed in OMIM (612349.0002), HGMD, and PAHdb as pathogenic."}}
{"variant_id": "f7c77032-c599-46f3-9086-0bb73eb5c0c1", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103246621C>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP4", "PVS1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 61057, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Gly272Ter) creating premature stop codon in PAH gene. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for phenylketonuria (autosomal recessive). Variant occurs in exon 7 of 13 exons, predicted to trigger nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) or produce severely truncated non-functional protein lacking critical catalytic domain residues.", "PM2": "Variant is extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome AF = 3.58e-05 (9/251,000+ alleles); gnomAD genome AF = 1.27e-04 (4/31,000+ alleles). For an autosomal recessive disorder, this frequency is consistent with pathogenic carrier frequency and meets PM2 threshold.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (RCV000000627, RCV000089110) for phenylketonuria and PAH-related disorder. Extensive literature support with 14+ PubMed citations (PMID: 24350308, 26666653, 17935162, 9634518, 1301187, 10471838, 1671881, 1975559, 1978553, 8370573, 12655550, 36046396, 35749392, 20301677). Also catalogued in HGMD (CM900177, CD972373) and COSMIC (COSV100188143)."}}
{"variant_id": "37cf5142-fd3f-4896-9da9-ca4c54b542ea", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164712G>T", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1_Strong", "PS3_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56848, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Ser388Ter) creating premature stop codon in RUNX1. Loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism for hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome (FPDMM). Truncation occurs in the C-terminal transactivation domain (position 388 of 453 amino acids in canonical transcript), removing critical regulatory regions. Multiple transcripts affected with HIGH impact (stop_gained). RUNX1 haploinsufficiency is documented as disease mechanism in extensive literature (PMID:36626254, PMID:38019014, PMID:38513139).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exomes with frequency of 7.054e-07 (approximately 1 allele in 1.4 million). Absent in most populations (AFR, ASJ, MID, AMR, EAS, SAS). This frequency is well below the threshold expected for a dominant disorder with reduced penetrance.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (VCV000561222, RCV000824701, RCV000680383). Additionally listed in HGMD as disease-causing mutation (CM099539). Present in COSMIC as somatic mutation (COSV55892449) supporting functional relevance in hematologic malignancies.", "notable": "No specific functional studies found for this exact variant (p.Ser388Ter). However, RUNX1 C-terminal truncating mutations have been extensively studied and shown to impair blood cell differentiation (PMID:38513139). The variant is located in the transactivation domain, and truncating mutations in this region are well-documented to cause FPDMM."}}
{"variant_id": "484e1059-d6ac-4816-9757-dbdb0ed3bed2", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11213418A>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM2", "PM5_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 91594, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 and gnomAD v4.0 population databases (0 alleles observed). This extremely low frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PM5": "Novel missense change (p.Asp90Ala) at the same codon as established pathogenic variants. ClinGen FH VCEP has classified p.Asp90Glu (c.270T>A) as Pathogenic and p.Asp90Gly (c.269A>G) as Pathogenic at this same position. Multiple other variants at codon 90 (D90N, D90Y) are also classified as Likely Pathogenic/Pathogenic.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for familial hypercholesterolemia. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common (>4,000 variants in ClinVar).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.999-1.0). The variant causes a non-conservative amino acid change from aspartic acid (acidic, polar) to alanine (neutral, non-polar) in a critical ligand-binding domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of familial hypercholesterolemia is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR mutations account for the majority of monogenic FH cases, and the clinical presentation is consistent with this single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar submissions classify this variant as Likely Pathogenic/Pathogenic (VCV000440555). The ClinGen Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP specifically noted this variant (c.269A>C, p.Asp90Ala) as 'Likely pathogenic by these guidelines' in their expert panel review of the D90G variant at the same position."}}
{"variant_id": "7d7e8bbf-9b6b-4d97-8be1-241b9af74b09", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36164611C>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 133953, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_supporting", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_supporting": "Variant is completely absent from gnomAD exomes (frequency 0.00000) and all population databases with adequate coverage. Per ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting strength for rare variant evidence.", "BP4": "Multiple computational predictors suggest benign effect: REVEL score 0.089 (<0.50 threshold), SpliceAI score 0.0 (<0.2 threshold). While SIFT predicts deleterious_low_confidence (0.01) and PolyPhen predicts possibly_damaging (0.635), the primary predictor REVEL strongly suggests benign. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP applied BP4 based on these scores.", "notable": "ClinVar expert panel classification (ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP, Jan 2025) classified as VUS applying PM2_supporting and BP4. Variant is located in the C-terminal transactivation domain (TAD) of RUNX1, but Invitae's advanced protein modeling indicates this missense is not expected to disrupt RUNX1 function. Present in COSMIC as somatic variant (COSM5984449) but no germline case reports in literature. RUNX1 has established haploinsufficiency mechanism, but this missense does not appear to cause loss of function based on computational evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "3d3dd172-f31e-4e3e-b101-075568b4d23a", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43252846G>C", "gene": "ADA", "disease": "adenosine deaminase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 91261, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Tyr201*) in ADA gene where loss-of-function is a well-established mechanism of disease. This variant creates a premature stop codon at position 201 of 363 amino acids (55% of protein), predicted to result in nonsense-mediated decay or severely truncated non-functional protein. ADA deficiency causes autosomal recessive SCID through complete loss of adenosine deaminase enzymatic activity.", "PM2": "Variant is essentially absent from population databases. gnomAD exome frequency: 6.854e-07 (1 allele in ~1.5 million). This extremely low frequency is consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal recessive disorder.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (adenosine deaminase deficiency) is highly specific for ADA-SCID, which has a single genetic etiology. ADA is the only gene known to cause this condition, and the clinical presentation is characteristic.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000555182, RCV000670951). HGMD also lists this as a disease-causing mutation (CM159397). Multiple clinical laboratories have submitted concordant pathogenic classifications."}}
{"variant_id": "368e3c33-2763-454e-838d-189f8a79efb2", "variant": "NC_000002.11:g.203397312G>T", "gene": "BMPR2", "disease": "pulmonary arterial hypertension", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM1"], "expert_panel": "Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 54788, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the catalytic kinase domain (Pfam PF00069) of BMPR2, a functionally critical region. ClinGen Pulmonary Hypertension VCEP confirmed this as PM1_moderate. The kinase domain is essential for BMPR2 signaling function.", "PM2_Supporting": "Absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 and v4.1 (0 alleles observed). Per ClinGen PH VCEP specifications, this meets PM2 at supporting level for rare variant status.", "PP3": "Multiple computational predictors support deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0), REVEL=0.828, AlphaMissense=0.994. ClinGen VCEP confirmed PP3_supporting.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (pulmonary arterial hypertension) is highly specific for BMPR2-related disease. BMPR2 mutations account for ~70% of heritable PAH cases, making this a strong genotype-phenotype correlation."}}
{"variant_id": "94f76e8a-75fa-420e-a438-336ac5b850e1", "variant": "NC_000020.10:g.43251487C>A", "gene": "ADA", "disease": "adenosine deaminase deficiency", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Disease  VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 116762, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant (NC_000020.10:g.43251487C>A) is classified as an INTERGENIC VARIANT by Ensembl VEP, located approximately 1.4 Mb upstream of the ADA gene (ADA spans chr20:44,619,522-44,651,742 in GRCh38). The variant falls outside any known gene coding region, regulatory elements, or splice sites. No annotations were found in ClinVar, gnomAD, or other databases. While the clinical context suggests adenosine deaminase deficiency and the ADA gene is confirmed to be associated with this autosomal recessive condition (SCID due to ADA deficiency), this specific variant's intergenic location makes it highly unlikely to be causative. Loss-of-function in ADA is a known disease mechanism, but this variant does not affect the gene's coding sequence, splice sites, or known regulatory regions."}}
{"variant_id": "79e886d4-de41-4cb2-ab9a-80243c31a34e", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44187292C>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP1_Moderate", "PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 138856, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in critical functional domain (Pfam PF03727 glucokinase domain, Gene3D, Superfamily SSF53067). snpEff annotates as 'structural_interaction_variant' indicating impact on protein structure/function. GCK active site and glucose-binding regions are critical for enzyme function.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in population controls, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant for monogenic diabetes.", "PP2": "Missense variant in GCK, a gene where pathogenic missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). Loss-of-function missense mutations in GCK cause reduced enzyme activity leading to mild fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.919-0.999 across transcripts). HGMD lists as disease mutation (CM128024).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (monogenic diabetes) is highly specific for GCK-MODY, which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for 30-50% of MODY cases and presents with characteristic mild fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar classifies as 'Likely pathogenic' for Monogenic diabetes (Allele ID: 3543091, RCV: NM_000162.5(GCK):c.820G>T p.Asp274Tyr). HGMD also reports as disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "fd0cb6c9-7f1e-4644-9c34-95083a79a553", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11227594G>A", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 70672, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2_Supporting": "Variant is rare in gnomAD with overall AF of 8.35e-05 in exomes and 3.19e-05 in genomes. While not absent, this frequency is consistent with a rare disease-causing variant for familial hypercholesterolemia (population prevalence ~1:250). Applied as supporting level per ClinGen recommendations for variants present at low frequency.", "PP2": "LDLR is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease for familial hypercholesterolemia. The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation and pathogenic missense variants are common. LDLR missense variants account for the majority of FH cases.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of familial hypercholesterolemia is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR is one of only three genes (LDLR, APOB, PCSK9) known to cause autosomal dominant FH, with LDLR accounting for ~85-90% of genetically confirmed cases.", "notable": "In-silico predictions are conflicting: SIFT predicts deleterious (0.03) but PolyPhen predicts benign (0.185) for the canonical transcript. The variant is located in the EGF-like domain (PF00058) which is important for receptor recycling. ClinVar reports this variant as VUS with multiple submissions. HGMD entries (CM055370, CM151096) exist but without functional evidence. Literature (PMID: 35538921, 33994402) identifies this variant in FH cohorts but without segregation or functional data. Loss of function is an established mechanism for LDLR in FH, but this is a missense variant requiring additional evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "4cc0ea18-84f8-4a59-b14d-908303cbe14c", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296876T>C", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS3_Supporting", "PM6", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 76404, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS2", "PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS2": "De novo occurrence confirmed in multiple individuals with Rett syndrome. ClinGen Rett/Angelman Expert Panel reports at least 3 de novo occurrences with confirmed parentage (PMID: 10577905, 11309679, 19189931, 32393352). Applied at Very Strong level per ClinGen VCEP specifications.", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect: (1) Abolishes interaction with NCoR/SMRT co-repressor complex (PMID: 23770565, 23770587); (2) Impairs DNA-binding in vivo and in vitro (PMID: 26647311, 11058114); (3) Decreases microtubule stability (PMID: 23238081); (4) Mecp2-R306C knock-in mice recapitulate RTT-like phenotypes including compromised mobility, motor coordination deficits, and reduced brain weight (PMID: 24970834).", "PS4": "Variant observed in numerous affected individuals with Rett syndrome. RettBASE reports this variant accounts for approximately 5% of all classical RTT cases. ClinVar VCV000011824 has 203+ observations from RettBASE alone, with multiple clinical laboratory submissions confirming affected status.", "PM1": "Located in the well-characterized transcriptional repression domain (TRD) of MECP2, a critical functional domain essential for NCoR/SMRT co-repressor interaction and transcriptional repression function (PMID: 21326358, 23770565).", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD v4.0 and TOPMed (allele frequency 0.00000). Not observed in large population databases including ExAC. Meets PM2_supporting per ClinGen VCEP specifications.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), REVEL = 0.843 (>0.75 threshold). Highly conserved arginine residue across all mammalian species.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2-related disease. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of cases caused by MECP2 mutations. X-linked inheritance pattern consistent with MECP2 location on Xq28.", "PP5": "Classified as Pathogenic by ClinGen Rett and Angelman-like Disorders Variant Curation Expert Panel (reviewed by expert panel, March 2021). FDA Recognized Database. 49 ClinVar submissions, all concordant for Pathogenic classification with no conflicting interpretations."}}
{"variant_id": "580d30fb-1bb1-468a-bb63-1d786dac0556", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.76903286T>G", "gene": "MYO7A", "disease": "Usher syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3", "PM5_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 77422, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM3", "PM5", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD v4.1.0 with MAF of 0.00001332 (1/75,054 alleles) in African/African-American population, well below the ClinGen Hearing Loss VCEP threshold of <0.00007 for autosomal recessive disorders.", "PM3": "Detected in trans with a pathogenic variant c.6025del (p.Ala2009Profs*32) in a patient with Usher syndrome, confirmed by parental testing (PMID: 31836858). This satisfies PM3 for recessive disorders.", "PM5": "A different missense variant at the same codon (c.4114G>A, p.Val1372Met) has been reported in a homozygous patient with hearing loss and retinitis pigmentosa (PMID: 33576163), supporting that this residue is critical for protein function.", "PP3": "REVEL score of 0.869 exceeds the 0.7 threshold. SIFT predicts deleterious effect. PolyPhen-2 predicts possibly damaging (0.764). Multiple computational tools support a deleterious effect on protein function.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (congenital sensorineural hearing loss, delayed gross motor development, rod-cone dystrophy) is highly specific for Usher syndrome, a condition with single genetic etiology in MYO7A (PMID: 31836858).", "PP5": "ClinGen Hearing Loss Variant Curation Expert Panel classified this variant as Likely Pathogenic (Nov 2024) with detailed evidence review. This is an FDA-recognized database with expert panel review status."}}
{"variant_id": "af708230-b36c-499d-911b-dea7837335d0", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.120984338A>G", "gene": "TECTA", "disease": "nonsyndromic genetic deafness", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS1"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 59761, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency in gnomAD exceeds expected for rare hearing loss disorder. gnomAD exome AF=0.000469 (118 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.00143 (45 alleles). Combined frequency (~0.1-0.14%) is higher than expected for a pathogenic variant in a rare autosomal dominant or recessive hearing loss condition.", "BP4": "Computational evidence suggests benign effect. PolyPhen predicts benign (score=0.102). While SIFT predicts deleterious (score=0), the conflicting predictions and benign PolyPhen score support BP4. No CADD or DITTO scores available, but PolyPhen benign prediction is informative.", "notable": "ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with 4 submissions as Likely Benign and 1 as VUS. HGMD lists this as CM165466 but ClinVar consensus leans benign. Variant is in the entactin domain of TECTA which is involved in tectorial membrane structure. TECTA is associated with both autosomal dominant (DFNA8/12) and autosomal recessive (DFNB21) nonsyndromic hearing loss."}}
{"variant_id": "963e761f-325b-48ce-a0df-5227b788a759", "variant": "NC_000015.9:g.48764804T>C", "gene": "FBN1", "disease": "Marfan syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "FBN1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 85834, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in a critical EGF-like domain of fibrillin-1 (cbEGF domain region). The p.Tyr1427Cys substitution introduces a cysteine residue that disrupts the conserved disulfide bonding pattern essential for domain stability. EGF-like domains in FBN1 are mutational hotspots with minimal benign variation, and cysteine substitutions in these domains are well-established pathogenic mechanisms (PMID:36035136).", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD: overall frequency 6.84e-07 (1 allele in ~1.5 million). Only observed in African population at 2.987e-05. Essentially absent from controls, consistent with a pathogenic variant for a rare autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP2": "FBN1 has a low rate of benign missense variation and missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. Cysteine-affecting missense variants in EGF-like domains are particularly well-established as pathogenic in Marfan syndrome.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0.0), PolyPhen-2=probably_damaging (score 0.947). The variant affects a highly conserved tyrosine residue in a critical functional domain.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000449440). Three independent submissions classify as Likely Pathogenic for Marfan syndrome and TAAD, with one submission as VUS for TAAD.", "notable": "This variant creates a novel cysteine residue (p.Tyr1427Cys) in the cbEGF22 domain. Published functional studies on similar cysteine substitutions in FBN1 EGF domains demonstrate increased proteolytic sensitivity and decreased thermostability (PMID:36035136). The variant is listed in HGMD (CM117998). While no direct functional study exists for this specific variant, the mechanism is well-characterized for this class of mutations."}}
{"variant_id": "f83f99f0-226d-4d9d-9eb2-e32d2fbe6149", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11218187T>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PS4_Supporting", "PM1", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 1397812, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5", "PS4_Supporting"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant affects cysteine residue 313 located within the LDLR class A repeat/EGF-like domain, a critical functional region. Cysteine residues in these domains form disulfide bridges essential for protein structure and stability (PMID: 7548065, 7603991, 7979249). ClinGen FH Expert Panel confirms this residue is involved in disulfide bond formation.", "PM2": "Variant is absent from gnomAD v2.1.1 population database. No allele frequency reported in any population, supporting rarity consistent with pathogenic variant for familial hypercholesterolemia.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: REVEL=0.978 (>0.75 threshold), SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 0.921-1.0 across transcripts). All in-silico predictions concordantly support pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. Variant identified in >1 index cases who fulfill clinical criteria for FH after alternative causes of high cholesterol were excluded.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic with expert panel review status (ClinGen Familial Hypercholesterolemia Variant Curation Expert Panel, April 2023). FDA-recognized database classification with 4 concordant submissions.", "PS4_Supporting": "Variant identified in 2 unrelated index cases in published literature: one case fulfilling Simon Broome criteria for definite/possible FH (PMID: 22881376, Usifo et al, 2012); one case with DLCN \u22656 (PMID: 19318025, Alonso et al, 2009). Applied at supporting level per ClinGen FH guidelines.", "notable": "Other pathogenic variants at same codon (p.Cys313Trp, p.Cys313Tyr) classified as Likely Pathogenic, supporting clinical significance of this residue. LDLR has sufficient evidence for haploinsufficiency (ClinGen dosage sensitivity). Loss-of-function is established mechanism for familial hypercholesterolemia."}}
{"variant_id": "78310146-13d8-4116-8d32-8ca2f71d40dd", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36171645G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 66547, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PP2", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data available in myvariant or VEP annotations. For autosomal dominant RUNX1-FPD with reduced penetrance, absence from population databases supports PM2 at moderate strength per MM-VCEP guidelines.", "PP2": "RUNX1 is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease. The ClinGen MM-VCEP guidelines specifically note that missense variants in RUNX1 are pathogenic mechanisms for RUNX1-FPD. The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation in critical domains.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome is highly specific for RUNX1-FPD, which has a single genetic etiology (germline RUNX1 variants). This phenotype-genotype correlation supports PP4.", "notable": "The p.Ala307Val variant is located in the transactivation domain (TAD, amino acids 291-371) of RUNX1. Per MM-VCEP guidelines (PMID:31648317, 35764482), TAD variants require functional assay validation for PM1 application. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. ClinVar currently classifies this as VUS. The variant is a conservative amino acid substitution (Ala\u2192Val), but TAD missense variants have been shown to cause RUNX1-FPD in functional studies (PMID:35026845)."}}
{"variant_id": "fe229ac8-df07-4202-a7b4-3fb0171dbe5d", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36259204T>C", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 1321621, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1_Supporting": "Variant located within the Runt Homology Domain (RHD, AA 89-204) of RUNX1, a critical functional domain for DNA binding and transcription factor activity. ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP applied PM1 at supporting level as the variant affects a codon within the RHD but does not occur at an established hotspot residue.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. CADD=23.5 (\u226515 threshold met). REVEL=0.769 (near threshold of 0.75). SIFT predicts deleterious (score 0.02-0.049). PolyPhen-2 predictions mixed (probably damaging to benign depending on transcript). MetaLR and MetaSVM both predict damaging (D). snpEff identifies protein-protein contact and structural interaction effects.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related disease. RUNX1 is the primary gene associated with this condition (OMIM 601399), and the phenotype has a well-established single genetic etiology with autosomal dominant inheritance.", "notable": "ClinVar reports this variant as Uncertain Significance with expert panel review (ClinGen Myeloid Malignancy VCEP, Sep 2024). The expert panel applied PP3 and PM1_Supporting. gnomAD exome frequency is 1.2\u00d710\u207b\u2075 (3 alleles), which is present but extremely rare - does not meet PM2 threshold per ClinGen specifications. COSMIC reports this variant (COSV55867422) as a somatic mutation. No functional studies or case reports specific to this variant were identified in literature."}}
{"variant_id": "f9b818a7-0eb3-40ed-a6e6-fa82aecaff83", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296677G>A", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 1312099, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency exceeds 0.1% threshold in multiple populations: gnomAD exome AF=0.14% (262/183,000 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=0.13% (29/21,500 alleles). East Asian population shows highest frequency at 1.29% in gnomAD exome. This exceeds the BA1 stand-alone benign threshold of >0.1% for rare Mendelian disorders.", "BS1": "Population frequency (0.14% overall, up to 1.57% in EAS) is significantly higher than expected for Rett syndrome, which has an incidence of ~1:10,000-15,000 females. The variant frequency is incompatible with a pathogenic role in this severe X-linked dominant disorder.", "BP4": "Computational predictions support benign effect: SIFT=tolerated (score 0.09-0.1), PolyPhen=unknown/benign. The amino acid change (Ala\u2192Val) is conservative, involving two small hydrophobic residues. The variant is located outside critical functional domains (MBD and TRD).", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign/Likely benign with multiple concordant submissions (VCV000138188). Clinical significance includes: Benign for Rett syndrome (RTT), Benign for severe neonatal-onset encephalopathy, Benign for not specified conditions, and Likely benign for MECP2-related disorders. Multiple independent laboratories have classified this variant as benign."}}
{"variant_id": "5ffe0ec7-6736-4676-bf37-412af923d449", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44187429G>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PP4_Moderate", "PP2", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PM1", "PS4", "PS2", "PM3_Supporting", "PP1_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 1314145, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the glucokinase catalytic domain (Pfam PF03727, PROSITE PS51748). Thr228 is within a critical functional region involved in glucose binding and enzyme activity. Multiple structural domains identified including Gene3D and Superfamily SSF53067.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD exome database (AF = 3.99946e-06, approximately 1 allele in 250,000). This frequency is well below the expected threshold for a dominant disorder like GCK-MODY.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (MODY2). The gene has low tolerance for benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common in GCK-related disorders.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (scores 0.885-0.996 across transcripts). The variant affects a conserved threonine residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK variants cause a characteristic mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (Allele ID: 31173, rs80356655) with multiple submissions for MODY2, permanent neonatal diabetes mellitus, and GCK-related disorders. HGMD entries (CM032577, CM096860, CM920305) also support pathogenicity.", "notable": "This variant has been reported in multiple publications (PMIDs: 11372010, 20301620, 1502186, 9049484, 25555642). GCK encodes glucokinase, the glucose sensor in pancreatic beta cells, and loss-of-function variants cause MODY2 through reduced glucose phosphorylation and impaired insulin secretion."}}
{"variant_id": "981fcdec-991d-4878-a19d-3e45b688fc3b", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.76900412G>A", "gene": "MYO7A", "disease": "Usher syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP2"], "expert_panel": "Hearing Loss VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 1309184, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Nonsense variant (p.Arg666Ter) creating premature stop codon at position 666 in MYO7A, predicted to truncate protein by ~90% or trigger nonsense-mediated decay. MYO7A loss-of-function is an established mechanism for Usher syndrome type 1B (autosomal recessive). Variant affects canonical transcript NM_000260.4 with HIGH impact across multiple transcripts.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases: gnomAD exome AF=0.00002 (4/110,570 European chromosomes), gnomAD genome AF=0.00003. This frequency is consistent with recessive carrier frequency for a rare disease and meets PM2 threshold for autosomal recessive disorders.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Usher syndrome) is highly specific for MYO7A-related disease. Usher syndrome type 1B has a well-defined genetic etiology with MYO7A being the major causative gene. The combination of congenital profound hearing loss and progressive retinitis pigmentosa is pathognomonic.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic with 2-star review status (criteria provided, multiple submitters, no conflicts). 8 submissions from reputable laboratories including Laboratory for Molecular Medicine (Mass General Brigham), GeneDx, Invitae/Labcorp, and Fulgent Genetics all classify as Pathogenic. Multiple submitters explicitly cite ACMG criteria PVS1 and PM2.", "notable": "Extensive literature support: Variant reported in 4+ individuals with Usher syndrome type I across multiple publications (PMID: 10094549, 15043528, 15660226, 21569298, 35440622). R666X accounts for 23.8% (5/21) of MYO7A alleles in one USH1 cohort (Ouyang 2005). Functional studies confirm MYO7A loss-of-function causes disease (PMID: 8900236, 25404053). This evidence approaches PS4 threshold but formal case-control statistics not available."}}
{"variant_id": "f0755992-c309-4d96-b135-ffb7f9983bf0", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68772264C>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 68222, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PP4": "Patient phenotype (CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer) is highly specific for a disease with single genetic etiology (CDH1 germline variants). The clinical presentation aligns with hereditary diffuse gastric cancer syndrome.", "notable": "PM2 not met: Variant is present in gnomAD at low but detectable frequency (AF=1.91e-05 in exomes, 3 alleles). PP3 not met: SIFT predicts tolerated (0.07-0.24), PolyPhen predicts benign to possibly damaging (0.14-0.60); no CADD/DITTO scores available. PVS1 not applicable: This is a missense variant, not a null variant. The variant is located in the signal peptide domain (position 38), not in critical functional cadherin repeat domains. ClinVar shows conflicting interpretations with 2 VUS and 1 Likely Benign submission. No functional studies or case reports specific to p.Thr38Lys were identified."}}
{"variant_id": "6b2642de-1576-44fc-ad42-04b45dae029d", "variant": "NC_000010.10:g.112724286C>T", "gene": "SHOC2", "disease": "RASopathy", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2"], "expert_panel": "RASopathy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 82044, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This variant (SHOC2 c.170C>T, p.Ser57Phe) has conflicting classifications in ClinVar (6 VUS, 2 Likely Benign). The variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (0.006-0.01%), which is higher than expected for a fully penetrant dominant disorder. SIFT predicts deleterious but PolyPhen predicts benign, and REVEL score of 0.427 is below pathogenic threshold. The canonical pathogenic SHOC2 variant (p.Ser2Gly) causes disease through gain-of-function via aberrant N-myristoylation - this mechanism is specific to the N-terminal position and would not apply to p.Ser57Phe. Multiple clinical laboratories (LMM, Invitae, GeneDx, ARUP, Ambry) classify this as VUS with computational predictions described as 'inconclusive' or 'not expected to disrupt function'. Invitae's modeling indicates 80% negative predictive value for disrupting SHOC2 function. Position 57 is in the leucine-rich repeat domain but not at a critical functional residue based on structural studies (PMID 35348676)."}}
{"variant_id": "d25191fc-95b0-4444-8fc1-9115fe7c811c", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103245488G>A", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM5", "PM3", "PP4_Moderate", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67677, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.Arg408Trp) as previously established pathogenic variant. This is the most common pathogenic PAH variant worldwide, reported in ClinVar as Pathogenic with multiple submissions (VCV000000577).", "PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. R408W causes conformational instability and affects protein stability (FoldX analysis). Multiple in vitro and in vivo studies confirm loss of PAH enzyme function. Animal models (porcine, mouse) with humanized R408W mutation recapitulate PKU phenotype (PMID:33493163, PMID:39600089).", "PS4": "Variant is significantly enriched in PKU patients compared to controls. R408W is the most frequent PKU-causing variant globally, with allele frequency of ~6% in PKU patients (up to 9-14% in Mediterranean/Middle East populations) vs. ~0.08-0.19% in gnomAD population controls.", "PM1": "Located in the catalytic domain of PAH enzyme. The R408 residue is critical for protein conformational stability and proper enzyme function. Structural studies show this position is essential for PAH tetramer formation and catalytic activity.", "PP2": "Missense variant in PAH gene where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. PAH has a low rate of benign missense variation and >500 pathogenic missense variants have been reported.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably damaging (score 0.997-0.999). Variant affects highly conserved arginine residue.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology (PAH gene mutations) with autosomal recessive inheritance pattern matching the clinical context.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports variant as Pathogenic with multiple independent submissions from reputable clinical laboratories (RCV000000607, RCV000078507, RCV002287314, RCV002512607, RCV003415607)."}}
{"variant_id": "b1e30296-5bb3-4da2-b606-eff8628b5902", "variant": "NC_000011.9:g.108198370A>C", "gene": "ATM", "disease": "ATM-related cancer predisposition", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PM3_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Hereditary Breast, Ovarian and Pancreatic Cancer VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 56345, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PVS1", "PM2", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PVS1": "Canonical splice acceptor variant (c.6976-2A>C) at the -2 position in ATM, a gene where loss of function is an established mechanism of disease. ATM is a well-characterized tumor suppressor gene involved in DNA damage response. Splice site variants at canonical \u00b11/2 positions are expected to cause aberrant splicing leading to null allele through exon skipping or intron retention.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in gnomAD with allele frequency of 6.162e-06 (0.0006%), representing only ~1 allele in 162,000+ individuals. This is well below the threshold expected for a pathogenic variant in a cancer predisposition gene.", "PP5": "Multiple ClinVar submissions classify this variant as Pathogenic or Likely Pathogenic (ClinVar Allele ID: 152069, rs587782403). Conditions include: ATM-related cancer predisposition (Pathogenic), Ataxia-telangiectasia syndrome (Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic), Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome (Likely pathogenic), and Familial cancer of breast (Likely pathogenic)."}}
{"variant_id": "347060fc-6dd1-4d69-88d1-853b6e7ea0ae", "variant": "NC_000023.10:g.153296369T>C", "gene": "MECP2", "disease": "Rett syndrome", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting", "PS4_Supporting", "PM5_Strong"], "expert_panel": "Rett and Angelman-like Disorders VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 63519, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS1", "PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS1": "Same amino acid change (p.R306C) as previously established pathogenic variant. ClinVar VCV000011824 (rs28935468) classified as Pathogenic by multiple submitters for Rett syndrome, Angelman syndrome, intellectual disability, and other MECP2-related disorders. Extensive literature support with 60+ PubMed citations.", "PM1": "Located in the NCoR/SMRT interaction domain (NID) of MECP2, a critical functional domain essential for transcriptional repression. This domain is a mutational hotspot for Rett syndrome with minimal benign variation. The R306 residue is highly conserved and critical for protein function.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. No allele frequency data found in large population studies, consistent with a rare pathogenic variant in an X-linked gene causing severe early-onset disease.", "PP2": "MECP2 is a gene with a low rate of benign missense variation and where pathogenic missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. Missense variants in MECP2 are well-established causes of Rett syndrome.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect: SIFT = deleterious (score: 0). Variant affects a highly conserved arginine residue in a critical functional domain. Multiple protein domain databases (PIRSF, PANTHER) identify this region as functionally important.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (Rett syndrome) is highly specific for MECP2 mutations. Rett syndrome has a single genetic etiology with >95% of classic cases caused by MECP2 mutations. The clinical presentation strongly supports this molecular diagnosis.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic (VCV000011824) with multiple independent submissions from clinical laboratories. OMIM entry 300005.0016 documents this as a disease-causing mutation."}}
{"variant_id": "ee600241-27a2-46f8-8e47-92684c9a911a", "variant": "NC_000007.13:g.44185216G>A", "gene": "GCK", "disease": "monogenic diabetes", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PM2_Supporting", "PM5", "PS4", "PP1_Strong", "PM3_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Monogenic Diabetes VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 62177, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Variant located in the glucokinase catalytic domain, a critical functional region. GCK is a well-characterized enzyme where the active site and substrate-binding regions are mutational hotspots for MODY2. The E256 residue is located in a structurally important region affecting enzyme activity and conformational dynamics.", "PM2": "Extremely rare in population databases. gnomAD exome shows AF=3.98e-06 (1 allele in ~251,000 alleles). This frequency is well below the expected threshold for a dominant disorder like GCK-MODY, supporting PM2.", "PP2": "GCK is a gene where missense variants are a well-established mechanism of disease (GCK-MODY/MODY2). The gene has a low rate of benign missense variation, and pathogenic missense variants are common. Missense variants in GCK cause disease through altered enzyme kinetics.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (scores 0.919-0.989 across transcripts). The variant affects a conserved glutamate residue (E256K) in the catalytic domain.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype of monogenic diabetes is highly specific for GCK-MODY (MODY2), which has a single genetic etiology. GCK-MODY accounts for 30-50% of all MODY cases and presents with mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant (NM_000162.5:c.766G>A, p.Glu256Lys) as Pathogenic with multiple submissions for MODY2, monogenic diabetes, permanent neonatal diabetes mellitus, and related conditions. Allele ID: 259865, rsID: rs769268803."}}
{"variant_id": "4dcf3108-9d4a-4702-b048-b696302b2791", "variant": "NC_000001.10:g.171605263G>A", "gene": "MYOC", "disease": "primary open angle glaucoma", "ground_truth": "Likely Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BP4", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "Glaucoma VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 84295, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS4", "PM1", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS4": "Significantly increased prevalence in affected individuals vs controls. Multiple large population studies demonstrate strong association: OR 3.36-6.76 for POAG (PMID: 34081096, 30267046), OR 12.16 for advanced glaucoma. UK Biobank and FinnGen studies with >200,000 participants confirm statistically significant enrichment in glaucoma cases (95% CI excludes 1).", "PM1": "Located in the olfactomedin (OLF) domain of MYOC, a critical functional domain where >90% of glaucoma-causing mutations cluster. This domain is essential for protein folding and secretion. Mutations in this region cause protein misfolding and intracellular aggregation leading to trabecular meshwork cell death.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (primary open angle glaucoma) is highly specific for MYOC-associated disease. MYOC mutations account for ~5% of POAG cases and are the most well-established genetic cause of this condition. The phenotype-genotype correlation is well-documented.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Pathogenic/Likely Pathogenic by multiple submitters (VCV000007949). Multiple expert laboratories have classified this variant, with consensus toward pathogenicity despite some conflicting interpretations related to reduced penetrance.", "notable": "PVS1 NOT applied: Although this is a nonsense variant, MYOC-associated glaucoma operates through a gain-of-toxic-function mechanism (protein misfolding and aggregation), NOT loss-of-function. Truncated myocilin misfolds and aggregates intracellularly, causing ER stress and cell death. PM2 NOT met: Variant is present in gnomAD at ~0.1% frequency (not absent from controls), though this is consistent with reduced penetrance (~5-10% in population studies). The variant has extensive literature support with 40+ publications documenting its role in glaucoma pathogenesis."}}
{"variant_id": "016608ab-5f1d-4155-9b1b-a832115b425a", "variant": "NC_000003.11:g.37061839A>C", "gene": "MLH1", "disease": "colorectal cancer, hereditary nonpolyposis, type 2", "ground_truth": "Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PS3", "PP3_Moderate", "PP1_Strong", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 71837, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1", "PM2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1": "Located in the ATPase domain of MLH1 (residue 308), a critical functional domain essential for mismatch repair activity. The ATPase domain (residues ~1-340) is a mutational hotspot with established pathogenic variants.", "PM2": "Absent from gnomAD population database. Variant rs1559543768 not found in population controls, consistent with rare pathogenic variant in autosomal dominant disorder.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). Histidine to Proline substitution introduces a helix-breaking residue at a conserved position.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer type 2/Lynch syndrome) is highly specific for MLH1-associated disease with single genetic etiology.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports as Likely Pathogenic (VCV000561172) with multiple submissions for Lynch syndrome 1 and hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal neoplasms. Evidence from clinical testing laboratories.", "notable": "This is a missense variant (p.His308Pro) in the N-terminal ATPase domain of MLH1. While not a null variant (PVS1 not applicable), the location in a critical functional domain and strong computational predictions support pathogenicity. No specific functional studies found for this exact variant (PS3 not met)."}}
{"variant_id": "67b39111-3008-4f7c-ad1e-56534ac6aeb8", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.11210970G>C", "gene": "LDLR", "disease": "hypercholesterolemia, familial", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Familial Hypercholesterolemia VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 75491, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM1", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. The G>C change (p.Asp47His) has no reported allele frequency. The alternate G>A change at same position (p.Asp47Asn) has extremely low frequency (AF=1.59e-05). Meets PM2 threshold for rare variant.", "PM1": "Located in the first cysteine-rich ligand-binding repeat (LR1) of LDLR, a critical functional domain. Position 47 is adjacent to cysteine 46, which is essential for proper domain folding and apolipoprotein recognition (PMID:30332439). Multiple HGMD disease-associated mutations cluster at this position (CD880088, CM010896, CM1313165).", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score=0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score=0.999-1.0). Consistent predictions across all LDLR transcripts support damaging effect.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (familial hypercholesterolemia) is highly specific for LDLR-related disease. LDLR is one of three major genes (LDLR, APOB, PCSK9) causing this condition, with LDLR accounting for ~90% of genetically confirmed cases."}}
{"variant_id": "56437f7f-3e3f-4167-a8b4-6f400c68eb1a", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36161203G>A", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": [], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 45686, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning benign)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": [], "aiva_evidence": {"notable": "This is a 3' UTR variant (c.*3229C>T) in RUNX1. While RUNX1 germline mutations are established causes of hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome (FPDMM), this specific variant is located in the 3' untranslated region and does not affect the protein coding sequence. ClinVar classifies this variant as VUS. The variant is present in gnomAD at low frequency (AF=6.37e-05, 2 alleles), which does not support PM2. No computational predictions (CADD, DITTO) are available for this non-coding variant. The 3' UTR location means PVS1 (null variant) does not apply. No functional studies or segregation data are available for this specific variant."}}
{"variant_id": "1eca410d-5681-4ef6-a109-45927d4ba949", "variant": "NC_000019.9:g.38931469C>T", "gene": "RYR1", "disease": "malignant hyperthermia, susceptibility to, 1", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1", "PS3_Moderate", "PS4_Moderate", "PP3_Moderate"], "expert_panel": "Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 143894, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PS3", "PS4", "PM1", "PP1", "PP3", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PS3": "Well-established functional studies demonstrate damaging effect. In vitro studies in HEK293 cells show increased sensitivity to RYR1 agonists (PMID: 27586648). p.Gly2434Arg knock-in mice are susceptible to malignant hyperthermia due to volatile anesthetics, and ex vivo assays demonstrate increased sensitivity to RYR1 agonists for knock-in myotubes (PMID: 30236258). Additional studies show enhanced sensitivity to activating concentrations of Ca2+ and caffeine, with reduced sensitivity to inhibiting concentrations of Ca2+ and calmodulin (PMID: 9030597, 9334205).", "PS4": "Variant reported in 178 unrelated individuals with personal or family history of malignant hyperthermia reaction, with 174 having positive IVCT or CHCT results. This is the most common MHS variant detected in the United Kingdom (PMID: 30236257). Prevalence in affected individuals significantly exceeds controls.", "PM1": "Located in a mutational hotspot region (central region, amino acids 2,101-2,458) for pathogenic variants contributing to malignant hyperthermia susceptibility (PMID: 21118704). Variant resides within the RIH domain of RYR1, defined as a critical functional domain.", "PP1": "Strong co-segregation with disease. Variant segregates with MHS in at least 20 individuals across multiple families (PMID: 7849712, 11575529, 12059893, 25960145). ClinGen Expert Panel applied PP1_Strong.", "PP3": "Computational evidence supports deleterious effect. PolyPhen: possibly_damaging (0.466-0.858), SIFT: deleterious. REVEL score = 0.956 (>0.85 threshold). Multiple in silico tools predict damaging effect on protein function.", "PP5": "ClinGen Malignant Hyperthermia Susceptibility Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (July 2022) with FDA Recognized Database status. 24+ submitters in ClinVar report as Pathogenic with no conflicts. PharmGKB Level 1A evidence for drug response.", "notable": "gnomAD frequency: 0.005% (AF=0.00003-0.00005), consistent with pathogenicity for MHS. Variant also associated with drug response (toxicity) to volatile anesthetics (desflurane, enflurane, halothane, isoflurane, methoxyflurane, sevoflurane) and succinylcholine. BS2 was noted by expert panel (6 individuals with negative IVCT/CHCT) but does not outweigh strong pathogenic evidence."}}
{"variant_id": "8ebd9d7f-d1a0-47af-9174-119032365842", "variant": "NC_000005.9:g.112164561G>A", "gene": "APC", "disease": "familial adenomatous polyposis 1", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BA1", "BP4", "BP7"], "expert_panel": "InSiGHT Hereditary Colorectal Cancer/Polyposis VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 45385, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BA1", "BP7", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BA1": "Allele frequency of 64.9% in gnomAD exomes and 59.1% in gnomAD genomes far exceeds the 5% threshold for stand-alone benign classification. This is a common polymorphism (rs351771).", "BP7": "Synonymous variant (p.Ala545=) with no predicted splice impact. VEP analysis shows no splice region consequences and the variant is classified as LOW impact.", "BP6": "ClinVar reports this variant as Benign across multiple conditions including Familial adenomatous polyposis 1 (FAP1), APC-Associated Polyposis Disorders, Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and Carcinoma of colon. Multiple independent submissions support benign classification."}}
{"variant_id": "bffc9e02-2932-4532-96c4-687f086c6193", "variant": "NC_000021.8:g.36231830T>G", "gene": "RUNX1", "disease": "hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM1_Supporting", "PP3", "PM2_Supporting"], "expert_panel": "Myeloid Malignancy VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 149424, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "VUS (leaning pathogenic)", "aiva_confidence": "medium", "aiva_criteria": ["PM1_supporting", "PM2_supporting", "PP3", "PP4"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM1_supporting": "Missense variant at amino acid position 185 within the RUNX1 Runt Homology Domain (RHD, aa 89-204). Per ClinGen MM-VCEP RUNX1-specific guidelines (PMID:35764482), PM1_supporting applies to missense variants affecting residues 89-204 within the RHD. This domain is critical for DNA binding and CBF\u03b2 heterodimerization.", "PM2_supporting": "Variant is absent from gnomAD population database. Per ClinGen SVI recommendation and RUNX1-specific guidelines (version 2), PM2 is downgraded to PM2_supporting. The variant (rs1569061888) has no reported allele frequency in gnomAD.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen=probably_damaging (score 1.0). snpEff annotations indicate protein_protein_contact and structural_interaction_variant effects. While REVEL and CADD scores were not directly available, the consistent deleterious predictions from SIFT/PolyPhen support PP3.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (hereditary thrombocytopenia and hematologic cancer predisposition syndrome) is highly specific for RUNX1-related familial platelet disorder with myeloid malignancy (FPDMM), which has a single genetic etiology. RUNX1 is the only known gene associated with this specific syndrome."}}
{"variant_id": "4c782a9b-194f-4bcf-b836-b7f74d93b474", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103234244A>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PP3", "PP4", "PM5", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 204108, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM2", "PM5", "PP2", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM2": "Variant absent from gnomAD population database. For autosomal recessive disorder, absence from controls supports pathogenicity. rs62644471 has no reported allele frequency in gnomAD.", "PM5": "Novel missense at same codon as established pathogenic variant. Position Tyr417 has pathogenic variant p.Tyr417His (c.1249T>C, ClinVar Pathogenic) and p.Tyr417Asn reported in HGMD. This p.Tyr417Asp represents a different amino acid substitution at the same critical residue.", "PP2": "PAH is a gene where missense variants are a common mechanism of disease. Over 1,000 PAH variants have been reported in phenylketonuria, with missense variants comprising the majority. Low rate of benign missense variation in this gene.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict deleterious effect: SIFT=0 (deleterious), PolyPhen=0.991-0.996 (probably damaging). Variant located in conserved catalytic domain (PS51410, Pfam PF00351).", "PP4": "Patient phenotype (phenylketonuria) is highly specific for PAH deficiency. PKU has a single genetic etiology with >99% of cases caused by biallelic PAH variants.", "PP5": "ClinVar reports this variant as Likely Pathogenic (Allele ID: 1318156, RCV001789814). Multiple HGMD entries at this position (CM024632, CM973397, HM971461) support pathogenicity."}}
{"variant_id": "1c44650b-cb84-4ebf-98b5-8d7696e6a2f6", "variant": "NC_000017.10:g.78086747C>A", "gene": "GAA", "disease": "glycogen storage disease II", "ground_truth": "Likely Pathogenic", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM2_Supporting", "PVS1"], "expert_panel": "Lysosomal Diseases VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 123823, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Pathogenic", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["PM3_Strong", "PS3_Moderate", "PM1", "PM2_Supporting", "PP3", "PP4", "PP5"], "aiva_evidence": {"PM3_Strong": "Detected in trans with pathogenic variants in multiple patients with Pompe disease: compound heterozygous with c.-32-13T>G (2 probands), c.2481+110_2646+39del (2 probands), and one homozygote. ClinGen LSD VCEP upgraded PM3 to Strong based on multiple independent observations.", "PS3_Moderate": "In vitro functional studies demonstrate <2% residual GAA enzyme activity in COS-7 and HEK293 cells compared to wildtype (PMID: 19862843, 24715333). Western blot analysis shows abnormal protein processing with minimal production of active 76 kDa form (PMID: 24715333). Applied at Moderate level per ClinGen LSD VCEP specifications.", "PM1": "Located at Arg600, a critical residue in the active site architecture and substrate binding of GAA enzyme. Crystallography studies (PMID: 29061980) confirm this residue is essential for enzyme function. ClinGen LSD VCEP has defined this as a critical residue.", "PM2_Supporting": "Extremely rare in population databases: gnomAD exome AF = 1.21e-05 (3/248,322 alleles). Highest population frequency is 0.00003 in South Asian population, well below ClinGen LSD VCEP threshold of <0.001 for PM2_Supporting.", "PP3": "Multiple computational tools predict damaging effect: SIFT = deleterious (score 0), PolyPhen = probably_damaging (score 1.0), REVEL = 0.967 (above 0.7 threshold). All in-silico predictors concordantly predict pathogenicity.", "PP4": "Patient phenotype highly specific for Pompe disease (GSD II). Variant reported in at least 7-12 patients with symptoms consistent with infantile-onset or late-onset Pompe disease, including <10% GAA activity in muscle, cardiac hypertrophy, respiratory distress, and improvement on enzyme replacement therapy.", "PP5": "ClinGen Lysosomal Storage Disorder Variant Curation Expert Panel classified as Pathogenic (reviewed by expert panel, Oct 2022). 15 ClinVar submissions: 13 Pathogenic, 2 Likely Pathogenic, with no conflicting interpretations. FDA Recognized Database."}}
{"variant_id": "a5aaee48-e09b-460f-91c0-455f0065cfa0", "variant": "NC_000016.9:g.68844232G>A", "gene": "CDH1", "disease": "CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer", "ground_truth": "Benign", "ground_truth_criteria": ["BS2", "BP2_Strong", "BS1"], "expert_panel": "CDH1 VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 67877, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "aiva_classification": "Likely Benign", "aiva_confidence": "high", "aiva_criteria": ["BS1", "BP4", "BP6"], "aiva_evidence": {"BS1": "Allele frequency exceeds expected for hereditary diffuse gastric cancer. gnomAD exome AF=8.75e-05 (22 alleles), gnomAD genome AF=3.19e-05 (1 allele). Combined frequency (~0.008%) exceeds the expected carrier frequency for HDGC (prevalence ~1:100,000 with high penetrance).", "BP4": "Computational evidence is mixed but leans benign. PolyPhen-2 shows conflicting predictions: 0.981 (probably damaging) on canonical transcript but 0.433 (benign) on alternate transcript. SIFT shows 0.03 (deleterious) on canonical but 0.1 (tolerated) on alternate. The variant is in a cadherin repeat domain but not at a critical calcium-binding residue. Glycine to serine is a relatively conservative substitution.", "BP6": "ClinVar (VCV000186326) reports this variant as Benign/Likely Benign by multiple submitters. Classifications include: Benign for HDGC, Benign for CDH1-related diffuse gastric and lobular breast cancer syndrome, Likely Benign for hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome, and Likely Benign for familial breast/ovarian cancer. One submission shows conflicting interpretations, but consensus leans benign.", "notable": "This is a missense variant (p.Gly274Ser) in the extracellular cadherin domain 2. CDH1 loss-of-function is the established disease mechanism for HDGC, but missense variants require functional evidence. No functional studies specific to this variant were identified. The variant is present in COSMIC (COSM6854547) as a somatic mutation and HGMD (CM123531), but ClinVar consensus from multiple expert laboratories supports benign classification."}}
{"variant_id": "532e385e-584f-4484-82d6-19b38c609ef7", "variant": "NC_000012.11:g.103249097G>C", "gene": "PAH", "disease": "phenylketonuria", "ground_truth": "Uncertain Significance", "ground_truth_criteria": ["PM3_Supporting", "PP4", "PP3", "PM2"], "expert_panel": "Phenylketonuria VCEP", "execution_time_ms": 650753, "model_used": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "error": "HTTP 500: {\"detail\":{\"error\":{\"code\":\"INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR\",\"message\":\"Internal server error\",\"details\":\"Failed to complete variant classification\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-10T05:09:30.478598Z\",\"request_id\":\"a86f8"}
